:"197. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #57","paragraphs":["RECALL Critical event. Need: identify: all affected product."]},{"heading":"198. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Recall traceability/workflow."]},{"heading":"199. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«In a recall scenario, how quickly can you identify all affected batches, inventory locations and distribution destinations;»"]},{"heading":"200. VERY STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"201. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #58","paragraphs":["DISTRIBUTION TRACEABILITY Batch leaves: factory. Need know: where it went."]}]],["Σημεία 201–225 · OPPORTUNITY",[{"heading":"202. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["ERP/distribution integration."]},{"heading":"203. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #59","paragraphs":["COLD CHAIN Some products: temperature-sensitive."]},{"heading":"204. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Temperature monitoring + exception workflow."]},{"heading":"205. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«When a temperature excursion occurs in storage or transport, how quickly is it linked to affected product and quality assessment;»"]},{"heading":"206. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #60","paragraphs":["TEMPERATURE EXCURSIONS Need: investigation."]},{"heading":"207. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Excursion case management."]},{"heading":"208. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #61","paragraphs":["CLINICAL TRIAL OPERATIONS Pharma may run: clinical trials."]},{"heading":"209. Complex ecosystem:","paragraphs":["sites, investigators, patients, vendors, data, documents."]},{"heading":"210. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Clinical operations workflow."]},{"heading":"211. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which clinical-trial coordination task today generates the most manual follow-up across sites or vendors;»"]},{"heading":"212. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #62","paragraphs":["STUDY DOCUMENTS Clinical trials: document-heavy."]},{"heading":"213. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Trial document management."]},{"heading":"214. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How much time does the team spend chasing missing or outdated study documents;»"]},{"heading":"215. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN 