 analytics."]},{"heading":"295. NEED","paragraphs":["historical failure data."]},{"heading":"296. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Do you have enough historical failure and telemetry data to distinguish useful predictive signals from noise;»"]},{"heading":"297. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #87","paragraphs":["FIELD AI Could help: technician: diagnostics."]},{"heading":"298. Need:","paragraphs":["validated recommendations."]},{"heading":"299. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #88","paragraphs":["DOCUMENT AI Telecom also has: contracts, network docs, procedures, site reports."]},{"heading":"300. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Document search/extraction."]}]],["Σημεία 301–325 · ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #89",[{"heading":"301. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #89","paragraphs":["SITE ACQUISITION / NETWORK SITES Telecom infrastructure projects: need: candidate sites, permits, leases, construction, commissioning."]},{"heading":"302. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Site acquisition / rollout workflow."]},{"heading":"303. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which step from candidate site to on-air status creates the longest delay today;»"]},{"heading":"304. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #90","paragraphs":["SITE DOCUMENTS Each site: may have: lease, permit, drawings, technical docs."]},{"heading":"305. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Site document repository."]},{"heading":"306. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can you see all critical site documents, expiry dates and approvals from one location;»"]},{"heading":"307. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #91","paragraphs":["SITE LEASES Tower/site leases: need: renewal tracking."]},{"heading":"308. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Lease management."]},{"heading":"309. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How are lease expiries, rent changes and renewal actions tracked across sites;»"]},{"heading":"310. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #92","paragraphs":["PERMIT TRACKING Network expansion: depends on: permits."]},{"heading":"311. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Permit workflow."]},{"heading":"312. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which permit/approval type creates the most schedule uncertainty in rollout;»"]},{"heading":"313. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #93","paragraphs":["CONTRACTOR MANAGEMENT Tower/fiber work: often outsourced."]},{"heading":"314. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Contractor portal."]},{"heading":"315. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How do you track contractor progress, quality and SLA across many network sites;»"]},{"heading":"316. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #94","paragraphs":["SITE ACCEPTANCE Build complete. Need: inspection + acceptance."]},{"heading":"317. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Digital acceptance workflow."]},{"heading":"318. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How many manual documents and approvals are needed from construction completion to operational acceptance;»"]},{"heading":"319. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #95","paragraphs":["NETWORK ROLLOUT REPORTING Management wants: sites planned, built, live."]},{"heading":"320. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Rollout dashboard."]},{"heading":"321. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which rollout status requires the most manual consolidation across contractors and regions;»"]},{"heading":"322. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #96","paragraphs":["POWER / ENERGY AT NETWORK SITES Sites consume: energy."]},{"heading":"323. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Energy monitoring."]},{"heading":"324. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can you compare energy consumption and abnormal usage across network sites;»"]},{"heading":"325. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #97","paragraphs":["BACKUP POWER Network sites may have: batteries/generators."]}]],["Σημεία 326–350 · OPPORTUNITY",[{"heading":"326. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Asset/maintenance monitoring."]},{"heading":"327. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How is backup-power readiness and maintenance tracked today across sites;»"]},{"heading":"328. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #98","paragraphs":["PARTNER INTERCONNECTION Third parties: connect to telecom systems."]},{"heading":"329. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Partner API/onboarding workflow."]},{"heading":"330. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How long does it take to technically onboard a new partner and what typically delays the process;»"]},{"heading":"331. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #99","paragraphs":["SERVICE ASSURANCE Need: know: whether customer service actually works."]},{"heading":"332. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Service assurance analytics."]},{"heading":"333. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can you measure service health from the customer's service perspective rather than only individual network elements;»"]},{"heading":"334. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Network up: does not always mean: customer service good."]},{"heading":"335. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #100","paragraphs":["CLOSED-LOOP OPERATIONS Alert ↓ Diagnosis ↓ Action ↓ Verification."]},{"heading":"336. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Automation/orchestration."]},{"heading":"337. BUT","paragraphs":["must introduce: carefully."]},{"heading":"338. NEVER PROMISE","paragraphs":["autonomous network changes without: very strong controls."]},{"heading":"339. DECISION MAKERS","paragraphs":["Depending project: CIO CTO COO Chief Network Officer Head of OSS/BSS Customer Operations Director Digital Director Billing Director NOC Director Field Service Director Enterprise Business Director CFO Head of Data."]},{"heading":"340. CTO / NETWORK","paragraphs":["Cares about: network performance, reliability, automation, architecture."]},{"heading":"341. CIO","paragraphs":["Cares about: BSS, integration, data, security."]},{"heading":"342. COO","paragraphs":["Cares about: end-to-end operations, efficiency, customer impact."]},{"heading":"343. CUSTOMER OPERATIONS","paragraphs":["Cares about: call volume, FCR, complaints, service time."]},{"heading":"344. BILLING DIRECTOR","paragraphs":["Cares about: accuracy, exceptions, revenue leakage."]},{"heading":"345. NOC DIRECTOR","paragraphs":["Cares about: alarms, outages, MTTR, automation."]},{"heading":"346. FIELD SERVICE","paragraphs":["Cares about: dispatch, first-time fix, productivity."]},{"heading":"347. ENTERPRISE DIRECTOR","paragraphs":["Cares about: customer delivery, SLA, complex orders."]},{"heading":"348. CFO","paragraphs":["Cares about: revenue assurance, opex, capex, ROI."]},{"heading":"349. HEAD OF DATA","paragraphs":["Cares about: scale, quality, real-time pipelines, analytics."]},{"heading":"350. WHO TO APPROACH FIRST","paragraphs":["Customer onboarding/provisioning: Customer Ops / BSS / Digital."]}]],["Σημεία 351–375 · Billing:",[{"heading":"351. Billing:","paragraphs":["Billing + IT."]},{"heading":"352. Network operations:","paragraphs":["NOC / Network Operations."]},{"heading":"353. Field service:","paragraphs":["Field Service Director."]},{"heading":"354. Data:","paragraphs":["Head of Data + business owner."]},{"heading":"355. Major transformation:","paragraphs":["COO + CIO + CTO."]},{"heading":"356. RESEARCH BEFORE OUTREACH","paragraphs":["Look for: Fiber rollout 5G expansion New digital brand New BSS/OSS program New customer app Acquisition/merger Network modernization Enterprise-services expansion."]},{"heading":"357. TRIGGER","paragraphs":["Large fiber rollout."]},{"heading":"358. HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["More complexity: between: build, inventory, serviceability, customer activation."]},{"heading":"359. OUTREACH EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι επεκτείνετε σημαντικά το fiber footprint. Σε τέτοιες φάσεις συχνά το challenge δεν είναι μόνο η κατασκευή αλλά το πώς rollout status, network inventory and commercial serviceability stay synchronized. Δεν γνωρίζω αν ισχύει σε εσάς, αλλά θα είχε νόημα να καταλάβω πού εμφανίζεται σήμερα το μεγαλύτερο handoff gap;»"]},{"heading":"360. ANOTHER TRIGGER","paragraphs":["New customer app."]},{"heading":"361. POSSIBLE PAIN","paragraphs":["Front-end digital but: legacy back-end."]},{"heading":"362. DISCOVERY OPENING","paragraphs":["«Θα ήθελα να χαρτογραφήσουμε τη διαδρομή από customer order μέχρι active service και να δούμε πού υπάρχουν fallout, waiting time or manual intervention.»"]},{"heading":"363. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["«Ποια customer process φαίνεται digital externally αλλά still depends heavily on manual OSS/BSS work internally;»"]},{"heading":"364. STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"365. NETWORK OPENING","paragraphs":["«Θα ήθελα να καταλάβω τη διαδρομή από first alarm μέχρι service restoration και πού χάνεται περισσότερο time.»"]},{"heading":"366. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["«If a major network issue happens, how quickly can you identify all affected customers and communicate consistent status to customer care;»"]},{"heading":"367. VERY STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"368. SCALE QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Αν order volume or network footprint αυξανόταν 30%, ποιο operational process would become the first bottleneck;»"]},{"heading":"369. METRICS TO DISCOVER","paragraphs":["Depending project: Orders/day Activation time Order fallout rate Billing complaints Calls/customer First-contact resolution Churn."]},{"heading":"370. NETWORK METRICS","paragraphs":["Alarms Incidents MTTR Availability Field visits First-time fix Capacity utilization."]},{"heading":"371. BUSINESS CASE — ACTIVATION","paragraphs":["Faster activation: could mean: faster revenue start better CX."]},{"heading":"372. BUSINESS CASE — ORDER FALLOUT","paragraphs":["Less manual intervention."]},{"heading":"373. BUSINESS CASE — BILLING","paragraphs":["Fewer errors/disputes."]},{"heading":"374. BUSINESS CASE — CALL CENTER","paragraphs":["Reduce repetitive contacts."]},{"heading":"375. BUSINESS CASE — MTTR","paragraphs":["Faster restoration: may reduce customer impact."]}]],["Σημεία 376–400 · BUSINESS CASE — FIELD SERVICE",[{"heading":"376. BUSINESS CASE — FIELD SERVICE","paragraphs":["Better first-time fix: may reduce repeat visits."]},{"heading":"377. BUSINESS CASE — REVENUE ASSURANCE","paragraphs":["Identify missing billing/reconciliation gaps."]},{"heading":"378. DON'T INVENT SAVINGS","paragraphs":["Use: customer baseline."]},{"heading":"379. TECHNICAL DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: CRM? Order Management? Product Catalog? Billing? Mediation? OSS? Network Inventory? NMS?"]},{"heading":"380. ALSO","paragraphs":["Fault management? Field service? Data platform? API gateway? Identity provider? Cloud/on-prem?"]},{"heading":"381. NMS","paragraphs":["Network Management System."]},{"heading":"382. SOURCE OF TRUTH","paragraphs":["Ask: «Which system is authoritative for customer, service, order, product, billing and network-resource data;»"]},{"heading":"383. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Different domains: likely: different systems."]},{"heading":"384. NEED","paragraphs":["data ownership map."]},{"heading":"385. REAL-TIME NEEDS","paragraphs":["Network incident: yes."]},{"heading":"386. Monthly commercial report:","paragraphs":["not necessarily."]},{"heading":"387. DON'T MAKE EVERYTHING REAL-TIME","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"388. TELECOM SCALE","paragraphs":["Architecture must consider: huge volumes."]},{"heading":"389. Especially:","paragraphs":["usage, network telemetry, alarms."]},{"heading":"390. PERFORMANCE / RESILIENCE","paragraphs":["critical."]},{"heading":"391. NETWORK INTEGRATION","paragraphs":["May touch: critical operational systems."]},{"heading":"392. MUST INVOLVE","paragraphs":["network architecture + cyber."]},{"heading":"393. TELECOM POC","paragraphs":["Could test: order fallout analytics OSS/BSS integration alarm correlation agent assist network data pipeline."]},{"heading":"394. PROTOTYPE","paragraphs":["Could test: customer self-service flow technician app enterprise portal."]},{"heading":"395. PILOT","paragraphs":["Could be: one product, one region, one workflow, one network domain."]},{"heading":"396. PILOT SUCCESS CRITERIA","paragraphs":["Cycle time Accuracy Manual-work reduction User adoption System reliability."]},{"heading":"397. TELECOM OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε ήδη BSS.» Response: «Τότε δεν θα ξεκινούσα από replacement. Θα ήθελα να δω πού υπάρχουν order fallout, duplicate entry or gaps between CRM, order management, billing and provisioning.»"]},{"heading":"398. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε ήδη OSS.» Response: «Τότε το question is where OSS processes still require manual correlation, escalation or handoff between network and customer operations.»"]},{"heading":"399. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Το network είναι πολύ critical για αλλαγές.» Response: «Σωστά. Τότε θα ξεκινήσουμε με read-only integration or controlled workflow where appropriate rather than touching control logic unnecessarily.»"]},{"heading":"400. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Οι technicians χρησιμοποιούν ήδη 3 apps.» Response: «Τότε η λύση δεν πρέπει να γίνει τέταρτο app χωρίς λόγο. Πρέπει να δούμε αν μπορούμε να consolidate context or remove steps from the current workflow.»"]}]],["Σημεία 401–425 · OBJECTION",[{"heading":"401. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Θέλουμε AI στο NOC.» Response: «Ποιο task θέλετε να improve first — alarm correlation, anomaly detection, incident summarization or root-cause assistance — και ποια historical telemetry/incidents υπάρχουν για validation;»"]},{"heading":"402. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Θέλουμε AI στο call center.» Response: «Θα ξεκινούσα από agent assist and knowledge retrieval before autonomous handling of complex customer cases.»"]},{"heading":"403. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No network team involved: in OSS project."]},{"heading":"404. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No customer operations: in provisioning project."]},{"heading":"405. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["AI network project: without historical incident/telemetry data."]},{"heading":"406. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["Direct connection: to control layer without architecture/security review."]},{"heading":"407. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No reliable network inventory."]},{"heading":"408. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["Customer app project: without end-to-end backend process mapping."]},{"heading":"409. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No source of truth."]},{"heading":"410. STAKEHOLDER MAP EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Customer Operations Director Business Owner Order Management Manager Champion CIO Technical Buyer CTO/Network Technical Stakeholder CFO/COO Economic Buyer Procurement Paper Process."]},{"heading":"411. NETWORK PROJECT","paragraphs":["NOC Director Business Owner Network Operations Manager Champion CTO Technical Buyer Security Control Stakeholder COO Economic."]},{"heading":"412. BILLING PROJECT","paragraphs":["Billing Director Problem Owner Revenue Assurance Manager Champion IT/Data Technical CFO Economic."]},{"heading":"413. FIELD SERVICE PROJECT","paragraphs":["Field Service Director Business Owner Regional Operations Manager Champion IT Technical COO Economic."]},{"heading":"414. CHAMPION SIGNAL","paragraphs":["Operations Manager: shares: real fallout/incidents, brings: IT + Network + Customer Ops."]},{"heading":"415. FALSE CHAMPION","paragraphs":["Innovation team: likes AI but: cannot access real operations/data owners."]},{"heading":"416. MULTI-THREADING","paragraphs":["Telecom enterprise sale often needs: Commercial / Customer Operations IT Network Data Security Finance."]},{"heading":"417. TELECOM DEMO","paragraphs":["Show: real order journey."]},{"heading":"418. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Customer orders fiber ↓ serviceability verified ↓ order accepted ↓ network resources reserved ↓ installation scheduled ↓ technician completes ↓ service activated ↓ billing begins ↓ customer notified."]},{"heading":"419. VERY STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"420. NETWORK DEMO","paragraphs":["Alarm appears ↓ correlated with related alarms ↓ affected service identified ↓ incident created ↓ team assigned ↓ field intervention ↓ service restored ↓ affected customers updated."]},{"heading":"421. CUSTOMER CARE DEMO","paragraphs":["Customer calls ↓ agent sees products ↓ device status ↓ network incident ↓ billing context ↓ resolves or routes correctly."]},{"heading":"422. FIELD DEMO","paragraphs":["Work order ↓ technician receives context ↓ remote diagnostics checked ↓ required parts confirmed ↓ onsite work ↓ photos/tests ↓ closure ↓ customer notified."]},{"heading":"423. TELECOM PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["Should cover: Business workflow Customer/service volume OSS/BSS landscape Network criticality Integrations Data scale Security Availability/resilience Rollout Support."]},{"heading":"424. CUSTOMER VOLUME MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"425. NETWORK ELEMENT VOLUME MATTERS","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 426–450 · ORDER VOLUME MATTERS",[{"heading":"426. ORDER VOLUME MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"427. TELEMETRY VOLUME MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"428. CRITICALITY MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"429. PHASED IMPLEMENTATION","paragraphs":["Example: Phase 1 Order fallout analytics. Phase 2 Workflow automation. Phase 3 Provisioning orchestration."]},{"heading":"430. NETWORK EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Phase 1 Read-only alarm analytics. Phase 2 Incident-assist workflows. Phase 3 Controlled automation."]},{"heading":"431. TELECOM AI OPPORTUNITIES","paragraphs":["Potentially: Alarm correlation Anomaly detection Churn analytics Customer-service assistance Field-service diagnostics Fraud analytics Traffic forecasting Document search."]},{"heading":"432. GOOD AI PRINCIPLE","paragraphs":["Use AI first: to: assist, summarize, classify, prioritize."]},{"heading":"433. BE MORE CAREFUL","paragraphs":["when AI: changes network config or: makes financial/security-sensitive decisions."]},{"heading":"434. CUSTOMER AI","paragraphs":["Need: verified: billing, plan, order, incident data."]},{"heading":"435. NETWORK AI","paragraphs":["Need: telemetry + topology + incident history."]},{"heading":"436. FIELD AI","paragraphs":["Need: reliable technical knowledge."]},{"heading":"437. FRAUD AI","paragraphs":["Needs: specialist governance."]},{"heading":"438. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will eliminate outages.»"]},{"heading":"439. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will eliminate churn.»"]},{"heading":"440. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will run the network fully autonomously.»"]},{"heading":"441. TELECOM VALUE HYPOTHESIS EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["FACT: Large fiber expansion. CHANGE: More network and more customer activations. POSSIBLE PROBLEM: Build, inventory and activation data become harder to synchronize. IMPACT: Order fallout + delayed revenue + customer frustration. CAPABILITY: Integrated rollout/serviceability/provisioning workflow. QUESTION: «As the fiber footprint expands, which handoff between rollout, inventory and customer activation is becoming hardest to scale?»"]},{"heading":"442. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["FACT: New customer app launched. CHANGE: More digital self-service. POSSIBLE PROBLEM: Backend processes still fragmented. QUESTION: «Which digital customer journeys still fall back to call center because the underlying OSS/BSS process is not fully integrated?»"]},{"heading":"443. FACT ≠ CONCLUSION","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"444. TELECOM SALES OPENING #1","paragraphs":["«Θα ήθελα να καταλάβω πού υπάρχει σήμερα το περισσότερο manual intervention από customer order μέχρι active service.»"]},{"heading":"445. OPENING #2","paragraphs":["«Ποια digital journey looks simple to the customer but is still operationally complex behind the scenes;»"]},{"heading":"446. OPENING #3","paragraphs":["«Όταν υπάρχει outage, πόσο γρήγορα μπορείτε να connect network incident with actual affected customers;»"]},{"heading":"447. OPENING #4","paragraphs":["«Which process generates the most handoffs between BSS, OSS and human operations today;»"]},{"heading":"448. OPENING #5","paragraphs":["«Αν order volume or network footprint αυξανόταν 30%, ποιο process would become the first bottleneck;»"]},{"heading":"449. WHAT NOT TO SAY","paragraphs":["«Θα αντικαταστήσουμε όλο το OSS/BSS.»"]},{"heading":"450. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«AI will run your NOC.»"]}]],["Σημεία 451–475 · DON'T SAY",[{"heading":"451. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«We'll eliminate outages.»"]},{"heading":"452. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Network integration is easy.»"]},{"heading":"453. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«We'll make everything real-time.»"]},{"heading":"454. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«100% secure.»"]},{"heading":"455. KEY TELECOM TERMS","paragraphs":["Salesperson should know: OSS BSS NOC Provisioning Service Assurance Network Inventory CPE Revenue Assurance Mediation Churn."]},{"heading":"456. ALSO","paragraphs":["MTTR First-Time Fix Order Fallout Serviceability Interconnect Roaming SLA MVNO."]},{"heading":"457. MVNO","paragraphs":["Mobile Virtual Network Operator."]},{"heading":"458. TELECOM DISCOVERY CARD","paragraphs":["Operator Type [ ] Customer Segments [ ] CRM [ ] Order Management [ ] Billing [ ] Product Catalog [ ] OSS [ ] Network Inventory [ ] Field Service [ ] Data Platform [ ] Order Activation Time [ ] Fallout Rate [ ] Major Incident Process [ ] Main Manual Process [ ] Main Integration Gap [ ] Business Owner [ ] Technical Owner [ ] Network Owner [ ] Economic Buyer [ ]"]},{"heading":"459. QUALIFICATION","paragraphs":["Pain measurable? Customer/revenue/network impact? Business owner? IT involved? Network involved? Security involved where needed? Data accessible? Timing/budget real?"]},{"heading":"460. TELECOM OPPORTUNITY SCORE","paragraphs":["Business/operational pain __/5 Customer/network impact __/5 Technical/data feasibility __/5 Network/security feasibility __/5 Stakeholder support __/5 Timing/strategic fit __/5 Total: /30."]},{"heading":"461. 26–30","paragraphs":["Strong."]},{"heading":"462. 20–25","paragraphs":["Good."]},{"heading":"463. 14–19","paragraphs":["Early/risky."]},{"heading":"464. Below 14","paragraphs":["Do not overinvest."]},{"heading":"465. ROLE PLAY 1","paragraphs":["Customer Operations Director: «Οι activations μας καθυστερούν.» Sales: «Ποιο step δημιουργεί σήμερα μεγαλύτερη queue — order validation, inventory, provisioning, installation or final activation;»"]},{"heading":"466. ROLE PLAY 2","paragraphs":["NOC Director: «Έχουμε πάρα πολλά alarms.» Sales: «How many alarms represent independent issues versus symptoms of the same root incident and how is correlation handled today;»"]},{"heading":"467. ROLE PLAY 3","paragraphs":["Billing Director: «Έχουμε πολλές billing complaints.» Sales: «Which complaint types repeat most and can you trace them to product configuration, usage mediation, discount logic or manual adjustments;»"]},{"heading":"468. ROLE PLAY 4","paragraphs":["Field Service Director: «Έχουμε πολλές δεύτερες επισκέψεις.» Sales: «What are the top reasons for repeat visit — missing parts, wrong diagnosis, incomplete customer/network information or skill mismatch;»"]},{"heading":"469. ROLE PLAY 5","paragraphs":["CIO: «Έχουμε πάρα πολλά legacy systems.» Sales: «Ποιο end-to-end customer or operational process suffers most because of those system boundaries;»"]},{"heading":"470. ROLE PLAY 6","paragraphs":["CTO: «Δεν θέλω νέα εφαρμογή να αγγίζει το network.» Sales: «Τότε θα μπορούσαμε να ξεκινήσουμε from approved read-only interfaces and analytics, ώστε να create value without changing control logic.»"]},{"heading":"471. ROLE PLAY 7","paragraphs":["CEO: «Τι μπορείτε να κάνετε για τον οργανισμό μας;» Sales: «Θα ξεκινούσα από τέσσερα σημεία: πού customers περιμένουν activation, πού billing or service data διαφωνούν, πού network incidents αργούν να συνδεθούν με customer impact και πού people κάνουν manual work επειδή OSS, BSS and data platforms δεν επικοινωνούν σωστά.»"]},{"heading":"472. ROLE PLAY 8","paragraphs":["Customer: «Θέλουμε AI στο NOC.» Sales: «Θα ξεχώριζα πρώτα alarm correlation, anomaly detection, incident summarization and automated network actions. Τα πρώτα μπορούν να evaluated με controlled data πολύ πιο εύκολα από autonomous changes.»"]},{"heading":"473. ROLE PLAY 9","paragraphs":["Customer: «Θέλουμε νέο self-service app.» Sales: «Ποιες 3–5 high-volume customer tasks σήμερα αναγκάζουν ακόμη τον customer να πάρει τηλέφωνο και γιατί δεν ολοκληρώνονται end-to-end digitally;»"]},{"heading":"474. ACCOUNT EXPANSION","paragraphs":["Successful: order-management improvement. Could expand: to: provisioning billing customer self-service enterprise orders."]},{"heading":"475. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["Alarm analytics ↓ incident workflow ↓ field service ↓ service assurance."]}]],["Σημεία 476–481 · ANOTHER",[{"heading":"476. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["Customer 360 ↓ agent assist ↓ churn/retention analytics."]},{"heading":"477. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["One network region ↓ national rollout."]},{"heading":"478. BUT","paragraphs":["always: new discovery technical validation business case."]},{"heading":"479. TELECOM GOLDEN RULE","paragraphs":["«Στις τηλεπικοινωνίες η μεγαλύτερη software ευκαιρία βρίσκεται συχνά εκεί όπου ένα customer order πρέπει να γίνει πραγματική network service ή όπου ένα network event πρέπει να μετατραπεί γρήγορα σε customer action — αλλά OSS, BSS, network data και ανθρώπινες ομάδες δεν έχουν την ίδια εικόνα.»"]},{"heading":"480. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["RESEARCH OPERATOR / NETWORK / DIGITAL INITIATIVES ↓ IDENTIFY COMMERCIAL OR NETWORK TRIGGER ↓ SPEAK TO PROCESS OWNER ↓ MAP ORDER → PROVISIONING → ACTIVATION OR ALARM → INCIDENT → RESTORATION ↓ FIND FALLOUT / WAITING / MANUAL HANDOFFS ↓ QUANTIFY CUSTOMER / REVENUE / NETWORK IMPACT ↓ INVOLVE IT + NETWORK + SECURITY + DATA ↓ MAP CRM / ORDER / BILLING / OSS / INVENTORY / NOC SYSTEMS ↓ IDENTIFY SOURCE OF TRUTH ↓ BUILD BUSINESS CASE ↓ PROTOTYPE / POC IN CONTROLLED SCOPE ↓ VALIDATE SCALE + RELIABILITY + SECURITY ↓ PILOT ONE PRODUCT / REGION / WORKFLOW ↓ MEASURE REAL OUTCOME ↓ SCALE CAREFULLY ↓ EXPAND RESPONSIBLY."]},{"heading":"481. Η ΜΙΑ ΦΡΑΣΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΘΥΜΑΤΑΙ Η ΟΜΑΔΑ","paragraphs":["«Σε Telecom δεν ξεκινάμε ρωτώντας “θέλετε AI, νέο OSS ή νέο app;”. Ξεκινάμε από το πού κολλάει ένα order πριν γίνει ενεργή υπηρεσία, πού ένα network incident αργεί να μετατραπεί σε action, πού customer και network data δεν συμφωνούν και ποιο high-volume process εξακολουθεί να χρειάζεται ανθρώπους για να γεφυρώνουν με το χέρι systems που θα έπρεπε να συνεργάζονται.» Αυτό είναι: DISTILLOGIC TELECOM PLAYBOOK."]}]],["Πριν απαντήσεις στο quiz",["Ξανασκέψου το εισαγωγικό περιστατικό. Ποιο γεγονός είναι επιβεβαιωμένο, ποια πληροφορία λείπει και ποια ενέργεια θα μείωνε την αβεβαιότητα; Μία απάντηση μπορεί να ακούγεται εμπορικά ελκυστική αλλά να προηγείται της απαιτούμενης επιβεβαίωσης.","Οι δύο ερωτήσεις εφαρμογής γενικών αρχών συνδέονται και με τις προαιρετικές «Γενικές σημειώσεις». Το PDF βρίσκεται μόνιμα στο μενού, δεν αποτελεί ξεχωριστό υποχρεωτικό μάθημα και η ανάγνωσή του δεν βαθμολογείται.","Η καλή σχέση δεν αποδεικνύει εσωτερική επιρροή. Εξετάζουμε πράξεις, πρόσβαση και γνώση της διαδικασίας. Γενικές σημειώσεις: B2B και χαρτογράφηση εμπλεκομένων.","Η αβεβαιότητα επιλογής μειώνεται με σαφήνεια και διαχείριση κινδύνου, όχι κατ’ ανάγκη με περισσότερες επιλογές. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Buyer Indecision."]]],"scenario":["Πάροχος έχει διαφορετικές καταστάσεις παραγγελίας σε πωλήσεις, provisioning και billing, με παράπονα για υπηρεσίες που χρεώθηκαν πριν ενεργοποιηθούν.","Από την παραγγελία έως ενεργοποίηση και έναρξη χρέωσης, με γεγονότα και υπευθύνους. Το κενό βρίσκεται στη σύνδεση επιχειρησιακών σταδίων."],"minutes":46,"version":1,"additional_curriculum":37,"question_rows":[["Πάροχος έχει διαφορετικές καταστάσεις παραγγελίας σε πωλήσεις, provisioning και billing, με παράπονα για υπηρεσίες που χρεώθηκαν πριν ενεργοποιηθούν. Ποια διαδρομή διερευνάς;","Από την παραγγελία έως ενεργοποίηση και έναρξη χρέωσης, με γεγονότα και υπευθύνους.","Μόνο την εμφάνιση του λογαριασμού.","Μόνο νέα καμπάνια εξυπηρέτησης πελατών.","Αντικατάσταση όλου του δικτύου ως προϋπόθεση.","Το κενό βρίσκεται στη σύνδεση επιχειρησιακών σταδίων."],["Πάροχος έχει διαφορετικές καταστάσεις παραγγελίας σε πωλήσεις, provisioning και billing, με παράπονα για υπηρεσίες που χρεώθηκαν πριν ενεργοποιηθούν. Ποια υπόθεση δεν πρέπει να γίνει χωρίς επιβεβαίωση;","Ότι το «ολοκληρώθηκε» σημαίνει το ίδιο σε εμπορικό σύστημα, provisioning και billing.","Ότι χρειάζεται τεχνικός έλεγχος των interfaces.","Ότι πρέπει να χαρτογραφηθούν οι εξαιρέσεις.","Ότι η ημερομηνία ενεργοποίησης είναι σημαντική.","Η ίδια λέξη μπορεί να περιγράφει διαφορετικά γεγονότα."],["Πάροχος έχει διαφορετικές καταστάσεις παραγγελίας σε πωλήσεις, provisioning και billing, με παράπονα για υπηρεσίες που χρεώθηκαν πριν ενεργοποιηθούν. Πώς μετράς έναν πιλότο;","Συμφωνία καταστάσεων, χρόνος ενεργοποίησης και εξαιρέσεις λανθασμένης χρέωσης.","Μόνο πλήθος νέων dashboard widgets.","Μόνο το ότι όλες οι ομάδες παρακολούθησαν την παρουσίαση.","Μόνο αύξηση πωλήσεων χωρίς σύνδεση με την αλλαγή.","Ο πιλότος πρέπει να ελέγχει τη συγκεκριμένη επιχειρησιακή ασυνέπεια."],["Σε σύνθετη πώληση ο συνομιλητής απαντά πάντα γρήγορα, αλλά δεν μπορεί να φέρει άλλους αρμοδίους ή να εξηγήσει τη διαδικασία απόφασης. Πώς τον αξιολογείς;","Ως χρήσιμη επαφή, με ακόμη ανεπιβεβαίωτη δυνατότητα να λειτουργήσει ως εσωτερικός υποστηρικτής της απόφασης.","Ως ισχυρό champion, επειδή η ταχύτητα απάντησης αποδεικνύει επιρροή.","Ως οικονομικό αγοραστή, επειδή διαθέτει χρόνο για συζήτηση.","Ως ακατάλληλη επαφή που πρέπει να διαγραφεί άμεσα.","Η καλή σχέση δεν αποδεικνύει εσωτερική επιρροή. Εξετάζουμε πράξεις, πρόσβαση και γνώση της διαδικασίας. Γενικές σημειώσεις: B2B και χαρτογράφηση εμπλεκομένων."],["Έχεις δύο συμβατές λύσεις και ο πελάτης καθυστερεί από φόβο λανθασμένης επιλογής. Ποια παρέμβαση βοηθά περισσότερο;","Συγκρίνω τις δύο σε συμφωνημένα κριτήρια, εξηγώ το σκεπτικό μιας σύστασης και προτείνω ελεγχόμενο επόμενο βήμα.","Προσθέτω άλλες πέντε λύσεις ώστε να αισθανθεί πλήρη ελευθερία.","Προσφέρω έκπτωση χωρίς να συζητήσω τον φόβο της απόφασης.","Παρουσιάζω τον φόβο ως απόδειξη ότι δεν έχει πραγματική ανάγκη.","Η αβεβαιότητα επιλογής μειώνεται με σαφήνεια και διαχείριση κινδύνου, όχι κατ’ ανάγκη με περισσότερες επιλογές. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Buyer Indecision."]],"source_note":"Πηγή: ΜΑΘΗΜΑ 31.docx, κεφάλαιο 46. Διατηρείται το κείμενο των αριθμημένων σημείων, με ενοποίηση των σπασμένων γραμμών και αφαίρεση επαναλαμβανόμενης μορφοποίησης. Τα παραδείγματα δεν αλλάζουν τους κανόνες της εφαρμογής."},"di-enterprise-47":{"pillar":"distillogic","title":"47. Αυτοκίνητο και κινητικότητα","goal":"Να αναγνωρίζεις πραγματικές ανάγκες, να διερευνάς τα στοιχεία και να επιλέγεις υπεύθυνο επόμενο βήμα.","sections":[["Από την έννοια στην επαγγελματική πράξη",["Όμιλος leasing και συνεργείων δυσκολεύεται να συνδέσει όχημα, συμβόλαιο, service και διαθεσιμότητα αντικατάστασης.","Στη μελέτη που ακολουθεί σύνδεσε κάθε πιθανή λύση με συγκεκριμένη διαδικασία, υπεύθυνο, επίπτωση και στοιχεία που μπορούν να επαληθευτούν. Η τεχνική δυνατότητα, η οικονομική αξία και η εξουσιοδότηση για απόφαση είναι διαφορετικά ερωτήματα. Τα παραδείγματα του κεφαλαίου σε βοηθούν να τα διερευνάς χωρίς να υπόσχεσαι κάτι που δεν έχει εγκριθεί.","Η ύλη περιγράφει ενδεικτικές επιχειρηματικές ανάγκες και μεθόδους πώλησης. Δεν αποτελεί κατάλογο έτοιμων λειτουργιών των δύο CRM, δεσμευτική προσφορά, αλλαγή αμοιβών ή νέα πολιτική πιστοποίησης. Για πραγματική εργασία ισχύουν οι εγκεκριμένοι εταιρικοί όροι και οι αρμοδιότητες. Το μάθημα 60 είναι προετοιμασία, όχι δεύτερη επίσημη τελική εξέταση."]],["Το αντικείμενο του κεφαλαίου",["ΑΥΤΟΚΙΝΗΤΟ & ΚΙΝΗΤΙΚΟΤΗΤΑ Πώς πουλάμε software και technology services σε automotive groups, dealers, leasing, fleets, mobility providers και after-sales organizations"]],["Σημεία 1–25 · Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ",[{"heading":"1. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ","paragraphs":["Στο Automotive: δεν πουλάμε: «ένα app για αυτοκίνητα». Πουλάμε: ΚΑΛΥΤΕΡΟ CUSTOMER JOURNEY, ΚΑΛΥΤΕΡΟ AFTER-SALES, ΠΙΟ ΑΠΟΔΟΤΙΚΟ WORKSHOP, ΚΑΛΥΤΕΡΟ FLEET CONTROL ΚΑΙ ΠΙΟ ΕΝΙΑΙΑ ΔΙΑΧΕΙΡΙΣΗ ΟΧΗΜΑΤΩΝ, SERVICE ΚΑΙ DATA."]},{"heading":"2. ΤΙ ΕΙΝΑΙ AUTOMOTIVE CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["Μπορεί να είναι: Automotive Dealer Group Importer / Distributor Car Manufacturer Leasing Company Fleet Management Company Rental Company Workshop Network Roadside Assistance Company Mobility Platform EV Charging Operator."]},{"heading":"3. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ CUSTOMER ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["Lead ↓ Vehicle Search ↓ Test Drive ↓ Offer ↓ Finance / Leasing ↓ Sale ↓ Delivery ↓ Service ↓ Warranty ↓ Trade-in / Renewal."]},{"heading":"4. Η AFTER-SALES ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["Service Booking ↓ Vehicle Check-in ↓ Diagnosis ↓ Estimate ↓ Approval ↓ Repair ↓ Quality Check ↓ Payment ↓ Vehicle Return."]},{"heading":"5. Η FLEET ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["Vehicle Acquisition ↓ Assignment ↓ Usage ↓ Maintenance ↓ Fuel / Charging ↓ Incidents ↓ Replacement ↓ Disposal."]},{"heading":"6. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #1","paragraphs":["LEAD MANAGEMENT Customer asks: about car."]},{"heading":"7. Leads may come from:","paragraphs":["website, dealership, social, phone, marketplace."]},{"heading":"8. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Automotive CRM."]},{"heading":"9. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πώς εξασφαλίζετε ότι κάθε vehicle inquiry έχει owner, follow-up και next action;»"]},{"heading":"10. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #2","paragraphs":["LEAD RESPONSE TIME Customer asks: today. Dealer responds: tomorrow."]},{"heading":"11. Result:","paragraphs":["lead may be lost."]},{"heading":"12. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Lead routing/automation."]},{"heading":"13. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πόσο γρήγορα γίνεται first response σε digital vehicle inquiry σήμερα;»"]},{"heading":"14. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #3","paragraphs":["VEHICLE INVENTORY VISIBILITY Customer asks: «Υπάρχει αυτό το αυτοκίνητο διαθέσιμο;»"]},{"heading":"15. Salesperson checks:","paragraphs":["multiple systems."]},{"heading":"16. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Unified vehicle inventory."]},{"heading":"17. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Μπορεί η Sales team να δει live διαθέσιμα, reserved, in-transit και sold vehicles από ένα σημείο;»"]},{"heading":"18. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #4","paragraphs":["STOCK LOCATION Vehicle exists. But: which branch?"]},{"heading":"19. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Location-based stock visibility."]},{"heading":"20. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πόσο χρόνο χρειάζεται today to locate exact vehicle configuration across dealer network;»"]},{"heading":"21. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #5","paragraphs":["VEHICLE CONFIGURATION Different: model, trim, engine, options, color."]},{"heading":"22. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Vehicle configuration / product catalog."]},{"heading":"23. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πόσο εύκολα μπορεί salesperson να δημιουργήσει accurate configuration and price χωρίς manual checking;»"]},{"heading":"24. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #6","paragraphs":["QUOTE GENERATION Offer may include: vehicle, options, discount, finance, trade-in."]},{"heading":"25. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Digital quote workflow."]}]],["Σημεία 26–50 · DISCOVERY QUESTION",[{"heading":"26. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πόσο manual είναι today from customer requirement to complete commercial offer;»"]},{"heading":"27. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #7","paragraphs":["DISCOUNT APPROVAL Salesperson asks: manager: for discount."]},{"heading":"28. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Approval workflow."]},{"heading":"29. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which discount or commercial approval creates the most waiting during sales process;»"]},{"heading":"30. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #8","paragraphs":["TEST DRIVE Need: schedule vehicle, salesperson, customer."]},{"heading":"31. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Test-drive scheduling."]},{"heading":"32. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How is test-drive availability managed across branches today;»"]},{"heading":"33. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #9","paragraphs":["TRADE-IN Customer gives old car. Need: valuation."]},{"heading":"34. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Trade-in appraisal workflow."]},{"heading":"35. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πόσο structured and consistent is trade-in appraisal process across dealerships;»"]},{"heading":"36. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #10","paragraphs":["USED VEHICLE APPRAISAL Need: condition, mileage, service history, damage."]},{"heading":"37. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Digital appraisal checklist."]},{"heading":"38. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How much variation exists between different appraisers for similar used vehicles;»"]},{"heading":"39. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #11","paragraphs":["USED-CAR RECONDITIONING Trade-in arrives. Needs: inspection, repairs, cleaning, photography."]},{"heading":"40. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Reconditioning workflow."]},{"heading":"41. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πόσος χρόνος περνά από vehicle acquisition until it becomes sale-ready and where does it wait most;»"]},{"heading":"42. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #12","paragraphs":["VEHICLE DAYS IN STOCK Unsold car: ties up capital."]},{"heading":"43. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Inventory aging analytics."]},{"heading":"44. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Μπορείτε να δείτε stock aging and margin risk by vehicle, model and branch;»"]},{"heading":"45. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #13","paragraphs":["VEHICLE PRICING Used/new vehicle pricing: changes."]},{"heading":"46. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Pricing analytics."]},{"heading":"47. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How often are prices reviewed and what data is used to decide price changes;»"]},{"heading":"48. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #14","paragraphs":["ONLINE-TO-DEALER HANDOFF Customer builds car online. Then visits: dealer."]},{"heading":"49. Problem:","paragraphs":["dealer doesn't know: what customer already did."]},{"heading":"50. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Omnichannel customer context."]}]],["Σημεία 51–75 · DISCOVERY QUESTION",[{"heading":"51. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can customer continue in dealership from where they stopped online without repeating requirements;»"]},{"heading":"52. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #15","paragraphs":["DIGITAL SALES JOURNEY Customer may want: configure, finance, reserve, pay deposit."]},{"heading":"53. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Digital commerce journey."]},{"heading":"54. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which parts of vehicle purchase can customer complete digitally today and where must process fall back to manual handling;»"]},{"heading":"55. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #16","paragraphs":["FINANCE / LEASING APPLICATION Vehicle sale often linked: to financing."]},{"heading":"56. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Finance application integration."]},{"heading":"57. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How many manual handoffs exist between dealer, customer and finance provider before approval;»"]},{"heading":"58. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Credit decisions: high-risk."]},{"heading":"59. Sales must not promise:","paragraphs":["«AI approves financing automatically.»"]},{"heading":"60. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #17","paragraphs":["CONTRACT GENERATION Sale/leasing: needs: documents."]},{"heading":"61. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Automated contract generation."]},{"heading":"62. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How much of contract preparation and checking is still manual;»"]},{"heading":"63. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #18","paragraphs":["VEHICLE DELIVERY Vehicle sold. Need: prep, documents, registration, accessories, handover."]},{"heading":"64. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Delivery-readiness workflow."]},{"heading":"65. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«What most often delays a vehicle from sold status to customer handover;»"]},{"heading":"66. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #19","paragraphs":["DELIVERY CHECKLIST Need: nothing forgotten."]},{"heading":"67. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Digital PDI / delivery checklist."]},{"heading":"68. PDI","paragraphs":["Pre-Delivery Inspection."]},{"heading":"69. SALESPERSON SHOULD KNOW TERM","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"70. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How is PDI completion linked to actual customer delivery scheduling;»"]},{"heading":"71. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #20","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER COMMUNICATION BEFORE DELIVERY Customer asks: «Πότε θα είναι έτοιμο;»"]},{"heading":"72. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Automated milestone communication."]},{"heading":"73. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #21","paragraphs":["SERVICE BOOKING Customer needs: service."]},{"heading":"74. Booking comes through:","paragraphs":["phone, website, dealer."]},{"heading":"75. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Online service booking."]}]],["Σημεία 76–100 · DISCOVERY QUESTION",[{"heading":"76. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«What percentage of workshop bookings still require phone handling;»"]},{"heading":"77. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #22","paragraphs":["WORKSHOP CAPACITY Workshop has: bays, technicians, specialties."