ing":"342. Leasing:","paragraphs":["Leasing Operations."]},{"heading":"343. Data/integration:","paragraphs":["CIO + business owner."]},{"heading":"344. RESEARCH BEFORE OUTREACH","paragraphs":["Look for: New dealership locations New brand/import agreement EV expansion Fleet growth Leasing growth New DMS/CRM Digital retail initiative Connected-car initiative."]},{"heading":"345. TRIGGER","paragraphs":["Dealer group expands."]},{"heading":"346. HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["More branches: may increase: lead, stock, service, reporting complexity."]},{"heading":"347. OUTREACH EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι επεκτείνετε το dealer network σας. Σε τέτοιες φάσεις συχνά αυξάνεται η πολυπλοκότητα σε vehicle inventory, lead routing, workshop visibility και group reporting. Δεν γνωρίζω αν ισχύει σε εσάς, αλλά θα είχε νόημα να καταλάβω ποιο process είναι πιο δύσκολο να standardize across branches;»"]},{"heading":"348. ANOTHER TRIGGER","paragraphs":["Large EV fleet adoption."]},{"heading":"349. POSSIBLE PAIN","paragraphs":["charging + scheduling + TCO."]},{"heading":"350. DISCOVERY OPENING","paragraphs":["«Θα ήθελα να χαρτογραφήσουμε τη διαδρομή από vehicle lead μέχρι delivery και μετά από service booking μέχρι vehicle return, ώστε να δούμε πού υπάρχει το περισσότερο manual work or waiting time.»"]}]],["Σημεία 351–375 · ANOTHER",[{"heading":"351. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["«Ποια automotive process φαίνεται digital στον customer αλλά πίσω από τη σκηνή still depends on DMS, Excel, calls and manual re-entry;»"]},{"heading":"352. STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"353. FLEET OPENING","paragraphs":["«Μπορείτε σήμερα να δείτε πραγματικό cost, utilization and downtime για κάθε vehicle χωρίς να ενώσετε δεδομένα από διαφορετικά systems;»"]},{"heading":"354. STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"355. SCALE QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Αν ο αριθμός των vehicles or service jobs αυξανόταν 30%, ποιο process would become the first bottleneck;»"]},{"heading":"356. METRICS TO DISCOVER","paragraphs":["Dealer: Leads Response time Conversion Days in stock Delivery cycle Service bookings."]},{"heading":"357. Workshop:","paragraphs":["Repair cycle time Technician utilization First-time fix Repeat repair Parts waiting time."]},{"heading":"358. Fleet:","paragraphs":["Utilization Downtime Maintenance cost Fuel/energy cost Cost/km Accident rate."]},{"heading":"359. BUSINESS CASE — STOCK","paragraphs":["Reduce aging: may protect: capital/margin."]},{"heading":"360. BUSINESS CASE — WORKSHOP","paragraphs":["Higher productive utilization: may increase capacity."]},{"heading":"361. BUSINESS CASE — PARTS","paragraphs":["Fewer delays: can reduce repair cycle."]},{"heading":"362. BUSINESS CASE — CUSTOMER STATUS","paragraphs":["Reduce repetitive calls."]},{"heading":"363. BUSINESS CASE — FLEET","paragraphs":["Reduced downtime: may improve operational availability."]},{"heading":"364. BUSINESS CASE — EV CHARGING","paragraphs":["Better scheduling: may reduce operational disruption/energy cost."]},{"heading":"365. DON'T INVENT NUMBERS","paragraphs":["Use customer baseline."]},{"heading":"366. TECHNICAL DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: DMS? CRM? ERP? Workshop system? Parts system? Fleet platform? Telematics? Charging platform?"]},{"heading":"367. ALSO","paragraphs":["OEM portals? Finance/leasing systems? APIs? Data warehouse? Mobile apps? Identity provider?"]},{"heading":"368. SOURCE OF TRUTH","paragraphs":["Ask: «Which system is authoritative for customer, VIN, stock, service history, parts and contract data;»"]},{"heading":"369. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Different data domains: may have: different masters."]},{"heading":"370. NEED","paragraphs":["data ownership map."]},{"heading":"371. REAL-TIME NEEDS","paragraphs":["Vehicle stock reservation: may need fast update."]},{"heading":"372. Telematics alerts:","paragraphs":["may need fast update."]},{"heading":"373. Monthly management report:","paragraphs":["doesn't."]},{"heading":"374. DON'T MAKE EVERYTHING REAL-TIME","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"375. CONNECTED VEHICLE SECURITY","paragraphs":["Highly sensitive."]}]],["Σημεία 376–400 · Read-only analytics:",[{"heading":"376. Read-only analytics:","paragraphs":["very different from: vehicle control."]},{"heading":"377. NEVER CASUALLY CONNECT","paragraphs":["to: vehicle control functions."]},{"heading":"378. Need:","paragraphs":["OEM/security/architecture validation."]},{"heading":"379. AUTOMOTIVE POC","paragraphs":["Could test: CRM-DMS integration workshop status workflow fleet dashboard telematics data integration document AI."]},{"heading":"380. PROTOTYPE","paragraphs":["Could test: service booking vehicle appraisal technician workflow EV charging portal."]},{"heading":"381. PILOT","paragraphs":["Could be: one dealership, one workshop, one fleet, one region."]},{"heading":"382. PILOT SUCCESS CRITERIA","paragraphs":["Cycle time Adoption Data accuracy Manual-work reduction Customer response time."]},{"heading":"383. AUTOMOTIVE OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε ήδη DMS.» Response: «Τότε δεν ξεκινάμε από replacement. Θα ήθελα να δω πού υπάρχουν gaps γύρω από DMS — CRM, customer journey, workshop, OEM portals, analytics or fleet data.»"]},{"heading":"384. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Οι technicians δεν θέλουν άλλο app.» Response: «Τότε η λύση πρέπει να αφαιρεί clicks, calls and duplicate entry. Αν γίνει απλώς άλλο ένα system, δεν δημιουργεί αξία.»"]},{"heading":"385. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε telematics ήδη.» Response: «Τότε το question is whether the data is actually connected to maintenance, cost, dispatch or vehicle lifecycle decisions.»"]},{"heading":"386. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Θέλουμε AI για predictive maintenance.» Response: «Θα χρειαστούμε αρκετό failure history, telemetry and maintenance data ώστε να validate whether useful predictive patterns really exist.»"]},{"heading":"387. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Θέλουμε customer app.» Response: «Ποιες 3–5 high-frequency owner tasks θα λύνει καλύτερα από web, phone or current dealer contact;»"]},{"heading":"388. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Θέλουμε όλα τα connected vehicle data.» Response: «Πρώτα πρέπει να ξεκαθαρίσουμε ποια operational or customer decisions require them. More data does not automatically mean more value.»"]},{"heading":"389. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No workshop users involved: in after-sales project."]},{"heading":"390. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No fleet operations: in telematics project."]},{"heading":"391. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["AI predictive maintenance: without historical failures."]},{"heading":"392. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["Connected-vehicle project: without security architecture."]},{"heading":"393. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No reliable VIN master."]},{"heading":"394. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["Customer app: without use-case/adoption evidence."]},{"heading":"395. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No source of truth."]},{"heading":"396. STAKEHOLDER MAP EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["After-Sales Director Business Owner Service Manager Champion CIO Technical Buyer CFO/COO Economic Buyer Procurement Paper Process."]},{"heading":"397. DEALER SALES PROJECT","paragraphs":["Sales Director Problem Owner CRM/Digital Manager Champion IT Technical CFO/CEO Economic."]},{"heading":"398. FLEET PROJECT","paragraphs":["Fleet Director Business Owner Fleet Operations Manager Champion IT/Data Technical CFO/COO Economic."]},{"heading":"399. EV CHARGING PROJECT","paragraphs":["Mobility/EV Director Business Owner Charging Operations Manager Champion IT/Platform Technical Energy/Operations Stakeholder CFO Economic."]},{"heading":"400. CHAMPION SIGNAL","paragraphs":["Service Manager: shares: real cycle times, parts delays, technician data, brings IT + Parts + Finance."]}]],["Σημεία 401–425 · FALSE CHAMPION",[{"heading":"401. FALSE CHAMPION","paragraphs":["Innovation employee: likes connected-car AI but: cannot access workshop, fleet or OEM data owners."]},{"heading":"402. MULTI-THREADING","paragraphs":["Automotive enterprise project often needs: Sales / Customer After-Sales Parts Operations IT Data Finance."]},{"heading":"403. AUTOMOTIVE DEMO","paragraphs":["Show: real customer lifecycle."]},{"heading":"404. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Lead ↓ vehicle matched ↓ quote ↓ test drive ↓ finance ↓ order ↓ PDI ↓ delivery ↓ service reminder ↓ booking ↓ repair."]},{"heading":"405. STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"406. WORKSHOP DEMO","paragraphs":["Booking ↓ check-in ↓ diagnosis ↓ parts check ↓ estimate ↓ customer approval ↓ repair ↓ quality check ↓ pickup notification."]},{"heading":"407. FLEET DEMO","paragraphs":["Vehicle assigned ↓ mileage/usage captured ↓ maintenance due ↓ workshop scheduled ↓ downtime tracked ↓ cost updated ↓ replacement decision."]},{"heading":"408. EV DEMO","paragraphs":["Vehicle returns ↓ battery level identified ↓ next route requirement known ↓ charging slot assigned ↓ vehicle charged ↓ ready for dispatch."]},{"heading":"409. AUTOMOTIVE PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["Should cover: Customer/vehicle journey Dealer/workshop/fleet scope Existing systems VIN/customer data Integrations Mobile/offline needs Security/privacy Rollout Support."]},{"heading":"410. NUMBER OF VEHICLES MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"411. NUMBER OF DEALERSHIPS MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"412. SERVICE VOLUME MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"413. NUMBER OF TECHNICIANS MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"414. TELEMATICS VOLUME MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"415. PHASED IMPLEMENTATION","paragraphs":["Example: Phase 1 Service booking/status. Phase 2 Workshop workflow. Phase 3 CRM/customer lifecycle."]},{"heading":"416. FLEET EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Phase 1 Vehicle master/TCO. Phase 2 Maintenance. Phase 3 Telematics analytics."]},{"heading":"417. AUTOMOTIVE AI OPPORTUNITIES","paragraphs":["Potentially: Lead prioritization Document extraction Workshop knowledge assistance Predictive maintenance Damage-image analysis Demand forecasting Customer-service assistance."]},{"heading":"418. LEAD AI","paragraphs":["Could support: prioritization."]},{"heading":"419. But:","paragraphs":["don't assume model knows: who will buy."]},{"heading":"420. WORKSHOP AI","paragraphs":["Could help: search: technical knowledge/history."]},{"heading":"421. Must not:","paragraphs":["invent repair instructions."]},{"heading":"422. DAMAGE IMAGE AI","paragraphs":["Potential: vehicle-return/appraisal support."]},{"heading":"423. Needs:","paragraphs":["representative images + validation."]},{"heading":"424. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI detects every scratch.»"]},{"heading":"425. PREDICTIVE MAINTENANCE","paragraphs":["Potential: if strong history exists."]}]],["Σημεία 426–450 · CUSTOMER ASSISTANT",[{"heading":"426. CUSTOMER ASSISTANT","paragraphs":["Can help: service booking, repair status, basic vehicle questions."]},{"heading":"427. Must use:","paragraphs":["verified systems/knowledge."]},{"heading":"428. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will diagnose every car problem.»"]},{"heading":"429. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will value every used car correctly.»"]},{"heading":"430. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will eliminate workshop delays.»"]},{"heading":"431. AUTOMOTIVE VALUE HYPOTHESIS EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["FACT: Dealer group expanded. CHANGE: More branches, vehicles and customers. POSSIBLE PROBLEM: Lead, stock and service visibility becomes fragmented. IMPACT: Slower response + duplicate work + inconsistent CX. CAPABILITY: Integrated dealer/customer/vehicle workflow. QUESTION: «As your dealer network expands, which process is becoming hardest to standardize across sales, stock and after-sales?»"]},{"heading":"432. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["FACT: Fleet moving toward EVs. CHANGE: Charging becomes operational dependency. POSSIBLE PROBLEM: Vehicle schedule and charging schedule conflict. IMPACT: Unavailable vehicles + higher operating complexity. CAPABILITY: EV fleet/charging orchestration. QUESTION: «How are you coordinating vehicle availability, route requirements and charging capacity as the EV fleet grows?»"]},{"heading":"433. FACT ≠ CONCLUSION","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"434. AUTOMOTIVE SALES OPENING #1","paragraphs":["«Θα ήθελα να καταλάβω πού υπάρχει σήμερα το περισσότερο manual coordination από vehicle lead μέχρι delivery και after-sales.»"]},{"heading":"435. OPENING #2","paragraphs":["«Ποια workshop process creates the most waiting for customer, technician or vehicle;»"]},{"heading":"436. OPENING #3","paragraphs":["«Can you see true TCO and downtime by fleet vehicle without combining multiple systems manually;»"]},{"heading":"437. OPENING #4","paragraphs":["«Which customer journey looks digital from the outside but still depends heavily on DMS, calls, emails or duplicate entry internally;»"]},{"heading":"438. OPENING #5","paragraphs":["«Αν ο αριθμός των service jobs or fleet vehicles αυξανόταν 30%, ποιο process would become the first bottleneck;»"]},{"heading":"439. WHAT NOT TO SAY","paragraphs":["«Θα αντικαταστήσουμε το DMS.»"]},{"heading":"440. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«AI θα κάνει όλη τη διάγνωση.»"]},{"heading":"441. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Connected vehicle data solve everything.»"]},{"heading":"442. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«We'll collect all driver data.»"]},{"heading":"443. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«EV charging is just a booking problem.»"]},{"heading":"444. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Predictive maintenance will eliminate breakdowns.»"]},{"heading":"445. KEY AUTOMOTIVE TERMS","paragraphs":["Salesperson should know: DMS VIN PDI Workshop Work Order Warranty Claim Recall Telematics Fleet TCO First-Time Fix."]},{"heading":"446. ALSO","paragraphs":["Vehicle Off Road Parts Backorder Trade-in Reconditioning EV Charging OTA Update CPE — NO, NOT AUTOMOTIVE Important: don't mix telecom terminology."]},{"heading":"447. AUTOMOTIVE DISCOVERY CARD","paragraphs":["Business Type [ ] Vehicles / Stock [ ] Dealerships / Locations [ ] DMS [ ] CRM [ ] ERP [ ] Workshop System [ ] Parts System [ ] Telematics [ ] Fleet Platform [ ] Charging Platform [ ] Main Manual Process [ ] Main Customer Pain [ ] Main Vehicle/Workshop Pain [ ] Main Integration Gap [ ] Business Owner [ ] Technical Owner [ ] Economic Buyer [ ]"]},{"heading":"448. QUALIFICATION","paragraphs":["Pain measurable? Customer/operational impact? Process owner? IT/data involved? OEM/vendor data accessible? Security/privacy feasible? Timing/budget real?"]},{"heading":"449. AUTOMOTIVE OPPORTUNITY SCORE","paragraphs":["Business pain __/5 Customer/operational impact __/5 Technical/data feasibility __/5 Stakeholder support __/5 Timing __/5 Strategic fit __/5 Total: /30."]},{"heading":"450. 26–30","paragraphs":["Strong."]}]],["Σημεία 451–470 · 20–25",[{"heading":"451. 20–25","paragraphs":["Good."]},{"heading":"452. 14–19","paragraphs":["Early/risky."]},{"heading":"453. Below 14","paragraphs":["Do not overinvest."]},{"heading":"454. ROLE PLAY 1","paragraphs":["Sales Director: «Έχουμε πολλά leads αλλά όχι αρκετές πωλήσεις.» Sales: «Πού βλέπετε μεγαλύτερη απώλεια — response time, qualification, vehicle availability, quote, finance or follow-up;»"]},{"heading":"455. ROLE PLAY 2","paragraphs":["After-Sales Director: «Τα αυτοκίνητα μένουν πολλές μέρες στο συνεργείο.» Sales: «Πού περνάει περισσότερο waiting time — diagnosis, parts, approval, technician availability or quality check;»"]},{"heading":"456. ROLE PLAY 3","paragraphs":["Parts Director: «Έχουμε stock αλλά τα συνεργεία λένε ότι δεν βρίσκουν parts.» Sales: «Is the problem actual stock, location visibility, reservation, catalog matching or inter-branch transfer;»"]},{"heading":"457. ROLE PLAY 4","paragraphs":["Fleet Director: «Θέλω να μειώσω fleet cost.» Sales: «Can you currently break cost down per vehicle into depreciation/lease, fuel or energy, maintenance, downtime and incidents;»"]},{"heading":"458. ROLE PLAY 5","paragraphs":["CIO: «Έχουμε ήδη DMS, CRM και πολλές OEM εφαρμογές.» Sales: «Τότε το opportunity μπορεί να βρίσκεται between systems. Ποια customer or vehicle data ξαναγράφονται ή reconciled manually today;»"]},{"heading":"459. ROLE PLAY 6","paragraphs":["EV Fleet Manager: «Έχουμε πρόβλημα με φόρτιση.» Sales: «Is the constraint charger availability, grid/energy limit, scheduling, vehicle route requirements or charger reliability;»"]},{"heading":"460. ROLE PLAY 7","paragraphs":["CEO: «Τι μπορείτε να κάνετε για τον όμιλό μας;» Sales: «Θα ξεκινούσα από τέσσερα σημεία: πού χάνεται customer context από Sales σε After-Sales, πού vehicles περιμένουν χωρίς value-added work, πού stock or parts data δεν είναι αξιόπιστα και πού fleet/dealer management δεν έχει ενιαία εικόνα λόγω fragmented systems.»"]},{"heading":"461. ROLE PLAY 8","paragraphs":["Customer: «Θέλουμε AI για used-car inspection.» Sales: «Θα χρειαστούμε representative images, clear damage categories and human-validation rules ώστε να μετρήσουμε accuracy before operational use.»"]},{"heading":"462. ROLE PLAY 9","paragraphs":["Customer: «Θέλουμε rollout σε όλα τα dealerships.» Sales: «Αν branches έχουν διαφορετικά workflows, DMS setup or staff habits, θα πρότεινα representative pilot and then rollout based on proven adoption and integration.»"]},{"heading":"463. ACCOUNT EXPANSION","paragraphs":["Successful: workshop workflow. Could expand: to: parts warranty customer portal dealer analytics."]},{"heading":"464. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["CRM integration ↓ vehicle lifecycle ↓ after-sales retention."]},{"heading":"465. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["Fleet maintenance ↓ telematics ↓ TCO ↓ EV charging."]},{"heading":"466. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["One dealership ↓ network."]},{"heading":"467. BUT","paragraphs":["always: new discovery technical validation business case."]},{"heading":"468. AUTOMOTIVE GOLDEN RULE","paragraphs":["«Στο Automotive η μεγαλύτερη software ευκαιρία βρίσκεται συχνά εκεί όπου customer, vehicle, dealer, workshop, parts και fleet systems πρέπει να μοιραστούν την ίδια πληροφορία — αλλά σήμερα αυτή περνά χειροκίνητα, αργεί ή υπάρχει σε διαφορετικές εκδόσεις.»"]},{"heading":"469. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["RESEARCH COMPANY / DEALER NETWORK / FLEET / EV INITIATIVES ↓ IDENTIFY COMMERCIAL OR OPERATIONAL TRIGGER ↓ SPEAK TO PROCESS OWNER ↓ MAP LEAD → SALE → DELIVERY → SERVICE OR VEHICLE → FLEET → MAINTENANCE → REPLACEMENT ↓ FIND WAITING / DUPLICATE ENTRY / DATA GAPS ↓ QUANTIFY CUSTOMER / VEHICLE / COST IMPACT ↓ INVOLVE IT + OPERATIONS + PARTS + FINANCE ↓ MAP DMS / CRM / ERP / TELEMATICS / FLEET SYSTEMS ↓ IDENTIFY SOURCE OF TRUTH BY CUSTOMER + VIN ↓ BUILD BUSINESS CASE ↓ PROTOTYPE / POC IN CONTROLLED SCOPE ↓ PILOT ONE BRANCH / WORKSHOP / FLEET ↓ MEASURE CYCLE TIME + ADOPTION + DATA QUALITY + COST ↓ SCALE CAREFULLY ↓ EXPAND RESPONSIBLY."]},{"heading":"470. Η ΜΙΑ ΦΡΑΣΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΘΥΜΑΤΑΙ Η ΟΜΑΔΑ","paragraphs":["«Σε Automotive & Mobility δεν ξεκινάμε ρωτώντας “θέλετε νέο dealer app, telematics ή AI;”. Ξεκινάμε από το πού περιμένει ο customer ή το όχημα, πού stock, service ή parts information δεν συμφωνούν, πού fleet vehicles μένουν εκτός λειτουργίας και ποια διαδικασία αναγκάζει ανθρώπους να γεφυρώνουν με το χέρι συστήματα που θα έπρεπε να συνεργάζονται.» Αυτό είναι: DISTILLOGIC AUTOMOTIVE & MOBILITY PLAYBOOK."]}]],["Πριν απαντήσεις στο quiz",["Ξανασκέψου το εισαγωγικό περιστατικό. Ποιο γεγονός είναι επιβεβαιωμένο, ποια πληροφορία λείπει και ποια ενέργεια θα μείωνε την αβεβαιότητα; Μία απάντηση μπορεί να ακούγεται εμπορικά ελκυστική αλλά να προηγείται της απαιτούμενης επιβεβαίωσης.","Οι δύο ερωτήσεις εφαρμογής γενικών αρχών συνδέονται και με τις προαιρετικές «Γενικές σημειώσεις». Το PDF βρίσκεται μόνιμα στο μενού, δεν αποτελεί ξεχωριστό υποχρεωτικό μάθημα και η ανάγνωσή του δεν βαθμολογείται.","Η παραχώρηση εξετάζεται μαζί με αξία, κόστος και εξουσιοδότηση. Γενικές σημειώσεις: διαπραγμάτευση και παραχωρήσεις.","Ανάγκη και χρονική προτεραιότητα δεν είναι το ίδιο. Γενικές σημειώσεις: κόστος αδράνειας και πραγματική δέσμευση."]]],"scenario":["Όμιλος leasing και συνεργείων δυσκολεύεται να συνδέσει όχημα, συμβόλαιο, service και διαθεσιμότητα αντικατάστασης.","Σταθερή ταυτότητα οχήματος και σύνδεση των σχετικών γεγονότων/συστημάτων. Χωρίς συνεπή ταυτότητα, οι πληροφορίες δεν συσχετίζονται αξιόπιστα."],"minutes":45,"version":1,"additional_curriculum":37,"question_rows":[["Όμιλος leasing και συνεργείων δυσκολεύεται να συνδέσει όχημα, συμβόλαιο, service και διαθεσιμότητα αντικατάστασης. Ποιο στοιχείο είναι βασικό πριν σχεδιαστεί κοινό portal;","Σταθερή ταυτότητα οχήματος και σύνδεση των σχετικών γεγονότων/συστημάτων.","Μόνο κοινά χρώματα μεταξύ εταιρειών του ομίλου.","Μόνο ο αριθμός followers της αντιπροσωπείας.","Μόνο ο μέσος προϋπολογισμός διαφήμισης.","Χωρίς συνεπή ταυτότητα, οι πληροφορίες δεν συσχετίζονται αξιόπιστα."],["Όμιλος leasing και συνεργείων δυσκολεύεται να συνδέσει όχημα, συμβόλαιο, service και διαθεσιμότητα αντικατάστασης. Ποια ερώτηση αποκαλύπτει επίπτωση;","Πόσο συχνά καθυστερεί όχημα εκτός λειτουργίας επειδή λείπει ενημέρωση για service ή ανταλλακτικό;","Θέλετε εφαρμογή με περισσότερα μενού;","Ποιο μοντέλο αυτοκινήτου σας αρέσει;","Να μεταφέρουμε όλα τα αρχεία χωρίς αξιολόγηση;","Ο χρόνος ακινησίας συνδέει τη ροή δεδομένων με το επιχειρηματικό αποτέλεσμα."],["Όμιλος leasing και συνεργείων δυσκολεύεται να συνδέσει όχημα, συμβόλαιο, service και διαθεσιμότητα αντικατάστασης. Ποια ομάδα χρειάζεται στο discovery;","Στόλος/after-sales, συμβόλαια ή οικονομικά και IT ανάλογα με τη ροή.","Μόνο ο τελικός οδηγός.","Μόνο η διαφημιστική εταιρεία.","Μόνο η διοίκηση χωρίς ανθρώπους λειτουργίας.","Η διαδρομή του οχήματος διασχίζει διαφορετικές ευθύνες."],["Στη διαπραγμάτευση ζητείται μικρότερη τιμή. Ποια παραχώρηση διατηρεί καθαρή εμπορική λογική;","Εγκεκριμένη ανταλλαγή με συγκεκριμένο αντίκρισμα, όπως διαφορετικό scope ή όρους, καταγεγραμμένη στην προσφορά.","Έκπτωση τώρα με αόριστη προσδοκία μελλοντικών έργων.","Μείωση τιμής που θα αντισταθμιστεί με μη συμφωνημένη μείωση ποιότητας.","Προσωρινή τιμή που θα αλλάξει μετά την υπογραφή.","Η παραχώρηση εξετάζεται μαζί με αξία, κόστος και εξουσιοδότηση. Γενικές σημειώσεις: διαπραγμάτευση και παραχωρήσεις."],["Ο πελάτης λέει «το πρόβλημα είναι σημαντικό» αλλά δεν επιθυμεί αλλαγή φέτος. Ποια ερώτηση διερευνά τη χρονική προτεραιότητα χωρίς πίεση;","Τι θα συμβεί αν η διαδικασία παραμείνει όπως είναι και ποιο γεγονός θα έκανε την αλλαγή προτεραιότητα;","Να γράψω ότι συμφωνήσατε για να κρατήσουμε την τιμή;","Θέλετε να χάσετε την ευκαιρία που παίρνουν οι ανταγωνιστές σας;","Αφού υπάρχει πρόβλημα, γιατί δεν υπογράφετε σήμερα;","Ανάγκη και χρονική προτεραιότητα δεν είναι το ίδιο. Γενικές σημειώσεις: κόστος αδράνειας και πραγματική δέσμευση."]],"source_note":"Πηγή: ΜΑΘΗΜΑ 31.docx, κεφάλαιο 47. Διατηρείται το κείμενο των αριθμημένων σημείων, με ενοποίηση των σπασμένων γραμμών και αφαίρεση επαναλαμβανόμενης μορφοποίησης. Τα παραδείγματα δεν αλλάζουν τους κανόνες της εφαρμογής."},"di-enterprise-48":{"pillar":"distillogic","title":"48. Επαγγελματικές υπηρεσίες","goal":"Να αναγνωρίζεις πραγματικές ανάγκες, να διερευνάς τα στοιχεία και να επιλέγεις υπεύθυνο επόμενο βήμα.","sections":[["Από την έννοια στην επαγγελματική πράξη",["Συμβουλευτική εταιρεία δεν έχει έγκαιρη εικόνα ωρών, κόστους και περιθωρίου ανά έργο, παρότι διαθέτει λογιστικό σύστημα.","Στη μελέτη που ακολουθεί σύνδεσε κάθε πιθανή λύση με συγκεκριμένη διαδικασία, υπεύθυνο, επίπτωση και στοιχεία που μπορούν να επαληθευτούν. Η τεχνική δυνατότητα, η οικονομική αξία και η εξουσιοδότηση για απόφαση είναι διαφορετικά ερωτήματα. Τα παραδείγματα του κεφαλαίου σε βοηθούν να τα διερευνάς χωρίς να υπόσχεσαι κάτι που δεν έχει εγκριθεί.","Η ύλη περιγράφει ενδεικτικές επιχειρηματικές ανάγκες και μεθόδους πώλησης. Δεν αποτελεί κατάλογο έτοιμων λειτουργιών των δύο CRM, δεσμευτική προσφορά, αλλαγή αμοιβών ή νέα πολιτική πιστοποίησης. Για πραγματική εργασία ισχύουν οι εγκεκριμένοι εταιρικοί όροι και οι αρμοδιότητες. Το μάθημα 60 είναι προετοιμασία, όχι δεύτερη επίσημη τελική εξέταση."]],["Το αντικείμενο του κεφαλαίου",["ΕΠΑΓΓΕΛΜΑΤΙΚΕΣ ΥΠΗΡΕΣΙΕΣ Πώς πουλάμε software και technology services σε consulting firms, accounting firms, legal firms, engineering firms, advisory companies και άλλες knowledge-based επιχειρήσεις"]],["Σημεία 1–25 · Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ",[{"heading":"1. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ","paragraphs":["Στα Professional Services: δεν πουλάμε: «ένα CRM»ή«ένα project management tool». Πουλάμε: ΚΑΛΥΤΕΡΟ ΕΛΕΓΧΟ ΠΕΛΑΤΩΝ, ΕΡΓΩΝ, ΑΝΘΡΩΠΩΝ, ΧΡΟΝΟΥ, ΠΑΡΑΓΩΓΙΚΟΤΗΤΑΣ ΚΑΙ PROFITABILITY."]},{"heading":"2. ΤΙ ΕΙΝΑΙ PROFESSIONAL SERVICES COMPANY","paragraphs":["Μπορεί να είναι: Consulting Firm Accounting Firm Audit Firm Legal Firm Engineering Consultancy Architecture Firm IT Services Company Advisory Company Recruitment / Executive Search Firm Marketing / Creative Agency Technical Consultancy."]},{"heading":"3. ΤΟ BUSINESS MODEL","paragraphs":["Η εταιρεία συνήθως: πουλάει: Expertise Time Project delivery Retainer Advisory Specialist teams."]},{"heading":"4. ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["Lead ↓ Qualification ↓ Proposal ↓ Contract ↓ Client Onboarding ↓ Project Setup ↓ Resource Assignment ↓ Delivery ↓ Timesheets / Expenses ↓ Billing ↓ Profitability Review ↓ Renewal / Expansion."]},{"heading":"5. ΤΟ ΜΕΓΑΛΟ ΠΡΟΒΛΗΜΑ","paragraphs":["Σε service firms: revenue εξαρτάται από: ΠΟΙΟΙ ΑΝΘΡΩΠΟΙ ΔΟΥΛΕΥΟΥΝ, ΣΕ ΠΟΙΑ PROJECTS, ΓΙΑ ΠΟΣΟ ΧΡΟΝΟ ΚΑΙ ΜΕ ΤΙ MARGIN."]},{"heading":"6. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #1","paragraphs":["LEAD MANAGEMENT Prospect arrives: from: referral, website, partner, outbound, event."]},{"heading":"7. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["CRM."]},{"heading":"8. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πώς εξασφαλίζετε ότι κάθε qualified opportunity έχει owner, next step and expected close date;»"]},{"heading":"9. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #2","paragraphs":["RELATIONSHIP-BASED SALES Partners/senior staff: hold relationships: in their heads."]},{"heading":"10. RISK","paragraphs":["If person leaves: relationship history may leave too."]},{"heading":"11. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Relationship CRM."]},{"heading":"12. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How much client relationship knowledge exists only in individual inboxes, phones or memory;»"]},{"heading":"13. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #3","paragraphs":["DUPLICATE OUTREACH Two partners: contact same client."]},{"heading":"14. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Account ownership + activity visibility."]},{"heading":"15. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πώς αποφεύγετε duplicate or conflicting outreach to the same enterprise account;»"]},{"heading":"16. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #4","paragraphs":["PROPOSAL CREATION Every proposal: built: from scratch."]},{"heading":"17. Result:","paragraphs":["time lost."]},{"heading":"18. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Proposal automation/template system."]},{"heading":"19. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πόσες ώρες χρειάζεται average team to build and internally approve a proposal;»"]},{"heading":"20. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #5","paragraphs":["PROPOSAL VERSIONING Proposal v1. v3. Final-final. Final-final-2."]},{"heading":"21. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Controlled proposal workflow."]},{"heading":"22. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How do you ensure sales, delivery and finance are working from the latest commercial proposal version;»"]},{"heading":"23. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #6","paragraphs":["SCOPE DEFINITION Professional services project: can fail commercially: because scope unclear."]},{"heading":"24. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Structured scope/proposal workflow."]},{"heading":"25. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How is scope translated from sales conversation into something delivery can reliably execute and finance can bill;»"]}]],["Σημεία 26–50 · VERY STRONG",[{"heading":"26. VERY STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"27. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #7","paragraphs":["SALES → DELIVERY HANDOFF Sales sells. Delivery starts. Team asks: «What exactly did we promise?»"]},{"heading":"28. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Structured handoff."]},{"heading":"29. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πόση information has to be reconstructed after a deal closes because sales context was not transferred completely;»"]},{"heading":"30. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #8","paragraphs":["CLIENT ONBOARDING New client may require: contract, NDA, contacts, billing details, access, documents."]},{"heading":"31. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Client onboarding workflow."]},{"heading":"32. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πόσα departments are involved from signed agreement until the project team is ready to start work;»"]},{"heading":"33. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #9","paragraphs":["KYC / CONFLICT / CLIENT ACCEPTANCE Some firms: legal, audit, advisory: may need: client acceptance checks."]},{"heading":"34. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Controlled onboarding/case workflow."]},{"heading":"35. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Do not claim: software decides: legal/compliance acceptability."]},{"heading":"36. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which onboarding checks create the longest delay before engagement can start;»"]},{"heading":"37. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #10","paragraphs":["PROJECT SETUP Project must have: client, scope, budget, owner, rates, team, dates."]},{"heading":"38. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Professional Services Automation."]},{"heading":"39. PSA","paragraphs":["Professional Services Automation. Important term."]},{"heading":"40. PSA MAY INCLUDE","paragraphs":["Projects Resources Time Billing Utilization Profitability."]},{"heading":"41. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #11","paragraphs":["RESOURCE PLANNING Need answer: «Who is available next month?»"]},{"heading":"42. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Resource planning platform."]},{"heading":"43. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can delivery leadership see current and future availability by role, skill and seniority;»"]},{"heading":"44. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #12","paragraphs":["STAFFING PROJECTS New project: needs: 1 PM, 2 consultants, 1 analyst."]},{"heading":"45. Problem:","paragraphs":["right people may be: on other projects."]},{"heading":"46. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Skill/capacity-based staffing."]},{"heading":"47. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How long does it take to find and confirm the right people for a new engagement;»"]},{"heading":"48. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #13","paragraphs":["BENCH Employee available: but: not billable."]},{"heading":"49. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Bench visibility."]},{"heading":"50. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can management see current bench, expected roll-offs and upcoming demand in one place;»"]}]],["Σημεία 51–75 · ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #14",[{"heading":"51. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #14","paragraphs":["UTILIZATION Important professional-services metric."]},{"heading":"52. Simplified:","paragraphs":["how much available employee time: is used: on productive/billable work."]},{"heading":"53. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Utilization analytics."]},{"heading":"54. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can you see utilization by person, team, grade and practice area without manual consolidation;»"]},{"heading":"55. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["High utilization: is not always: good."]},{"heading":"56. Too high:","paragraphs":["may create: burnout, delivery risk, no capacity."]},{"heading":"57. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #15","paragraphs":["BILLABLE VS NON-BILLABLE TIME Time can be: billable, internal, sales, training, admin."]},{"heading":"58. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Time categorization."]},{"heading":"59. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How accurately can you understand where non-billable time is going today;»"]},{"heading":"60. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #16","paragraphs":["TIMESHEETS Employees forget: to submit time."]},{"heading":"61. Result:","paragraphs":["billing delayed, profitability unclear."]},{"heading":"62. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Timesheet workflow."]},{"heading":"63. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How much time is lost each month chasing incomplete or inaccurate timesheets;»"]},{"heading":"64. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #17","paragraphs":["TIMESHEET QUALITY Person enters: 8 hours: “project work”."]},{"heading":"65. Not useful enough.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"66. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Structured activity/time coding."]},{"heading":"67. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Is time captured at the level needed to understand project profitability and billing accurately;»"]},{"heading":"68. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #18","paragraphs":["TIME ENTRY FRICTION Complex timesheet: users delay it."]},{"heading":"69. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Simple/mobile time entry."]},{"heading":"70. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«What makes timesheet completion difficult for employees today;»"]},{"heading":"71. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #19","paragraphs":["PROJECT BUDGET Project sold: €100,000. Need know: how much effort: has been consumed."]},{"heading":"72. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Budget-to-actual dashboard."]},{"heading":"73. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How early can project manager see that effort is running ahead of commercial budget;»"]},{"heading":"74. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #20","paragraphs":["PROJECT PROFITABILITY Revenue alone: not enough."]},{"heading":"75. Need know:","paragraphs":["revenue minus: delivery cost."]}]],["Σημεία 76–100 · OPPORTUNITY",[{"heading":"76. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Project profitability analytics."]},{"heading":"77. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can you see expected and actual margin by project before project closure;»"]},{"heading":"78. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"79. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #21","paragraphs":["MARGIN EROSION Project starts: with 30% margin. Ends: with 8%."]},{"heading":"80. WHY?","paragraphs":["Possible: more hours, senior resources, rework, scope creep."]},{"heading":"81. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Early margin-warning system."]},{"heading":"82. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which signals tell you early that engagement margin is deteriorating;»"]},{"heading":"83. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #22","paragraphs":["SCOPE CREEP Client asks: «Can you also do this small thing?» Again. Again. Again."]},{"heading":"84. Result:","paragraphs":["unpaid work."]},{"heading":"85. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Change request / scope tracking."]},{"heading":"86. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How are out-of-scope requests identified, approved and commercially handled today;»"]},{"heading":"87. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #23","paragraphs":["CHANGE ORDERS Additional work: needs: agreement."]},{"heading":"88. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Change-order workflow."]},{"heading":"89. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How much additional work is started before formal commercial approval;»"]},{"heading":"90. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #24","paragraphs":["FIXED-FEE PROJECT RISK Fixed revenue. But: effort can grow."]},{"heading":"91. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Effort/budget forecasting."]},{"heading":"92. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How do you forecast remaining effort on fixed-fee engagements;»"]},{"heading":"93. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #25","paragraphs":["TIME & MATERIALS Client billed: based on: hours/rates."]},{"heading":"94. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Time-to-billing integration."]},{"heading":"95. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How many manual steps exist between approved timesheet and client invoice;»"]},{"heading":"96. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #26","paragraphs":["RETAINER Client pays: recurring fee."]},{"heading":"97. Need track:","paragraphs":["service usage, commitments, renewal."]},{"heading":"98. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Retainer/contract management."]},{"heading":"99. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can account team see whether retainer clients are overusing, underusing or approaching renewal;»"]},{"heading":"100. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #27","paragraphs":["MILESTONE BILLING Invoice triggered: when milestone complete."]}]],["Σημεία 101–125 · OPPORTUNITY",[{"heading":"101. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Delivery-to-billing workflow."]},{"heading":"102. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How is milestone completion communicated and approved before finance can invoice;»"]},{"heading":"103. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #28","paragraphs":["WIP Work in Progress."]},{"heading":"104. Work performed:","paragraphs":["but not yet billed."]},{"heading":"105. Important professional-services concept.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"106. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["WIP dashboard."]},{"heading":"107. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How much unbilled work is sitting in WIP and why has it not yet become in