nal efficiency."]}]],["Σημεία 351–375 · CFO",[{"heading":"352. CFO","paragraphs":["Cares about: project profitability, billing, cash, WIP."]},{"heading":"353. DELIVERY LEADER","paragraphs":["Cares about: staffing, project health, delivery quality."]},{"heading":"354. RESOURCE MANAGER","paragraphs":["Cares about: availability, utilization, skills, future demand."]},{"heading":"355. SALES DIRECTOR","paragraphs":["Cares about: pipeline, proposals, conversion, handoff."]},{"heading":"356. CIO","paragraphs":["Cares about: CRM, PSA, integrations, security."]},{"heading":"357. KNOWLEDGE LEADER","paragraphs":["Cares about: reuse, search, access, institutional knowledge."]},{"heading":"358. WHO TO APPROACH FIRST","paragraphs":["Resource/utilization: COO / Delivery / Resource Management."]},{"heading":"359. Profitability/billing:","paragraphs":["CFO."]},{"heading":"360. CRM/proposals:","paragraphs":["Sales / Managing Partner."]},{"heading":"361. Knowledge:","paragraphs":["Knowledge/Delivery + CIO."]},{"heading":"362. Major transformation:","paragraphs":["COO + CFO + CIO."]},{"heading":"363. RESEARCH BEFORE OUTREACH","paragraphs":["Look for: Rapid hiring New office/country Acquisition New service line Large consulting framework win New PSA/ERP/CRM initiative AI/knowledge-management initiative."]},{"heading":"364. TRIGGER","paragraphs":["Firm expands rapidly."]},{"heading":"365. HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["More people/projects: may increase: resource-planning and margin complexity."]},{"heading":"366. OUTREACH EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι η εταιρεία σας επεκτείνεται σημαντικά. Σε professional-services firms τέτοια ανάπτυξη συχνά δυσκολεύει resource planning, project profitability και pipeline-to-capacity visibility. Δεν γνωρίζω αν ισχύει σε εσάς, αλλά θα είχε νόημα να καταλάβω ποιο από αυτά είναι σήμερα το πιο δύσκολο να scale;»"]},{"heading":"367. ANOTHER TRIGGER","paragraphs":["New service practice."]},{"heading":"368. POSSIBLE PAIN","paragraphs":["skills/capacity/knowledge."]},{"heading":"369. DISCOVERY OPENING","paragraphs":["«Θα ήθελα να χαρτογραφήσουμε τη διαδρομή από opportunity μέχρι staffed project and final billing και να δούμε πού υπάρχει το περισσότερο manual work or information loss.»"]},{"heading":"370. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["«Ποιο process σήμερα συνδέει πιο δύσκολα Sales, Delivery, Resource Management and Finance;»"]},{"heading":"371. VERY STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"372. SCALE QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Αν ο αριθμός των ενεργών projects αυξανόταν 30%, ποια internal process would become the first bottleneck;»"]},{"heading":"373. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["«Πού skilled people χάνουν σήμερα περισσότερο χρόνο σε administration rather than client work;»"]},{"heading":"374. METRICS TO DISCOVER","paragraphs":["Pipeline value Win rate Backlog Utilization Bench Revenue per consultant Project margin."]},{"heading":"375. ALSO","paragraphs":["WIP DSO / collection time Proposal creation time Staffing time Timesheet compliance Scope changes."]},{"heading":"376. BUSINESS CASE — RESOURCE PLANNING","paragraphs":["Better staffing: may reduce: bench + over-allocation."]}]],["Σημεία 376–400 · BUSINESS CASE — PROJECT MARGIN",[{"heading":"377. BUSINESS CASE — PROJECT MARGIN","paragraphs":["Earlier visibility: may reduce: uncontrolled margin erosion."]},{"heading":"378. BUSINESS CASE — PROPOSALS","paragraphs":["Less senior time: spent: rebuilding standard content."]},{"heading":"379. BUSINESS CASE — TIMESHEETS","paragraphs":["Faster/more accurate: billing."]},{"heading":"380. BUSINESS CASE — WIP","paragraphs":["Better visibility: can accelerate: billing readiness."]},{"heading":"381. BUSINESS CASE — KNOWLEDGE","paragraphs":["Less repeated work."]},{"heading":"382. BUT","paragraphs":["don't invent: ROI. Use: customer baseline."]},{"heading":"383. TECHNICAL DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: CRM? PSA? ERP? HRIS? Timesheet system? Project management? Document management? Knowledge system?"]},{"heading":"384. ALSO","paragraphs":["Billing? Resource planning? Data warehouse? Identity provider? Collaboration platform?"]},{"heading":"385. SOURCE OF TRUTH","paragraphs":["Ask: «Which system is authoritative for client, opportunity, project, employee, skill, time and billing data;»"]},{"heading":"386. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Different domains: may have: different systems."]},{"heading":"387. NEED","paragraphs":["data ownership map."]},{"heading":"388. COMMON INTEGRATION MAP","paragraphs":["CRM ↓ PSA ↓ Project / Time ↓ ERP / Billing ↓ BI."]},{"heading":"389. HRIS","paragraphs":["feeds: people/availability."]},{"heading":"390. KNOWLEDGE PLATFORM","paragraphs":["may connect: documents/project metadata."]},{"heading":"391. REAL-TIME NEEDS","paragraphs":["Resource booking: may need: fresh data."]},{"heading":"392. Monthly profitability report:","paragraphs":["not necessarily real time."]},{"heading":"393. DON'T MAKE EVERYTHING REAL-TIME","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"394. PROFESSIONAL SERVICES POC","paragraphs":["Could test: proposal knowledge search CRM-PSA integration resource planning project profitability dashboard AI knowledge assistant."]},{"heading":"395. PROTOTYPE","paragraphs":["Could test: project setup client onboarding staffing workflow."]},{"heading":"396. PILOT","paragraphs":["Could be: one practice, one region, one service line."]},{"heading":"397. PILOT SUCCESS CRITERIA","paragraphs":["Reduced admin time Faster staffing Better data completeness User adoption Earlier margin visibility."]},{"heading":"398. PROFESSIONAL SERVICES OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε ήδη CRM.» Response: «Τότε θα ήθελα να δω τι συμβαίνει μετά το close. Πόσο καλά opportunity data περνούν into project setup, staffing and billing;»"]},{"heading":"399. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε already project management software.» Response: «Τότε το question is whether it connects to resource capacity, project economics and billing or only tracks tasks.»"]},{"heading":"400. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε timesheet system.» Response: «Τότε θα ήθελα να δω whether time data actually feeds project profitability, resource planning and invoicing reliably.»"]},{"heading":"401. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Οι consultants δεν ενημερώνουν systems.» Response: «Τότε πρέπει να understand what feels like duplicate administration and remove steps rather than just enforce more data entry.»"]}]],["Σημεία 401–425 · OBJECTION",[{"heading":"402. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Θέλουμε AI για proposals.» Response: «Μπορούμε να χρησιμοποιήσουμε AI για drafting and approved-content retrieval, αλλά credentials, capabilities and client references must remain verified before anything goes to the client.»"]},{"heading":"403. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Θέλουμε AI knowledge base.» Response: «Then permissions and client confidentiality are as important as search quality. The assistant must only retrieve content the user is authorized to access.»"]},{"heading":"404. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No finance: in profitability project."]},{"heading":"405. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No resource management: in staffing project."]},{"heading":"406. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["CRM project: without delivery handoff."]},{"heading":"407. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["AI knowledge: without access controls."]},{"heading":"408. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["Proposal AI: using unverified credentials."]},{"heading":"409. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No reliable skills data."]},{"heading":"410. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["Timesheets unreliable: but management wants precise profitability."]},{"heading":"411. STAKEHOLDER MAP EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["COO Business Owner Resource Management Director Champion CIO Technical Buyer CFO Economic Buyer Practice Leaders Key Stakeholders."]},{"heading":"412. PROJECT PROFITABILITY PROJECT","paragraphs":["CFO Business Owner Finance/PSA Manager Champion Delivery Business Stakeholder IT Technical COO Executive Sponsor."]},{"heading":"413. KNOWLEDGE PROJECT","paragraphs":["Knowledge Director Business Owner Senior Consultant / KM Manager Champion CIO Technical Security Control Stakeholder."]},{"heading":"414. CRM / PROPOSAL PROJECT","paragraphs":["Sales Director Business Owner Business Development Manager Champion Delivery Stakeholder CIO Technical Managing Partner Executive Sponsor."]},{"heading":"415. CHAMPION SIGNAL","paragraphs":["Resource Manager: shares: real staffing data, brings: Delivery + HR + Finance + IT."]},{"heading":"416. FALSE CHAMPION","paragraphs":["Consultant: likes automation but: cannot influence firm-wide processes or data owners."]},{"heading":"417. MULTI-THREADING","paragraphs":["Professional-services transformation often needs: Sales Delivery Resource Management Finance HR IT Leadership."]},{"heading":"418. PROFESSIONAL SERVICES DEMO","paragraphs":["Show: real flow."]},{"heading":"419. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Opportunity won ↓ SOW imported ↓ project created ↓ budget established ↓ skills required ↓ resources assigned ↓ time captured ↓ margin monitored ↓ invoice generated."]},{"heading":"420. STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"421. STAFFING DEMO","paragraphs":["Project requires: Data Engineer ↓ skills search ↓ 3 available people found ↓ availability/rate checked ↓ resource assigned ↓ capacity updated."]},{"heading":"422. PROFITABILITY DEMO","paragraphs":["Project sold: €100k ↓ planned effort: €60k ↓ actual effort rises ↓ forecast margin drops ↓ PM alerted ↓ scope/resource decision."]},{"heading":"423. KNOWLEDGE DEMO","paragraphs":["Consultant asks: «Have we solved similar problem before?» ↓ approved knowledge search ↓ relevant methodology found ↓ access checked ↓ reusable non-confidential material retrieved."]},{"heading":"424. PROFESSIONAL SERVICES PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["Should cover: Sales-to-delivery workflow Resource planning Time/billing Profitability Existing CRM/PSA/ERP Data ownership Access/security Rollout Adoption."]},{"heading":"425. NUMBER OF EMPLOYEES MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"426. NUMBER OF PROJECTS MATTERS","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 426–450 · BILLING MODELS MATTER",[{"heading":"427. BILLING MODELS MATTER","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"428. GEOGRAPHIC SPREAD MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"429. NUMBER OF LEGAL ENTITIES MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"430. CLIENT CONFIDENTIALITY MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"431. PHASED IMPLEMENTATION","paragraphs":["Example: Phase 1 CRM → project handoff. Phase 2 Resource planning + timesheets. Phase 3 Profitability + forecasting."]},{"heading":"432. OR","paragraphs":["Practice 1 ↓ Region ↓ Firm-wide."]},{"heading":"433. PROFESSIONAL SERVICES AI OPPORTUNITIES","paragraphs":["Potentially: Proposal drafting Knowledge search Meeting summarization Project status drafting Skills matching Contract extraction Time-entry assistance."]},{"heading":"434. GOOD AI PRINCIPLE","paragraphs":["Use AI: to reduce: search, drafting, classification, summarization."]},{"heading":"435. BE CAREFUL","paragraphs":["where AI might: invent: facts, references, capabilities, commercial commitments."]},{"heading":"436. PROPOSAL AI","paragraphs":["Needs: approved content."]},{"heading":"437. KNOWLEDGE AI","paragraphs":["Needs: permission-aware search."]},{"heading":"438. PROJECT AI","paragraphs":["Needs: current project data."]},{"heading":"439. STAFFING AI","paragraphs":["Needs: accurate skills and availability."]},{"heading":"440. CONTRACT AI","paragraphs":["Needs: human legal/commercial review."]},{"heading":"441. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will write every proposal perfectly.»"]},{"heading":"442. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will automatically choose best consultant.»"]},{"heading":"443. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will replace project managers.»"]},{"heading":"444. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI can reuse all client documents.»"]},{"heading":"445. PROFESSIONAL SERVICES VALUE HYPOTHESIS EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["FACT: Firm hiring rapidly. CHANGE: More people and projects. POSSIBLE PROBLEM: Resource visibility becomes harder. IMPACT: Bench + over-allocation + slower staffing. CAPABILITY: Integrated resource/capacity platform. QUESTION: «As the firm grows, how are you maintaining reliable visibility of skills, availability and future project demand?»"]},{"heading":"446. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["FACT: New practice launched. CHANGE: More proposals and cross-practice delivery. POSSIBLE PROBLEM: Knowledge/reuse/staffing fragmented. QUESTION: «How are you helping the new practice reuse firm knowledge and find the right delivery resources without rebuilding everything manually?»"]},{"heading":"447. FACT ≠ CONCLUSION","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"448. PROFESSIONAL SERVICES SALES OPENING #1","paragraphs":["«Θα ήθελα να καταλάβω πού χάνεται σήμερα περισσότερο information από Sales μέχρι Delivery and Finance.»"]},{"heading":"449. OPENING #2","paragraphs":["«Can you see future resource demand from pipeline and backlog before staffing becomes urgent;»"]},{"heading":"450. OPENING #3","paragraphs":["«Which project types most often suffer margin erosion and when does management usually notice;»"]},{"heading":"451. OPENING #4","paragraphs":["«Where do your most expensive people spend time on administration that does not require their level of expertise;»"]}]],["Σημεία 451–475 · VERY STRONG",[{"heading":"452. VERY STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"453. OPENING #5","paragraphs":["«If your active project portfolio increased 30%, which internal process would become the first bottleneck;»"]},{"heading":"454. WHAT NOT TO SAY","paragraphs":["«Χρειάζεστε νέο CRM.»"]},{"heading":"455. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«AI θα γράφει όλες τις προτάσεις.»"]},{"heading":"456. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Utilization πρέπει να είναι όσο πιο ψηλό γίνεται.»"]},{"heading":"457. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«We'll automate consultants.»"]},{"heading":"458. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«We can reuse all prior client work.»"]},{"heading":"459. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Project management tool solves profitability.»"]},{"heading":"460. KEY PROFESSIONAL SERVICES TERMS","paragraphs":["Salesperson should know: PSA Utilization Billable Time Bench WIP SOW MSA Rate Card Fixed Fee Time & Materials."]},{"heading":"461. ALSO","paragraphs":["Backlog Scope Creep Change Order Resource Planning Project Margin Retainer Practice Client Account."]},{"heading":"462. PROFESSIONAL SERVICES DISCOVERY CARD","paragraphs":["Firm Type [ ] Employees [ ] Active Projects [ ] CRM [ ] PSA [ ] ERP [ ] HRIS [ ] Project Management [ ] Time System [ ] Knowledge Platform [ ] Utilization [ ] Bench [ ] Main Staffing Pain [ ] Main Profitability Pain [ ] Main Manual Process [ ] Main Integration Gap [ ] Business Owner [ ] Technical Owner [ ] Economic Buyer [ ]"]},{"heading":"463. QUALIFICATION","paragraphs":["Pain measurable? Revenue/margin impact? Business owner? Delivery involved? Finance involved? Data quality sufficient? IT/security feasible? Timing/budget real?"]},{"heading":"464. PROFESSIONAL SERVICES OPPORTUNITY SCORE","paragraphs":["Business pain __/5 Revenue/margin impact __/5 Data/technical feasibility __/5 Adoption feasibility __/5 Stakeholder support __/5 Timing/strategic fit __/5 Total: /30."]},{"heading":"465. 26–30","paragraphs":["Strong."]},{"heading":"466. 20–25","paragraphs":["Good."]},{"heading":"467. 14–19","paragraphs":["Early/risky."]},{"heading":"468. Below 14","paragraphs":["Do not overinvest."]},{"heading":"469. ROLE PLAY 1","paragraphs":["COO: «Δεν ξέρω πάντα ποιοι είναι πραγματικά διαθέσιμοι.» Sales: «Is the problem time allocation, skills visibility, leave data, project end dates or the reliability of resource plans;»"]},{"heading":"470. ROLE PLAY 2","paragraphs":["CFO: «Μαθαίνουμε αργά ότι ένα project δεν βγάζει margin.» Sales: «Which data arrives too late today — actual time, resource cost, scope changes, expenses or forecast-to-complete;»"]},{"heading":"471. ROLE PLAY 3","paragraphs":["Sales Director: «Οι προτάσεις μάς παίρνουν πάρα πολύ χρόνο.» Sales: «Which part is repeated most — company credentials, methodology, case studies, team CVs, pricing or approvals;»"]},{"heading":"472. ROLE PLAY 4","paragraphs":["Managing Partner: «Οι consultants είναι πολύ απασχολημένοι.» Sales: «Are they busy on billable client work or is a meaningful share of senior time consumed by proposals, reporting, search and internal administration;»"]},{"heading":"473. ROLE PLAY 5","paragraphs":["Resource Director: «Sales sells projects without talking to us.» Sales: «Can we connect qualified pipeline and expected start dates to a forward-looking capacity view by skill so Sales sees delivery constraints earlier;»"]},{"heading":"474. ROLE PLAY 6","paragraphs":["CIO: «Έχουμε CRM, project tool, ERP και HR system.» Sales: «Then the opportunity may be in the handoffs. Where are client, project, people or financial data re-entered or reconciled manually today;»"]},{"heading":"475. ROLE PLAY 7","paragraphs":["CEO: «Τι μπορείτε να κάνετε για την εταιρεία μας;» Sales: «Θα ξεκινούσα από τέσσερα σημεία: πού Sales promises δεν συνδέονται καλά με delivery capacity, πού project margin γίνεται visible too late, πού senior people χάνουν χρόνο σε administration και πού knowledge exists αλλά δεν είναι reusable με ασφαλή και οργανωμένο τρόπο.»"]},{"heading":"476. ROLE PLAY 8","paragraphs":["Customer: «Θέλουμε AI για proposals.» Sales: «Θα ξεκινούσα με controlled drafting from approved content. Το AI μπορεί να βοηθήσει να βρούμε και να συνθέσουμε υλικό, αλλά client references, credentials, capabilities and commercial commitments πρέπει πάντα να verified before submission.»"]}]],["Σημεία 476–484 · ROLE PLAY 9",[{"heading":"477. ROLE PLAY 9","paragraphs":["Customer: «Θέλουμε AI για internal knowledge.» Sales: «Then access permissions and client confidentiality must be designed before broad search. A useful assistant must know not only what information exists but also who is allowed to see it.»"]},{"heading":"478. ACCOUNT EXPANSION","paragraphs":["Successful: resource planning. Could expand: to: project profitability hiring demand forecasting."]},{"heading":"479. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["CRM ↓ proposal automation ↓ sales-to-delivery handoff."]},{"heading":"480. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["Knowledge search ↓ proposal reuse ↓ project knowledge ↓ AI assistant."]},{"heading":"481. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["One practice ↓ whole firm."]},{"heading":"482. BUT","paragraphs":["always: new discovery business case data/access validation."]},{"heading":"483. PROFESSIONAL SERVICES GOLDEN RULE","paragraphs":["«Στα Professional Services η μεγαλύτερη software ευκαιρία βρίσκεται συχνά εκεί όπου η εταιρεία δεν μπορεί να συνδέσει καθαρά τέσσερα πράγματα: τι πούλησε, ποιον άνθρωπο έβαλε να το παραδώσει, πόσο χρόνο κατανάλωσε και πόσο πραγματικά κέρδισε.»"]},{"heading":"484. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["RESEARCH FIRM / SERVICES / GROWTH ↓ IDENTIFY GROWTH / CAPACITY / MARGIN TRIGGER ↓ SPEAK TO BUSINESS OWNER ↓ MAP LEAD → PROPOSAL → PROJECT → BILLING ↓ MAP PEOPLE → SKILLS → CAPACITY → ASSIGNMENT ↓ FIND MANUAL HANDOFFS / MARGIN GAPS / ADMIN WORK ↓ QUANTIFY TIME / UTILIZATION / PROFITABILITY IMPACT ↓ INVOLVE SALES + DELIVERY + RESOURCE + FINANCE + IT ↓ MAP CRM / PSA / ERP / HRIS / KNOWLEDGE SYSTEMS ↓ IDENTIFY SOURCE OF TRUTH ↓ BUILD BUSINESS CASE ↓ PILOT ONE PRACTICE / WORKFLOW ↓ MEASURE ADMIN TIME + STAFFING SPEED + MARGIN VISIBILITY ↓ SCALE ↓ EXPAND RESPONSIBLY."]},{"heading":"485. Η ΜΙΑ ΦΡΑΣΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΘΥΜΑΤΑΙ Η ΟΜΑΔΑ","paragraphs":["«Σε Professional Services δεν ξεκινάμε ρωτώντας “θέλετε CRM, PSA ή AI;”. Ξεκινάμε από το αν η εταιρεία ξέρει ποια projects έρχονται, ποιοι άνθρωποι είναι πραγματικά διαθέσιμοι, πού χάνεται senior time σε administration, πότε αρχίζει να πέφτει το project margin και αν Sales, Delivery και Finance βλέπουν την ίδια εμπορική πραγματικότητα.» Αυτό είναι: DISTILLOGIC PROFESSIONAL SERVICES PLAYBOOK."]}]],["Πριν απαντήσεις στο quiz",["Ξανασκέψου το εισαγωγικό περιστατικό. Ποιο γεγονός είναι επιβεβαιωμένο, ποια πληροφορία λείπει και ποια ενέργεια θα μείωνε την αβεβαιότητα; Μία απάντηση μπορεί να ακούγεται εμπορικά ελκυστική αλλά να προηγείται της απαιτούμενης επιβεβαίωσης.","Οι δύο ερωτήσεις εφαρμογής γενικών αρχών συνδέονται και με τις προαιρετικές «Γενικές σημειώσεις». Το PDF βρίσκεται μόνιμα στο μενού, δεν αποτελεί ξεχωριστό υποχρεωτικό μάθημα και η ανάγνωσή του δεν βαθμολογείται.","Η παρουσίαση πρέπει να αποδεικνύει ότι άκουσες και να βοηθά συγκεκριμένη απόφαση. Γενικές σημειώσεις: παρουσίαση χωρίς feature dump.","Η κοινωνική απόδειξη είναι χρήσιμη όταν το πλαίσιο και η τεκμηρίωση παραμένουν σαφή. Γενικές σημειώσεις: social proof και storytelling."]]],"scenario":["Συμβουλευτική εταιρεία δεν έχει έγκαιρη εικόνα ωρών, κόστους και περιθωρίου ανά έργο, παρότι διαθέτει λογιστικό σύστημα.","Πώς συνδέονται ανάθεση, χρόνος, κόστος και τιμολόγηση σε επίπεδο έργου. Η λογιστική εικόνα δεν ταυτίζεται πάντα με έγκαιρη λειτουργική εικόνα έργου."],"minutes":46,"version":1,"additional_curriculum":37,"question_rows":[["Συμβουλευτική εταιρεία δεν έχει έγκαιρη εικόνα ωρών, κόστους και περιθωρίου ανά έργο, παρότι διαθέτει λογιστικό σύστημα. Ποια διερεύνηση έχει προτεραιότητα;","Πώς συνδέονται ανάθεση, χρόνος, κόστος και τιμολόγηση σε επίπεδο έργου.","Αντικατάσταση του λογιστικού συστήματος πριν χαρτογραφηθεί η ροή.","Αύξηση τιμών χωρίς γνώση του κόστους.","Νέο website για να διορθωθεί η κερδοφορία έργων.","Η λογιστική εικόνα δεν ταυτίζεται πάντα με έγκαιρη λειτουργική εικόνα έργου."],["Συμβουλευτική εταιρεία δεν έχει έγκαιρη εικόνα ωρών, κόστους και περιθωρίου ανά έργο, παρότι διαθέτει λογιστικό σύστημα. Υψηλή αξιοποίηση προσωπικού σημαίνει πάντα καλό περιθώριο;","Όχι, εξετάζονται χρεώσιμες ώρες, επανεργασία, συμφωνημένη τιμή και πραγματικό κόστος.","Ναι, αρκεί οι ώρες να καταγράφονται σωστά.","Ναι, εφόσον η ομάδα είναι πλήρως απασχολημένη.","Όχι, αλλά αρκεί να μετρηθούν μόνο οι νέοι πελάτες.","Η δραστηριότητα δεν ισοδυναμεί αυτόματα με κερδοφορία."],["Συμβουλευτική εταιρεία δεν έχει έγκαιρη εικόνα ωρών, κόστους και περιθωρίου ανά έργο, παρότι διαθέτει λογιστικό σύστημα. Ποια απόδειξη κάνει μια βελτίωση αξιολογήσιμη;","Μείωση καθυστέρησης αναφοράς και ασυμφωνιών ωρών/τιμολόγησης σε αντιπροσωπευτικά έργα.","Μεγαλύτερος αριθμός πεδίων στο timesheet.","Περισσότερες εβδομαδιαίες συναντήσεις.","Εντυπωσιακή πρόβλεψη εσόδων χωρίς στοιχεία.","Η απόδειξη αφορά ποιότητα και χρήση της πληροφορίας."],["Μετά από discovery ο πελάτης ζητά παρουσίαση. Ποια διάταξη είναι πιο χρήσιμη για αξιολόγηση;","Επιβεβαιωμένο πρόβλημα, σχετική διαδρομή λύσης, τεκμήριο/όρια και συγκεκριμένο επόμενο βήμα.","Πλήρης κατάλογος λειτουργιών από τη λιγότερο στη περισσότερο τεχνική.","Ιστορικό εταιρείας και όλα τα λογότυπα πελατών πριν αναφερθεί η ανάγκη.","Όλες οι διαθέσιμες τιμές χωρίς σύνδεση με το συμφωνημένο αντικείμενο.","Η παρουσίαση πρέπει να αποδεικνύει ότι άκουσες και να βοηθά συγκεκριμένη απόφαση. Γενικές σημειώσεις: παρουσίαση χωρίς feature dump."],["Ένα case study πέτυχε μεγάλη εξοικονόμηση σε διαφορετική εταιρεία. Πώς το χρησιμοποιείς υπεύθυνα;","Εξηγώ το πλαίσιο και τις διαφορές και το χρησιμοποιώ ως ένδειξη προς αξιολόγηση, όχι εγγύηση ίδιου αποτελέσματος.","Μεταφέρω το ίδιο ποσοστό στο νέο business case επειδή πρόκειται για τον ίδιο κλάδο.","Αφαιρώ τους περιορισμούς για να μην αποδυναμωθεί η παρουσίαση.","Θεωρώ περιττή τη συλλογή baseline αφού υπάρχει προηγούμενο αποτέλεσμα.","Η κοινωνική απόδειξη είναι χρήσιμη όταν το πλαίσιο και η τεκμηρίωση παραμένουν σαφή. Γενικές σημειώσεις: social proof και storytelling."]],"source_note":"Πηγή: ΜΑΘΗΜΑ 31.docx, κεφάλαιο 48. Διατηρείται το κείμενο των αριθμημένων σημείων, με ενοποίηση των σπασμένων γραμμών και αφαίρεση επαναλαμβανόμενης μορφοποίησης. Τα παραδείγματα δεν αλλάζουν τους κανόνες της εφαρμογής."},"di-enterprise-49":{"pillar":"distillogic","title":"49. Όμιλοι εταιρειών","goal":"Να αναγνωρίζεις πραγματικές ανάγκες, να διερευνάς τα στοιχεία και να επιλέγεις υπεύθυνο επόμενο βήμα.","sections":[["Από την έννοια στην επαγγελματική πράξη",["Όμιλος έχει διαφορετικά ERP ανά θυγατρική και χρειάζεται κοινή αναφορά χωρίς να διακόψει τις τοπικές λειτουργίες.","Στη μελέτη που ακολουθεί σύνδεσε κάθε πιθανή λύση με συγκεκριμένη διαδικασία, υπεύθυνο, επίπτωση και στοιχεία που μπορούν να επαληθευτούν. Η τεχνική δυνατότητα, η οικονομική αξία και η εξουσιοδότηση για απόφαση είναι διαφορετικά ερωτήματα. Τα παραδείγματα του κεφαλαίου σε βοηθούν να τα διερευνάς χωρίς να υπόσχεσαι κάτι που δεν έχει εγκριθεί.","Η ύλη περιγράφει ενδεικτικές επιχειρηματικές ανάγκες και μεθόδους πώλησης. Δεν αποτελεί κατάλογο έτοιμων λειτουργιών των δύο CRM, δεσμευτική προσφορά, αλλαγή αμοιβών ή νέα πολιτική πιστοποίησης. Για πραγματική εργασία ισχύουν οι εγκεκριμένοι εταιρικοί όροι και οι αρμοδιότητες. Το μάθημα 60 είναι προετοιμασία, όχι δεύτερη επίσημη τελική εξέταση."]],["Το αντικείμενο του κεφαλαίου",["ΟΜΙΛΟΙ ΕΤΑΙΡΕΙΩΝ Πώς πουλάμε software και technology services σε μεγάλους ομίλους με πολλές θυγατρικές, business units και διαφορετικά συστήματα"]],["Σημεία 1–25 · Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ",[{"heading":"1. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ","paragraphs":["Σε έναν μεγάλο όμιλο: δεν πουλάμε: «ένα software για όλες τις εταιρείες». Πουλάμε: ΚΑΛΥΤΕΡΟ ΕΛΕΓΧΟ, ΣΥΝΔΕΣΗ, STANDARDIZATION ΚΑΙ VISIBILITY ΜΕΤΑΞΥ ΠΟΛΛΩΝ ΕΤΑΙΡΕΙΩΝ ΧΩΡΙΣ ΝΑ ΚΑΤΑΣΤΡΕΦΟΥΜΕ Ο,ΤΙ ΗΔΗ ΛΕΙΤΟΥΡΓΕΙ."]},{"heading":"2. ΤΙ ΕΙΝΑΙ CORPORATE GROUP","paragraphs":["Μπορεί να έχει: Holding Company Parent Company Subsidiaries Business Units Divisions Regional Companies Joint Ventures Shared Services."]},{"heading":"3. ΠΑΡΑΔΕΙΓΜΑ","paragraphs":["Ένας όμιλος μπορεί να έχει: Energy, Logistics, Construction, Retail, Real Estate, Technology."]},{"heading":"4. ΚΑΘΕ ΕΤΑΙΡΕΙΑ","paragraphs":["μπορεί να έχει: δικό της: ERP CRM HR system Finance process Reporting."]},{"heading":"5. ΤΟ ΜΕΓΑΛΟ PROBLEM","paragraphs":["Management asks: «Τι γίνεται συνολικά στον όμιλο;» Και η απάντηση: χρειάζεται: 20 Excel files."]},{"heading":"6. SOFTWARE OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["συχνά δεν είναι: replacement. Είναι: INTEGRATION + STANDARDIZATION + GROUP VISIBILITY."]},{"heading":"7. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #1","paragraphs":["GROUP REPORTING Parent company: needs: consolidated view."]},{"heading":"8. Data arrives from:","paragraphs":["different subsidiaries."]},{"heading":"9. Different:","paragraphs":["formats, definitions, timings."]},{"heading":"10. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Group reporting platform."]},{"heading":"11. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Πόσο manual είναι σήμερα η συγκέντρωση management data από όλες τις θυγατρικές;»"]},{"heading":"12. FOLLOW-UP","paragraphs":["«Which report takes the longest to consolidate and validate;»"]},{"heading":"13. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #2","paragraphs":["DIFFERENT KPI DEFINITIONS Subsidiary A says: active customer = X. Subsidiary B: different definition."]},{"heading":"14. Result:","paragraphs":["group numbers: not comparable."]},{"heading":"15. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Common KPI model / data governance."]},{"heading":"16. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Ποια group KPIs έχουν διαφορετικό definition across subsidiaries today;»"]},{"heading":"17. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #3","paragraphs":["MULTIPLE ERP SYSTEMS Company acquired businesses. Now: SAP, Microsoft, Oracle, local ERP, custom systems."]},{"heading":"18. WRONG APPROACH","paragraphs":["«Let's replace everything.»"]},{"heading":"19. BETTER APPROACH","paragraphs":["First ask: which business process: needs group-level consistency?"]},{"heading":"20. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which group process suffers most because subsidiaries operate on different ERP platforms;»"]},{"heading":"21. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #4","paragraphs":["MULTIPLE CRM SYSTEMS Different sales organizations: different CRMs."]},{"heading":"22. Result:","paragraphs":["group customer relationship: fragmented."]},{"heading":"23. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["CRM integration / group customer view."]},{"heading":"24. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can group management see a complete relationship with one corporate customer across subsidiaries;»"]},{"heading":"25. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 26–50 · ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #5",[{"heading":"26. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #5","paragraphs":["SAME CUSTOMER — MULTIPLE SUBSIDIARIES Example: large client buys: logistics from one company, energy from another, software from another."]},{"heading":"27. But group doesn't know:","paragraphs":["full relationship value."]},{"heading":"28. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Group customer 360."]},{"heading":"29. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can you identify all business relationships that the group has with one enterprise customer across legal entities;»"]},{"heading":"30. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #6","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER DUPLICATES Same customer: entered: multiple times."]},{"heading":"31. Different spellings.","paragraphs":["Different IDs."]},{"heading":"32. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Master customer data."]},{"heading":"33. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How often does the same customer appear as multiple different records across group systems;»"]},{"heading":"34. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #7","paragraphs":["MASTER DATA MANAGEMENT MDM."]},{"heading":"35. Important enterprise concept.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"36. Common master-data domains:","paragraphs":["Customer Supplier Product Employee Asset Legal Entity."]},{"heading":"37. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Master Data Management."]},{"heading":"38. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which master-data domain creates the most reconciliation problems across subsidiaries today;»"]},{"heading":"39. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #8","paragraphs":["SUPPLIER DUPLICATION Same supplier: used by: multiple subsidiaries."]},{"heading":"40. But group:","paragraphs":["doesn't see: total spend."]},{"heading":"41. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Group supplier master / spend analytics."]},{"heading":"42. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can procurement see total group spend with one supplier across all entities;»"]},{"heading":"43. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #9","paragraphs":["CENTRAL PROCUREMENT Group can potentially buy: at scale."]},{"heading":"44. But subsidiaries:","paragraphs":["buy independently."]},{"heading":"45. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Central procurement platform."]},{"heading":"46. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which categories are purchased separately by subsidiaries even though they could potentially be negotiated group-wide;»"]},{"heading":"47. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #10","paragraphs":["PURCHASE REQUEST STANDARDIZATION Every subsidiary: different approval flow."]},{"heading":"48. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Group procurement workflow."]},{"heading":"49. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which procurement steps should be standardized group-wide and which genuinely need local variation;»"]},{"heading":"50. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #11","paragraphs":["APPROVAL MATRIX €5k: local manager. €100k: group CFO. €1m: board."]}]],["Σημεία 51–75 · OPPORTUNITY",[{"heading":"51. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Dynamic approval workflow."]},{"heading":"52. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How are approval thresholds managed across legal entities, countries and categories today;»"]},{"heading":"53. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #12","paragraphs":["SHARED SERVICES Large groups: centralize functions: finance, HR, procurement, IT, legal."]},{"heading":"54. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Shared-services workflow platform."]},{"heading":"55. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which shared-service process generates the highest volume of internal requests today;»"]},{"heading":"56. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #13","paragraphs":["INTERNAL SERVICE REQUESTS Subsidiary asks: group IT or finance or legal for help."]},{"heading":"57. Email chains.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"58. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Internal service portal."]},{"heading":"59. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How are internal requests assigned, prioritized and measured across shared services today;»"]},{"heading":"60. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #14","paragraphs":["SLA BETWEEN INTERNAL TEAMS Internal departments: need expectations."]},{"heading":"61. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Internal SLA tracking."]},{"heading":"62. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which shared-service requests most frequently miss expected response time;»"]},{"heading":"63. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #15","paragraphs":["GROUP IT SUPPORT Different subsidiaries: send: different issues."]},{"heading":"64. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Group ITSM."]},{"heading":"65. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can Group IT see demand, backlog and recurring issues by subsidiary;»"]},{"heading":"66. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #16","paragraphs":["ACCESS REQUESTS New employee: needs access to: ERP, CRM, email, apps."]},{"heading":"67. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Identity/access workflow."]},{"heading":"68. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How many manual approvals are required today to provision access for a new group employee;»"]},{"heading":"69. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #17","paragraphs":["JOINER / MOVER / LEAVER Employee: joins, changes role, leaves."]},{"heading":"70. Access must follow.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"71. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["HR-to-identity automation."]},{"heading":"72. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How reliably does system access change when employees move between subsidiaries or roles;»"]},{"heading":"73. SECURITY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"74. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #18","paragraphs":["GROUP HR DATA Different HR systems."]},{"heading":"75. Management wants:","paragraphs":["group headcount, cost, turnover, skills."]}]],["Σημεία 76–100 · OPPORTUNITY",[{"heading":"76. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["HR data integration."]},{"heading":"77. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How much manual consolidation is required to produce reliable group headcount and people metrics;»"]},{"heading":"78. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #19","paragraphs":["EMPLOYEE MASTER Same employee: may move between: entities."]},{"heading":"79. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Group employee identity/master data."]},{"heading":"80. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #20","paragraphs":["SKILLS VISIBILITY Group has: thousands of employees."]},{"heading":"81. One subsidiary:","paragraphs":["needs data engineer. Another: already has one."]},{"heading":"82. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Group skills marketplace."]},{"heading":"83. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Can the group find internal skills across subsidiaries before hiring externally;»"]},{"heading":"84. VERY STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"85. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #21","paragraphs":["INTERNAL MOBILITY Employee can move: between group companies."]},{"heading":"86. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Internal talent marketplace."]},{"heading":"87. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How easy is it today for group companies to discover internal candidates from other entities;»"]},{"heading":"88. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #22","paragraphs":["FINANCIAL CONSOLIDATION Group has: multiple legal entities."]},{"heading":"89. Need:","paragraphs":["consolidate: financial results."]},{"heading":"90. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Finance/data integration."]},{"heading":"91. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Which step of financial consolidation requires the most manual reconciliation across subsidiaries;»"]},{"heading":"92. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #23","paragraphs":["CHART OF ACCOUNTS DIFFERENCES Different companies: different accounting structures."]},{"heading":"93. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Mapping/governance layer."]},{"heading":"94. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How much manual mapping is required to translate subsidiary accounts into the group reporting structure;»"]},{"heading":"95. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #24","paragraphs":["INTERCOMPANY TRANSACTIONS Subsidiary A: sells service: to subsidiary B."]},{"heading":"96. Finance must:","paragraphs":["reconcile."]},{"heading":"97. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Intercompany workflow."]},{"heading":"98. DISCOVERY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«How much manual effort goes into intercompany matching and dispute resolution;»"]},{"heading":"99. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #25","paragraphs":["INTERCOMPANY INVOICES Two entities: book differently."]},{"heading":"100. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Intercompany reconciliation automation."]}]],["Σημεία 101–125 · ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #26",[{"heading":"101. ΚΥΡΙΟ PAIN #26","paragraphs":["GROUP CASH VISIBILITY Parent company: wants: cash position."]},{"headin