? Student Portal? Research System? Identity?"]},{"heading":"432. ALSO ASK","paragraphs":["APIs? Cloud/on-prem? Vendor restrictions? Data warehouse? SSO? Security requirements?"]},{"heading":"433. SOURCE OF TRUTH","paragraphs":["Public: «Which system is authoritative for citizen/entity, case, document, payment and permit data;»"]},{"heading":"434. Education:","paragraphs":["«Which system is authoritative for student identity, enrollment, course, grade and financial data;»"]},{"heading":"435. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Different domains: may have: different masters."]},{"heading":"436. REAL-TIME NEEDS","paragraphs":["Citizen emergency report: possibly fast."]},{"heading":"437. Monthly dashboard:","paragraphs":["not necessarily."]},{"heading":"438. DON'T MAKE EVERYTHING REAL-TIME","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"439. PUBLIC POC","paragraphs":["Could test: request classification document extraction citizen case workflow legacy integration internal knowledge assistant."]},{"heading":"440. EDUCATION POC","paragraphs":["Could test: admissions workflow SIS-LMS integration student-service portal knowledge assistant."]},{"heading":"441. PROTOTYPE","paragraphs":["Public: one service."]},{"heading":"442. Education:","paragraphs":["one department/program."]},{"heading":"443. PILOT SUCCESS CRITERIA","paragraphs":["Cycle time Data accuracy User adoption Reduced manual work Status visibility Security/privacy validation."]},{"heading":"444. PUBLIC-SECTOR OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε ήδη portal.» Response: «Τότε δεν θα ξεκινούσα από replacement. Θα ήθελα να δω τι συμβαίνει μετά την υποβολή και πού ο back-office workflow παραμένει manual.»"]},{"heading":"445. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε legacy system που δεν αλλάζει.» Response: «Τότε θα εξετάσουμε αν μπορεί να παραμείνει system of record και να δημιουργήσουμε integration/workflow layer γύρω του όπου υπάρχει πραγματικό value.»"]},{"heading":"446. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Οι υπάλληλοι δεν θα χρησιμοποιήσουν άλλο system.» Response: «Τότε η λύση πρέπει να αφαιρεί duplicate entry and chasing. Αν προσθέτει απλώς άλλο login, adoption πιθανότατα θα αποτύχει.»"]},{"heading":"447. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Θέλουμε AI για να εγκρίνει αιτήσεις.» Response: «Θα χώριζα πρώτα το process σε document extraction, classification, eligibility rules, review and final decision. Τα πρώτα μπορούν να υποστηριχθούν τεχνολογικά πολύ διαφορετικά από την τελική διοικητική απόφαση.»"]},{"heading":"448. EDUCATION OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε ήδη SIS.» Response: «Τότε θα ήθελα να δω πού υπάρχουν gaps around SIS — admissions, LMS, student services, finance or reporting.»"]},{"heading":"449. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Θέλουμε chatbot για students.» Response: «Ποια 5 questions generate the most repetitive student inquiries and which approved systems or policies contain the answers;»"]},{"heading":"450. OBJECTION","paragraphs":["«Θέλουμε AI να εντοπίζει φοιτητές που θα εγκαταλείψουν.» Response: «Αυτό χρειάζεται careful governance. Θα πρέπει να ξεκαθαρίσουμε ποια data χρησιμοποιούνται, για ποιο support purpose και πώς human staff reviews any signal before action.»"]}]],["Σημεία 451–475 · RED FLAG",[{"heading":"451. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["Public portal: without back-office mapping."]},{"heading":"452. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No process owner."]},{"heading":"453. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["AI decision project: without governance."]},{"heading":"454. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No procurement/legal understanding."]},{"heading":"455. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No security/privacy involvement."]},{"heading":"456. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["Legacy integration: assumed easy."]},{"heading":"457. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["No clear data ownership."]},{"heading":"458. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["Education project: without registrar/student-services involvement."]},{"heading":"459. STAKEHOLDER MAP EXAMPLE — PUBLIC","paragraphs":["Operations Director Business Owner Service Manager Champion CIO Technical Buyer Security/Data Protection Control Stakeholders Finance/Executive Sponsor Economic/Executive Buyer Procurement Paper Process."]},{"heading":"460. GRANT PROJECT","paragraphs":["Program Director Business Owner Program Operations Manager Champion IT Technical Finance/Compliance Control Stakeholders."]},{"heading":"461. EDUCATION PROJECT","paragraphs":["Registrar Business Owner Student Services Manager Champion CIO Technical Buyer Finance/Academic Affairs Stakeholders Rector / COO equivalent Executive Sponsor."]},{"heading":"462. ADMISSIONS PROJECT","paragraphs":["Admissions Director Problem Owner Admissions Operations Champion IT Technical Academic Leadership Decision Stakeholder."]},{"heading":"463. CHAMPION SIGNAL — PUBLIC","paragraphs":["Operations Manager: shares: real backlog, cycle time, process maps, brings: IT + Finance + frontline staff."]},{"heading":"464. FALSE CHAMPION","paragraphs":["Innovation employee: likes AI but: cannot access process owners or procurement path."]},{"heading":"465. CHAMPION SIGNAL — EDUCATION","paragraphs":["Registrar/Student Services leader: shares: real request volume, brings: IT + Finance + Academic Affairs."]},{"heading":"466. MULTI-THREADING","paragraphs":["Public-sector deal often needs: Business department IT Security/privacy Finance Procurement Legal Executive sponsor."]},{"heading":"467. Education deal often needs:","paragraphs":["Registrar / Student Services Academic Affairs IT Finance Leadership."]},{"heading":"468. PUBLIC DEMO","paragraphs":["Show: real citizen case."]},{"heading":"469. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Citizen submits request ↓ documents checked ↓ case created ↓ department assigned ↓ approval requested ↓ decision recorded ↓ citizen notified ↓ audit trail stored."]},{"heading":"470. FIELD-SERVICE DEMO","paragraphs":["Citizen reports issue ↓ GPS/location captured ↓ department routed ↓ crew assigned ↓ photo proof ↓ issue closed ↓ citizen updated."]},{"heading":"471. GRANT DEMO","paragraphs":["Application ↓ document check ↓ eligibility review ↓ evaluation ↓ approval ↓ payment milestone ↓ monitoring."]},{"heading":"472. EDUCATION DEMO","paragraphs":["Applicant ↓ application ↓ documents ↓ admission review ↓ offer ↓ enrollment ↓ course registration ↓ student portal."]},{"heading":"473. STUDENT SERVICE DEMO","paragraphs":["Student requests transcript ↓ case created ↓ identity verified ↓ data retrieved ↓ certificate generated ↓ student notified."]},{"heading":"474. PUBLIC-SECTOR PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["Should cover: Service/process Citizen journey Existing systems Legacy integrations Security/privacy Audit trail Accessibility User roles Procurement constraints Rollout Support."]},{"heading":"475. EDUCATION PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["Should cover: Student journey Existing SIS/LMS Integrations Admissions/student services Security/privacy Academic/admin roles Rollout Support."]}]],["Σημεία 476–500 · NUMBER OF USERS MATTERS",[{"heading":"476. NUMBER OF USERS MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"477. NUMBER OF CASES MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"478. NUMBER OF DEPARTMENTS MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"479. DOCUMENT VOLUME MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"480. PROCUREMENT COMPLEXITY MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"481. SECURITY SENSITIVITY MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"482. EDUCATION STUDENT VOLUME MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"483. PHASED IMPLEMENTATION — PUBLIC","paragraphs":["Example: Phase 1 One high-volume citizen service. Phase 2 Case management integration. Phase 3 Additional services/departments."]},{"heading":"484. EDUCATION","paragraphs":["Phase 1 Admissions. Phase 2 Enrollment/student services. Phase 3 Cross-campus integration."]},{"heading":"485. PUBLIC AI OPPORTUNITIES","paragraphs":["Request classification Document extraction Case summarization Approved knowledge search Form assistance Internal drafting."]},{"heading":"486. EDUCATION AI OPPORTUNITIES","paragraphs":["Student-service assistant Knowledge search Admission document extraction Scheduling support Case summarization."]},{"heading":"487. GOLDEN AI PRINCIPLE","paragraphs":["Use AI first: to: ASSIST THE PROCESS not: to replace: AUTHORIZED DECISIONS."]},{"heading":"488. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will decide citizen eligibility.»"]},{"heading":"489. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will replace public officers.»"]},{"heading":"490. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will decide admissions.»"]},{"heading":"491. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«AI will automatically grade fairly.»"]},{"heading":"492. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«One portal solves public administration.»"]},{"heading":"493. DON'T CLAIM","paragraphs":["«Legacy systems must all be replaced.»"]},{"heading":"494. PUBLIC VALUE HYPOTHESIS EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["FACT: Organization launched more digital applications. CHANGE: More requests enter online. POSSIBLE PROBLEM: Back-office processing remains manual. IMPACT: Backlog + status calls + staff workload. CAPABILITY: Integrated case-management workflow. QUESTION: «As more applications move online, which internal review or approval step is becoming hardest to scale?»"]},{"heading":"495. EDUCATION VALUE HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["FACT: Institution expanding programs. CHANGE: More students/applications. POSSIBLE PROBLEM: Admissions/student services become overloaded. IMPACT: Longer response times + more admin effort. CAPABILITY: Integrated admissions/student-service workflow. QUESTION: «As student volume grows, which admissions or student-service process is becoming the hardest to scale without adding equivalent administrative staff?»"]},{"heading":"496. FACT ≠ CONCLUSION","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"497. WHAT NOT TO SAY","paragraphs":["«Ο δημόσιος τομέας είναι πίσω τεχνολογικά.»"]},{"heading":"498. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Θα καταργήσουμε τη γραφειοκρατία.»"]},{"heading":"499. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Θα τα κάνουμε όλα paperless.»"]},{"heading":"500. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«AI θα κάνει τις εγκρίσεις.»"]}]],["Σημεία 501–525 · DON'T SAY",[{"heading":"501. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Θα αλλάξουμε όλα τα legacy systems.»"]},{"heading":"502. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Το SIS σας είναι παλιό, χρειάζεστε νέο.»"]},{"heading":"503. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Students want an app.»"]},{"heading":"504. KEY PUBLIC-SECTOR TERMS","paragraphs":["Salesperson should know: Case Management Citizen Portal DMS Public Procurement Grant Management Permit GIS Audit Trail Interoperability Shared Services."]},{"heading":"505. KEY EDUCATION TERMS","paragraphs":["SIS LMS Admissions Enrollment Registrar Student Services Curriculum Transcript Research Grant Accreditation."]},{"heading":"506. PUBLIC-SECTOR DISCOVERY CARD","paragraphs":["Organization Type [ ] Main Citizen Services [ ] Requests / Month [ ] Case Management [ ] Document System [ ] ERP [ ] Portal [ ] Payment System [ ] Identity [ ] Main Manual Process [ ] Main Backlog [ ] Main Status-Call Driver [ ] Main Integration Gap [ ] Business Owner [ ] CIO / Technical Owner [ ] Procurement Path [ ] Executive Sponsor [ ]"]},{"heading":"507. EDUCATION DISCOVERY CARD","paragraphs":["Institution Type [ ] Students [ ] Applications [ ] SIS [ ] LMS [ ] ERP / Finance [ ] Student Portal [ ] Admissions System [ ] Main Student-Service Pain [ ] Main Manual Process [ ] Main Integration Gap [ ] Business Owner [ ] Academic Owner [ ] Technical Owner [ ] Economic / Executive Sponsor [ ]"]},{"heading":"508. PUBLIC QUALIFICATION","paragraphs":["Pain measurable? Citizen/service impact? Process owner? IT involved? Security/privacy involved? Procurement path understood? Data/integration feasible? Budget/timing real?"]},{"heading":"509. EDUCATION QUALIFICATION","paragraphs":["Student/admin pain measurable? Process owner? Registrar/Academic stakeholder involved? IT involved? Data/privacy feasible? Budget/timing real?"]},{"heading":"510. PUBLIC / EDUCATION OPPORTUNITY SCORE","paragraphs":["Business/service pain __/5 Citizen/student impact __/5 Technical/data feasibility __/5 Governance/procurement feasibility __/5 Stakeholder support __/5 Timing/strategic fit __/5 Total: /30."]},{"heading":"511. 26–30","paragraphs":["Strong."]},{"heading":"512. 20–25","paragraphs":["Good."]},{"heading":"513. 14–19","paragraphs":["Early/risky."]},{"heading":"514. Below 14","paragraphs":["Do not overinvest."]},{"heading":"515. ROLE PLAY 1","paragraphs":["Public Operations Director: «Έχουμε μεγάλο backlog αιτημάτων.» Sales: «Σε ποιο step δημιουργείται το μεγαλύτερο waiting — document completion, assignment, review, approval or external dependency;»"]},{"heading":"516. ROLE PLAY 2","paragraphs":["CIO: «Έχουμε πολλά legacy systems.» Sales: «Ποιο citizen journey or internal process suffers most because those systems don't exchange data effectively;»"]},{"heading":"517. ROLE PLAY 3","paragraphs":["Public Service Manager: «Οι πολίτες μας παίρνουν συνέχεια τηλέφωνο.» Sales: «Ποιες 3–5 ερωτήσεις αφορούν απλώς status, required documents or next step and could potentially be exposed through secure self-service;»"]},{"heading":"518. ROLE PLAY 4","paragraphs":["Procurement Director: «Η διαδικασία έχει πολλές εγκρίσεις.» Sales: «Which approvals are required by policy and which delays are simply caused by manual routing or lack of visibility;»"]},{"heading":"519. ROLE PLAY 5","paragraphs":["University Registrar: «Έχουμε πάρα πολλά student requests.» Sales: «Which requests are standard and repeatable versus those requiring academic or administrative judgment;»"]},{"heading":"520. ROLE PLAY 6","paragraphs":["Admissions Director: «Οι applications καθυστερούν.» Sales: «Where is most of the waiting time — missing documents, academic review, eligibility checks, approvals or communication;»"]},{"heading":"521. ROLE PLAY 7","paragraphs":["University CIO: «Έχουμε SIS και LMS αλλά δεν συνεργάζονται καλά.» Sales: «Which student or course data require manual sync today and which errors does that create downstream;»"]},{"heading":"522. ROLE PLAY 8","paragraphs":["Public CEO / Director General: «Τι μπορείτε να κάνετε για τον οργανισμό μας;» Sales: «Θα ξεκινούσα από το πού ο πολίτης περιμένει χωρίς ουσιαστικό λόγο, πού το ίδιο data ξαναγράφεται, ποια υπόθεση περνά από πολλά departments χωρίς visibility και ποια high-volume process απαιτεί skilled staff για καθαρά administrative work.»"]},{"heading":"523. ROLE PLAY 9","paragraphs":["University President / Rector: «Τι μπορείτε να κάνετε για το πανεπιστήμιο;» Sales: «Θα ξεκινούσα από το student journey: admissions, enrollment, student services and academic administration. Θα δούμε πού students επαναλαμβάνουν information, πού staff χάνουν χρόνο σε manual tasks και πού SIS, LMS and finance δεν μοιράζονται σωστά data.»"]},{"heading":"524. ROLE PLAY 10","paragraphs":["Customer: «Θέλουμε AI να απαντά στους πολίτες.» Sales: «Θα ξεκινούσα από administrative questions with approved answers and clear escalation. Για rights, eligibility or case-specific decisions, χρειάζονται πολύ αυστηρότερα controls and human review.»"]},{"heading":"525. ROLE PLAY 11","paragraphs":["University: «Θέλουμε AI για student support.» Sales: «Πρώτα θα ξεχωρίσουμε informational support από academic or welfare decisions. Timetables, deadlines and procedures are very different use cases from recommendations affecting a student's academic path.»"]}]],["Σημεία 526–536 · ACCOUNT EXPANSION — PUBLIC",[{"heading":"526. ACCOUNT EXPANSION — PUBLIC","paragraphs":["Successful: case-management workflow. Could expand: to: Citizen portal payments inspections analytics."]},{"heading":"527. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["Grant management ↓ payment workflow ↓ monitoring ↓ reporting."]},{"heading":"528. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["Field-service workflow ↓ GIS ↓ asset management."]},{"heading":"529. EDUCATION EXPANSION","paragraphs":["Admissions ↓ enrollment ↓ student services ↓ alumni."]},{"heading":"530. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["SIS integration ↓ LMS ↓ finance ↓ analytics."]},{"heading":"531. BUT","paragraphs":["always: new discovery governance business case."]},{"heading":"532. PUBLIC-SECTOR GOLDEN RULE","paragraphs":["«Στον δημόσιο τομέα η μεγαλύτερη software ευκαιρία βρίσκεται συχνά εκεί όπου ο πολίτης βλέπει μία ψηφιακή υπηρεσία, αλλά πίσω από αυτήν άνθρωποι εξακολουθούν να μεταφέρουν documents, approvals και data με email, Excel ή χειροκίνητη καταχώριση.»"]},{"heading":"533. EDUCATION GOLDEN RULE","paragraphs":["«Στην εκπαίδευση η μεγαλύτερη software ευκαιρία βρίσκεται συχνά εκεί όπου ο student περνά από admissions, enrollment, courses, services και finance, αλλά κάθε στάδιο λειτουργεί σε διαφορετικό system και η πληροφορία δεν ακολουθεί τον student ομαλά.»"]},{"heading":"534. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ PUBLIC-SECTOR ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["RESEARCH ORGANIZATION / SERVICES / DIGITAL INITIATIVES ↓ IDENTIFY SERVICE OR POLICY TRIGGER ↓ SPEAK TO PROCESS OWNER ↓ MAP CITIZEN REQUEST END-TO-END ↓ FIND MANUAL ROUTING / WAITING / RE-ENTRY ↓ QUANTIFY CASE VOLUME / BACKLOG / SERVICE IMPACT ↓ INVOLVE IT + SECURITY + FINANCE + PROCUREMENT ↓ MAP LEGACY / DMS / ERP / PORTAL / IDENTITY SYSTEMS ↓ IDENTIFY SOURCE OF TRUTH ↓ BUILD BUSINESS CASE ↓ PILOT ONE HIGH-VOLUME SERVICE ↓ MEASURE CYCLE TIME + ADOPTION + DATA QUALITY ↓ SCALE TO OTHER SERVICES ↓ EXPAND RESPONSIBLY."]},{"heading":"535. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ EDUCATION ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["RESEARCH INSTITUTION / STUDENT JOURNEY ↓ IDENTIFY GROWTH / SERVICE TRIGGER ↓ SPEAK TO REGISTRAR / ADMISSIONS / STUDENT SERVICES ↓ MAP APPLICATION → ENROLLMENT → STUDENT SERVICE ↓ FIND HANDOFFS / DUPLICATE ENTRY / WAITING ↓ QUANTIFY ADMIN WORK + STUDENT IMPACT ↓ INVOLVE IT + FINANCE + ACADEMIC STAKEHOLDERS ↓ MAP SIS / LMS / ERP / PORTALS ↓ IDENTIFY SOURCE OF TRUTH ↓ BUILD BUSINESS CASE ↓ PILOT ONE DEPARTMENT OR JOURNEY ↓ MEASURE ADMIN TIME + SERVICE QUALITY + ADOPTION ↓ SCALE ↓ EXPAND RESPONSIBLY."]},{"heading":"536. Η ΜΙΑ ΦΡΑΣΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΘΥΜΑΤΑΙ Η ΟΜΑΔΑ","paragraphs":["«Σε Public Sector & Education δεν ξεκινάμε ρωτώντας “θέλετε portal, AI ή νέο system;”. Ξεκινάμε από το πού πολίτης ή φοιτητής περιμένει χωρίς λόγο, πού η ίδια πληροφορία ξαναγράφεται, πού μία υπόθεση χάνει ownership όταν περνά από διαφορετικά departments και ποιο high-volume administrative process μπορεί να γίνει απλούστερο, πιο διαφανές και πιο αξιόπιστο χωρίς να αφαιρέσουμε τον ανθρώπινο έλεγχο από αποφάσεις που τον χρειάζονται.» Αυτό είναι: DISTILLOGIC PUBLIC SECTOR & EDUCATION PLAYBOOK."]}]],["Πριν απαντήσεις στο quiz",["Ξανασκέψου το εισαγωγικό περιστατικό. Ποιο γεγονός είναι επιβεβαιωμένο, ποια πληροφορία λείπει και ποια ενέργεια θα μείωνε την αβεβαιότητα; Μία απάντηση μπορεί να ακούγεται εμπορικά ελκυστική αλλά να προηγείται της απαιτούμενης επιβεβαίωσης.","Οι δύο ερωτήσεις εφαρμογής γενικών αρχών συνδέονται και με τις προαιρετικές «Γενικές σημειώσεις». Το PDF βρίσκεται μόνιμα στο μενού, δεν αποτελεί ξεχωριστό υποχρεωτικό μάθημα και η ανάγνωσή του δεν βαθμολογείται.","Προσαρμοστική πώληση σημαίνει καλύτερη κατανόηση, όχι διαφορετική αλήθεια. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Adaptive Selling.","Η αναγνώριση μοτίβου δεν αντικαθιστά την επιβεβαίωση της συγκεκριμένης περίπτωσης. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Active Listening."]]],"scenario":["Πανεπιστήμιο δέχεται online αιτήσεις, αλλά τις ανακαταχωρίζει χειροκίνητα σε συστήματα φοιτητών και οικονομικών.","Στη διαδρομή μετά την υποβολή: έλεγχος, ανάθεση, απόφαση, εγγραφή και ενημέρωση συστημάτων. Ψηφιακή φόρμα δεν σημαίνει ολοκληρωμένη ψηφιακή διαδικασία."],"minutes":51,"version":1,"additional_curriculum":37,"question_rows":[["Πανεπιστήμιο δέχεται online αιτήσεις, αλλά τις ανακαταχωρίζει χειροκίνητα σε συστήματα φοιτητών και οικονομικών. Πού αρχίζει η σωστή διερεύνηση;","Στη διαδρομή μετά την υποβολή: έλεγχος, ανάθεση, απόφαση, εγγραφή και ενημέρωση συστημάτων.","Σε νέο portal χωρίς εξέταση της εσωτερικής διαδικασίας.","Στην αυτόματη αποδοχή όλων των πλήρων αιτήσεων.","Στην κατάργηση του συστήματος φοιτητών μόνο επειδή είναι παλιό.","Ψηφιακή φόρμα δεν σημαίνει ολοκληρωμένη ψηφιακή διαδικασία."],["Πανεπιστήμιο δέχεται online αιτήσεις, αλλά τις ανακαταχωρίζει χειροκίνητα σε συστήματα φοιτητών και οικονομικών. Το AI προτείνεται για τελική απόφαση εισαγωγής. Τι κάνεις;","Διαχωρίζω υποστήριξη ταξινόμησης/εξαγωγής από εξουσιοδοτημένη απόφαση και ζητώ αρμόδια αξιολόγηση.","Το περιλαμβάνω ως απλό πρόσθετο του portal.","Υπόσχομαι δικαιότερες αποφάσεις χωρίς έλεγχο δεδομένων.","Παραλείπω ανθρώπινη επανεξέταση για καλύτερη ταχύτητα.","Η ευαίσθητη απόφαση δεν αντιμετωπίζεται ως συνηθισμένος αυτοματισμός."],["Πανεπιστήμιο δέχεται online αιτήσεις, αλλά τις ανακαταχωρίζει χειροκίνητα σε συστήματα φοιτητών και οικονομικών. Ποιοι περιορισμοί πρέπει να αποτυπωθούν στην ευκαιρία;","Διαδικασία προμηθειών, ασφάλεια/ιδιωτικότητα, προσβασιμότητα και ιδιοκτησία δεδομένων.","Μόνο χρώματα και λογότυπο ιδρύματος.","Μόνο το πλήθος αιτήσεων του προηγούμενου έτους.","Μόνο η επιθυμητή ημερομηνία παρουσίασης.","Η υλοποιησιμότητα περιλαμβάνει θεσμικούς και λειτουργικούς περιορισμούς."],["Ο τεχνικός και ο οικονομικός υπεύθυνος θέλουν διαφορετική παρουσίαση της ίδιας πρότασης. Τι προσαρμόζεις;","Γλώσσα, βάθος και παραδείγματα στον ρόλο, κρατώντας ίδιες τις αληθείς δυνατότητες, τους όρους και τους περιορισμούς.","Τις πραγματικές δυνατότητες ώστε κάθε συνομιλητής να ακούσει αυτό που επιθυμεί.","Τους εγκεκριμένους όρους χωρίς εσωτερική έγκριση.","Την ύπαρξη τεχνικού ρίσκου μόνο στον τεχνικό, κρύβοντάς το από τον οικονομικό αγοραστή.","Προσαρμοστική πώληση σημαίνει καλύτερη κατανόηση, όχι διαφορετική αλήθεια. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Adaptive Selling."],["Σε meeting ο πελάτης περιγράφει καθυστέρηση, ενώ εσύ αναγνωρίζεις μια γνώριμη χρήση του προϊόντος. Ποια αντίδραση διατηρεί ενεργητική ακρόαση;","Συνοψίζω όσα άκουσα, ζητώ επιβεβαίωση και διερευνώ επίπτωση πριν συνδέσω τη λύση.","Διακόπτω για demo επειδή γνωρίζω ήδη την κατάλληλη λειτουργία.","Συμπληρώνω μόνος μου τα άγνωστα από προηγούμενο πελάτη.","Μεταφέρω τη συζήτηση στην τιμή πριν καταλάβω τη διαδικασία.","Η αναγνώριση μοτίβου δεν αντικαθιστά την επιβεβαίωση της συγκεκριμένης περίπτωσης. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Active Listening."]],"source_note":"Πηγή: ΜΑΘΗΜΑ 31.docx, κεφάλαιο 50. Διατηρείται το κείμενο των αριθμημένων σημείων, με ενοποίηση των σπασμένων γραμμών και αφαίρεση επαναλαμβανόμενης μορφοποίησης. Τα παραδείγματα δεν αλλάζουν τους κανόνες της εφαρμογής."},"di-enterprise-51":{"pillar":"distillogic","title":"51. Σύνθετα σενάρια επιχειρηματικών πωλήσεων","goal":"Να αναγνωρίζεις πραγματικές ανάγκες, να διερευνάς τα στοιχεία και να επιλέγεις υπεύθυνο επόμενο βήμα.","sections":[["Από την έννοια στην επαγγελματική πράξη",["Σενάριο πώλησης φαίνεται ελκυστικό: υπάρχει σημαντικό πρόβλημα και θετικό demo, αλλά δεν έχει επιβεβαιωθεί ιδιοκτήτης προβλήματος, απόφαση ή τεχνική εφικτότητα.","Στη μελέτη που ακολουθεί σύνδεσε κάθε πιθανή λύση με συγκεκριμένη διαδικασία, υπεύθυνο, επίπτωση και στοιχεία που μπορούν να επαληθευτούν. Η τεχνική δυνατότητα, η οικονομική αξία και η εξουσιοδότηση για απόφαση είναι διαφορετικά ερωτήματα. Τα παραδείγματα του κεφαλαίου σε βοηθούν να τα διερευνάς χωρίς να υπόσχεσαι κάτι που δεν έχει εγκριθεί.","Η ύλη περιγράφει ενδεικτικές επιχειρηματικές ανάγκες και μεθόδους πώλησης. Δεν αποτελεί κατάλογο έτοιμων λειτουργιών των δύο CRM, δεσμευτική προσφορά, αλλαγή αμοιβών ή νέα πολιτική πιστοποίησης. Για πραγματική εργασία ισχύουν οι εγκεκριμένοι εταιρικοί όροι και οι αρμοδιότητες. Το μάθημα 60 είναι προετοιμασία, όχι δεύτερη επίσημη τελική εξέταση."]],["Το αντικείμενο του κεφαλαίου",["ΠΡΑΓΜΑΤΙΚΑ ΣΕΝΑΡΙΑ ENTERPRISE ΠΩΛΗΣΕΩΝ Από το Research μέχρι το Close"]],["Σημεία 1–25 · Ο ΣΤΟΧΟΣ ΤΟΥ ΜΑΘΗΜΑΤΟΣ",[{"heading":"1. Ο ΣΤΟΧΟΣ ΤΟΥ ΜΑΘΗΜΑΤΟΣ","paragraphs":["Μέχρι τώρα μάθαμε: Account Research Stakeholder Mapping Discovery MEDDPICC Business Case Proposal Procurement Negotiation Closing Account Expansion. Τώρα: θα τα ενώσουμε όλα."]},{"heading":"2. Ο ΠΩΛΗΤΗΣ ΔΕΝ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΣΚΕΦΤΕΤΑΙ","paragraphs":["«Τι να πω στον πελάτη;» Πρέπει να σκέφτεται: «Τι πρέπει να μάθω για να ξέρω ποιο είναι το σωστό επόμενο βήμα;»"]},{"heading":"3. ENTERPRISE SALE = SEQUENCE","paragraphs":["RESEARCH ↓ HYPOTHESIS ↓ STAKEHOLDER ↓ OUTREACH ↓ DISCOVERY ↓ QUALIFICATION ↓ TECHNICAL VALIDATION ↓ BUSINESS CASE ↓ PROPOSAL ↓ PROCUREMENT ↓ NEGOTIATION ↓ CLOSE ↓ DELIVERY ↓ EXPANSION."]},{"heading":"4. ΣΕ ΚΑΘΕ ΣΤΑΔΙΟ","paragraphs":["υπάρχει διαφορετικός στόχος."]},{"heading":"5. RESEARCH GOAL","paragraphs":["Δεν είναι: να μάθουμε: τα πάντα. Είναι: να βρούμε: Why this company? Why now? Who might care?"]},{"heading":"6. OUTREACH GOAL","paragraphs":["Δεν είναι: να πουλήσουμε. Είναι: ΝΑ ΚΕΡΔΙΣΟΥΜΕ ΤΗΝ ΕΠΟΜΕΝΗ ΣΥΖΗΤΗΣΗ."]},{"heading":"7. DISCOVERY GOAL","paragraphs":["Δεν είναι: να παρουσιάσουμε. Είναι: ΝΑ ΚΑΤΑΛΑΒΟΥΜΕ ΤΟ ΠΡΟΒΛΗΜΑ."]},{"heading":"8. QUALIFICATION GOAL","paragraphs":["Δεν είναι: να πείσουμε τον εαυτό μας: ότι έχουμε deal. Είναι: ΝΑ ΑΠΟΔΕΙΞΟΥΜΕ ΟΤΙ ΥΠΑΡΧΕΙ DEAL."]},{"heading":"9. PROPOSAL GOAL","paragraphs":["Δεν είναι: να στείλουμε PDF. Είναι: ΝΑ ΒΟΗΘΗΣΟΥΜΕ ΤΟΝ ΠΕΛΑΤΗ ΝΑ ΠΑΡΕΙ ΑΠΟΦΑΣΗ."]},{"heading":"10. NEGOTIATION GOAL","paragraphs":["Δεν είναι: να κρατήσουμε κάθε ευρώ. Είναι: ΝΑ ΦΤΑΣΟΥΜΕ ΣΕ ΒΙΩΣΙΜΗ ΣΥΜΦΩΝΙΑ."]},{"heading":"11. CLOSE GOAL","paragraphs":["Δεν είναι: να ακούσουμε: «Ναι, μας αρέσει.» Είναι: ΝΑ ΟΛΟΚΛΗΡΩΘΕΙ Η ΠΡΑΓΜΑΤΙΚΗ ΑΓΟΡΑΣΤΙΚΗ ΔΙΑΔΙΚΑΣΙΑ."]},{"heading":"12. CASE 1","paragraphs":["MANUFACTURING COMPANY Έχουμε: μεγάλη βιομηχανία."]},{"heading":"13. RESEARCH FINDINGS","paragraphs":["FACT: εταιρεία ανακοίνωσε: νέα παραγωγική γραμμή."]},{"heading":"14. FACT:","paragraphs":["προσλαμβάνει: automation engineers."]},{"heading":"15. FACT:","paragraphs":["έχει: 3 εργοστάσια."]},{"heading":"16. WRONG CONCLUSION","paragraphs":["«Χρειάζονται MES.»"]},{"heading":"17. CORRECT HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["New production line: may create: more complexity in: production visibility, maintenance, quality, reporting."]},{"heading":"18. VALUE HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["FACT: New line. CHANGE: Higher production complexity. POSSIBLE PROBLEM: Current reporting/processes may not scale. IMPACT: Delays, manual reporting, poor visibility. QUESTION: «As the new line comes online, which production or reporting process is becoming hardest to scale?»"]},{"heading":"19. STAKEHOLDERS","paragraphs":["Potential: Plant Manager Operations Director Production Director CIO Maintenance Manager CFO."]},{"heading":"20. WHO FIRST?","paragraphs":["Likely: Plant / Operations."]},{"heading":"21. WRONG OUTREACH","paragraphs":["«Γεια σας, είμαστε software company και κάνουμε MES, AI και Industry 4.0.»"]},{"heading":"22. BETTER OUTREACH","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι επεκτείνετε την παραγωγή με νέα γραμμή. Σε τέτοιες φάσεις συχνά μεγαλώνει η πολυπλοκότητα σε production reporting, maintenance coordination και quality visibility. Δεν γνωρίζω αν είναι θέμα για εσάς, αλλά θα είχε νόημα να καταλάβω ποιο process δυσκολεύεται περισσότερο καθώς η παραγωγή μεγαλώνει;»"]},{"heading":"23. FIRST CALL","paragraphs":["Customer: «Έχουμε ήδη ERP.»"]},{"heading":"24. BAD RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Το ERP δεν αρκεί.»"]},{"heading":"25. GOOD RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Σίγουρα. Δεν θα ξεκινούσα από replacement. Θα ήθελα να δω τι καλύπτει ήδη καλά το ERP και πού η πραγματική παραγωγική πληροφορία εξακολουθεί να περνά μέσω Excel, email or manual reports.»"]}]],["Σημεία 26–50 · DISCOVERY",[{"heading":"26. DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: «Πώς βλέπετε σήμερα actual production versus plan;»"]},{"heading":"27. ASK","paragraphs":["«Πόσο χρόνο χρειάζεται να δημιουργηθεί daily production report;»"]},{"heading":"28. ASK","paragraphs":["«Πού καταγράφεται downtime;»"]},{"heading":"29. ASK","paragraphs":["«Τι συμβαίνει όταν machine fault stops production;»"]},{"heading":"30. ASK","paragraphs":["«If volume increased 30%, which process would break first;»"]},{"heading":"31. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«Κάθε βάρδια στέλνει Excel. Μετά ένας production manager συγκεντρώνει τα δεδομένα.»"]},{"heading":"32. NOW WE HAVE","paragraphs":["possible pain."]},{"heading":"33. BUT NOT ENOUGH","paragraphs":["Need quantify."]},{"heading":"34. FOLLOW-UP","paragraphs":["«Πόσες γραμμές και βάρδιες στέλνουν αυτά τα reports;»"]},{"heading":"35. FOLLOW-UP","paragraphs":["«Πόσο χρόνο ξοδεύει management καθημερινά για consolidation;»"]},{"heading":"36. FOLLOW-UP","paragraphs":["«What decisions are delayed because data arrives late;»"]},{"heading":"37. NOW","paragraphs":["potential business case: exists."]},{"heading":"38. MEDDPICC","paragraphs":["Metrics: reporting hours."]},{"heading":"39. Economic Buyer:","paragraphs":["possibly COO/CFO."]},{"heading":"40. Decision Criteria:","paragraphs":["integration, reliability, ease of use."]},{"heading":"41. Decision Process:","paragraphs":["unknown."]},{"heading":"42. Paper Process:","paragraphs":["unknown."]},{"heading":"43. Pain:","paragraphs":["manual production reporting."]},{"heading":"44. Champion:","paragraphs":["maybe Production Manager."]},{"heading":"45. Competition:","paragraphs":["Excel + current process."]},{"heading":"46. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Competition is not always: another vendor."]},{"heading":"47. COMPETITION CAN BE","paragraphs":["DO NOTHING."]},{"heading":"48. CASE 1 NEXT STEP","paragraphs":["Not: proposal."]},{"heading":"49. BETTER NEXT STEP","paragraphs":["Workshop: Production + IT."]},{"heading":"50. OBJECTIVE","paragraphs":["Map: current reporting flow."]}]],["Σημεία 51–75 · TECHNICAL DISCOVERY",[{"heading":"51. TECHNICAL DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: ERP? Machines? SCADA? PLC? APIs? Database?"]},{"heading":"52. DON'T PROMISE","paragraphs":["machine connectivity: before validation."]},{"heading":"53. BUSINESS CASE","paragraphs":["Current: 20 hours/week: manual consolidation. Example only if customer confirms."]},{"heading":"54. Potential value:","paragraphs":["less admin, faster visibility, better data consistency."]},{"heading":"55. PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["Phase 1: digital production reporting."]},{"heading":"56. NOT","paragraphs":["«Complete smart factory transformation.»"]},{"heading":"57. WHY?","paragraphs":["Smaller scope: lower risk, faster proof."]},{"heading":"58. PILOT","paragraphs":["One line."]},{"heading":"59. SUCCESS CRITERIA","paragraphs":["Adoption Data accuracy Reporting time Availability of information."]},{"heading":"60. EXPANSION","paragraphs":["If successful: production reporting ↓ downtime ↓ maintenance ↓ quality ↓ multiple factories."]},{"heading":"61. CASE 1 GOLDEN LESSON","paragraphs":["ΜΗΝ ΠΟΥΛΑΣ MES. Βρες: πού production information: χάνεται."]},{"heading":"62. CASE 2","paragraphs":["LOGISTICS COMPANY Company: large 3PL."]},{"heading":"63. RESEARCH","paragraphs":["FACT: new warehouse announced."]},{"heading":"64. FACT:","paragraphs":["e-commerce fulfillment growing."]},{"heading":"65. FACT:","paragraphs":["many job openings: warehouse operations."]},{"heading":"66. HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["More volume: may create: picking, inventory, reporting, customer-visibility pressure."]},{"heading":"67. POTENTIAL STAKEHOLDERS","paragraphs":["COO Warehouse Director Logistics Director CIO Customer Operations CFO."]},{"heading":"68. OUTREACH","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι επεκτείνετε τις fulfillment operations. Σε περιβάλλον με αυξανόμενο order volume, συχνά εμφανίζονται bottlenecks σε picking, stock visibility, client reporting and exception management. Δεν γνωρίζω αν είναι θέμα για εσάς, αλλά ποια process δυσκολεύεται περισσότερο καθώς μεγαλώνει ο όγκος;»"]},{"heading":"69. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε WMS.»"]},{"heading":"70. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Τότε δεν ξεκινάμε από replacement. Πού υπάρχουν gaps γύρω από το WMS — order intake, client integration, returns, reporting or transport handoff;»"]},{"heading":"71. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«Οι πελάτες μας ζητούν συνέχεια status.»"]},{"heading":"72. POSSIBLE PAIN","paragraphs":["No self-service visibility."]},{"heading":"73. DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["«Τι ζητούν πιο συχνά;»"]},{"heading":"74. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Πού είναι η παραγγελία, αν έφυγε, τι stock έχουν.»"]},{"heading":"75. ASK","paragraphs":["«Πόσα τέτοια requests παίρνετε ημερησίως;»"]}]],["Σημεία 76–100 · ASK",[{"heading":"76. ASK","paragraphs":["«Πόσο employee time χρειάζεται για response;»"]},{"heading":"77. ASK","paragraphs":["«Does the data already exist in WMS/TMS;»"]},{"heading":"78. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["If data already exists: portal may be useful."]},{"heading":"79. If data unreliable:","paragraphs":["portal is not first solution."]},{"heading":"80. FIRST FIX","paragraphs":["data/process."]},{"heading":"81. THEN","paragraphs":["self-service."]},{"heading":"82. BUSINESS CASE","paragraphs":["Potential: support-call reduction."]},{"heading":"83. BUT","paragraphs":["never invent percentage."]},{"heading":"84. PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["Could be: client portal integrating: WMS + TMS."]},{"heading":"85. PILOT","paragraphs":["One major customer."]},{"heading":"86. SUCCESS","paragraphs":["status accuracy, client adoption, reduced manual status requests."]},{"heading":"87. CASE 2 GOLDEN LESSON","paragraphs":["ΤΟ PORTAL ΔΕΝ ΕΙΝΑΙ Η ΛΥΣΗ ΑΝ ΤΑ DATA ΠΙΣΩ ΤΟΥ ΔΕΝ ΕΙΝΑΙ ΑΞΙΟΠΙΣΤΑ."]},{"heading":"88. CASE 3","paragraphs":["HOTEL GROUP Group: 8 hotels."]},{"heading":"89. RESEARCH","paragraphs":["FACT: acquired two new properties."]},{"heading":"90. HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["More properties: may create: reporting, guest profile, operations, system fragmentation."]},{"heading":"91. POTENTIAL STAKEHOLDERS","paragraphs":["COO Group Operations Director CIO Revenue Director Guest Experience CFO."]},{"heading":"92. OUTREACH","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι ο όμιλος προσθέτει νέα properties. Σε hotel groups που αναπτύσσονται, συχνά γίνεται δυσκολότερο να υπάρχει consistent visibility σε guest journey, room operations και management reporting across properties. Δεν γνωρίζω αν αποτελεί issue για εσάς, αλλά ποιο process είναι πιο δύσκολο να standardize καθώς το group μεγαλώνει;»"]},{"heading":"93. DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Customer says: «Τα hotels χρησιμοποιούν διαφορετικά PMS.»"]},{"heading":"94. WRONG","paragraphs":["«Πρέπει να τα αλλάξετε όλα.»"]},{"heading":"95. RIGHT","paragraphs":["«Which group-level processes genuinely suffer because PMS platforms differ?»"]},{"heading":"96. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Management reporting και guest history.»"]},{"heading":"97. NOW","paragraphs":["two possible opportunities: Data integration Shared guest profile."]},{"heading":"98. NEED PRIORITIZE","paragraphs":["Ask: «Which creates more measurable business pain today?»"]},{"heading":"99. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Reporting.»"]},{"heading":"100. START THERE","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 101–125 · TECHNICAL",[{"heading":"101. TECHNICAL","paragraphs":["Map: PMS A, PMS B, PMS C, APIs, data definitions."]},{"heading":"102. BUSINESS","paragraphs":["Which KPIs? Occupancy? ADR? RevPAR? Operational issues?"]},{"heading":"103. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Need: common definitions."]},{"heading":"104. NOT JUST DASHBOARD","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"105. PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["Group reporting/data layer."]},{"heading":"106. PILOT","paragraphs":["2 properties."]},{"heading":"107. EXPANSION","paragraphs":["Reporting ↓ guest profile ↓ CRM ↓ loyalty ↓ operations."]},{"heading":"108. CASE 3 GOLDEN LESSON","paragraphs":["ΜΗΝ ΞΕΚΙΝΑΣ ΑΠΟ SYSTEM REPLACEMENT ΟΤΑΝ INTEGRATION ΛΥΝΕΙ ΤΟ ΠΡΩΤΟ BUSINESS PROBLEM."]},{"heading":"109. CASE 4","paragraphs":["BANK Bank announces: new digital onboarding."]},{"heading":"110. FACT","paragraphs":["Digital initiative exists."]},{"heading":"111. DON'T ASSUME","paragraphs":["pain."]},{"heading":"112. HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["Customer-facing digital process: may still have: manual KYC/back office."]},{"heading":"113. STAKEHOLDERS","paragraphs":["Head of Digital Operations Compliance Risk CIO Security."]},{"heading":"114. OUTREACH","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι επενδύετε στο digital onboarding. Σε τέτοιες initiatives συχνά το challenge μεταφέρεται από το front end στο back office — KYC, documents, exception review and core activation. Δεν γνωρίζω αν ισχύει σε εσάς. Ποιο step είναι σήμερα πιο δύσκολο να scale;»"]},{"heading":"115. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«KYC review.»"]},{"heading":"116. DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: «What creates the workload: document collection, screening, data gathering or analyst decision;»"]},{"heading":"117. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Οι analysts ψάχνουν data σε 4 systems.»"]},{"heading":"118. POSSIBLE OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Analyst workspace."]},{"heading":"119. DON'T JUMP TO AI","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"120. ASK","paragraphs":["«Can the required data be integrated reliably first?»"]},{"heading":"121. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«We also want AI.»"]},{"heading":"122. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«AI may help with extraction or summarization, but first I would separate the data-access problem from the judgment problem. If analysts spend time just collecting information, integration may create value before AI decision support.»"]},{"heading":"123. VERY IMPORTANT LESSON","paragraphs":["DON'T FORCE AI INTO A PROCESS WHOSE BASIC DATA FLOW IS BROKEN."]},{"heading":"124. CASE 4 BUSINESS CASE","paragraphs":["Measure: analyst preparation time cases/day backlog turnaround time."]},{"heading":"125. POC","paragraphs":["One KYC case type."]}]],["Σημεία 126–150 · AI POC",[{"heading":"126. AI POC","paragraphs":["Potential later: document summarization."]},{"heading":"127. CONTROL","paragraphs":["Human analyst remains: decision maker."]},{"heading":"128. CASE 5","paragraphs":["CONSTRUCTION Large contractor: wins €200M project."]},{"heading":"129. TRIGGER","paragraphs":["Strong."]},{"heading":"130. POSSIBLE PAINS","paragraphs":["RFIs, subcontractor coordination, variations, documents, reporting."]},{"heading":"131. WRONG APPROACH","paragraphs":["Pitch: full construction management platform."]},{"heading":"132. BETTER","paragraphs":["Find: one important bottleneck."]},{"heading":"133. OUTREACH","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι αναλάβατε το νέο project. Σε μεγάλα έργα, RFIs, document revisions, site-to-commercial handoffs και variations often become difficult to control as volume grows. Δεν γνωρίζω πού θα είναι το μεγαλύτερο pressure για εσάς, αλλά θα είχε νόημα να καταλάβω which workflow you are most concerned about as execution ramps up;»"]},{"heading":"134. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Variations.»"]},{"heading":"135. DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: «Where do variations get lost today?»"]},{"heading":"136. Possibilities:","paragraphs":["initial instruction, evidence, cost estimate, approval, billing."]},{"heading":"137. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Work happens before commercial team knows.»"]},{"heading":"138. CORE PAIN","paragraphs":["Site-to-commercial handoff."]},{"heading":"139. SOLUTION HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["Site instruction/variation early-warning workflow."]},{"heading":"140. METRIC","paragraphs":["Value of: unapproved work."]},{"heading":"141. ASK","paragraphs":["«How much work value typically sits unapproved at any point;»"]},{"heading":"142. VERY STRONG COMMERCIAL DISCOVERY","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"143. CHAMPION","paragraphs":["Could be: Commercial Manager."]},{"heading":"144. But need:","paragraphs":["Site buy-in."]},{"heading":"145. MULTI-THREAD","paragraphs":["Commercial + Site + IT."]},{"heading":"146. PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["One project."]},{"heading":"147. SUCCESS","paragraphs":["variation capture, time to commercial review, visibility, audit trail."]},{"heading":"148. CASE 5 GOLDEN LESSON","paragraphs":["ΒΡΕΣ ΤΟ HANDOFF ΠΟΥ ΧΑΝΕΙ ΧΡΗΜΑ."]},{"heading":"149. CASE 6","paragraphs":["PHARMA Company: new manufacturing capacity."]},{"heading":"150. HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["More batches: more: QA review, deviations, lab work."]}]],["Σημεία 151–175 · STAKEHOLDERS",[{"heading":"151. STAKEHOLDERS","paragraphs":["Quality Director Manufacturing QC Validation IT."]},{"heading":"152. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«Batch release takes too long.»"]},{"heading":"153. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«We'll automate batch release.»"]},{"heading":"154. ASK","paragraphs":["«What actually delays release?»"]},{"heading":"155. Potential:","paragraphs":["lab result, missing document, deviation, QA review."]},{"heading":"156. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«QA checks hundreds of records manually.»"]},{"heading":"157. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Review-by-exception."]},{"heading":"158. BUT","paragraphs":["regulated process."]},{"heading":"159. NEED","paragraphs":["Quality + Validation."]},{"heading":"160. DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["«Which checks are simple completeness checks versus quality judgments;»"]},{"heading":"161. THIS QUESTION IS CRITICAL","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"162. WHY?","paragraphs":["Automate: repetitive checks. Keep: human judgment."]},{"heading":"163. POC","paragraphs":["Controlled: one record type."]},{"heading":"164. SUCCESS","paragraphs":["traceability, accuracy, QA time, validation evidence."]},{"heading":"165. CASE 6 GOLDEN LESSON","paragraphs":["ΣΤΑ REGULATED INDUSTRIES ΑΥΤΟΜΑΤΟΠΟΙΟΥΜΕ ΠΡΩΤΑ ADMINISTRATIVE WORK — ΟΧΙ ΑΥΘΑΙΡΕΤΑ HUMAN JUDGMENT."]},{"heading":"166. CASE 7","paragraphs":["TELECOM Operator: expands fiber."]},{"heading":"167. CUSTOMER ISSUE","paragraphs":["Activations delayed."]},{"heading":"168. DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: «Where does order spend most time between sale and active service?»"]},{"heading":"169. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Orders fail because inventory says ports are available but field says they aren't.»"]},{"heading":"170. ROOT PROBLEM","paragraphs":["Network inventory accuracy."]},{"heading":"171. WRONG SOLUTION","paragraphs":["New customer app."]},{"heading":"172. RIGHT FOCUS","paragraphs":["Inventory reconciliation."]},{"heading":"173. BUSINESS IMPACT","paragraphs":["activation delay, customer calls, technician visits, delayed revenue."]},{"heading":"174. STAKEHOLDERS","paragraphs":["Customer Operations Network Inventory OSS CIO Finance."]},{"heading":"175. PILOT","paragraphs":["One region."]}]],["Σημεία 176–200 · SUCCESS",[{"heading":"176. SUCCESS","paragraphs":["fewer fallout orders, better availability accuracy, faster activation."]},{"heading":"177. GOLDEN LESSON","paragraphs":["ΠΟΛΛΕΣ ΦΟΡΕΣ ΤΟ CUSTOMER EXPERIENCE PROBLEM ΞΕΚΙΝΑ ΑΠΟ BACK-END DATA."]},{"heading":"178. CASE 8","paragraphs":["PROFESSIONAL SERVICES FIRM Consultancy: growing rapidly."]},{"heading":"179. CEO says:","paragraphs":["«Everyone is busy but profitability isn't improving.»"]},{"heading":"180. DON'T OFFER","paragraphs":["CRM."]},{"heading":"181. DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: «Can you see project margin and resource utilization accurately by engagement;»"]},{"heading":"182. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«At month end.»"]},{"heading":"183. PAIN","paragraphs":["Visibility too late."]},{"heading":"184. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What changes after month end that you can no longer fix;»"]},{"heading":"185. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Projects have already overspent hours.»"]},{"heading":"186. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Project profitability/forecasting."]},{"heading":"187. MAP","paragraphs":["CRM → PSA → timesheets → ERP."]},{"heading":"188. POSSIBLE ROOT CAUSE","paragraphs":["Timesheets late."]},{"heading":"189. OR","paragraphs":["scope creep."]},{"heading":"190. OR","paragraphs":["resource mix too senior."]},{"heading":"191. NEED","paragraphs":["identify actual cause."]},{"heading":"192. BUSINESS CASE","paragraphs":["Early margin visibility."]},{"heading":"193. PILOT","paragraphs":["One practice."]},{"heading":"194. GOLDEN LESSON","paragraphs":["REVENUE GROWTH DOES NOT MEAN HEALTHY GROWTH IF DELIVERY ECONOMICS ARE INVISIBLE."]},{"heading":"195. CASE 9","paragraphs":["CORPORATE GROUP Group acquired: 3 companies."]},{"heading":"196. Group CFO:","paragraphs":["«I need one dashboard.»"]},{"heading":"197. BAD SALES RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Yes, we'll build dashboard.»"]},{"heading":"198. GOOD RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Before the dashboard, we need to confirm common KPI definitions and authoritative sources. Otherwise we risk creating one screen with inconsistent numbers.»"]},{"heading":"199. DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: «Which KPI is hardest to consolidate today?»"]},{"heading":"200. CFO:","paragraphs":["«Revenue by customer.»"]}]],["Σημεία 201–225 · Problem:",[{"heading":"201. Problem:","paragraphs":["same customer: different IDs."]},{"heading":"202. ROOT PAIN","paragraphs":["Customer master data."]},{"heading":"203. DASHBOARD","paragraphs":["is not first problem."]},{"heading":"204. FIRST","paragraphs":["Entity matching / MDM."]},{"heading":"205. THEN","paragraphs":["reporting."]},{"heading":"206. GOLDEN LESSON","paragraphs":["NEVER SOLVE A DATA QUALITY PROBLEM WITH A PRETTIER DASHBOARD."]},{"heading":"207. CASE 10","paragraphs":["PUBLIC SECTOR Public body: has online application portal."]},{"heading":"208. Citizens complain:","paragraphs":["slow response."]},{"heading":"209. Don't redesign portal immediately.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"210. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What happens after submit?»"]},{"heading":"211. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Application arrives as PDF by email and employee enters it into internal system.»"]},{"heading":"212. ROOT PAIN","paragraphs":["Manual back office."]},{"heading":"213. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Portal-to-case integration."]},{"heading":"214. BUSINESS IMPACT","paragraphs":["re-entry time, errors, backlog, status calls."]},{"heading":"215. PILOT","paragraphs":["One high-volume service."]},{"heading":"216. GOLDEN LESSON","paragraphs":["DIGITAL FRONT-END ≠ DIGITAL PROCESS."]},{"heading":"217. NOW WE MOVE TO","paragraphs":["FULL SALES SIMULATION"]},{"heading":"218. SIMULATION COMPANY","paragraphs":["Company: large food manufacturer."]},{"heading":"219. PUBLIC INFORMATION","paragraphs":["3 factories export growth new production line hiring Quality staff."]},{"heading":"220. TASK FOR SALESPERSON","paragraphs":["Build: Account Brief."]},{"heading":"221. ACCOUNT BRIEF","paragraphs":["Company FoodCo. Trigger New production line + export growth. Possible Pain Traceability, quality, production reporting, batch visibility. Target Roles COO, Production, Quality, CIO. First Hypothesis More production/export volume may increase complexity in quality and traceability."]},{"heading":"222. FIRST OUTREACH","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι επεκτείνετε την παραγωγή και τις εξαγωγές. Σε food manufacturers που μεγαλώνουν, συχνά δυσκολεύει η traceability μεταξύ raw material, batch, quality and final shipment. Δεν γνωρίζω αν είναι θέμα για εσάς, αλλά πώς διαχειρίζεστε σήμερα αυτή τη σύνδεση καθώς ο όγκος αυξάνεται;»"]},{"heading":"223. CUSTOMER RESPONDS","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε ERP, όλα καταγράφονται.»"]},{"heading":"224. YOUR RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Αυτό είναι σημαντικό. Το ερώτημα τότε δεν είναι αν υπάρχει system, αλλά πόσο εύκολα μπορείτε να reconstruct one batch end-to-end όταν χρειάζεται. Αν αύριο είχατε complaint για συγκεκριμένο lot, πόσο χρόνο θα χρειαζόταν η ομάδα να δείξει raw material, production, QC and shipment history;»"]},{"heading":"225. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Ίσως 2–3 ώρες.»"]}]],["Σημεία 226–250 · GREAT",[{"heading":"226. GREAT","paragraphs":["Now possible pain."]},{"heading":"227. FOLLOW-UP","paragraphs":["«What makes it take that long?»"]},{"heading":"228. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Some data in ERP, some in Excel, some in lab system.»"]},{"heading":"229. ROOT PROBLEM","paragraphs":["Fragmented traceability."]},{"heading":"230. DO NOT PRESENT YET","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"231. ASK IMPACT","paragraphs":["«When is this slow reconstruction most painful — customer complaint, audit, recall or internal investigation;»"]},{"heading":"232. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Audit and complaint.»"]},{"heading":"233. ASK VOLUME","paragraphs":["«How often does team need to perform such investigation;»"]},{"heading":"234. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Several times per month.»"]},{"heading":"235. NOW","paragraphs":["business case stronger."]},{"heading":"236. STAKEHOLDERS","paragraphs":["Need bring: Quality Production IT Operations."]},{"heading":"237. NEXT MEETING","paragraphs":["Not: demo."]},{"heading":"238. NEXT MEETING","paragraphs":["Traceability workshop."]},{"heading":"239. WORKSHOP AGENDA","paragraphs":["Select one real batch. Trace backwards. Trace forwards. Identify systems. Identify manual steps. Identify missing links."]},{"heading":"240. THIS IS REAL ENTERPRISE DISCOVERY","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"241. AFTER WORKSHOP","paragraphs":["Suppose: ERP holds production order, LIMS holds tests, Excel holds receiving checks, WMS holds shipment."]},{"heading":"242. SOLUTION HYPOTHESIS","paragraphs":["Traceability integration layer/dashboard."]},{"heading":"243. NOT","paragraphs":["replace: all systems."]},{"heading":"244. TECHNICAL VALIDATION","paragraphs":["Can systems: export/API?"]},{"heading":"245. DATA KEYS","paragraphs":["Need common identifiers: batch, lot, material, product."]},{"heading":"246. KEY RISK","paragraphs":["Identifiers: inconsistent."]},{"heading":"247. MAY NEED","paragraphs":["data-quality work first."]},{"heading":"248. BUSINESS CASE","paragraphs":["Current: 2 hours/investigation."]},{"heading":"249. Number:","paragraphs":["customer must provide."]},{"heading":"250. Also value:","paragraphs":["audit readiness, complaint response, recall readiness."]}]],["Σημεία 251–275 · DON'T INVENT",[{"heading":"251. DON'T INVENT","paragraphs":["financial risk of recall."]},{"heading":"252. PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["Phase 1: one factory + one product family."]},{"heading":"253. DELIVERABLES","paragraphs":["Data mapping Integrations Traceability view Search User roles Audit logging."]},{"heading":"254. SUCCESS CRITERIA","paragraphs":["Example: If customer agrees: trace one batch: in under X minutes."]},{"heading":"255. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Customer defines target."]},{"heading":"256. NEGOTIATION","paragraphs":["Procurement asks: «20% discount.»"]},{"heading":"257. BAD RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«OK.»"]},{"heading":"258. BETTER","paragraphs":["«If we reduce commercial value, we need to adjust another element. We can look at scope, payment terms or rollout sequence. Which is most flexible on your side?»"]},{"heading":"259. GIVE / GET","paragraphs":["Discount in exchange for: faster payment, reduced scope, reference rights if appropriate, longer commitment."]},{"heading":"260. NEVER OFFER","paragraphs":["fake reference agreement."]},{"heading":"261. CLOSING","paragraphs":["Need confirm: Security approval? Legal? Procurement? Signatory? PO? Start date?"]},{"heading":"262. Customer says:","paragraphs":["«Commercially we're aligned.»"]},{"heading":"263. That is not:","paragraphs":["closed-won."]},{"heading":"264. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What still needs to happen internally before we can start?»"]},{"heading":"265. PROCUREMENT","paragraphs":["«Security review and PO.»"]},{"heading":"266. NOW","paragraphs":["real close plan."]},{"heading":"267. CLOSED WON","paragraphs":["when: contract/PO requirements complete and: project can actually start."]},{"heading":"268. SIMULATION GOLDEN LESSON","paragraphs":["The salesperson did not: pitch software. They discovered: business/process/data problem."]},{"heading":"269. NOW","paragraphs":["BAD SALE SIMULATION Salesperson: «We offer custom software, AI, cloud, mobile applications and integrations. Would you like a demo?»"]},{"heading":"270. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«No.»"]},{"heading":"271. WHY?","paragraphs":["No: context, pain, relevance, trigger."]},{"heading":"272. BAD SALE #2","paragraphs":["«We noticed your company uses SAP. We can build better software.»"]},{"heading":"273. WRONG","paragraphs":["Technology: does not prove: pain."]},{"heading":"274. BAD SALE #3","paragraphs":["«We can reduce your costs 30%.»"]},{"heading":"275. WRONG","paragraphs":["No baseline."]}]],["Σημεία 276–300 · BAD SALE #4",[{"heading":"276. BAD SALE #4","paragraphs":["«Our AI can automate your company.»"]},{"heading":"277. WRONG","paragraphs":["Meaningless."]},{"heading":"278. BAD SALE #5","paragraphs":["«Can I send a proposal?» before discovery."]},{"heading":"279. WRONG","paragraphs":["Proposal has no foundation."]},{"heading":"280. BAD SALE #6","paragraphs":["Customer: «How much does it cost?» Sales: immediately gives: price."]},{"heading":"281. Better:","paragraphs":["understand: scope first."]},{"heading":"282. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«It depends mainly on users, workflows, integrations and criticality. I can give you a meaningful range once we understand those four areas rather than give you a number that may be misleading.»"]},{"heading":"283. BAD SALE #7","paragraphs":["Customer: «Send information.» Sales: sends: 30-page company presentation."]},{"heading":"284. Better:","paragraphs":["send: relevant: 1–2 page material."]},{"heading":"285. BAD SALE #8","paragraphs":["No reply. Sales: «Just following up.» again. again. again."]},{"heading":"286. Better follow-up:","paragraphs":["add: context/value."]},{"heading":"287. Example:","paragraphs":["«One point I didn't mention in my previous note: in similar operational workflows, we often find that the biggest issue is not the primary system itself but the handoffs between teams. If useful, I can show you the 5 questions we normally use to identify whether that exists.»"]},{"heading":"288. BAD SALE #9","paragraphs":["One friendly person: says: «I like the idea.» Sales marks: 90% close probability."]},{"heading":"289. WRONG","paragraphs":["Friendly contact: ≠ champion."]},{"heading":"290. CHAMPION TEST","paragraphs":["Do they: Share internal information? Introduce stakeholders? Help navigate decision? Push internally?"]},{"heading":"291. BAD SALE #10","paragraphs":["Technical demo: before pain."]},{"heading":"292. Customer sees:","paragraphs":["features. Not: value."]},{"heading":"293. BETTER DEMO","paragraphs":["Show: customer's workflow."]},{"heading":"294. CORE ENTERPRISE SALES QUESTIONS","paragraphs":["Every salesperson must learn:"]},{"heading":"295. QUESTION 1","paragraphs":["«How does this process work today?»"]},{"heading":"296. QUESTION 2","paragraphs":["«Where does it usually slow down or break?»"]},{"heading":"297. QUESTION 3","paragraphs":["«What happens when it does?»"]},{"heading":"298. QUESTION 4","paragraphs":["«How often does that happen?»"]},{"heading":"299. QUESTION 5","paragraphs":["«Who is affected?»"]},{"heading":"300. QUESTION 6","paragraphs":["«How do you measure the impact today?»"]}]],["Σημεία 301–325 · QUESTION 7",[{"heading":"301. QUESTION 7","paragraphs":["«Why is this important now?»"]},{"heading":"302. QUESTION 8","paragraphs":["«What have you already tried?»"]},{"heading":"303. QUESTION 9","paragraphs":["«What would a successful outcome look like?»"]},{"heading":"304. QUESTION 10","paragraphs":["«Who else needs to be involved?»"]},{"heading":"305. QUESTION 11","paragraphs":["«How would a decision like this normally be made?»"]},{"heading":"306. QUESTION 12","paragraphs":["«What happens if nothing changes?»"]},{"heading":"307. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Don't ask: all 12: mechanically."]},{"heading":"308. Conversation:","paragraphs":["not: interrogation."]},{"heading":"309. LISTEN","paragraphs":["then: follow the answer."]},{"heading":"310. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«It's slow.»"]},{"heading":"311. Don't move:","paragraphs":["to next scripted question."]},{"heading":"312. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What makes it slow?»"]},{"heading":"313. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Approvals.»"]},{"heading":"314. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which approval?»"]},{"heading":"315. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Finance.»"]},{"heading":"316. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What is Finance waiting for?»"]},{"heading":"317. THIS","paragraphs":["is: real discovery."]},{"heading":"318. ROOT CAUSE LADDER","paragraphs":["Problem: process slow. ↓ Why? Approval slow. ↓ Why? Missing information. ↓ Why? Different system. ↓ Why? Manual data collection."]},{"heading":"319. NOW","paragraphs":["root problem: not: approval. It's: data availability."]},{"heading":"320. SALESPERSON MUST LEARN","paragraphs":["THE FIRST PAIN IS OFTEN NOT THE REAL PAIN."]},{"heading":"321. DISCOVERY TEST","paragraphs":["At end of meeting: salesperson should be able to say: «If I understood correctly...»"]},{"heading":"322. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["«If I understood correctly, the issue isn't that you lack a WMS. The issue is that client status requests require staff to combine WMS and TMS information manually, which creates around X requests per day and takes Y team hours. Your priority is to reduce this before the new warehouse goes live. Is that correct?»"]},{"heading":"323. IF CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«Yes.» Good."]},{"heading":"324. IF CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«Not exactly.» Even better: let them correct us."]},{"heading":"325. QUALIFICATION SIMULATION","paragraphs":["Opportunity: looks great."]}]],["Σημεία 326–350 · Pain:",[{"heading":"326. Pain:","paragraphs":["strong."]},{"heading":"327. Champion:","paragraphs":["strong."]},{"heading":"328. But:","paragraphs":["no budget."]},{"heading":"329. Is it deal?","paragraphs":["Maybe not yet."]},{"heading":"330. Another:","paragraphs":["Budget exists. Pain weak."]},{"heading":"331. Is it deal?","paragraphs":["Risky."]},{"heading":"332. Another:","paragraphs":["Pain strong. Budget strong. No access to Economic Buyer."]},{"heading":"333. Risk:","paragraphs":["high."]},{"heading":"334. Another:","paragraphs":["Everything good. Procurement says: RFP mandatory next year."]},{"heading":"335. Timeline:","paragraphs":["different than salesperson thought."]},{"heading":"336. LESSON","paragraphs":["QUALIFICATION IS NOT «DO THEY LIKE US?»"]},{"heading":"337. MEDDPICC PRACTICE","paragraphs":["For each opportunity ask: Metrics What measurable impact?"]},{"heading":"338. Economic Buyer","paragraphs":["Who controls money/final business approval?"]},{"heading":"339. Decision Criteria","paragraphs":["What will solution be judged on?"]},{"heading":"340. Decision Process","paragraphs":["Who decides and in what order?"]},{"heading":"341. Paper Process","paragraphs":["What legal/procurement/security steps?"]},{"heading":"342. Pain","paragraphs":["What actual problem exists?"]},{"heading":"343. Champion","paragraphs":["Who wins internally if problem solved and acts on our behalf?"]},{"heading":"344. Competition","paragraphs":["Vendor? Internal team? Existing system? Do nothing?"]},{"heading":"345. SALES MANAGER REVIEW","paragraphs":["Every opportunity: should answer: these."]},{"heading":"346. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["Salesperson says: «Customer is very interested.»"]},{"heading":"347. Manager asks:","paragraphs":["«What measurable pain?»"]},{"heading":"348. Salesperson:","paragraphs":["doesn't know."]},{"heading":"349. Opportunity:","paragraphs":["not qualified."]},{"heading":"350. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["«They asked for proposal.»"]}]],["Σημεία 351–375 · Manager:",[{"heading":"351. Manager:","paragraphs":["«Who is Economic Buyer?»"]},{"heading":"352. Unknown.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"353. Risk.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"354. RED FLAG","paragraphs":["«Close next month.»"]},{"heading":"355. Manager:","paragraphs":["«What steps remain?»"]},{"heading":"356. Salesperson:","paragraphs":["doesn't know."]},{"heading":"357. Close date:","paragraphs":["fiction."]},{"heading":"358. ACCOUNT REVIEW FORMAT","paragraphs":["Every salesperson should present:"]},{"heading":"359. 1. ACCOUNT","paragraphs":["Company."]},{"heading":"360. 2. TRIGGER","paragraphs":["Why now?"]},{"heading":"361. 3. PAIN","paragraphs":["Confirmed problem."]},{"heading":"362. 4. IMPACT","paragraphs":["Measured/estimated with customer data."]},{"heading":"363. 5. STAKEHOLDERS","paragraphs":["Who matters?"]},{"heading":"364. 6. CHAMPION","paragraphs":["Who helps?"]},{"heading":"365. 7. TECHNICAL FIT","paragraphs":["Can we deliver?"]},{"heading":"366. 8. COMPETITION","paragraphs":["Who/what?"]},{"heading":"367. 9. DECISION PROCESS","paragraphs":["How buy?"]},{"heading":"368. 10. NEXT STEP","paragraphs":["Specific meeting/action."]},{"heading":"369. BAD NEXT STEP","paragraphs":["«Follow up.»"]},{"heading":"370. GOOD NEXT STEP","paragraphs":["«Technical workshop with CIO and Operations on 17 October to validate ERP API availability and agree pilot scope.»"]},{"heading":"371. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Next step: must have: Action Owner Date Objective."]},{"heading":"372. PIPELINE REVIEW","paragraphs":["Never ask only: «How much pipeline?»"]},{"heading":"373. Ask:","paragraphs":["«How much qualified pipeline?»"]},{"heading":"374. Example","paragraphs":["€1M pipeline: but 80%: no Economic Buyer, no next meeting."]},{"heading":"375. Not healthy.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 376–400 · Another:",[{"heading":"376. Another:","paragraphs":["€300k pipeline: all: qualified, multi-threaded, real next steps."]},{"heading":"377. More valuable.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"378. REAL SALES DISCIPLINE","paragraphs":["DON'T CONFUSE ACTIVITY WITH PROGRESS."]},{"heading":"379. 100 emails:","paragraphs":["activity."]},{"heading":"380. One meaningful discovery:","paragraphs":["progress."]},{"heading":"381. 10 demos:","paragraphs":["activity."]},{"heading":"382. One validated business case:","paragraphs":["progress."]},{"heading":"383. 20 LinkedIn connections:","paragraphs":["activity."]},{"heading":"384. One champion introduction:","paragraphs":["progress."]},{"heading":"385. SALES SIMULATION EXERCISE 1","paragraphs":["Scenario: Retail chain: opens 30 new stores."]},{"heading":"386. Student must answer:","paragraphs":["Trigger? Possible pain? First stakeholder? First 3 discovery questions? Potential metric? Pilot?"]},{"heading":"387. POSSIBLE GOOD ANSWER","paragraphs":["Trigger: rapid store expansion."]},{"heading":"388. Hypothesis:","paragraphs":["inventory/omnichannel/store operations may become harder."]},{"heading":"389. Stakeholder:","paragraphs":["COO / Retail Operations."]},{"heading":"390. Questions:","paragraphs":["«Which store process becomes hardest as locations grow?» «Where does HQ lack real-time visibility?» «Which data is manually consolidated across stores?»"]},{"heading":"391. Pilot:","paragraphs":["5 stores."]},{"heading":"392. SALES SIMULATION EXERCISE 2","paragraphs":["Scenario: Hotel group: reviews dropping."]},{"heading":"393. WRONG","paragraphs":["«Sell reputation management software.»"]},{"heading":"394. First discover:","paragraphs":["why reviews dropped."]},{"heading":"395. Could be:","paragraphs":["housekeeping, check-in, maintenance, restaurant, communication."]},{"heading":"396. Need root cause.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"397. SALES SIMULATION EXERCISE 3","paragraphs":["Scenario: Logistics company: customer asks for AI."]},{"heading":"398. Salesperson asks:","paragraphs":["«What decision or operational task do you want AI to improve?»"]},{"heading":"399. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Route planning.»"]},{"heading":"400. Ask:","paragraphs":["Current process? Constraints? Data? Baseline? Success metric?"]}]],["Σημεία 401–425 · Do not:",[{"heading":"401. Do not:","paragraphs":["sell AI first."]},{"heading":"402. SALES SIMULATION EXERCISE 4","paragraphs":["Scenario: Bank: asks: «Can you build onboarding platform?»"]},{"heading":"403. Don't answer immediately:","paragraphs":["«Yes.»"]},{"heading":"404. Ask:","paragraphs":["Customer type? Products? KYC? Core system? Volume? Security? Existing process?"]},{"heading":"405. THEN:","paragraphs":["technical team validates."]},{"heading":"406. SALES SIMULATION EXERCISE 5","paragraphs":["Scenario: Pharma says: «We need AI for Quality.»"]},{"heading":"407. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which Quality task?»"]},{"heading":"408. If answer:","paragraphs":["«Deviation summaries.» Possible."]},{"heading":"409. If:","paragraphs":["«Automatic final release decisions.» Much higher risk."]},{"heading":"410. Salesperson must:","paragraphs":["know difference."]},{"heading":"411. SALES SIMULATION EXERCISE 6","paragraphs":["Scenario: Corporate group: wants central system."]},{"heading":"412. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What must actually be common across subsidiaries?»"]},{"heading":"413. This single question:","paragraphs":["can save: huge wrong project."]},{"heading":"414. SALES SIMULATION EXERCISE 7","paragraphs":["Scenario: Customer says: «Send us your prices.»"]},{"heading":"415. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«I can give you useful pricing once we understand the scope. For projects like this the biggest cost drivers are usually number of workflows, integrations, users and required service level. Can we clarify those first?»"]},{"heading":"416. SALES SIMULATION EXERCISE 8","paragraphs":["Customer: «Your competitor is 20% cheaper.»"]},{"heading":"417. WRONG","paragraphs":["«We'll match it.»"]},{"heading":"418. BETTER","paragraphs":["«Let's make sure we're comparing the same scope, support, integrations and delivery responsibility. Which part of their proposal is commercially stronger for you?»"]},{"heading":"419. Need understand:","paragraphs":["price or: scope difference."]},{"heading":"420. SALES SIMULATION EXERCISE 9","paragraphs":["Customer: «We need it in 6 weeks.»"]},{"heading":"421. NEVER SAY","paragraphs":["«Yes.» without validation."]},{"heading":"422. Response:","paragraphs":["«We'll need to validate scope, integrations and dependencies before committing to that date. Which business event makes six weeks important?»"]},{"heading":"423. NOW","paragraphs":["understand urgency."]},{"heading":"424. Could be:","paragraphs":["real."]},{"heading":"425. Could be:","paragraphs":["arbitrary."]}]],["Σημεία 426–450 · SALES SIMULATION EXERCISE 10",[{"heading":"426. SALES SIMULATION EXERCISE 10","paragraphs":["Customer: «Can you guarantee it will work?»"]},{"heading":"427. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can define acceptance criteria, testing and delivery responsibilities clearly. But I wouldn't make an absolute guarantee before technical validation of the environment and dependencies.»"]},{"heading":"428. GOOD ENTERPRISE BEHAVIOR","paragraphs":["Honest confidence."]},{"heading":"429. NOT","paragraphs":["false certainty."]},{"heading":"430. SALES ROLEPLAY — DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Customer: «Our process is inefficient.»"]},{"heading":"431. Salesperson:","paragraphs":["«Walk me through one real case from start to finish.»"]},{"heading":"432. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"433. Why?","paragraphs":["Abstract: becomes: concrete."]},{"heading":"434. Customer describes:","paragraphs":["actual workflow."]},{"heading":"435. Then ask:","paragraphs":["«Where does it wait?»"]},{"heading":"436. Then:","paragraphs":["«Who touches it?»"]},{"heading":"437. Then:","paragraphs":["«Which systems?»"]},{"heading":"438. Then:","paragraphs":["«What gets re-entered?»"]},{"heading":"439. Then:","paragraphs":["«What happens when exception occurs?»"]},{"heading":"440. THIS IS PROCESS DISCOVERY","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"441. SALES ROLEPLAY — TECHNICAL","paragraphs":["CIO: «What architecture do you recommend?»"]},{"heading":"442. Salesperson shouldn't:","paragraphs":["invent architecture."]},{"heading":"443. Response:","paragraphs":["«Before our technical team recommends architecture, we'd want to understand your system landscape, integration constraints, security requirements and expected load. I can make sure those questions are covered in the technical workshop.»"]},{"heading":"444. PROFESSIONAL","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"445. SALES ROLEPLAY — CFO","paragraphs":["CFO: «What ROI do I get?»"]},{"heading":"446. WRONG","paragraphs":["«300%.»"]},{"heading":"447. BETTER","paragraphs":["«Let's build it from your baseline. We need current effort, error/rework cost, volume and expected improvement. I'd rather give you a conservative business case based on your numbers than generic ROI.»"]},{"heading":"448. SALES ROLEPLAY — PROCUREMENT","paragraphs":["Procurement: «Give me 15% discount.»"]},{"heading":"449. Sales:","paragraphs":["«If price needs to move, let's look at what we can trade rather than reduce value unconditionally. We could discuss scope, payment schedule or rollout sequence. Which is more flexible for you?»"]},{"heading":"450. SALES ROLEPLAY — CEO","paragraphs":["CEO: «Why should I care?»"]}]],["Σημεία 451–475 · DON'T TALK",[{"heading":"451. DON'T TALK","paragraphs":["APIs, React, Node, cloud."]},{"heading":"452. Talk:","paragraphs":["outcome."]},{"heading":"453. Example:","paragraphs":["«Because today your teams spend around X hours consolidating data before management sees the issue. The project is aimed at reducing that delay and giving you earlier operational visibility.»"]},{"heading":"454. SALES ROLEPLAY — OPERATIONS","paragraphs":["Operations: «We don't have time for another project.»"]},{"heading":"455. Good response:","paragraphs":["«Then the project has to remove workload rather than create a long transformation burden. Which small workflow would be valuable enough to improve but limited enough to pilot without disrupting operations?»"]},{"heading":"456. EXCELLENT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"457. SALES ROLEPLAY — IT","paragraphs":["IT: «Business keeps buying tools without involving us.»"]},{"heading":"458. Sales:","paragraphs":["«Then we'd prefer to bring architecture, security and integration into discovery early so we don't propose something the IT environment cannot support.»"]},{"heading":"459. BUILDS TRUST","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"460. SALES ROLEPLAY — CHAMPION","paragraphs":["Champion says: «I'll speak to CFO.»"]},{"heading":"461. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What do you think CFO will need to see to support this?»"]},{"heading":"462. Great champion enablement.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"463. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Would it help if we prepared a one-page business case you can use internally?»"]},{"heading":"464. Good.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"465. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Tell CFO to approve.»"]},{"heading":"466. ENABLE","paragraphs":["don't manipulate."]},{"heading":"467. SALES ROLEPLAY — NO DECISION","paragraphs":["Customer: keeps delaying."]},{"heading":"468. Don't chase forever.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"469. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Has the priority changed, or is there a specific dependency preventing a decision?»"]},{"heading":"470. If:","paragraphs":["priority gone, requalify."]},{"heading":"471. Maybe:","paragraphs":["close-lost / nurture."]},{"heading":"472. DISQUALIFICATION","paragraphs":["is: good sales."]},{"heading":"473. Why?","paragraphs":["Protect: time."]},{"heading":"474. TIER A ACCOUNT","paragraphs":["Never allow: random outreach."]},{"heading":"475. Before contact:","paragraphs":["need: Account Owner Research Stakeholder Trigger Hypothesis Objective."]}]],["Σημεία 476–500 · TIER A FIRST CALL",[{"heading":"476. TIER A FIRST CALL","paragraphs":["should not be: practice session."]},{"heading":"477. New salesperson:","paragraphs":["learns first: on: Tier C."]},{"heading":"478. Then:","paragraphs":["Tier B."]},{"heading":"479. Then:","paragraphs":["Tier A."]},{"heading":"480. ENTERPRISE SALES SCORECARD","paragraphs":["Before opportunity advances: score:"]},{"heading":"481. Pain","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"482. Measurable impact","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"483. Champion","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"484. Economic Buyer access","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"485. Technical fit","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"486. Decision process clarity","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"487. Maximum","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"488. 25–30","paragraphs":["Strong."]},{"heading":"489. 19–24","paragraphs":["Promising."]},{"heading":"490. 13–18","paragraphs":["Early/risky."]},{"heading":"491. Below 13","paragraphs":["Don't overinvest."]},{"heading":"492. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Score: not truth."]},{"heading":"493. It forces:","paragraphs":["thinking."]},{"heading":"494. DAILY SALESPERSON TRAINING","paragraphs":["Take: one company."]},{"heading":"495. Spend:","paragraphs":["15 minutes."]},{"heading":"496. Build:","paragraphs":["Trigger Stakeholders Hypothesis 3 discovery questions Potential metric."]},{"heading":"497. THEN","paragraphs":["manager reviews."]},{"heading":"498. DAILY ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["One salesperson: customer."]},{"heading":"499. One:","paragraphs":["seller."]},{"heading":"500. 10-minute discovery.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 501–525 · Customer must give:",[{"heading":"501. Customer must give:","paragraphs":["incomplete answers."]},{"heading":"502. Salesperson:","paragraphs":["must follow: the clues."]},{"heading":"503. MANAGER SHOULD SCORE","paragraphs":["Question quality Listening Follow-up Business understanding No premature pitching Next-step quality."]},{"heading":"504. WEEKLY TRAINING","paragraphs":["One full account simulation."]},{"heading":"505. MONDAY","paragraphs":["Research."]},{"heading":"506. TUESDAY","paragraphs":["Outreach."]},{"heading":"507. WEDNESDAY","paragraphs":["Discovery roleplay."]},{"heading":"508. THURSDAY","paragraphs":["Business case/proposal."]},{"heading":"509. FRIDAY","paragraphs":["Negotiation/close."]},{"heading":"510. THIS TURNS THEORY","paragraphs":["into: sales muscle."]},{"heading":"511. MANAGER QUESTION","paragraphs":["after every roleplay: «What did you learn?»"]},{"heading":"512. NOT","paragraphs":["«Did you pitch well?»"]},{"heading":"513. SECOND QUESTION","paragraphs":["«What is still unknown?»"]},{"heading":"514. THIRD","paragraphs":["«What is the next best step?»"]},{"heading":"515. THESE 3 QUESTIONS","paragraphs":["build: enterprise thinking."]},{"heading":"516. FINAL EXAM SIMULATION","paragraphs":["Salesperson receives: company profile."]},{"heading":"517. They have:","paragraphs":["30 minutes."]},{"heading":"518. Must produce:","paragraphs":["Account Brief Trigger Stakeholder Map Value Hypothesis Outreach message."]},{"heading":"519. Then:","paragraphs":["15-minute discovery."]},{"heading":"520. Then:","paragraphs":["must produce: Problem Statement MEDDPICC status Next-step recommendation."]},{"heading":"521. Then:","paragraphs":["customer gives: technical info."]},{"heading":"522. Salesperson must decide:","paragraphs":["Proposal? Workshop? PoC? Disqualify?"]},{"heading":"523. Then:","paragraphs":["negotiation."]},{"heading":"524. Customer asks:","paragraphs":["discount."]},{"heading":"525. Salesperson:","paragraphs":["must use: Give/Get."]}]],["Σημεία 526–550 · Then:",[{"heading":"526. Then:","paragraphs":["procurement."]},{"heading":"527. Must identify:","paragraphs":["legal, security, PO, signatory."]},{"heading":"528. FINAL PASS CRITERIA","paragraphs":["Salesperson: does NOT: pitch too early."]},{"heading":"529. Understands:","paragraphs":["business process."]},{"heading":"530. Finds:","paragraphs":["measurable pain."]},{"heading":"531. Maps:","paragraphs":["stakeholders."]},{"heading":"532. Knows:","paragraphs":["what is unknown."]},{"heading":"533. Does not:","paragraphs":["invent technical capability."]},{"heading":"534. Does not:","paragraphs":["invent ROI."]},{"heading":"535. Does not:","paragraphs":["promise impossible timeline."]},{"heading":"536. Gets:","paragraphs":["specific next step."]},{"heading":"537. Can:","paragraphs":["disqualify."]},{"heading":"538. Can:","paragraphs":["protect company credibility."]},{"heading":"539. ENTERPRISE SELLER MATURITY — LEVEL 1","paragraphs":["Knows: scripts."]},{"heading":"540. LEVEL 2","paragraphs":["Knows: questions."]},{"heading":"541. LEVEL 3","paragraphs":["Understands: processes."]},{"heading":"542. LEVEL 4","paragraphs":["Understands: business impact."]},{"heading":"543. LEVEL 5","paragraphs":["Can navigate: organization + economics + technology + politics."]},{"heading":"544. DISTILLOGIC TARGET","paragraphs":["LEVEL 4–5."]},{"heading":"545. NOT","paragraphs":["telemarketers."]},{"heading":"546. NOT","paragraphs":["brochure senders."]},{"heading":"547. NOT","paragraphs":["feature sellers."]},{"heading":"548. BUT","paragraphs":["BUSINESS-TECHNOLOGY ADVISORS."]},{"heading":"549. ENTERPRISE SALES GOLDEN RULE #1","paragraphs":["«Never pitch before you understand.»"]},{"heading":"550. GOLDEN RULE #2","paragraphs":["«Never propose before you can describe the problem better than the customer described it at the start.»"]}]],["Σημεία 551–560 · GOLDEN RULE #3",[{"heading":"551. GOLDEN RULE #3","paragraphs":["«Never promise technical delivery without technical validation.»"]},{"heading":"552. GOLDEN RULE #4","paragraphs":["«Never invent ROI, urgency or capability.»"]},{"heading":"553. GOLDEN RULE #5","paragraphs":["«A friendly contact is not automatically a champion.»"]},{"heading":"554. GOLDEN RULE #6","paragraphs":["«A verbal yes is not a closed deal.»"]},{"heading":"555. GOLDEN RULE #7","paragraphs":["«A proposal is not progress if the buying process is unknown.»"]},{"heading":"556. GOLDEN RULE #8","paragraphs":["«Do not automate a broken process before understanding why it is broken.»"]},{"heading":"557. GOLDEN RULE #9","paragraphs":["«Do not sell AI when integration or basic data quality is the real problem.»"]},{"heading":"558. GOLDEN RULE #10","paragraphs":["«The best next step is specific, mutual and connected to the customer's decision process.»"]},{"heading":"559. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ ΡΟΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΞΕΡΕΙ ΟΛΗ Η ΟΜΑΔΑ ΑΠ' ΕΞΩ","paragraphs":["ACCOUNT ↓ TRIGGER ↓ HYPOTHESIS ↓ STAKEHOLDER ↓ OUTREACH ↓ DISCOVERY ↓ ROOT CAUSE ↓ BUSINESS IMPACT ↓ QUALIFICATION ↓ TECHNICAL VALIDATION ↓ BUSINESS CASE ↓ PILOT / SOLUTION WORKSHOP ↓ PROPOSAL ↓ PROCUREMENT / SECURITY / LEGAL ↓ NEGOTIATION ↓ CLOSE ↓ HANDOFF ↓ VALUE REALIZATION ↓ EXPANSION."]},{"heading":"560. Η ΜΙΑ ΦΡΑΣΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΘΥΜΑΤΑΙ Ο ΠΩΛΗΤΗΣ","paragraphs":["«Ο καλός enterprise salesperson δεν μπαίνει σε μια εταιρεία για να παρουσιάσει αυτά που πουλάει η DISTILLOGIC. Μπαίνει για να καταλάβει πού η επιχείρηση χάνει χρόνο, χρήμα, έλεγχο ή δυνατότητα ανάπτυξης, να αποδείξει ότι το πρόβλημα αξίζει να λυθεί και μετά να φέρει τους σωστούς ανθρώπους της DISTILLOGIC για να δουν αν μπορούμε πραγματικά να το λύσουμε.» ΑΥΤΟ ΕΙΝΑΙ ENTERPRISE SALES."]}]],["Πριν απαντήσεις στο quiz",["Ξανασκέψου το εισαγωγικό περιστατικό. Ποιο γεγονός είναι επιβεβαιωμένο, ποια πληροφορία λείπει και ποια ενέργεια θα μείωνε την αβεβαιότητα; Μία απάντηση μπορεί να ακούγεται εμπορικά ελκυστική αλλά να προηγείται της απαιτούμενης επιβεβαίωσης.","Οι δύο ερωτήσεις εφαρμογής γενικών αρχών συνδέονται και με τις προαιρετικές «Γενικές σημειώσεις». Το PDF βρίσκεται μόνιμα στο μενού, δεν αποτελεί ξεχωριστό υποχρεωτικό μάθημα και η ανάγνωσή του δεν βαθμολογείται.","Η καλή σχέση δεν αποδεικνύει εσωτερική επιρροή. Εξετάζουμε πράξεις, πρόσβαση και γνώση της διαδικασίας. Γενικές σημειώσεις: B2B και χαρτογράφηση εμπλεκομένων.","Η αβεβαιότητα επιλογής μειώνεται με σαφήνεια και διαχείριση κινδύνου, όχι κατ’ ανάγκη με περισσότερες επιλογές. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Buyer Indecision."]]],"scenario":["Σενάριο πώλησης φαίνεται ελκυστικό: υπάρχει σημαντικό πρόβλημα και θετικό demo, αλλά δεν έχει επιβεβαιωθεί ιδιοκτήτης προβλήματος, απόφαση ή τεχνική εφικτότητα.","Τεκμηριωμένη ανάγκη με ανοικτά κενά απόφασης και τεχνικής αξιολόγησης. Η αξιολόγηση διακρίνει τι γνωρίζουμε από όσα μένουν να επιβεβαιωθούν."],"minutes":43,"version":1,"additional_curriculum":37,"question_rows":[["Σενάριο πώλησης φαίνεται ελκυστικό: υπάρχει σημαντικό πρόβλημα και θετικό demo, αλλά δεν έχει επιβεβαιωθεί ιδιοκτήτης προβλήματος, απόφαση ή τεχνική εφικτότητα. Ποια καταχώριση αντικατοπτρίζει τα διαθέσιμα στοιχεία;","Τεκμηριωμένη ανάγκη με ανοικτά κενά απόφασης και τεχνικής αξιολόγησης.","Commit επειδή η παρουσίαση άρεσε στους συμμετέχοντες.","Closed won με αναμενόμενη συμπλήρωση των όρων.","Άμεση απώλεια επειδή δεν απαντήθηκαν όλα στην πρώτη κλήση.","Η αξιολόγηση διακρίνει τι γνωρίζουμε από όσα μένουν να επιβεβαιωθούν."],["Σενάριο πώλησης φαίνεται ελκυστικό: υπάρχει σημαντικό πρόβλημα και θετικό demo, αλλά δεν έχει επιβεβαιωθεί ιδιοκτήτης προβλήματος, απόφαση ή τεχνική εφικτότητα. Ποιο επόμενο βήμα είναι ισχυρότερο;","Συμφωνημένη συνάντηση με problem owner και IT, συγκεκριμένη ατζέντα και απαιτούμενα στοιχεία.","Αποστολή γενικής παρουσίασης σε όλη την εταιρεία.","Αναμονή χωρίς ημερομηνία επειδή υπάρχει ενδιαφέρον.","Έκπτωση για να παρακαμφθεί η τεχνική συζήτηση.","Ένα καλό επόμενο βήμα κλείνει συγκεκριμένα κενά."],["Σενάριο πώλησης φαίνεται ελκυστικό: υπάρχει σημαντικό πρόβλημα και θετικό demo, αλλά δεν έχει επιβεβαιωθεί ιδιοκτήτης προβλήματος, απόφαση ή τεχνική εφικτότητα. Σε νέο σενάριο πελάτης δεν έχει μετρήσει την επίπτωση. Τι κάνεις;","Συμφωνώ τρόπο συλλογής baseline αντί να επινοήσω εξοικονόμηση.","Χρησιμοποιώ τον τζίρο ως άμεση εκτίμηση κόστους προβλήματος.","Δηλώνω ότι δεν υπάρχει ανάγκη μέχρι να έχει έτοιμο business case.","Αντιγράφω το αποτέλεσμα άλλου πελάτη χωρίς προσαρμογή.","Η ποσοτικοποίηση πρέπει να στηρίζεται σε επαληθεύσιμα δεδομένα."],["Σε σύνθετη πώληση ο συνομιλητής απαντά πάντα γρήγορα, αλλά δεν μπορεί να φέρει άλλους αρμοδίους ή να εξηγήσει τη διαδικασία απόφασης. Πώς τον αξιολογείς;","Ως χρήσιμη επαφή, με ακόμη ανεπιβεβαίωτη δυνατότητα να λειτουργήσει ως εσωτερικός υποστηρικτής της απόφασης.","Ως ισχυρό champion, επειδή η ταχύτητα απάντησης αποδεικνύει επιρροή.","Ως οικονομικό αγοραστή, επειδή διαθέτει χρόνο για συζήτηση.","Ως ακατάλληλη επαφή που πρέπει να διαγραφεί άμεσα.","Η καλή σχέση δεν αποδεικνύει εσωτερική επιρροή. Εξετάζουμε πράξεις, πρόσβαση και γνώση της διαδικασίας. Γενικές σημειώσεις: B2B και χαρτογράφηση εμπλεκομένων."],["Έχεις δύο συμβατές λύσεις και ο πελάτης καθυστερεί από φόβο λανθασμένης επιλογής. Ποια παρέμβαση βοηθά περισσότερο;","Συγκρίνω τις δύο σε συμφωνημένα κριτήρια, εξηγώ το σκεπτικό μιας σύστασης και προτείνω ελεγχόμενο επόμενο βήμα.","Προσθέτω άλλες πέντε λύσεις ώστε να αισθανθεί πλήρη ελευθερία.","Προσφέρω έκπτωση χωρίς να συζητήσω τον φόβο της απόφασης.","Παρουσιάζω τον φόβο ως απόδειξη ότι δεν έχει πραγματική ανάγκη.","Η αβεβαιότητα επιλογής μειώνεται με σαφήνεια και διαχείριση κινδύνου, όχι κατ’ ανάγκη με περισσότερες επιλογές. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Buyer Indecision."]],"source_note":"Πηγή: ΜΑΘΗΜΑ 31.docx, κεφάλαιο 51. Διατηρείται το κείμενο των αριθμημένων σημείων, με ενοποίηση των σπασμένων γραμμών και αφαίρεση επαναλαμβανόμενης μορφοποίησης. Τα παραδείγματα δεν αλλάζουν τους κανόνες της εφαρμογής."},"di-enterprise-52":{"pillar":"distillogic","title":"52. Αντιρρήσεις και δύσκολες συζητήσεις","goal":"Να αναγνωρίζεις πραγματικές ανάγκες, να διερευνάς τα στοιχεία και να επιλέγεις υπεύθυνο επόμενο βήμα.","sections":[["Από την έννοια στην επαγγελματική πράξη",["Μετά την παρουσίαση ο πελάτης λέει «είστε ακριβοί», ενώ δεν έχει γίνει σύγκριση αντικειμένου, κινδύνου ή χρόνου υλοποίησης.","Στη μελέτη που ακολουθεί σύνδεσε κάθε πιθανή λύση με συγκεκριμένη διαδικασία, υπεύθυνο, επίπτωση και στοιχεία που μπορούν να επαληθευτούν. Η τεχνική δυνατότητα, η οικονομική αξία και η εξουσιοδότηση για απόφαση είναι διαφορετικά ερωτήματα. Τα παραδείγματα του κεφαλαίου σε βοηθούν να τα διερευνάς χωρίς να υπόσχεσαι κάτι που δεν έχει εγκριθεί.","Η ύλη περιγράφει ενδεικτικές επιχειρηματικές ανάγκες και μεθόδους πώλησης. Δεν αποτελεί κατάλογο έτοιμων λειτουργιών των δύο CRM, δεσμευτική προσφορά, αλλαγή αμοιβών ή νέα πολιτική πιστοποίησης. Για πραγματική εργασία ισχύουν οι εγκεκριμένοι εταιρικοί όροι και οι αρμοδιότητες. Το μάθημα 60 είναι προετοιμασία, όχι δεύτερη επίσημη τελική εξέταση."]],["Το αντικείμενο του κεφαλαίου",["ΑΝΤΙΡΡΗΣΕΙΣ, ΔΥΣΚΟΛΕΣ ΣΥΖΗΤΗΣΕΙΣ ΚΑΙ ΠΩΣ ΤΙΣ ΧΕΙΡΙΖΟΜΑΣΤΕ Πώς απαντάμε χωρίς πίεση, χωρίς άμυνα και χωρίς να χαρίζουμε αξία"]],["Σημεία 1–25 · Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ",[{"heading":"1. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ","paragraphs":["Objection: δεν σημαίνει πάντα: «Όχι.» Μπορεί να σημαίνει: «Δεν καταλαβαίνω ακόμα.» ή: «Δεν σε εμπιστεύομαι ακόμα.» ή: «Δεν βλέπω αρκετή αξία.» ή: «Δεν έχω priority.» ή: «Θέλω καλύτερους όρους.» ή: «Δεν έχω εσωτερική υποστήριξη.»"]},{"heading":"2. Ο ΚΑΚΟΣ ΠΩΛΗΤΗΣ","paragraphs":["ακούει: «Είστε ακριβοί.» και απαντά: «Μπορούμε να κάνουμε έκπτωση.»"]},{"heading":"3. Ο ΚΑΛΟΣ ΠΩΛΗΤΗΣ","paragraphs":["ρωτά: «Σε σχέση με ποιο benchmark ή ποια εναλλακτική σας φαίνεται υψηλό το κόστος;»"]},{"heading":"4. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΔΟΜΗ","paragraphs":["Όταν υπάρχει objection: ΑΚΟΥ ↓ ΜΗΝ ΑΜΥΝΘΕΙΣ ↓ ΔΙΕΥΚΡΙΝΙΣΕ ↓ ΒΡΕΣ ΤΟ ΠΡΑΓΜΑΤΙΚΟ ΘΕΜΑ ↓ ΑΠΑΝΤΗΣΕ ↓ ΕΛΕΓΞΕ ΑΝ ΛΥΘΗΚΕ."]},{"heading":"5. ΜΗΝ ΚΑΝΕΙΣ","paragraphs":["instant rebuttal."]},{"heading":"6. ΟΧΙ","paragraphs":["«Ναι αλλά...»"]},{"heading":"7. ΚΑΛΥΤΕΡΑ","paragraphs":["«Καταλαβαίνω. Τι ακριβώς σας προβληματίζει περισσότερο;»"]},{"heading":"8. ΣΤΟ ENTERPRISE","paragraphs":["μία objection: συχνά έχει: άλλη objection: από πίσω."]},{"heading":"9. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«Είστε ακριβοί.»"]},{"heading":"10. ΠΙΘΑΝΗ ΠΡΑΓΜΑΤΙΚΗ ΕΝΝΟΙΑ","paragraphs":["budget too low, competitor cheaper, value not clear, procurement pressure, scope too big."]},{"heading":"11. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«Δεν έχουμε budget.»"]},{"heading":"12. ΜΠΟΡΕΙ ΝΑ ΣΗΜΑΙΝΕΙ","paragraphs":["όχι φέτος, όχι για αυτό, δεν είναι priority, budget υπάρχει αλλού, δεν έχει χτιστεί business case."]},{"heading":"13. ΠΡΩΤΟΣ ΚΑΝΟΝΑΣ","paragraphs":["ΜΗΝ ΠΡΟΣΠΑΘΕΙΣ ΝΑ ΚΕΡΔΙΣΕΙΣ ΤΗΝ ΕΝΣΤΑΣΗ. Προσπάθησε: να καταλάβεις: την ένσταση."]},{"heading":"14. OBJECTION #1","paragraphs":["«ΕΙΣΤΕ ΑΚΡΙΒΟΙ.»"]},{"heading":"15. BAD RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Μπορούμε να κατεβάσουμε την τιμή.»"]},{"heading":"16. BETTER RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Σε σχέση με ποια επιλογή ή ποιο budget expectation σας φαίνεται υψηλό;»"]},{"heading":"17. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["«Είναι το total investment που σας προβληματίζει ή το value που πιστεύετε ότι παίρνετε για αυτό το ποσό;»"]},{"heading":"18. WHY?","paragraphs":["Need know: price problem or: value problem."]},{"heading":"19. IF CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«Competitor is 20% cheaper.»"]},{"heading":"20. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Let's compare the scope, integrations, support, delivery responsibility and assumptions side by side. Which part of their proposal is stronger for you commercially;»"]},{"heading":"21. DON'T ATTACK COMPETITOR","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"22. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Δεν ξέρουν τι κάνουν.»"]},{"heading":"23. IF SCOPE SAME","paragraphs":["then discuss: commercial trade-offs."]},{"heading":"24. GIVE / GET","paragraphs":["«If price needs to move, let's look at what we can adjust together — scope, payment terms, rollout sequence or support model.»"]},{"heading":"25. NEVER","paragraphs":["give concession: for nothing."]}]],["Σημεία 26–50 · OBJECTION #2",[{"heading":"26. OBJECTION #2","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΕΧΟΥΜΕ BUDGET.»"]},{"heading":"27. BAD RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Μπορούμε να το κάνουμε φθηνότερα.»"]},{"heading":"28. BETTER","paragraphs":["«Είναι θέμα ότι δεν υπάρχει διαθέσιμο budget αυτή την περίοδο ή ότι το project δεν έχει ακόμα αρκετά υψηλή priority για να χρηματοδοτηθεί;»"]},{"heading":"29. GREAT QUESTION","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"30. IF NO BUDGET THIS YEAR","paragraphs":["ask: «When is the next budgeting window and what would need to be ready before then?»"]},{"heading":"31. IF NOT PRIORITY","paragraphs":["requalify."]},{"heading":"32. DON'T CREATE","paragraphs":["fake urgency."]},{"heading":"33. IF PAIN STRONG","paragraphs":["build: business case."]},{"heading":"34. OBJECTION #3","paragraphs":["«ΣΤΕΙΛΤΕ ΜΑΣ ΜΙΑ ΠΡΟΣΦΟΡΑ.»"]},{"heading":"35. Often sounds good.","paragraphs":["But can be dangerous."]},{"heading":"36. ASK","paragraphs":["«Βεβαίως. Για να μην σας στείλω generic proposal, θα ήθελα πρώτα να επιβεβαιώσω scope, users, integrations, success criteria and decision process.»"]},{"heading":"37. IF THEY REFUSE DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["red flag."]},{"heading":"38. POSSIBLE RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Μπορώ να στείλω ένα indicative range and approach, αλλά θα το χαρακτηρίσω ως preliminary μέχρι να επιβεβαιώσουμε scope.»"]},{"heading":"39. GOOD","paragraphs":["honest boundary."]},{"heading":"40. OBJECTION #4","paragraphs":["«ΣΤΕΙΛΤΕ ΜΟΥ EMAIL.»"]},{"heading":"41. Could mean:","paragraphs":["polite exit."]},{"heading":"42. DON'T SEND","paragraphs":["30 pages."]},{"heading":"43. ASK","paragraphs":["«Βεβαίως. Ποιο από τα θέματα που συζητήσαμε θα ήταν πιο χρήσιμο να καλύψω ώστε να σας στείλω κάτι σχετικό και όχι γενικό υλικό;»"]},{"heading":"44. GREAT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"45. Then send:","paragraphs":["short, relevant, specific."]},{"heading":"46. OBJECTION #5","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΕΧΩ ΧΡΟΝΟ.»"]},{"heading":"47. BAD","paragraphs":["«Θα σας πάρω μόνο 5 λεπτά.»"]},{"heading":"48. BETTER","paragraphs":["«Το καταλαβαίνω. Υπάρχει κάποιο συγκεκριμένο θέμα που θα άξιζε να συζητήσουμε σε άλλη στιγμή ή απλώς δεν είναι priority τώρα;»"]},{"heading":"49. This distinguishes:","paragraphs":["time from: interest."]},{"heading":"50. OBJECTION #6","paragraphs":["«ΚΑΛΕΣΤΕ ΜΕ ΤΟΥ ΧΡΟΝΟΥ.»"]}]],["Σημεία 51–75 · DON'T SAY",[{"heading":"51. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«ΟΚ.» and disappear."]},{"heading":"52. ASK","paragraphs":["«Τι αλλάζει τότε; Budget cycle, project timing, contract expiry ή άλλη priority;»"]},{"heading":"53. Need:","paragraphs":["future trigger."]},{"heading":"54. Then CRM:","paragraphs":["specific follow-up."]},{"heading":"55. GOOD NEXT STEP","paragraphs":["«Let's reconnect in January, after budget approval, and review whether the initiative has moved forward.»"]},{"heading":"56. OBJECTION #7","paragraphs":["«ΕΧΟΥΜΕ ΗΔΗ ΠΡΟΜΗΘΕΥΤΗ.»"]},{"heading":"57. BAD","paragraphs":["«Είμαστε καλύτεροι.»"]},{"heading":"58. BETTER","paragraphs":["«Αν ο υπάρχων supplier καλύπτει το need καλά, δεν υπάρχει λόγος να αλλάξετε. Υπάρχει κάποιο gap που εξακολουθεί να μένει unresolved;»"]},{"heading":"59. VERY STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"60. Why?","paragraphs":["Shows: confidence, not desperation."]},{"heading":"61. FOLLOW-UP","paragraphs":["«Σε ποια areas χρησιμοποιείτε τον supplier και πού χρειάζεστε additional capability or capacity;»"]},{"heading":"62. OPPORTUNITY MAY BE","paragraphs":["not replacement. Could be: complementary service."]},{"heading":"63. OBJECTION #8","paragraphs":["«ΕΙΜΑΣΤΕ ΙΚΑΝΟΠΟΙΗΜΕΝΟΙ ΜΕ ΤΟ ΥΠΑΡΧΟΝ SYSTEM.»"]},{"heading":"64. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Τότε δεν θα πρότεινα replacement. Υπάρχει κάποια process γύρω από το system που εξακολουθεί να χρειάζεται manual work, integration or reporting;»"]},{"heading":"65. If no meaningful pain:","paragraphs":["leave."]},{"heading":"66. GOOD SALES","paragraphs":["can say: «Then perhaps there isn't a project here right now.»"]},{"heading":"67. OBJECTION #9","paragraphs":["«ΤΟ ΦΤΙΑΧΝΟΥΜΕ ΕΣΩΤΕΡΙΚΑ.»"]},{"heading":"68. Don't attack internal team.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"69. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«That may absolutely be the right choice. Is the main constraint internal capacity, specialist skills, delivery speed, or do you already have everything needed in-house;»"]},{"heading":"70. POSSIBILITY","paragraphs":["Distillogic can: augment team."]},{"heading":"71. OR","paragraphs":["not needed."]},{"heading":"72. OBJECTION #10","paragraphs":["«ΘΑ ΤΟ ΚΑΝΕΙ ΤΟ IT ΜΑΣ.»"]},{"heading":"73. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Τότε ίσως το σωστό question είναι αν they need external capacity or specialist support, not a replacement supplier. Where does the internal team feel constrained today, if anywhere;»"]},{"heading":"74. OBJECTION #11","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΕΜΠΙΣΤΕΥΟΜΑΣΤΕ ΝΕΑ ΕΤΑΙΡΕΙΑ.»"]},{"heading":"75. Very important for Distillogic.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 76–100 · NEVER FAKE",[{"heading":"76. NEVER FAKE","paragraphs":["customers, team size, certifications, references."]},{"heading":"77. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Είναι απολύτως λογικό σε enterprise project. Δεν θα σας ζητούσα να βασιστείτε σε claims. Μπορούμε να μειώσουμε το ρίσκο με σαφές scope, τεχνική αξιολόγηση, συγκεκριμένα acceptance criteria, μικρό αρχικό pilot και διαφάνεια για το ποιοι θα παραδώσουν το έργο.»"]},{"heading":"78. GREAT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"79. TRUST IS BUILT WITH","paragraphs":["Transparency Process Technical competence Clear commitments Evidence."]},{"heading":"80. NOT","paragraphs":["fake size."]},{"heading":"81. OBJECTION #12","paragraphs":["«ΠΟΣΑ ΑΤΟΜΑ ΕΧΕΤΕ;»"]},{"heading":"82. Important.","paragraphs":["If delivery team: project-based: say truth."]},{"heading":"83. RESPONSE EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["«We operate with a core structure and build the delivery team according to project requirements. Για το συγκεκριμένο έργο θα σας παρουσιάσουμε ακριβώς ποιοι roles and seniority levels θα αναλάβουν, πριν υπάρξει commitment.»"]},{"heading":"84. DO NOT SAY","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε 100 developers.» if not true."]},{"heading":"85. OBJECTION #13","paragraphs":["«ΜΕ ΠΟΙΟΥΣ ΜΕΓΑΛΟΥΣ ΠΕΛΑΤΕΣ ΕΧΕΤΕ ΔΟΥΛΕΨΕΙ;»"]},{"heading":"86. If you have:","paragraphs":["approved references: use them."]},{"heading":"87. If not:","paragraphs":["don't invent."]},{"heading":"88. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Δεν θέλω να σας παρουσιάσω reference που δεν είναι σχετικό ή εγκεκριμένο. Αυτό που μπορώ να κάνω είναι να σας δείξω τον delivery approach, τα relevant capabilities της ομάδας και να validateάρουμε σε μικρό scope ότι μπορούμε να καλύψουμε το requirement.»"]},{"heading":"89. TRUST > EXAGGERATION","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"90. OBJECTION #14","paragraphs":["«ΕΧΕΤΕ ΞΑΝΑΚΑΝΕΙ ΑΚΡΙΒΩΣ ΑΥΤΟ;»"]},{"heading":"91. If no:","paragraphs":["say no."]},{"heading":"92. But distinguish:","paragraphs":["exact use case from: relevant transferable capability."]},{"heading":"93. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Όχι ακριβώς το ίδιο configuration. Έχουμε όμως relevant capability σε X, Y and Z. Πριν δεσμευτούμε, θα θέλαμε να validate the project-specific requirements with our technical team.»"]},{"heading":"94. PROFESSIONAL","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"95. OBJECTION #15","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ ΕΓΓΥΗΣΗ ΟΤΙ ΘΑ ΔΟΥΛΕΨΕΙ.»"]},{"heading":"96. BAD","paragraphs":["«Το εγγυόμαστε 100%.»"]},{"heading":"97. BETTER","paragraphs":["«Μπορούμε να συμφωνήσουμε clear acceptance criteria, testing, responsibilities and remediation process. Δεν θα ήταν υπεύθυνο να δώσω absolute guarantee πριν validateάρουμε το environment and dependencies.»"]},{"heading":"98. OBJECTION #16","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ FIXED PRICE.»"]},{"heading":"99. Fine:","paragraphs":["if scope: clear."]},{"heading":"100. Response:","paragraphs":["«Fixed price is possible when scope, assumptions and acceptance criteria are sufficiently defined. If important unknowns remain, we may first need a discovery phase so neither side prices uncertainty blindly.»"]}]],["Σημεία 101–125 · KEY RULE",[{"heading":"101. KEY RULE","paragraphs":["FIXED PRICE + UNCLEAR SCOPE = RISK."]},{"heading":"102. OBJECTION #17","paragraphs":["«ΔΩΣΤΕ ΜΟΥ ΤΙΜΗ ΤΩΡΑ.»"]},{"heading":"103. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Μπορώ να σας δώσω indicative range, but a responsible final price depends mainly on workflows, integrations, users, non-functional requirements and support. I'd rather be accurate than give a misleading number.»"]},{"heading":"104. OBJECTION #18","paragraphs":["«Ο ΑΝΤΑΓΩΝΙΣΤΗΣ ΜΟΥ ΕΔΩΣΕ FIXED PRICE ΧΩΡΙΣ DISCOVERY.»"]},{"heading":"105. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«That's a commercial choice they have made. For us, where material unknowns affect effort or risk, we prefer to make assumptions explicit rather than hide uncertainty in the contract.»"]},{"heading":"106. DON'T CALL THEM","paragraphs":["reckless."]},{"heading":"107. OBJECTION #19","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ ΝΑ ΤΟ ΕΧΩ ΣΕ 6 ΕΒΔΟΜΑΔΕΣ.»"]},{"heading":"108. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«We need to validate scope and dependencies before committing. What business event makes six weeks important?»"]},{"heading":"109. WHY?","paragraphs":["Need know: real deadline."]},{"heading":"110. IF REAL","paragraphs":["work backwards."]},{"heading":"111. POSSIBLE OPTIONS","paragraphs":["Smaller MVP Reduced integrations Phased rollout."]},{"heading":"112. DON'T SAY YES","paragraphs":["before validation."]},{"heading":"113. OBJECTION #20","paragraphs":["«Ο ΑΝΤΑΓΩΝΙΣΤΗΣ ΛΕΕΙ ΟΤΙ ΤΟ ΚΑΝΕΙ ΣΕ 4 ΕΒΔΟΜΑΔΕΣ.»"]},{"heading":"114. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«They may be assuming a different scope or starting point. Let's compare what “done” means in each proposal: integrations, migration, testing, security and production readiness.»"]},{"heading":"115. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["compare: definition of done."]},{"heading":"116. OBJECTION #21","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΜΠΟΡΟΥΜΕ ΝΑ ΔΩΣΟΥΜΕ ΠΡΟΣΒΑΣΗ ΣΤΑ SYSTEMS ΜΑΣ.»"]},{"heading":"117. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Then technical design has to work within that constraint. We should understand what approved interfaces, test environments, exports or controlled access models are possible before proposing architecture.»"]},{"heading":"118. DON'T PUSH","paragraphs":["security controls aside."]},{"heading":"119. OBJECTION #22","paragraphs":["«SECURITY ΔΕΝ ΘΑ ΤΟ ΕΓΚΡΙΝΕΙ.»"]},{"heading":"120. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Then Security needs to be part of the process early. Which specific requirements or architecture concerns do you expect will be blockers;»"]},{"heading":"121. GOOD","paragraphs":["bring blocker into room."]},{"heading":"122. OBJECTION #23","paragraphs":["«LEGAL ΘΑ ΜΑΣ ΚΑΘΥΣΤΕΡΗΣΕΙ.»"]},{"heading":"123. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Let's identify the likely legal topics now — data processing, IP, liability, subcontractors, terms — so they don't appear for the first time at the end.»"]},{"heading":"124. EARLY LEGAL","paragraphs":["reduces surprises."]},{"heading":"125. OBJECTION #24","paragraphs":["«PROCUREMENT ΘΑ ΖΗΤΗΣΕΙ ΜΕΓΑΛΗ ΕΚΠΤΩΣΗ.»"]}]],["Σημεία 126–150 · RESPONSE",[{"heading":"126. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Then let's align the value, scope and negotiable variables before procurement so commercial trade-offs are deliberate rather than reactive.»"]},{"heading":"127. OBJECTION #25","paragraphs":["«PROCUREMENT ΛΕΕΙ 20% ΚΑΤΩ.»"]},{"heading":"128. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«To move 20%, we'd need to adjust something material. We can look at scope, payment terms, service level or rollout. Which of those can move on your side;»"]},{"heading":"129. GIVE / GET","paragraphs":["always."]},{"heading":"130. OBJECTION #26","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΑΛΛΑΖΟΥΜΕ ΤΟΥΣ PAYMENT TERMS.»"]},{"heading":"131. Response:","paragraphs":["«Understood. Then payment terms may be non-negotiable. Let's identify which other commercial variables remain flexible so the overall deal stays workable.»"]},{"heading":"132. NEGOTIATION IS PACKAGE","paragraphs":["not: one issue."]},{"heading":"133. OBJECTION #27","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ 90 DAYS PAYMENT.»"]},{"heading":"134. Need assess:","paragraphs":["cash impact."]},{"heading":"135. Don't immediately accept.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"136. Possible response:","paragraphs":["«We can review that, but longer payment terms affect the commercial model. If 90 days is mandatory, let's consider milestone structure or pricing impact.»"]},{"heading":"137. OBJECTION #28","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ UNLIMITED SUPPORT.»"]},{"heading":"138. Response:","paragraphs":["«Let's define what support means in practical terms — hours, channels, severity, response targets, scope — because unlimited without boundaries is difficult for both sides to manage.»"]},{"heading":"139. OBJECTION #29","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ 24/7 SUPPORT.»"]},{"heading":"140. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which incidents genuinely require 24/7 response and what severity model do you use;»"]},{"heading":"141. Maybe only:","paragraphs":["P1 incidents."]},{"heading":"142. Don't oversell:","paragraphs":["24/7."]},{"heading":"143. OBJECTION #30","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ SLA 99.99%.»"]},{"heading":"144. Sales should not agree alone.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"145. Response:","paragraphs":["«That level needs architecture, hosting and support validation. Let's have technical team assess whether it is appropriate and what design/cost it implies.»"]},{"heading":"146. OBJECTION #31","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΟΛΟ ΤΟ SOURCE CODE.»"]},{"heading":"147. Need discuss:","paragraphs":["IP, escrow, ownership, custom work."]},{"heading":"148. Response:","paragraphs":["«Let's separate pre-existing IP, project-specific code and third-party components so ownership rights are clear and commercially fair.»"]},{"heading":"149. DON'T IMPROVISE","paragraphs":["legal terms."]},{"heading":"150. OBJECTION #32","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΟΛΟ ΤΟ IP ΝΑ ΕΙΝΑΙ ΔΙΚΟ ΜΑΣ.»"]}]],["Σημεία 151–175 · Response:",[{"heading":"151. Response:","paragraphs":["«We need to distinguish customer-specific deliverables from reusable pre-existing frameworks or components. Legal and commercial teams should define that explicitly.»"]},{"heading":"152. OBJECTION #33","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ SUBCONTRACTORS.»"]},{"heading":"153. If project model may use them:","paragraphs":["be transparent."]},{"heading":"154. Response:","paragraphs":["«Understood. We should clarify whether the restriction is absolute or related to specific data/access responsibilities, because delivery model needs to comply with that from the start.»"]},{"heading":"155. DON'T HIDE","paragraphs":["subcontracting."]},{"heading":"156. OBJECTION #34","paragraphs":["«ΟΛΗ Η ΟΜΑΔΑ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΕΙΝΑΙ ΣΤΗΝ ΕΛΛΑΔΑ.»"]},{"heading":"157. If can:","paragraphs":["validate."]},{"heading":"158. If not:","paragraphs":["say."]},{"heading":"159. Don't promise:","paragraphs":["staffing: not secured."]},{"heading":"160. OBJECTION #35","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ ΤΑ CVs ΤΗΣ ΟΜΑΔΑΣ.»"]},{"heading":"161. Response:","paragraphs":["«Yes. We'll provide the proposed roles and relevant profiles for the actual delivery team. We prefer to present people tied to the real project rather than generic profiles that may not be available.»"]},{"heading":"162. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Don't send: random CVs."]},{"heading":"163. OBJECTION #36","paragraphs":["«ΜΠΟΡΕΙΤΕ ΝΑ ΞΕΚΙΝΗΣΕΤΕ ΔΕΥΤΕΡΑ;»"]},{"heading":"164. Sales:","paragraphs":["must confirm: delivery availability."]},{"heading":"165. Response:","paragraphs":["«I need to confirm the required roles and availability before committing to Monday. I'd rather confirm accurately than promise and change it later.»"]},{"heading":"166. OBJECTION #37","paragraphs":["«ΜΠΟΡΕΙΤΕ ΝΑ ΒΑΛΕΤΕ 10 DEVELOPERS;»"]},{"heading":"167. Ask:","paragraphs":["why 10?"]},{"heading":"168. Customer may assume:","paragraphs":["more people = faster."]},{"heading":"169. Response:","paragraphs":["«Possibly, but team size should follow architecture, workstream parallelism and coordination needs. More people doesn't always shorten delivery.»"]},{"heading":"170. OBJECTION #38","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ DISCOVERY, ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΝΑ ΞΕΚΙΝΗΣΟΥΜΕ.»"]},{"heading":"171. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can keep discovery focused, but removing it entirely increases scope and delivery risk. We at least need to validate the critical workflows, integrations and acceptance criteria before build starts.»"]},{"heading":"172. OBJECTION #39","paragraphs":["«ΞΕΡΟΥΜΕ ΑΚΡΙΒΩΣ ΤΙ ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ.»"]},{"heading":"173. Great.","paragraphs":["Still validate."]},{"heading":"174. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Excellent. Can we walk through the requirements and acceptance criteria together so technical delivery can confirm assumptions and dependencies?»"]},{"heading":"175. OBJECTION #40","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ ΝΑ ΚΑΝΕΤΕ ΑΚΡΙΒΩΣ Ο,ΤΙ ΣΑΣ ΛΕΜΕ.»"]}]],["Σημεία 176–200 · Sometimes okay.",[{"heading":"176. Sometimes okay.","paragraphs":["But professional supplier: should flag risks."]},{"heading":"177. Response:","paragraphs":["«We'll follow agreed requirements, and where our team sees a material technical, security or usability risk, we'll surface it clearly rather than silently implement something we believe may fail.»"]},{"heading":"178. OBJECTION #41","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΩ ΝΑ ΑΚΟΥΣΩ ΤΕΧΝΙΚΑ.»"]},{"heading":"179. CEO/CFO perhaps.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"180. Response:","paragraphs":["«Understood. Let's stay at business outcome, investment, risk and timeline. Our technical teams can handle the implementation detail separately.»"]},{"heading":"181. ADAPT LANGUAGE","paragraphs":["to role."]},{"heading":"182. OBJECTION #42","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΩ ΝΑ ΑΚΟΥΣΩ BUSINESS, ΠΕΣ ΜΟΥ ARCHITECTURE.»"]},{"heading":"183. CIO/CTO.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"184. Sales should:","paragraphs":["bring technical lead."]},{"heading":"185. Response:","paragraphs":["«Absolutely. I'll bring our technical lead so we can discuss architecture at the right depth and avoid giving you superficial answers.»"]},{"heading":"186. OBJECTION #43","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ DEMO.»"]},{"heading":"187. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which workflow or capability would be most valuable to see so the demo answers a real question for you;»"]},{"heading":"188. Avoid:","paragraphs":["generic feature tour."]},{"heading":"189. OBJECTION #44","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΕΧΕΤΕ ΕΤΟΙΜΟ PRODUCT;»"]},{"heading":"190. For custom software company:","paragraphs":["this matters."]},{"heading":"191. Response:","paragraphs":["«Our model is custom technology delivery rather than forcing a generic product onto every process. The trade-off is that we need to understand the requirement properly before proposing scope.»"]},{"heading":"192. If off-the-shelf product is better:","paragraphs":["say so."]},{"heading":"193. GOOD SELLER CAN SAY","paragraphs":["«A standard product may be more appropriate here.»"]},{"heading":"194. OBJECTION #45","paragraphs":["«ΓΙΑΤΙ ΝΑ ΜΗΝ ΠΑΡΟΥΜΕ SAAS;»"]},{"heading":"195. Response:","paragraphs":["«You should, if a SaaS product covers the requirements with acceptable fit, cost and integration effort. Custom development makes sense when the process or integration needs create material gaps in standard solutions.»"]},{"heading":"196. EXCELLENT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"197. OBJECTION #46","paragraphs":["«ΓΙΑΤΙ ΝΑ ΜΗΝ ΠΑΡΟΥΜΕ MICROSOFT / SAP / SALESFORCE;»"]},{"heading":"198. Don't attack.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"199. Response:","paragraphs":["«You should evaluate them if they fit. Our role may be custom integration, extension or a separate workflow where large platforms don't cover the requirement economically or cleanly.»"]},{"heading":"200. OBJECTION #47","paragraphs":["«ΜΠΟΡΕΙΤΕ ΝΑ ΚΑΝΕΤΕ COPY ΑΥΤΟ ΤΟ SYSTEM;»"]}]],["Σημεία 201–225 · Ask:",[{"heading":"201. Ask:","paragraphs":["what exactly they value."]},{"heading":"202. Don't promise:","paragraphs":["copying proprietary system."]},{"heading":"203. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can understand the workflows and outcomes you value and design a lawful solution around your requirements. We wouldn't copy proprietary code or protected assets.»"]},{"heading":"204. OBJECTION #48","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ ΝΑ ΕΙΝΑΙ ΑΚΡΙΒΩΣ ΣΑΝ ΤΟΝ ΑΝΤΑΓΩΝΙΣΤΗ.»"]},{"heading":"205. Response:","paragraphs":["«Let's identify the specific capabilities and user journeys you want, rather than copying the whole product. That usually reveals what you actually need and avoids unnecessary scope.»"]},{"heading":"206. OBJECTION #49","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ AI.»"]},{"heading":"207. Response:","paragraphs":["«Which business decision or manual task do you want AI to improve?»"]},{"heading":"208. THE BEST FIRST QUESTION","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"209. OBJECTION #50","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ CHATBOT.»"]},{"heading":"210. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What questions should it answer, where will it get verified information and when should it escalate to a human;»"]},{"heading":"211. OBJECTION #51","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ AI AGENT ΝΑ ΚΑΝΕΙ ΤΑ ΠΑΝΤΑ.»"]},{"heading":"212. Response:","paragraphs":["«We should break “everything” into specific tasks, permissions, systems and risk levels. Some actions may be appropriate for automation; others may require approval or human review.»"]},{"heading":"213. OBJECTION #52","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ AI ΝΑ ΠΑΙΡΝΕΙ ΑΠΟΦΑΣΕΙΣ ΜΟΝΟ ΤΟΥ.»"]},{"heading":"214. Ask:","paragraphs":["what decisions?"]},{"heading":"215. High-risk if:","paragraphs":["finance, health, HR, compliance, public eligibility."]},{"heading":"216. Response:","paragraphs":["«We need to distinguish low-risk operational decisions from decisions affecting people, money, rights or safety. The latter need much stronger governance and often human oversight.»"]},{"heading":"217. OBJECTION #53","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΩ HUMAN REVIEW.»"]},{"heading":"218. If inappropriate:","paragraphs":["do not promise."]},{"heading":"219. Response:","paragraphs":["«For some low-risk tasks that may be possible. For higher-risk decisions, removing human oversight may create unacceptable operational or governance risk, so we'd need to evaluate that carefully.»"]},{"heading":"220. OBJECTION #54","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ ΝΑ ΜΟΥ ΠΕΙΤΕ ΤΙ ROI ΘΑ ΕΧΩ.»"]},{"heading":"221. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can calculate it, but from your baseline. We need current volume, time, cost, rework and expected improvement. I don't want to give you generic ROI.»"]},{"heading":"222. OBJECTION #55","paragraphs":["«ΑΝ ΔΕΝ ΜΠΟΡΕΙΤΕ ΝΑ ΜΟΥ ΠΕΙΤΕ ROI ΤΩΡΑ, ΔΕΝ ΞΕΡΕΤΕ ΤΙ ΠΟΥΛΑΤΕ.»"]},{"heading":"223. Response:","paragraphs":["«I can explain where value typically comes from. But an ROI number without your baseline would be an assumption presented as fact, and I don't think that would help your decision.»"]},{"heading":"224. STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"225. OBJECTION #56","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΕΧΟΥΜΕ ΠΡΟΒΛΗΜΑ.»"]}]],["Σημεία 226–250 · Then maybe:",[{"heading":"226. Then maybe:","paragraphs":["no deal."]},{"heading":"227. Ask once:","paragraphs":["«Understood. Is there any upcoming change — growth, new system, acquisition, compliance requirement — that may create pressure later;»"]},{"heading":"228. If no:","paragraphs":["leave professionally."]},{"heading":"229. DON'T MANUFACTURE PAIN","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"230. OBJECTION #57","paragraphs":["«ΑΥΤΟ ΔΕΝ ΕΙΝΑΙ PRIORITY.»"]},{"heading":"231. Response:","paragraphs":["«Understood. What is taking priority instead, and is there a specific event that might move this higher later;»"]},{"heading":"232. Requalify.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"233. OBJECTION #58","paragraphs":["«ΘΑ ΤΟ ΔΟΥΜΕ ΑΡΓΟΤΕΡΑ.»"]},{"heading":"234. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What would need to change for it to become actionable;»"]},{"heading":"235. If vague:","paragraphs":["likely weak opportunity."]},{"heading":"236. OBJECTION #59","paragraphs":["«ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΤΟ ΣΥΖΗΤΗΣΩ ΕΣΩΤΕΡΙΚΑ.»"]},{"heading":"237. Good.","paragraphs":["Ask: «Who else needs to be comfortable with it and what questions do you expect them to ask;»"]},{"heading":"238. Champion enablement.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"239. OBJECTION #60","paragraphs":["«Ο CEO ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΤΟ ΔΕΙ.»"]},{"heading":"240. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What will the CEO care about most — strategic impact, financial case, risk, timing;»"]},{"heading":"241. Prepare:","paragraphs":["executive version."]},{"heading":"242. OBJECTION #61","paragraphs":["«Ο CIO ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΕΙ ΑΛΛΟ SYSTEM.»"]},{"heading":"243. Response:","paragraphs":["«Then we shouldn't position this as another isolated system. We need to understand whether the use case can be solved through existing platforms, extensions or integration before proposing new architecture.»"]},{"heading":"244. OBJECTION #62","paragraphs":["«OPERATIONS ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΕΙ ΑΛΛΑΓΕΣ.»"]},{"heading":"245. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What disruption are they concerned about — training, downtime, workload, or losing an existing process that works;»"]},{"heading":"246. Resistance usually has reason.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"247. OBJECTION #63","paragraphs":["«ΟΙ ΧΡΗΣΤΕΣ ΔΕΝ ΘΑ ΤΟ ΧΡΗΣΙΜΟΠΟΙΗΣΟΥΝ.»"]},{"heading":"248. Response:","paragraphs":["«Then adoption must be treated as a core requirement, not a training issue at the end. We should involve representative users and identify what current work the solution removes.»"]},{"heading":"249. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["More features: does not mean: more adoption."]},{"heading":"250. OBJECTION #64","paragraphs":["«ΟΙ ΥΠΑΛΛΗΛΟΙ ΜΑΣ ΔΕΝ ΕΙΝΑΙ ΤΕΧΝΙΚΟΙ.»"]}]],["Σημεία 251–275 · Response:",[{"heading":"251. Response:","paragraphs":["«Then the UX and process need to be designed around their actual work. The user shouldn't need technical knowledge to complete a business task.»"]},{"heading":"252. OBJECTION #65","paragraphs":["«ΘΑ ΧΡΕΙΑΣΤΟΥΜΕ ΠΟΛΥ TRAINING.»"]},{"heading":"253. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which workflows feel fundamentally different from current work and which can be made intuitive enough to reduce training dependency;»"]},{"heading":"254. OBJECTION #66","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΜΠΟΡΟΥΜΕ ΝΑ ΣΤΑΜΑΤΗΣΟΥΜΕ ΤΗ ΛΕΙΤΟΥΡΓΙΑ ΓΙΑ MIGRATION.»"]},{"heading":"255. Response:","paragraphs":["«Then migration and cutover need phased planning, parallel operation or other continuity measures. We shouldn't design around an outage your operation cannot accept.»"]},{"heading":"256. OBJECTION #67","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ BIG BANG.»"]},{"heading":"257. Often wise.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"258. Response:","paragraphs":["«Agreed. Let's identify the smallest production scope that proves value while keeping integration and rollback manageable.»"]},{"heading":"259. OBJECTION #68","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ BIG BANG.»"]},{"heading":"260. Ask:","paragraphs":["why."]},{"heading":"261. If risk high:","paragraphs":["challenge respectfully."]},{"heading":"262. Response:","paragraphs":["«It may be possible, but let's compare big-bang risk with phased rollout. If systems, users and dependencies are extensive, phased implementation may protect business continuity.»"]},{"heading":"263. OBJECTION #69","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ POC.»"]},{"heading":"264. Fine.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"265. Maybe need:","paragraphs":["direct implementation."]},{"heading":"266. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which uncertainties are already sufficiently resolved so a PoC isn't needed;»"]},{"heading":"267. POC is not mandatory.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"268. OBJECTION #70","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΔΩΡΕΑΝ POC.»"]},{"heading":"269. Response:","paragraphs":["«That depends on scope and effort. If the PoC requires meaningful engineering, integrations or custom work, it should normally be treated as a defined project rather than open-ended free development.»"]},{"heading":"270. Don't work free:","paragraphs":["without strategy."]},{"heading":"271. OBJECTION #71","paragraphs":["«ΑΝ ΠΙΣΤΕΥΕΤΕ ΣΤΗ ΛΥΣΗ, ΚΑΝΤΕ ΤΟ ΔΩΡΕΑΝ ΚΑΙ ΘΑ ΠΛΗΡΩΣΟΥΜΕ ΑΝ ΔΟΥΛΕΨΕΙ.»"]},{"heading":"272. Response:","paragraphs":["«Confidence in the solution doesn't remove the cost of engineering work or customer dependencies. We can structure success criteria and staged commitment, but delivery effort needs a fair commercial model.»"]},{"heading":"273. OBJECTION #72","paragraphs":["«ΠΛΗΡΩΝΟΥΜΕ ΜΟΝΟ ΑΝ ΕΧΟΥΜΕ RESULT.»"]},{"heading":"274. Need define:","paragraphs":["what result? Who controls it?"]},{"heading":"275. Example:","paragraphs":["software delivered: but business adoption: not."]}]],["Σημεία 276–300 · Response:",[{"heading":"276. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can link payments to deliverables or acceptance criteria we can control. Business outcomes influenced by customer adoption, data quality or market conditions need to be treated differently.»"]},{"heading":"277. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"278. OBJECTION #73","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ PENALTY ΑΝ ΚΑΘΥΣΤΕΡΗΣΕΤΕ.»"]},{"heading":"279. Possible.","paragraphs":["But need: dependency symmetry."]},{"heading":"280. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can discuss delivery commitments, but dependencies and customer responsibilities also need to be explicit so delays are attributed fairly.»"]},{"heading":"281. OBJECTION #74","paragraphs":["«ΕΜΕΙΣ ΔΕΝ ΔΙΝΟΥΜΕ CUSTOMER RESPONSIBILITIES.»"]},{"heading":"282. Explain:","paragraphs":["without inputs/access/decisions: supplier cannot control timeline."]},{"heading":"283. Response:","paragraphs":["«For the schedule to be meaningful, we need to define the inputs, approvals and access required from both sides. Otherwise neither side can manage delivery predictably.»"]},{"heading":"284. OBJECTION #75","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΕΧΟΥΜΕ DATA.»"]},{"heading":"285. If AI/analytics project:","paragraphs":["critical."]},{"heading":"286. Response:","paragraphs":["«Then the first phase may be about data availability and quality rather than the model itself. We should validate what exists before defining expected AI performance.»"]},{"heading":"287. OBJECTION #76","paragraphs":["«ΤΑ DATA ΜΑΣ ΕΙΝΑΙ ΧΑΛΙΑ.»"]},{"heading":"288. Response:","paragraphs":["«Then data quality may be part of the actual business problem. Let's identify which fields or sources materially affect the workflow and avoid trying to clean everything without purpose.»"]},{"heading":"289. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Don't clean all data: just because."]},{"heading":"290. OBJECTION #77","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΞΕΡΟΥΜΕ ΠΟΥ ΕΙΝΑΙ ΤΑ DATA.»"]},{"heading":"291. Potential first project:","paragraphs":["data discovery."]},{"heading":"292. Response:","paragraphs":["«Then before solution design we may need a focused data-mapping phase to identify sources, owners and quality.»"]},{"heading":"293. OBJECTION #78","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΥΠΑΡΧΟΥΝ APIs.»"]},{"heading":"294. Response:","paragraphs":["«Then integration options need technical assessment — exports, database access, middleware, files or vendor interfaces. We shouldn't assume a clean real-time integration.»"]},{"heading":"295. OBJECTION #79","paragraphs":["«ΤΟ VENDOR ΔΕΝ ΜΑΣ ΑΦΗΝΕΙ ΝΑ ΣΥΝΔΕΘΟΥΜΕ.»"]},{"heading":"296. Response:","paragraphs":["«Then vendor restrictions are a real dependency. We need to understand what interfaces or contractual permissions are available before designing around that system.»"]},{"heading":"297. OBJECTION #80","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ REAL TIME.»"]},{"heading":"298. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which decision or customer experience requires real-time rather than minutes or hours;»"]},{"heading":"299. Maybe:","paragraphs":["real-time unnecessary."]},{"heading":"300. OBJECTION #81","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ MOBILE APP.»"]}]],["Σημεία 301–325 · Ask:",[{"heading":"301. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which task becomes materially better on mobile than responsive web or current tools;»"]},{"heading":"302. Don't sell app:","paragraphs":["because app sounds modern."]},{"heading":"303. OBJECTION #82","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ BLOCKCHAIN.»"]},{"heading":"304. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What trust, traceability or multi-party problem are you trying to solve that requires blockchain specifically;»"]},{"heading":"305. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"306. OBJECTION #83","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ CLOUD.»"]},{"heading":"307. Ask:","paragraphs":["why."]},{"heading":"308. Possible:","paragraphs":["scale, speed, corporate strategy."]},{"heading":"309. OBJECTION #84","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ CLOUD.»"]},{"heading":"310. Respect architecture policy.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"311. Response:","paragraphs":["«Then we'll evaluate architecture within your approved hosting and security constraints rather than forcing a cloud-first design.»"]},{"heading":"312. OBJECTION #85","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ON-PREMISE ΓΙΑΤΙ ΕΙΝΑΙ ΠΙΟ ΑΣΦΑΛΕΣ.»"]},{"heading":"313. Don't debate casually.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"314. Response:","paragraphs":["«Security depends on architecture and controls, not only hosting location. Let's have the security/architecture teams define the actual requirements before choosing model.»"]},{"heading":"315. OBJECTION #86","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ OWNERSHIP ΤΩΝ DATA.»"]},{"heading":"316. Usually important.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"317. Clarify:","paragraphs":["data ownership vs: hosting vs: access."]},{"heading":"318. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Let's define ownership, storage, access, retention and deletion separately so there is no ambiguity.»"]},{"heading":"319. OBJECTION #87","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΤΑ DATA ΝΑ ΧΡΗΣΙΜΟΠΟΙΟΥΝΤΑΙ ΓΙΑ AI TRAINING.»"]},{"heading":"320. Response:","paragraphs":["«That requirement should be explicit in architecture and contract. We need to define exactly how customer data are processed and what is or isn't retained or used.»"]},{"heading":"321. OBJECTION #88","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΤΑ DATA ΝΑ ΜΕΙΝΟΥΝ ΣΕ ΣΥΓΚΕΚΡΙΜΕΝΗ ΧΩΡΑ/ΠΕΡΙΟΧΗ.»"]},{"heading":"322. Need technical/legal validation.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"323. Response:","paragraphs":["«We'll need to validate hosting region, subprocessors and data flows before committing to that requirement.»"]},{"heading":"324. OBJECTION #89","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΝΑ ΚΑΝΕΤΕ ΟΛΗ ΤΗΝ ΑΣΦΑΛΕΙΑ.»"]},{"heading":"325. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can own the security responsibilities within our agreed scope, but enterprise security is shared across application, infrastructure, identity, customer environment and operational controls. Responsibilities need to be explicit.»"]}]],["Σημεία 326–350 · OBJECTION #90",[{"heading":"326. OBJECTION #90","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ 100% SECURE.»"]},{"heading":"327. Response:","paragraphs":["«No responsible provider can promise absolute security. We can design, implement and evidence agreed security controls and reduce risk to an appropriate level.»"]},{"heading":"328. STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"329. OBJECTION #91","paragraphs":["«ΑΝ ΓΙΝΕΙ BREACH, ΘΑ ΕΙΝΑΙ ΟΛΗ Η ΕΥΘΥΝΗ ΔΙΚΗ ΣΑΣ.»"]},{"heading":"330. Don't negotiate legal liability alone.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"331. Response:","paragraphs":["«Liability needs to match the actual responsibilities and causes involved. Legal teams should define that in the contract rather than assuming one party controls every layer of risk.»"]},{"heading":"332. OBJECTION #92","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΝΑ ΥΠΟΓΡΑΨΟΥΜΕ NDA ΠΡΙΝ ΜΙΛΗΣΟΥΜΕ.»"]},{"heading":"333. Maybe okay:","paragraphs":["early discovery without sensitive data."]},{"heading":"334. Or if sensitive:","paragraphs":["NDA first."]},{"heading":"335. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can keep the initial discussion at a non-confidential level. If we need sensitive architecture or business information, we should put the appropriate NDA in place before that.»"]},{"heading":"336. OBJECTION #93","paragraphs":["«ΥΠΟΓΡΑΨΤΕ ΤΟ NDA ΜΑΣ ΟΠΩΣ ΕΙΝΑΙ.»"]},{"heading":"337. Don't agree yourself.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"338. Response:","paragraphs":["«We'll have the appropriate legal review it and come back on any material points.»"]},{"heading":"339. OBJECTION #94","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΑΛΛΑΖΟΥΜΕ ΤΟΥΣ ΟΡΟΥΣ ΜΑΣ.»"]},{"heading":"340. Could be true.","paragraphs":["Could be procurement posture."]},{"heading":"341. Need identify:","paragraphs":["non-negotiable vs negotiable."]},{"heading":"342. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which provisions are policy-level non-negotiables and where is there room for project-specific adjustment;»"]},{"heading":"343. OBJECTION #95","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ BEST AND FINAL OFFER.»"]},{"heading":"344. Don't automatically discount.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"345. Ask internally:","paragraphs":["what is: floor? tradeables? strategy?"]},{"heading":"346. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can submit our final commercial position once scope and terms are aligned so the number reflects the actual deal rather than only headline price.»"]},{"heading":"347. OBJECTION #96","paragraphs":["«ΑΝ ΔΕΝ ΜΕΙΩΣΕΤΕ 10%, ΧΑΝΕΤΕ ΤΟ DEAL.»"]},{"heading":"348. Could be bluff.","paragraphs":["Could be real."]},{"heading":"349. Don't bluff back.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"350. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Is 10% the only remaining decision criterion or are there other unresolved commercial or technical issues;»"]}]],["Σημεία 351–375 · Excellent.",[{"heading":"351. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"352. If truly only price:","paragraphs":["decide internally."]},{"heading":"353. WALK-AWAY","paragraphs":["sometimes correct."]},{"heading":"354. OBJECTION #97","paragraphs":["«Ο ΑΝΤΑΓΩΝΙΣΤΗΣ ΕΙΝΑΙ ΜΕΓΑΛΥΤΕΡΗ ΕΤΑΙΡΕΙΑ.»"]},{"heading":"355. Don't deny.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"356. Response:","paragraphs":["«That's true if scale is a key criterion. The question is which criteria matter most for this project — scale, senior attention, flexibility, specialist fit, delivery model or commercial structure.»"]},{"heading":"357. Do not declare:","paragraphs":["we are better."]},{"heading":"358. Let customer decide criteria.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"359. OBJECTION #98","paragraphs":["«ΕΙΣΤΕ ΠΟΛΥ ΜΙΚΡΟΙ ΓΙΑ ΕΜΑΣ.»"]},{"heading":"360. Response:","paragraphs":["«That's a legitimate concern. Let's define the actual capacity, continuity and governance requirements for the project. If we cannot demonstrate them credibly, we shouldn't ask you to take that risk.»"]},{"heading":"361. VERY STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"362. OBJECTION #99","paragraphs":["«ΤΙ ΓΙΝΕΤΑΙ ΑΝ ΕΞΑΦΑΝΙΣΤΕΙ Η ΕΤΑΙΡΕΙΑ ΣΑΣ;»"]},{"heading":"363. Need address continuity.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"364. Possible:","paragraphs":["documentation, source control, handover, escrow where appropriate, support plan."]},{"heading":"365. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can address continuity contractually and operationally through documentation, repository access, handover procedures and other safeguards appropriate to the project.»"]},{"heading":"366. Don't overpromise.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"367. OBJECTION #100","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΕΓΓΥΗΣΗ ΟΤΙ ΟΙ ΙΔΙΟΙ ΑΝΘΡΩΠΟΙ ΘΑ ΜΕΙΝΟΥΝ ΜΕΧΡΙ ΤΟ ΤΕΛΟΣ.»"]},{"heading":"368. Can't guarantee:","paragraphs":["people never change."]},{"heading":"369. Better:","paragraphs":["«We can commit to role continuity, knowledge transfer and controlled replacement process. Absolute guarantee that no individual will ever change would not be realistic.»"]},{"heading":"370. PROFESSIONAL","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"371. OBJECTION #101","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΩ JUNIORS.»"]},{"heading":"372. Ask:","paragraphs":["what work?"]},{"heading":"373. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can define seniority by responsibility. Using senior people for every task can raise cost unnecessarily, while critical architecture, review and decision points should have the appropriate seniority.»"]},{"heading":"374. Explain team pyramid.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"375. OBJECTION #102","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ ΜΟΝΟ SENIORS.»"]}]],["Σημεία 376–400 · Response:",[{"heading":"376. Response:","paragraphs":["«That's possible commercially, but it may not be the most efficient delivery model. We can show which roles genuinely require senior expertise and where mixed seniority provides better economics without reducing quality.»"]},{"heading":"377. OBJECTION #103","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΩ ΕΝΑΝ ΑΝΘΡΩΠΟ ΝΑ ΜΙΛΑΩ.»"]},{"heading":"378. Good.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"379. Enterprise model:","paragraphs":["single accountable PM/account contact."]},{"heading":"380. But specialists:","paragraphs":["join when needed."]},{"heading":"381. OBJECTION #104","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΩ ΝΑ ΜΙΛΑΩ ΜΕ 10 ΑΤΟΜΑ.»"]},{"heading":"382. Response:","paragraphs":["«Agreed. We'll define one accountable commercial/project contact, while technical specialists join only where their expertise is needed.»"]},{"heading":"383. OBJECTION #105","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΝΑ ΜΙΛΑΜΕ ΚΑΤΕΥΘΕΙΑΝ ΜΕ DEVELOPERS.»"]},{"heading":"384. Could be useful.","paragraphs":["But governance needed."]},{"heading":"385. Response:","paragraphs":["«Direct technical collaboration can work well, as long as changes to scope, priorities or commitments still follow the agreed project governance.»"]},{"heading":"386. OBJECTION #106","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ PROJECT MANAGER.»"]},{"heading":"387. Ask:","paragraphs":["why."]},{"heading":"388. Maybe project small.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"389. If complex:","paragraphs":["explain coordination need."]},{"heading":"390. OBJECTION #107","paragraphs":["«PROJECT MANAGEMENT ΕΙΝΑΙ OVERHEAD.»"]},{"heading":"391. Response:","paragraphs":["«For very small scopes it can be light. For multi-team or integration-heavy projects, coordination, decisions, risks and customer dependencies still need ownership. The question is the right level of PM, not bureaucracy for its own sake.»"]},{"heading":"392. OBJECTION #108","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ DOCUMENTATION, ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΚΩΔΙΚΑ.»"]},{"heading":"393. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can keep documentation proportionate, but enough must exist for support, knowledge transfer, architecture and future change. Otherwise short-term speed creates long-term dependency.»"]},{"heading":"394. OBJECTION #109","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΧΡΕΙΑΖΟΜΑΣΤΕ TESTING, ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΝΑ ΒΓΟΥΜΕ ΓΡΗΓΟΡΑ.»"]},{"heading":"395. Do not agree.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"396. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can optimize testing based on risk, but removing it entirely creates unacceptable production risk. Let's identify the critical journeys that must be validated before release.»"]},{"heading":"397. OBJECTION #110","paragraphs":["«ΒΓΑΛΤΕ ΤΟ ΤΩΡΑ ΚΑΙ ΘΑ ΤΟ ΦΤΙΑΞΟΥΜΕ ΜΕΤΑ.»"]},{"heading":"398. Sometimes acceptable:","paragraphs":["low-risk beta."]},{"heading":"399. Sometimes dangerous:","paragraphs":["production-critical system."]},{"heading":"400. Ask:","paragraphs":["what risk is acceptable."]}]],["Σημεία 401–425 · Response:",[{"heading":"401. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can phase quality and scope, but we shouldn't knowingly release defects that create security, financial or operational risk beyond what you've explicitly accepted.»"]},{"heading":"402. OBJECTION #111","paragraphs":["«ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΟΛΑ ΤΑ FEATURES ΣΤΗΝ ΠΡΩΤΗ ΕΚΔΟΣΗ.»"]},{"heading":"403. Response:","paragraphs":["«Let's separate must-have capabilities required for the business outcome from features that can follow later. Larger first scope usually increases time and delivery risk.»"]},{"heading":"404. OBJECTION #112","paragraphs":["«ΟΛΑ ΕΙΝΑΙ MUST-HAVE.»"]},{"heading":"405. Great question:","paragraphs":["«If we had to launch with only five capabilities to achieve the core business outcome, which five would they be;»"]},{"heading":"406. Forces prioritization.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"407. OBJECTION #113","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΟΥΜΕ ΝΑ ΕΜΠΛΑΚΟΥΜΕ ΤΟΥΣ USERS ΑΚΟΜΑ.»"]},{"heading":"408. Risk.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"409. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can limit involvement, but if the system changes their daily workflow, representative users should validate requirements before build goes too far.»"]},{"heading":"410. OBJECTION #114","paragraphs":["«Ο CEO ΤΟ ΘΕΛΕΙ, ΔΕΝ ΧΡΕΙΑΖΕΤΑΙ DISCOVERY.»"]},{"heading":"411. Executive sponsorship:","paragraphs":["good. But not enough."]},{"heading":"412. Response:","paragraphs":["«CEO sponsorship gives the initiative priority, but delivery still needs validated workflows, users and system dependencies so we build the right thing.»"]},{"heading":"413. OBJECTION #115","paragraphs":["«Ο CIO ΤΟ ΕΝΕΚΡΙΝΕ, ΠΑΜΕ.»"]},{"heading":"414. Need:","paragraphs":["business owner."]},{"heading":"415. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Who owns the business outcome and user adoption on the operational side;»"]},{"heading":"416. OBJECTION #116","paragraphs":["«BUSINESS ΤΟ ΘΕΛΕΙ, IT ΘΑ ΤΟ ΒΡΕΙ.»"]},{"heading":"417. Dangerous.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"418. Response:","paragraphs":["«IT needs to validate integration, architecture, security and support early. Otherwise we risk designing a solution that business likes but the enterprise cannot safely operate.»"]},{"heading":"419. OBJECTION #117","paragraphs":["«IT ΤΟ ΘΕΛΕΙ, BUSINESS ΘΑ ΤΟ ΧΡΗΣΙΜΟΠΟΙΗΣΕΙ.»"]},{"heading":"420. Also dangerous.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"421. Response:","paragraphs":["«We should confirm a real business owner and measurable use case before implementation. Technical sponsorship alone doesn't guarantee adoption.»"]},{"heading":"422. OBJECTION #118","paragraphs":["«ΔΕΝ ΘΕΛΩ ΝΑ ΕΜΠΛΕΞΩ PROCUREMENT ΤΩΡΑ.»"]},{"heading":"423. Fine initially.","paragraphs":["But: need know process."]},{"heading":"424. Ask:","paragraphs":["«At what stage does procurement need to enter and what documentation will they require;»"]},{"heading":"425. OBJECTION #119","paragraphs":["«PROCUREMENT ΘΑ ΕΡΘΕΙ ΣΤΟ ΤΕΛΟΣ.»"]}]],["Σημεία 426–450 · Risk:",[{"heading":"426. Risk:","paragraphs":["late surprise."]},{"heading":"427. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Can we at least map their mandatory steps now so the close plan is realistic;»"]},{"heading":"428. OBJECTION #120","paragraphs":["«LEGAL ΘΑ ΤΟ ΔΕΙ ΑΦΟΥ ΣΥΜΦΩΝΗΣΟΥΜΕ ΟΛΑ.»"]},{"heading":"429. If major terms:","paragraphs":["risk."]},{"heading":"430. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can keep Legal involvement proportionate, but if there are likely issues around IP, data, liability or subcontracting, early visibility may save rework later.»"]},{"heading":"431. NOW","paragraphs":["DIFFICULT CONVERSATION: CUSTOMER IS ANGRY"]},{"heading":"432. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«ΜΑΣ ΑΠΟΓΟΗΤΕΥΣΑΤΕ.»"]},{"heading":"433. BAD RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Δεν φταίμε εμείς.»"]},{"heading":"434. BETTER","paragraphs":["«Θέλω να καταλάβω ακριβώς πού δεν καλύψαμε την προσδοκία σας. Ποιο ήταν το συγκεκριμένο outcome που περιμένατε και τι συνέβη αντί γι' αυτό;»"]},{"heading":"435. FIRST:","paragraphs":["understand."]},{"heading":"436. Then:","paragraphs":["facts."]},{"heading":"437. Then:","paragraphs":["responsibility."]},{"heading":"438. Then:","paragraphs":["recovery plan."]},{"heading":"439. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«ΜΑΣ ΕΙΠΑΤΕ ΟΤΙ ΘΑ ΕΙΝΑΙ ΕΤΟΙΜΟ.»"]},{"heading":"440. If true:","paragraphs":["don't evade."]},{"heading":"441. Say:","paragraphs":["«We committed to that date and missed it. Here's what caused it, what we own, and the recovery plan.»"]},{"heading":"442. ACCOUNTABILITY","paragraphs":["builds trust."]},{"heading":"443. Don't hide behind:","paragraphs":["technical language."]},{"heading":"444. CUSTOMER BLAMES DISTILLOGIC","paragraphs":["for customer-side delay."]},{"heading":"445. Don't attack.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"446. Say:","paragraphs":["«Let's separate the timeline into supplier and customer dependencies so we can agree factually what happened and prevent recurrence.»"]},{"heading":"447. DOCUMENTATION MATTERS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"448. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["SCOPE CREEP Customer: «Είναι μικρή αλλαγή, κάντε την.»"]},{"heading":"449. Response:","paragraphs":["«We can absolutely evaluate it. Let's first confirm effort and whether it affects agreed scope, timeline or budget. Small requests individually can become material when they accumulate.»"]},{"heading":"450. Don't be:","paragraphs":["rigid."]}]],["Σημεία 451–475 · Don't be:",[{"heading":"451. Don't be:","paragraphs":["free unlimited development."]},{"heading":"452. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER WANTS FREE EXTRA WORK"]},{"heading":"453. Say:","paragraphs":["«We want to help. This request sits outside the agreed scope, so we'll give you the impact and options before starting it.»"]},{"heading":"454. PROFESSIONAL","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"455. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER DELAYS APPROVAL"]},{"heading":"456. Say:","paragraphs":["«This approval is now on the critical path. If we receive it after X date, the delivery milestone will need to move accordingly.»"]},{"heading":"457. Factual.","paragraphs":["Not threatening."]},{"heading":"458. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER KEEPS CHANGING PRIORITIES"]},{"heading":"459. Say:","paragraphs":["«We can change priorities, but we need to agree what moves out or what impact it has on timeline and cost. Otherwise the team is being asked to deliver two priorities in the same capacity.»"]},{"heading":"460. EXCELLENT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"461. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER WANTS IMPOSSIBLE DEADLINE"]},{"heading":"462. Don't just say:","paragraphs":["«Impossible.»"]},{"heading":"463. Say:","paragraphs":["«With the current scope and dependencies, that date is not one we can responsibly commit to. We can either reduce scope, add approved parallel work where practical, or move the date.»"]},{"heading":"464. Give options.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"465. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER ASKS FOR SOMETHING UNSAFE"]},{"heading":"466. Say:","paragraphs":["«We can understand the business reason, but we can't recommend an implementation that bypasses the required security/control safeguards. Let's find another way to achieve the outcome.»"]},{"heading":"467. DISTILLOGIC CREDIBILITY","paragraphs":["matters more than: one sale."]},{"heading":"468. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER INSULTS TEAM"]},{"heading":"469. Maintain professionalism.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"470. Say:","paragraphs":["«We're happy to address performance concerns directly and factually. We need the conversation to stay focused on the work and expectations so we can resolve the issue productively.»"]},{"heading":"471. Boundaries:","paragraphs":["without aggression."]},{"heading":"472. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER WANTS TO BYPASS PM"]},{"heading":"473. Say:","paragraphs":["«You can speak directly with specialists when useful, but commitments affecting scope, timeline or commercial terms need to remain visible through the agreed project governance.»"]},{"heading":"474. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER THREATENS TO CANCEL"]},{"heading":"475. Don't panic-discount.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 476–500 · Ask:",[{"heading":"476. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What specifically has brought the project to that point — value, delivery, cost, trust or a change in business priority;»"]},{"heading":"477. Then:","paragraphs":["diagnose."]},{"heading":"478. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER GOES SILENT"]},{"heading":"479. Don't send:","paragraphs":["12: «Just following up.»"]},{"heading":"480. First:","paragraphs":["value follow-up."]},{"heading":"481. Then:","paragraphs":["direct qualification."]},{"heading":"482. Example:","paragraphs":["«I haven't been able to reconnect, so I want to check rather than keep chasing. Has the priority changed, or is there a specific dependency holding the project;»"]},{"heading":"483. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"484. If no response:","paragraphs":["nurture/close-lost."]},{"heading":"485. SALES TIME","paragraphs":["is valuable."]},{"heading":"486. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER SAYS NO"]},{"heading":"487. Don't argue.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"488. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Understood. For my learning, was the main reason timing, fit, price or internal priority;»"]},{"heading":"489. Short.","paragraphs":["Respectful."]},{"heading":"490. Don't turn lost deal:","paragraphs":["into hostile relationship."]},{"heading":"491. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["COMPETITOR WINS"]},{"heading":"492. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What decision criteria made the difference;»"]},{"heading":"493. Learn.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"494. Don't:","paragraphs":["badmouth winner."]},{"heading":"495. Keep account:","paragraphs":["healthy."]},{"heading":"496. Maybe future:","paragraphs":["expansion/rebid."]},{"heading":"497. DIFFICULT CONVERSATION:","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER CHOOSES DO NOTHING"]},{"heading":"498. Important competitor.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"499. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What made the cost or risk of change higher than the cost of leaving the current process as it is;»"]},{"heading":"500. Learn:","paragraphs":["business case weakness."]}]],["Σημεία 501–525 · OBJECTION HANDLING FORMULA",[{"heading":"501. OBJECTION HANDLING FORMULA","paragraphs":["A simple formula: A.C.Q.R.C."]},{"heading":"502. A = ACKNOWLEDGE","paragraphs":["«Καταλαβαίνω.»"]},{"heading":"503. C = CLARIFY","paragraphs":["«Όταν λέτε ακριβό, σε σχέση με τι;»"]},{"heading":"504. Q = QUESTION","paragraphs":["Explore root cause."]},{"heading":"505. R = RESPOND","paragraphs":["Answer only: real issue."]},{"heading":"506. C = CONFIRM","paragraphs":["«Does that address the concern or is there another issue behind it;»"]},{"heading":"507. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Don't use formula: robotically."]},{"heading":"508. PRICE ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Customer: «€150,000 είναι πάρα πολλά.»"]},{"heading":"509. Sales:","paragraphs":["«Σε σχέση με το budget που είχατε στο μυαλό σας ή σε σχέση με άλλη πρόταση;»"]},{"heading":"510. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Budget was €100k.»"]},{"heading":"511. Sales:","paragraphs":["«Understood. Is €100k a hard approved limit, or was it the initial estimate before scope was defined;»"]},{"heading":"512. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Hard limit.»"]},{"heading":"513. Now:","paragraphs":["options: reduce scope, phase, walk away."]},{"heading":"514. Not:","paragraphs":["random discount."]},{"heading":"515. PROCUREMENT ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Procurement: «We need 15% reduction.»"]},{"heading":"516. Sales:","paragraphs":["«What changed in the scope or commercial assumptions that requires 15%;»"]},{"heading":"517. Procurement:","paragraphs":["«Nothing. Policy.»"]},{"heading":"518. Sales:","paragraphs":["«Then if headline price must reduce, we'll need to adjust another variable so the commercial balance remains workable. Let's look at scope, payment timing or support.»"]},{"heading":"519. GOOD","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"520. TRUST ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["CIO: «You're too small.»"]},{"heading":"521. Sales:","paragraphs":["«That's a reasonable concern. Which part worries you most — delivery capacity, continuity, support, financial stability or breadth of expertise;»"]},{"heading":"522. CIO:","paragraphs":["«Continuity.»"]},{"heading":"523. Now answer:","paragraphs":["continuity."]},{"heading":"524. Not:","paragraphs":["general company pitch."]},{"heading":"525. COMPETITOR ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Customer: «Accenture can do this too.»"]}]],["Σημεία 526–550 · Sales:",[{"heading":"526. Sales:","paragraphs":["«Absolutely. The useful question is what criteria matter most for this specific project and which provider aligns best with them. What are your top three decision criteria;»"]},{"heading":"527. Neutral.","paragraphs":["Professional."]},{"heading":"528. DEADLINE ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Customer: «Go-live must be December 1.»"]},{"heading":"529. Sales:","paragraphs":["«What happens operationally if it isn't live on December 1?»"]},{"heading":"530. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Existing contract expires.»"]},{"heading":"531. Real deadline.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"532. Now:","paragraphs":["technical planning."]},{"heading":"533. Another customer:","paragraphs":["«CEO just wants it.»"]},{"heading":"534. Still priority.","paragraphs":["But: maybe scope must change."]},{"heading":"535. BUDGET ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Customer: «No budget.»"]},{"heading":"536. Sales:","paragraphs":["«Is there no budget allocated to this initiative specifically, or no discretionary budget available at all this year;»"]},{"heading":"537. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Not allocated.»"]},{"heading":"538. Sales:","paragraphs":["«What business case or sponsor would be required to get it allocated;»"]},{"heading":"539. Different from:","paragraphs":["dead opportunity."]},{"heading":"540. EXISTING VENDOR ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Customer: «We're happy with our current vendor.»"]},{"heading":"541. Sales:","paragraphs":["«Then I wouldn't suggest changing for the sake of changing. If there are areas they don't cover — capacity, integrations, data or a specific new initiative — that's where a conversation may make sense.»"]},{"heading":"542. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"543. NO PRIORITY ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Customer: «Interesting, but not priority.»"]},{"heading":"544. Sales:","paragraphs":["«Understood. What initiatives are ahead of it, and is there a trigger that could move this higher later;»"]},{"heading":"545. If no:","paragraphs":["exit."]},{"heading":"546. FREE WORK ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Customer: «Build prototype first and we'll decide.»"]},{"heading":"547. Sales:","paragraphs":["«We can define a prototype phase with clear objectives and limited scope. If it requires real design and engineering effort, we'll structure it as a paid phase rather than open-ended speculative build.»"]},{"heading":"548. CREDIBILITY","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"549. SALES PERSON'S INTERNAL CHECK","paragraphs":["Before answering objection: ask mentally: Is this a real objection or a negotiation tactic?"]},{"heading":"550. Then:","paragraphs":["Is it business, technical, commercial, trust or process?"]}]],["Σημεία 551–575 · Then:",[{"heading":"551. Then:","paragraphs":["Who owns the answer?"]},{"heading":"552. Example:","paragraphs":["security objection: not salesperson alone."]},{"heading":"553. Legal objection:","paragraphs":["not salesperson alone."]},{"heading":"554. Architecture objection:","paragraphs":["technical lead."]},{"heading":"555. Payment terms:","paragraphs":["commercial/finance."]},{"heading":"556. SALES DOESN'T NEED","paragraphs":["to answer: everything."]},{"heading":"557. STRONG RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«I don't want to guess. Let me bring the person who owns that area so we give you the correct answer.»"]},{"heading":"558. This builds:","paragraphs":["trust."]},{"heading":"559. WHEN TO PUSH BACK","paragraphs":["Push back when: Request creates unsafe delivery Timeline is unrealistic Scope is contradictory Commercial terms are unsustainable Customer expects false claims."]},{"heading":"560. PUSHBACK STYLE","paragraphs":["Not: «No.» Instead: «We can achieve the outcome, but not responsibly under that assumption. Here are the workable options.»"]},{"heading":"561. WHEN TO WALK AWAY","paragraphs":["No measurable need No access No sponsor Impossible economics Unacceptable legal risk Customer demands deception Delivery impossible No meaningful path to decision."]},{"heading":"562. WALKING AWAY","paragraphs":["is not: failure."]},{"heading":"563. BAD DEAL","paragraphs":["can destroy: margin, team, reputation."]},{"heading":"564. DISTILLOGIC RULE","paragraphs":["WE DO NOT WIN BAD PROJECTS."]},{"heading":"565. MANAGER OBJECTION DRILL","paragraphs":["Manager gives: random objection."]},{"heading":"566. Salesperson has:","paragraphs":["30 seconds."]},{"heading":"567. They must:","paragraphs":["Clarify. Ask one good question. Respond. Confirm next step."]},{"heading":"568. SAMPLE DRILL","paragraphs":["Manager: «You're too expensive.»"]},{"heading":"569. Seller:","paragraphs":["must not: discount immediately."]},{"heading":"570. SAMPLE","paragraphs":["Manager: «We already have SAP.» Seller: must not: attack SAP."]},{"heading":"571. SAMPLE","paragraphs":["Manager: «No budget.» Seller: must distinguish: budget vs priority."]},{"heading":"572. SAMPLE","paragraphs":["Manager: «Send a proposal.» Seller: must qualify: scope."]},{"heading":"573. SAMPLE","paragraphs":["Manager: «Need it in a month.» Seller: must ask: business reason."]},{"heading":"574. SAMPLE","paragraphs":["Manager: «Need AI.» Seller: must ask: task/decision."]},{"heading":"575. SAMPLE","paragraphs":["Manager: «Need 20% discount.» Seller: must: Give/Get."]}]],["Σημεία 576–600 · OBJECTION SCORECARD",[{"heading":"576. OBJECTION SCORECARD","paragraphs":["Score salesperson:"]},{"heading":"577. Listening","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"578. Clarifying question","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"579. Root-cause identification","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"580. Response quality","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"581. Protection of value","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"582. Next-step quality","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"583. TOTAL","paragraphs":["__/30"]},{"heading":"584. 26–30","paragraphs":["Excellent."]},{"heading":"585. 21–25","paragraphs":["Strong."]},{"heading":"586. 16–20","paragraphs":["Needs practice."]},{"heading":"587. Below 16","paragraphs":["Not ready for strategic accounts."]},{"heading":"588. FINAL EXERCISE","paragraphs":["Customer says: «Your competitor is cheaper, has more employees, has worked with bigger brands and says they can deliver faster.»"]},{"heading":"589. BAD SELLER","paragraphs":["panics."]},{"heading":"590. GOOD SELLER","paragraphs":["asks: «Those are all valid factors. Which of them is most important in your actual decision, and where do you still see risk with our proposal;»"]},{"heading":"591. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Delivery risk.»"]},{"heading":"592. NOW","paragraphs":["we know: real objection."]},{"heading":"593. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Let's address delivery risk directly. We can review proposed team, governance, milestones, acceptance criteria and continuity plan. If those don't give you enough confidence, then we may not be the right supplier for this project.»"]},{"heading":"594. THIS IS","paragraphs":["enterprise selling."]},{"heading":"595. FINAL GOLDEN RULE #1","paragraphs":["«Objection is information.»"]},{"heading":"596. GOLDEN RULE #2","paragraphs":["«Do not answer before you understand what the customer actually means.»"]},{"heading":"597. GOLDEN RULE #3","paragraphs":["«Never discount before you understand whether the problem is price or value.»"]},{"heading":"598. GOLDEN RULE #4","paragraphs":["«Never attack the competitor.»"]},{"heading":"599. GOLDEN RULE #5","paragraphs":["«Never lie to compensate for being a smaller or newer company.»"]},{"heading":"600. GOLDEN RULE #6","paragraphs":["«When you don't know, bring the person who does.»"]}]],["Σημεία 601–606 · GOLDEN RULE #7",[{"heading":"601. GOLDEN RULE #7","paragraphs":["«A concession should normally have a Give/Get.»"]},{"heading":"602. GOLDEN RULE #8","paragraphs":["«Do not promise what Delivery, Legal, Security or Finance has not validated.»"]},{"heading":"603. GOLDEN RULE #9","paragraphs":["«You do not need to win every objection. You need to understand whether a good deal still exists.»"]},{"heading":"604. GOLDEN RULE #10","paragraphs":["«Protect the relationship even when you lose the deal.»"]},{"heading":"605. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER OBJECTS ↓ LISTEN ↓ CLARIFY ↓ IDENTIFY REAL ISSUE ↓ CLASSIFY: BUSINESS / TECHNICAL / COMMERCIAL / TRUST / PROCESS ↓ INVOLVE RIGHT PERSON IF NEEDED ↓ RESPOND WITH FACTS ↓ DON'T OVERPROMISE ↓ TRADE — DON'T GIVE AWAY ↓ CONFIRM WHETHER CONCERN IS RESOLVED ↓ AGREE NEXT STEP ↓ REQUALIFY THE DEAL."]},{"heading":"606. Η ΜΙΑ ΦΡΑΣΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΘΥΜΑΤΑΙ Η ΟΜΑΔΑ","paragraphs":["«Όταν ο enterprise πελάτης λέει “είστε ακριβοί”, “δεν έχουμε budget”, “έχουμε ήδη supplier”, “θέλω AI”, “θέλω 20% έκπτωση” ή “δεν σας εμπιστεύομαι ακόμα”, ο καλός salesperson δεν ψάχνει την πιο έξυπνη έτοιμη απάντηση. Ψάχνει πρώτα να καταλάβει τι πραγματικά σημαίνει η ένσταση, ποιο ρίσκο βλέπει ο πελάτης και αν υπάρχει ένας δίκαιος, τεχνικά σωστός και εμπορικά βιώσιμος δρόμος για να συνεχίσει η συμφωνία.» ΑΥΤΟ ΕΙΝΑΙ ENTERPRISE OBJECTION HANDLING."]}]],["Πριν απαντήσεις στο quiz",["Ξανασκέψου το εισαγωγικό περιστατικό. Ποιο γεγονός είναι επιβεβαιωμένο, ποια πληροφορία λείπει και ποια ενέργεια θα μείωνε την αβεβαιότητα; Μία απάντηση μπορεί να ακούγεται εμπορικά ελκυστική αλλά να προηγείται της απαιτούμενης επιβεβαίωσης.","Οι δύο ερωτήσεις εφαρμογής γενικών αρχών συνδέονται και με τις προαιρετικές «Γενικές σημειώσεις». Το PDF βρίσκεται μόνιμα στο μενού, δεν αποτελεί ξεχωριστό υποχρεωτικό μάθημα και η ανάγνωσή του δεν βαθμολογείται.","Η παραχώρηση εξετάζεται μαζί με αξία, κόστος και εξουσιοδότηση. Γενικές σημειώσεις: διαπραγμάτευση και παραχωρήσεις.","Ανάγκη και χρονική προτεραιότητα δεν είναι το ίδιο. Γενικές σημειώσεις: κόστος αδράνειας και πραγματική δέσμευση."]]],"scenario":["Μετά την παρουσίαση ο πελάτης λέει «είστε ακριβοί», ενώ δεν έχει γίνει σύγκριση αντικειμένου, κινδύνου ή χρόνου υλοποίησης.","Διευκρίνιση του σημείου σύγκρισης και του τι περιλαμβάνει η εναλλακτική. Η αντίρρηση χρειάζεται κατανόηση πριν δοθεί εμπορική απάντηση."],"minutes":55,"version":1,"additional_curriculum":37,"question_rows":[["Μετά την παρουσίαση ο πελάτης λέει «είστε ακριβοί», ενώ δεν έχει γίνει σύγκριση αντικειμένου, κινδύνου ή χρόνου υλοποίησης. Ποια είναι η πιο χρήσιμη πρώτη απάντηση;","Διευκρίνιση του σημείου σύγκρισης και του τι περιλαμβάνει η εναλλακτική.","Άμεση έκπτωση με την ελπίδα να τελειώσει η συζήτηση.","Επιμονή ότι η υψηλή τιμή αποδεικνύει ποιότητα.","Αμφισβήτηση της ικανότητας του πελάτη να αξιολογήσει.","Η αντίρρηση χρειάζεται κατανόηση πριν δοθεί εμπορική απάντηση."],["Μετά την παρουσίαση ο πελάτης λέει «είστε ακριβοί», ενώ δεν έχει γίνει σύγκριση αντικειμένου, κινδύνου ή χρόνου υλοποίησης. Ο πελάτης φοβάται την υλοποίηση, όχι το κόστος. Τι ταιριάζει;","Σαφή στάδια, ευθύνες, αποδείξεις και κριτήρια αποδοχής.","Η ίδια έκπτωση σε μεγαλύτερο ποσοστό.","Περισσότερα άσχετα χαρακτηριστικά στο demo.","Πίεση για υπογραφή πριν συζητηθούν οι κίνδυνοι.","Η παρέμβαση πρέπει να απαντά στην πραγματική αβεβαιότητα."],["Μετά την παρουσίαση ο πελάτης λέει «είστε ακριβοί», ενώ δεν έχει γίνει σύγκριση αντικειμένου, κινδύνου ή χρόνου υλοποίησης. Πότε σταματά η διερεύνηση αντίρρησης;","Όταν εκφράζεται σαφές όριο ή αίτημα διακοπής επικοινωνίας.","Μόνο μετά από προκαθορισμένο αριθμό επαναλήψεων.","Όταν ο πωλητής εξαντλήσει όλες τις διαθέσιμες εκπτώσεις.","Ποτέ, εφόσον ο λογαριασμός είναι μεγάλος.","Το επαγγελματικό όριο δεν είναι αντίρρηση που πρέπει να ξεπεραστεί."],["Στη διαπραγμάτευση ζητείται μικρότερη τιμή. Ποια παραχώρηση διατηρεί καθαρή εμπορική λογική;","Εγκεκριμένη ανταλλαγή με συγκεκριμένο αντίκρισμα, όπως διαφορετικό scope ή όρους, καταγεγραμμένη στην προσφορά.","Έκπτωση τώρα με αόριστη προσδοκία μελλοντικών έργων.","Μείωση τιμής που θα αντισταθμιστεί με μη συμφωνημένη μείωση ποιότητας.","Προσωρινή τιμή που θα αλλάξει μετά την υπογραφή.","Η παραχώρηση εξετάζεται μαζί με αξία, κόστος και εξουσιοδότηση. Γενικές σημειώσεις: διαπραγμάτευση και παραχωρήσεις."],["Ο πελάτης λέει «το πρόβλημα είναι σημαντικό» αλλά δεν επιθυμεί αλλαγή φέτος. Ποια ερώτηση διερευνά τη χρονική προτεραιότητα χωρίς πίεση;","Τι θα συμβεί αν η διαδικασία παραμείνει όπως είναι και ποιο γεγονός θα έκανε την αλλαγή προτεραιότητα;","Να γράψω ότι συμφωνήσατε για να κρατήσουμε την τιμή;","Θέλετε να χάσετε την ευκαιρία που παίρνουν οι ανταγωνιστές σας;","Αφού υπάρχει πρόβλημα, γιατί δεν υπογράφετε σήμερα;","Ανάγκη και χρονική προτεραιότητα δεν είναι το ίδιο. Γενικές σημειώσεις: κόστος αδράνειας και πραγματική δέσμευση."]],"source_note":"Πηγή: ΜΑΘΗΜΑ 31.docx, κεφάλαιο 52. Διατηρείται το κείμενο των αριθμημένων σημείων, με ενοποίηση των σπασμένων γραμμών και αφαίρεση επαναλαμβανόμενης μορφοποίησης. Τα παραδείγματα δεν αλλάζουν τους κανόνες της εφαρμογής."},"di-enterprise-53":{"pillar":"distillogic","title":"53. Πρώτη προσέγγιση μεγάλων λογαριασμών","goal":"Να αναγνωρίζεις πραγματικές ανάγκες, να διερευνάς τα στοιχεία και να επιλέγεις υπεύθυνο επόμενο βήμα.","sections":[["Από την έννοια στην επαγγελματική πράξη",["Βρίσκεις ανακοίνωση νέου εργοστασίου και θέλεις να επικοινωνήσεις με τον υπεύθυνο λειτουργίας χωρίς γενικό μήνυμα μαζικής πώλησης.","Στη μελέτη που ακολουθεί σύνδεσε κάθε πιθανή λύση με συγκεκριμένη διαδικασία, υπεύθυνο, επίπτωση και στοιχεία που μπορούν να επαληθευτούν. Η τεχνική δυνατότητα, η οικονομική αξία και η εξουσιοδότηση για απόφαση είναι διαφορετικά ερωτήματα. Τα παραδείγματα του κεφαλαίου σε βοηθούν να τα διερευνάς χωρίς να υπόσχεσαι κάτι που δεν έχει εγκριθεί.","Η ύλη περιγράφει ενδεικτικές επιχειρηματικές ανάγκες και μεθόδους πώλησης. Δεν αποτελεί κατάλογο έτοιμων λειτουργιών των δύο CRM, δεσμευτική προσφορά, αλλαγή αμοιβών ή νέα πολιτική πιστοποίησης. Για πραγματική εργασία ισχύουν οι εγκεκριμένοι εταιρικοί όροι και οι αρμοδιότητες. Το μάθημα 60 είναι προετοιμασία, όχι δεύτερη επίσημη τελική εξέταση."]],["Το αντικείμενο του κεφαλαίου",["Πώς ανοίγουμε μεγάλους εταιρικούς λογαριασμούς χωρίς να ακουγόμαστε σαν τηλεπωλητές"]],["Σημεία 1–25 · Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ",[{"heading":"1. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ","paragraphs":["Cold outreach: δεν σημαίνει: «Παίρνω 100 τηλέφωνα και λέω τι πουλάμε.» Σημαίνει: ΒΡΙΣΚΩ ΣΩΣΤΗ ΕΤΑΙΡΕΙΑ + ΣΩΣΤΟ ΑΝΘΡΩΠΟ + ΣΩΣΤΟ ΛΟΓΟ ΕΠΙΚΟΙΝΩΝΙΑΣ."]},{"heading":"2. Ο ΣΤΟΧΟΣ ΤΗΣ ΠΡΩΤΗΣ ΕΠΑΦΗΣ","paragraphs":["Δεν είναι: να πουλήσουμε project. Είναι: ΝΑ ΚΕΡΔΙΣΟΥΜΕ ΤΗΝ ΕΠΟΜΕΝΗ ΣΥΖΗΤΗΣΗ."]},{"heading":"3. Ο ΠΩΛΗΤΗΣ ΔΕΝ ΛΕΕΙ","paragraphs":["«Θέλω να σας παρουσιάσω την εταιρεία μας.»"]},{"heading":"4. Ο ΠΕΛΑΤΗΣ ΔΕΝ ΞΥΠΝΗΣΕ","paragraphs":["το πρωί: για να μάθει: ποια είναι η DISTILLOGIC."]},{"heading":"5. Ο ΠΕΛΑΤΗΣ ΝΟΙΑΖΕΤΑΙ","paragraphs":["για: Τι αλλάζει στην επιχείρησή του. Ποιο πρόβλημα έχει. Ποιο ρίσκο έχει. Πού χάνει χρόνο. Τι πρέπει να βελτιώσει."]},{"heading":"6. ΠΡΙΝ ΑΠΟ ΟΠΟΙΑΔΗΠΟΤΕ ΕΠΑΦΗ","paragraphs":["Πρέπει να ξέρουμε: Γιατί αυτή η εταιρεία; Γιατί αυτός ο άνθρωπος; Γιατί τώρα;"]},{"heading":"7. ΑΝ ΔΕΝ ΜΠΟΡΟΥΜΕ ΝΑ ΑΠΑΝΤΗΣΟΥΜΕ","paragraphs":["και στα 3: δεν είμαστε: έτοιμοι."]},{"heading":"8. COLD CALL ≠ RANDOM CALL","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"9. COLD","paragraphs":["σημαίνει: δεν υπάρχει υπάρχουσα σχέση."]},{"heading":"10. Δεν σημαίνει:","paragraphs":["δεν ξέρουμε: τίποτα για τον account."]},{"heading":"11. ENTERPRISE COLD CALL","paragraphs":["πρέπει να είναι: RESEARCHED COLD CALL."]},{"heading":"12. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ CALL STRUCTURE","paragraphs":["OPENING ↓ REASON ↓ RELEVANT OBSERVATION ↓ HYPOTHESIS ↓ QUESTION ↓ LISTEN ↓ NEXT STEP."]},{"heading":"13. ΟΧΙ","paragraphs":["5 λεπτά: company presentation."]},{"heading":"14. OPENING","paragraphs":["Απλό: «Καλημέρα κύριε Παπαδόπουλε, Σπύρος από DISTILLOGIC Technologies.»"]},{"heading":"15. ΜΕΤΑ","paragraphs":["«Ξέρω ότι σας καλώ χωρίς να έχουμε μιλήσει ξανά. Να σας πω σε 20 δευτερόλεπτα γιατί σας πήρα και μου λέτε αν έχει νόημα;»"]},{"heading":"16. ΓΙΑΤΙ ΔΟΥΛΕΥΕΙ","paragraphs":["Δεν κρύβουμε: ότι είναι cold call."]},{"heading":"17. Δίνουμε:","paragraphs":["control: στον άλλον."]},{"heading":"18. ΟΧΙ","paragraphs":["«Σας πετυχαίνω σε καλή στιγμή;»"]},{"heading":"19. Γιατί;","paragraphs":["Η εύκολη απάντηση: είναι: «Όχι.»"]},{"heading":"20. ΚΑΛΥΤΕΡΟ","paragraphs":["«Να σας πω σε 20 δευτερόλεπτα γιατί σας καλώ;»"]},{"heading":"21. ΜΕΤΑ","paragraphs":["χρειαζόμαστε: context."]},{"heading":"22. EXAMPLE — LOGISTICS","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι επεκτείνετε τις fulfillment operations σας και ανοίγετε νέα αποθήκη.»"]},{"heading":"23. FACT","paragraphs":["όχι: assumption."]},{"heading":"24. THEN","paragraphs":["hypothesis: «Σε τέτοιες φάσεις συχνά αυξάνεται η πίεση σε order visibility, client reporting και operational handoffs.»"]},{"heading":"25. THEN","paragraphs":["important phrase: «Δεν γνωρίζω αν ισχύει σε εσάς.»"]}]],["Σημεία 26–50 · WHY?",[{"heading":"26. WHY?","paragraphs":["We don't pretend: to know internal problem."]},{"heading":"27. THEN QUESTION","paragraphs":["«Ποιο από αυτά, αν κάποιο, είναι πιο δύσκολο καθώς μεγαλώνει ο όγκος;»"]},{"heading":"28. NOW","paragraphs":["conversation starts."]},{"heading":"29. COMPLETE EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["«Καλημέρα κύριε Δημητρίου, Σπύρος από DISTILLOGIC Technologies. Ξέρω ότι σας καλώ χωρίς να έχουμε μιλήσει ξανά. Να σας πω σε 20 δευτερόλεπτα γιατί σας πήρα; Είδα ότι επεκτείνετε τις fulfillment operations σας. Σε τέτοιες φάσεις συχνά μεγαλώνει η πολυπλοκότητα σε order visibility, client reporting και operational handoffs. Δεν γνωρίζω αν είναι θέμα για εσάς. Ποιο process δυσκολεύεται περισσότερο όσο μεγαλώνει ο όγκος;»"]},{"heading":"30. ΑΥΤΟ","paragraphs":["είναι: enterprise cold opening."]},{"heading":"31. ΔΕΝ ΕΙΠΑΜΕ","paragraphs":["Node.js AI Cloud Developers Web apps."]},{"heading":"32. ΓΙΑΤΙ;","paragraphs":["Γιατί: δεν ξέρουμε ακόμα: αν χρειάζονται."]},{"heading":"33. BAD OPENING","paragraphs":["«Είμαστε μία καινοτόμος εταιρεία πληροφορικής που παρέχει ολοκληρωμένες λύσεις...»"]},{"heading":"34. DELETE IT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"35. BAD","paragraphs":["«Έχουμε εξειδικευμένους developers.»"]},{"heading":"36. SO WHAT?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"37. BAD","paragraphs":["«Θα ήθελα να σας παρουσιάσω τις υπηρεσίες μας.»"]},{"heading":"38. CUSTOMER THINKS","paragraphs":["«Γιατί;»"]},{"heading":"39. COLD CALL SECRET","paragraphs":["START WITH THEM. Not: with us."]},{"heading":"40. FIRST 30 SECONDS","paragraphs":["Customer should understand: Why you called them. Why now. Why conversation may be relevant."]},{"heading":"41. DIFFERENT OPENING — MANUFACTURING","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι επεκτείνετε την παραγωγή με νέα γραμμή. Συχνά σε τέτοιες επεκτάσεις production reporting and maintenance coordination become harder before companies notice they need more integration. Δεν γνωρίζω αν ισχύει σε εσάς. Πού βλέπετε σήμερα το μεγαλύτερο operational pressure;»"]},{"heading":"42. HOTEL","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι ο όμιλος προσθέτει νέα properties. Όσο μεγαλώνει ένα hotel group, συχνά management reporting and operational visibility γίνονται πιο δύσκολα όταν τα properties έχουν διαφορετικά systems. Δεν γνωρίζω αν αποτελεί θέμα για εσάς. Πώς το διαχειρίζεστε σήμερα;»"]},{"heading":"43. PROFESSIONAL SERVICES","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι μεγαλώνετε αρκετά την ομάδα σας. Σε consulting firms με γρήγορη ανάπτυξη συχνά resource planning and project-margin visibility become harder. Δεν γνωρίζω αν ισχύει σε εσάς. Ποιο από τα δύο σας πιέζει περισσότερο σήμερα;»"]},{"heading":"44. CORPORATE GROUP","paragraphs":["«Είδα ότι ο όμιλος έχει προχωρήσει σε νέες εξαγορές. Σε τέτοιες περιπτώσεις συνήθως finance, customer and supplier data become harder to consolidate across entities. Δεν γνωρίζω πού βρίσκεται η δική σας προτεραιότητα. Ποιο integration area δημιουργεί σήμερα τη μεγαλύτερη δυσκολία;»"]},{"heading":"45. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Cold call: should feel: like: business conversation. Not: sales script."]},{"heading":"46. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«Δεν ενδιαφέρομαι.»"]},{"heading":"47. DON'T FIGHT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"48. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Κατανοητό. Είναι επειδή το συγκεκριμένο θέμα δεν αποτελεί priority ή επειδή ήδη το έχετε καλύψει;»"]},{"heading":"49. ONE QUESTION","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"50. If customer:","paragraphs":["«Το έχουμε καλύψει.» Say: «Τέλεια. Τότε δεν θέλω να σας απασχολήσω χωρίς λόγο. Ευχαριστώ για τον χρόνο σας.»"]}]],["Σημεία 51–75 · PROFESSIONAL EXIT",[{"heading":"51. PROFESSIONAL EXIT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"52. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«Δεν έχω χρόνο.»"]},{"heading":"53. Response:","paragraphs":["«Το καταλαβαίνω. Να σας στείλω δύο γραμμές με το συγκεκριμένο reason που σας κάλεσα και αν είναι relevant το βλέπουμε όταν σας βολεύει;»"]},{"heading":"54. NOW EMAIL","paragraphs":["has context."]},{"heading":"55. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Στείλε μου email.»"]},{"heading":"56. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Βεβαίως. Για να σας στείλω κάτι σχετικό, ποιο από τα δύο έχει περισσότερο νόημα για εσάς αυτή την περίοδο — operational automation ή system/data integration;»"]},{"heading":"57. Even small answer:","paragraphs":["helps personalize email."]},{"heading":"58. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Δεν είμαι ο κατάλληλος.»"]},{"heading":"59. GREAT","paragraphs":["Ask: «Ποιος συνήθως έχει ownership για αυτό το process; Operations, IT ή άλλο τμήμα;»"]},{"heading":"60. NEVER","paragraphs":["say: «Δώστε μου το τηλέφωνό του.» immediately."]},{"heading":"61. Better:","paragraphs":["understand role."]},{"heading":"62. GATEKEEPERS","paragraphs":["Reception, assistant, secretary."]},{"heading":"63. NEVER","paragraphs":["treat gatekeeper: as enemy."]},{"heading":"64. Don't lie:","paragraphs":["«Με περιμένει.» if false."]},{"heading":"65. GATEKEEPER OPENING","paragraphs":["«Καλημέρα σας. Προσπαθώ να βρω ποιος έχει την ευθύνη για digital operations / IT transformation / warehouse operations στον όμιλο. Μπορείτε να με κατευθύνετε;»"]},{"heading":"66. SIMPLE","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"67. IF ASKED","paragraphs":["«Τι αφορά;»"]},{"heading":"68. Response:","paragraphs":["«Αφορά πιθανή βελτίωση σε operational workflows και system integrations. Δεν θέλω να σας δώσω λάθος όνομα, γι' αυτό προσπαθώ πρώτα να βρω ποιος έχει ownership.»"]},{"heading":"69. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«Είναι προσωπικό.»"]},{"heading":"70. DON'T TRICK","paragraphs":["the gatekeeper."]},{"heading":"71. EXECUTIVE ASSISTANT","paragraphs":["can become: valuable guide."]},{"heading":"72. Treat with:","paragraphs":["same professionalism: as executive."]},{"heading":"73. IF ASSISTANT SAYS","paragraphs":["«Send information.»"]},{"heading":"74. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Βεβαίως. Σε ποια διεύθυνση είναι καλύτερα να το στείλω και υπάρχει κάποιος συγκεκριμένος τίτλος/ρόλος στον οποίο πρέπει να απευθυνθεί;»"]},{"heading":"75. COLD CALL TONE","paragraphs":["Should be: Calm Normal Confident Curious."]}]],["Σημεία 76–100 · NOT",[{"heading":"76. NOT","paragraphs":["overexcited."]},{"heading":"77. NOT","paragraphs":["«Καλημέρααα! Τι κάνετεεε;»"]},{"heading":"78. NOT","paragraphs":["robotic."]},{"heading":"79. NOT","paragraphs":["apologetic."]},{"heading":"80. Confidence:","paragraphs":["does not mean: aggression."]},{"heading":"81. PACING","paragraphs":["Speak: slightly slower: than nervous instinct."]},{"heading":"82. SHORT SENTENCES","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"83. ONE QUESTION","paragraphs":["then: silence."]},{"heading":"84. DON'T ANSWER","paragraphs":["your own question."]},{"heading":"85. Customer:","paragraphs":["needs: space."]},{"heading":"86. SILENCE","paragraphs":["is not: failure."]},{"heading":"87. COLD CALL RULE","paragraphs":["LISTEN MORE AFTER THE FIRST QUESTION."]},{"heading":"88. PHONE DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["If customer engages: do not immediately: book meeting."]},{"heading":"89. Ask:","paragraphs":["1–2: useful questions."]},{"heading":"90. Example:","paragraphs":["«How do you manage it today?»"]},{"heading":"91. Then:","paragraphs":["«Where does the process create the most manual work?»"]},{"heading":"92. If real pain emerges:","paragraphs":["meeting."]},{"heading":"93. MEETING CTA","paragraphs":["Not: «Can I book 30 minutes to present our company?»"]},{"heading":"94. Better:","paragraphs":["«Θα είχε νόημα να κάνουμε ένα 25-minute call με εσάς και τον άνθρωπο από IT/Operations ώστε να mapάρουμε το process and see whether there is actually something worth pursuing?»"]},{"heading":"95. CTA HAS","paragraphs":["purpose."]},{"heading":"96. BETTER","paragraphs":["than: generic demo."]},{"heading":"97. FIRST MEETING LENGTH","paragraphs":["20–30 minutes: often enough."]},{"heading":"98. Do not ask:","paragraphs":["one hour: for cold prospect: without reason."]},{"heading":"99. VOICEMAIL","paragraphs":["If appropriate: short."]},{"heading":"100. Example:","paragraphs":["«Κύριε Παπαδόπουλε, Σπύρος Μελάς από DISTILLOGIC Technologies. Επικοινωνώ σχετικά με τη νέα επέκταση που κάνετε και ένα πιθανό θέμα γύρω από operational system integration. Θα σας στείλω και ένα σύντομο email με το context. Ευχαριστώ.»"]}]],["Σημεία 101–125 · Voicemail goal:",[{"heading":"101. Voicemail goal:","paragraphs":["recognition. Not: full pitch."]},{"heading":"102. NOW","paragraphs":["COLD EMAIL"]},{"heading":"103. COLD EMAIL GOAL","paragraphs":["Get: reply/conversation."]},{"heading":"104. NOT","paragraphs":["tell: whole company story."]},{"heading":"105. GOOD EMAIL STRUCTURE","paragraphs":["Trigger Observation Hypothesis Question Small CTA."]},{"heading":"106. EMAIL LENGTH","paragraphs":["Short."]},{"heading":"107. Executive:","paragraphs":["will scan."]},{"heading":"108. SUBJECT LINE","paragraphs":["Should be: simple."]},{"heading":"109. Examples:","paragraphs":["New warehouse operations Production reporting Group reporting after expansion Hotel operations across properties Resource planning Customer onboarding workflow."]},{"heading":"110. DON'T WRITE","paragraphs":["«Revolutionary AI Solution for Your Business!!!»"]},{"heading":"111. Don't sound:","paragraphs":["spam."]},{"heading":"112. EMAIL EXAMPLE — LOGISTICS","paragraphs":["Subject: Fulfillment operations Body: Hi John,I noticed your team is expanding fulfillment capacity.In similar growth phases, order visibility, client reporting and WMS/TMS handoffs can become harder to scale. I don't know if that's an issue for your operation.Which workflow is currently creating the most manual coordination as volume grows?If relevant, happy to compare notes for 20 minutes."]},{"heading":"113. NOTICE","paragraphs":["No: 10 services."]},{"heading":"114. No:","paragraphs":["company history."]},{"heading":"115. No:","paragraphs":["huge attachment."]},{"heading":"116. PERSONALIZATION","paragraphs":["does not mean: «I saw you like golf.»"]},{"heading":"117. Useful personalization:","paragraphs":["business context."]},{"heading":"118. Good:","paragraphs":["«I saw you've opened a second warehouse.»"]},{"heading":"119. Good:","paragraphs":["«I saw you're hiring a Revenue Systems Manager.»"]},{"heading":"120. Good:","paragraphs":["«I saw the group acquired X.»"]},{"heading":"121. Not useful:","paragraphs":["fake flattery."]},{"heading":"122. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«I'm a huge fan of your amazing company.»"]},{"heading":"123. EXECUTIVES CAN SEE","paragraphs":["sales manipulation."]},{"heading":"124. EMAIL CTA","paragraphs":["Avoid: «Would Tuesday at 10:00 or Wednesday at 11:00 work?» when: zero engagement."]},{"heading":"125. Better:","paragraphs":["«Would it be worth a short conversation?»"]}]],["Σημεία 126–150 · Once interest:",[{"heading":"126. Once interest:","paragraphs":["then schedule."]},{"heading":"127. FOLLOW-UP #1","paragraphs":["Do not: «Just following up.»"]},{"heading":"128. Add:","paragraphs":["new context."]},{"heading":"129. Example:","paragraphs":["«One point I didn't include in my previous note: in multi-site operations the bottleneck is often not the core system but the manual handoff between systems and teams. If that's relevant, I can send the five questions we normally use to assess it.»"]},{"heading":"130. FOLLOW-UP #2","paragraphs":["Could use: new trigger."]},{"heading":"131. Example:","paragraphs":["«I noticed you're also recruiting for a data integration role. That may be unrelated, but it reinforced my question around cross-system visibility.»"]},{"heading":"132. Careful:","paragraphs":["fact ≠ proof."]},{"heading":"133. FOLLOW-UP #3","paragraphs":["Direct qualification."]},{"heading":"134. Example:","paragraphs":["«I don't want to keep filling your inbox if this isn't a priority. Is this simply not relevant right now, or is there someone else who owns the topic?»"]},{"heading":"135. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"136. STOP","paragraphs":["after reasonable sequence."]},{"heading":"137. Don't send:","paragraphs":["20 emails."]},{"heading":"138. BRAND DAMAGE","paragraphs":["is real."]},{"heading":"139. A SIMPLE SEQUENCE","paragraphs":["Day 1: Email."]},{"heading":"140. Day 2–3:","paragraphs":["LinkedIn view/invite."]},{"heading":"141. Day 4–5:","paragraphs":["Call."]},{"heading":"142. Later:","paragraphs":["value follow-up."]},{"heading":"143. Then:","paragraphs":["final qualification message."]},{"heading":"144. Important:","paragraphs":["cadence should: adapt."]},{"heading":"145. Not:","paragraphs":["machine-gun outreach."]},{"heading":"146. TIER A","paragraphs":["needs: more careful strategy."]},{"heading":"147. TIER C","paragraphs":["can support: more experimentation."]},{"heading":"148. LINKEDIN","paragraphs":["not: place to: paste email."]},{"heading":"149. CONNECTION REQUEST","paragraphs":["Short."]},{"heading":"150. Example:","paragraphs":["«Hi John, I follow your work around logistics operations and would be glad to connect.»"]}]],["Σημεία 151–175 · Don't pitch:",[{"heading":"151. Don't pitch:","paragraphs":["in invite."]},{"heading":"152. After accepted:","paragraphs":["do not send: instant 300-word sales message."]},{"heading":"153. BAD","paragraphs":["«Thanks for connecting! We provide web development, AI, cloud...»"]},{"heading":"154. BETTER","paragraphs":["wait/contextualize."]},{"heading":"155. Example:","paragraphs":["«Thanks for connecting, John. I noticed the new fulfillment expansion. Out of curiosity, as volume grows, which part becomes harder first for your team — client visibility, warehouse workflow or systems integration?»"]},{"heading":"156. QUESTION","paragraphs":["creates: conversation."]},{"heading":"157. LINKEDIN RESEARCH","paragraphs":["Look at: Role Responsibilities Company changes Posts Hiring Projects."]},{"heading":"158. DO NOT","paragraphs":["over-personalize: private life."]},{"heading":"159. ENTERPRISE LINKEDIN GOAL","paragraphs":["Build: familiarity + relevance."]},{"heading":"160. NOT","paragraphs":["collect connections."]},{"heading":"161. 5,000 CONNECTIONS","paragraphs":["mean nothing: if: no meaningful relationships."]},{"heading":"162. LINKEDIN COMMENTS","paragraphs":["Can help: if: genuine."]},{"heading":"163. Don't write:","paragraphs":["«Great post!» on everything."]},{"heading":"164. Add:","paragraphs":["real thought."]},{"heading":"165. Example:","paragraphs":["If COO posts about: warehouse expansion: «Interesting point on scaling capacity. In these expansions the system handoffs often become the hidden bottleneck before physical capacity does.»"]},{"heading":"166. Don't hijack:","paragraphs":["post: to pitch."]},{"heading":"167. SALES NAVIGATOR","paragraphs":["Useful for: Account lists Role search Changes Hiring signals."]},{"heading":"168. But tool:","paragraphs":["does not replace: thinking."]},{"heading":"169. CONTACT PERSONA — CEO","paragraphs":["First message: very high level."]},{"heading":"170. CEO cares:","paragraphs":["strategy, growth, cost, risk."]},{"heading":"171. CEO email:","paragraphs":["short."]},{"heading":"172. Example:","paragraphs":["«I noticed the group is expanding into two new markets. In multi-country growth, reporting and operational standardization often become harder before management wants a full transformation. Which cross-company process is currently hardest to scale?»"]},{"heading":"173. CTO/CIO","paragraphs":["Can discuss: systems, integration, architecture, security."]},{"heading":"174. But don't dump:","paragraphs":["technical stack."]},{"heading":"175. COO","paragraphs":["Talk: process, capacity, handoffs, visibility."]}]],["Σημεία 176–200 · CFO",[{"heading":"176. CFO","paragraphs":["Talk: margin, cost, working capital, ROI, control."]},{"heading":"177. Department Manager","paragraphs":["Talk: daily pain."]},{"heading":"178. ALWAYS ADAPT","paragraphs":["language: to role."]},{"heading":"179. BAD CEO MESSAGE","paragraphs":["«We build APIs using Node.js and PostgreSQL.»"]},{"heading":"180. BAD CTO MESSAGE","paragraphs":["«We can increase your profits.» too generic."]},{"heading":"181. ROLE RELEVANCE","paragraphs":["matters."]},{"heading":"182. MULTI-THREADING IN OUTREACH","paragraphs":["If one account: has: Operations, IT, Finance."]},{"heading":"183. Do not send:","paragraphs":["same message: to all."]},{"heading":"184. COO MESSAGE","paragraphs":["business workflow."]},{"heading":"185. CIO MESSAGE","paragraphs":["integration complexity."]},{"heading":"186. CFO MESSAGE","paragraphs":["financial impact."]},{"heading":"187. But:","paragraphs":["one Account Owner."]},{"heading":"188. Do not let:","paragraphs":["3 Distillogic people: randomly contact same account."]},{"heading":"189. CRM CHECK","paragraphs":["before: every outreach."]},{"heading":"190. Ask:","paragraphs":["Has anyone contacted account? Who owns account? What happened? Any relationship?"]},{"heading":"191. TIER A","paragraphs":["mandatory."]},{"heading":"192. COLD CALL RESEARCH — 10 MINUTES","paragraphs":["Enough for: smaller account."]},{"heading":"193. Check:","paragraphs":["Website Recent changes LinkedIn company Target person's role Job openings Existing tech clues if relevant."]},{"heading":"194. TIER A","paragraphs":["research deeper."]},{"heading":"195. ACCOUNT BRIEF","paragraphs":["Before outreach: write: Trigger Hypothesis Stakeholder Opening Objective."]},{"heading":"196. Example:","paragraphs":["Trigger: new plant."]},{"heading":"197. Hypothesis:","paragraphs":["production reporting complexity."]},{"heading":"198. Stakeholder:","paragraphs":["Operations Director."]},{"heading":"199. Opening:","paragraphs":["new plant + reporting."]},{"heading":"200. Objective:","paragraphs":["discovery call."]}]],["Σημεία 201–225 · EASY.",[{"heading":"201. EASY.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"202. COLD CALL COMMON MISTAKE #1","paragraphs":["Speaking too much."]},{"heading":"203. RULE","paragraphs":["After: 30–40 seconds: ask question."]},{"heading":"204. MISTAKE #2","paragraphs":["Listing services."]},{"heading":"205. MISTAKE #3","paragraphs":["Using buzzwords."]},{"heading":"206. MISTAKE #4","paragraphs":["Fake personalization."]},{"heading":"207. MISTAKE #5","paragraphs":["Talking fast."]},{"heading":"208. MISTAKE #6","paragraphs":["Arguing with rejection."]},{"heading":"209. MISTAKE #7","paragraphs":["Asking: 10 questions: without listening."]},{"heading":"210. MISTAKE #8","paragraphs":["Booking demo: before pain."]},{"heading":"211. MISTAKE #9","paragraphs":["Promising capability: without technical validation."]},{"heading":"212. MISTAKE #10","paragraphs":["Not recording call: in CRM."]},{"heading":"213. CRM AFTER CALL","paragraphs":["Record: Contact What happened Pain/hypothesis Objection Next step Date."]},{"heading":"214. NOT","paragraphs":["«Called — no answer.» only."]},{"heading":"215. If no answer:","paragraphs":["still: record attempt."]},{"heading":"216. CRM SHOULD PREVENT","paragraphs":["duplicate outreach."]},{"heading":"217. CALLING A MOBILE","paragraphs":["Be respectful."]},{"heading":"218. If personal mobile:","paragraphs":["say quickly: who you are and: why you're calling."]},{"heading":"219. Never:","paragraphs":["hide identity."]},{"heading":"220. WHATSAPP","paragraphs":["Enterprise outreach: only when appropriate."]},{"heading":"221. If relationship exists:","paragraphs":["fine."]},{"heading":"222. Cold WhatsApp:","paragraphs":["can feel intrusive."]},{"heading":"223. Use judgment.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"224. VOICE NOTE","paragraphs":["Not ideal: for cold executive: unless context exists."]},{"heading":"225. EMAIL SIGNATURE","paragraphs":["Simple: Name Role Company Contact."]}]],["Σημεία 226–250 · Don't make:",[{"heading":"226. Don't make:","paragraphs":["giant marketing banner."]},{"heading":"227. COLD EMAIL WITH ATTACHMENT","paragraphs":["Usually avoid: first message."]},{"heading":"228. Why?","paragraphs":["Security + friction."]},{"heading":"229. Send:","paragraphs":["link or short text: when appropriate."]},{"heading":"230. MEETING REQUEST","paragraphs":["Be specific: about purpose."]},{"heading":"231. BAD","paragraphs":["«Let's have a meeting to discuss synergies.»"]},{"heading":"232. Meaningless.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"233. BETTER","paragraphs":["«A 25-minute discussion to map the current order-to-activation process and identify whether the delay is in order validation, provisioning or system handoff.»"]},{"heading":"234. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"235. WHEN PROSPECT ASKS","paragraphs":["«Τι ακριβώς κάνετε;»"]},{"heading":"236. Don't give:","paragraphs":["11-minute speech."]},{"heading":"237. Simple answer:","paragraphs":["«Η DISTILLOGIC σχεδιάζει και υλοποιεί custom software, integrations, data and AI solutions for business processes that standard systems don't cover well. Συνήθως ξεκινάμε από συγκεκριμένο operational problem rather than from technology.»"]},{"heading":"238. Then:","paragraphs":["back to them."]},{"heading":"239. > «Στη δική σας περίπτωση προσπαθώ πρώτα να καταλάβω αν υπάρχει πραγματικά τέτοιο gap.»","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"240. GOOD","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"241. WHEN ASKED","paragraphs":["«Έχετε λύση έτοιμη;»"]},{"heading":"242. Answer honestly:","paragraphs":["custom model."]},{"heading":"243. Don't pretend:","paragraphs":["product exists."]},{"heading":"244. WHEN ASKED","paragraphs":["«Τι κοστίζει;»"]},{"heading":"245. Do not evade.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"246. Say:","paragraphs":["«Depends on scope. The main cost drivers are workflows, integrations, users and criticality. Once we understand those, we can give a meaningful range.»"]},{"heading":"247. IF THEY DEMAND RANGE","paragraphs":["and you have internal pricing: give: responsible range."]},{"heading":"248. Do not invent:","paragraphs":["on the phone."]},{"heading":"249. WHEN TARGET SAYS","paragraphs":["«Ποιος σας έδωσε το τηλέφωνό μου;»"]},{"heading":"250. Be truthful.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 251–275 · NEVER invent:",[{"heading":"251. NEVER invent:","paragraphs":["referral."]},{"heading":"252. WHEN THEY SOUND ANNOYED","paragraphs":["Don't push."]},{"heading":"253. Say:","paragraphs":["«Κατανοητό, δεν θέλω να σας πιέσω. Ευχαριστώ για τον χρόνο σας.»"]},{"heading":"254. BRAND FIRST","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"255. CALL BLOCKS","paragraphs":["Salesperson can work: focused blocks."]},{"heading":"256. But:","paragraphs":["enterprise calls: should not become: call-center metric."]},{"heading":"257. Quality:","paragraphs":["matters."]},{"heading":"258. Measure:","paragraphs":["not only: calls/day."]},{"heading":"259. Measure:","paragraphs":["Relevant conversations Meetings created Qualified pain found Correct stakeholder access Next steps."]},{"heading":"260. 50 CALLS","paragraphs":["with no research: may be worse: than 10 good calls."]},{"heading":"261. KPI — CONNECT RATE","paragraphs":["Useful."]},{"heading":"262. KPI — CONVERSATION RATE","paragraphs":["Useful."]},{"heading":"263. KPI — MEETING RATE","paragraphs":["Useful."]},{"heading":"264. But most important:","paragraphs":["QUALIFIED OPPORTUNITIES CREATED."]},{"heading":"265. BAD KPI","paragraphs":["«Salesperson made 200 calls.»"]},{"heading":"266. So what?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"267. MANAGER SHOULD LISTEN","paragraphs":["to calls: for quality."]},{"heading":"268. Score:","paragraphs":["Opening Relevance Tone Question Listening Objection CTA."]},{"heading":"269. COLD CALL SCORECARD","paragraphs":["Opening:__/5"]},{"heading":"270. Relevance:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"271. Research:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"272. Question quality:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"273. Listening:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"274. Next step:","paragraphs":["__/5 Total: __/30."]},{"heading":"275. 26–30","paragraphs":["Ready for strong accounts."]}]],["Σημεία 276–300 · 21–25",[{"heading":"276. 21–25","paragraphs":["Good."]},{"heading":"277. 16–20","paragraphs":["Needs coaching."]},{"heading":"278. Below 16","paragraphs":["No Tier A calls."]},{"heading":"279. EMAIL SCORECARD","paragraphs":["Personal relevance:__/5"]},{"heading":"280. Trigger:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"281. Hypothesis:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"282. Clarity:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"283. Brevity:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"284. CTA:","paragraphs":["__/5 Total:__/30."]},{"heading":"285. LINKEDIN SCORECARD","paragraphs":["Profile relevance:__/5"]},{"heading":"286. Connection approach:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"287. No premature pitch:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"288. Business context:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"289. Question quality:","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"290. Follow-up:","paragraphs":["__/5 Total:__/30."]},{"heading":"291. ROLEPLAY 1","paragraphs":["Prospect: «Δεν ενδιαφέρομαι.» Salesperson: «Κατανοητό. Είναι επειδή το θέμα δεν αποτελεί priority ή το έχετε ήδη καλύψει;»"]},{"heading":"292. ROLEPLAY 2","paragraphs":["Prospect: «Έχουμε supplier.» Salesperson: «Αν σας καλύπτει πλήρως, δεν υπάρχει λόγος να αλλάξετε. Υπάρχει κάποιο gap που μένει unresolved ή όχι;»"]},{"heading":"293. ROLEPLAY 3","paragraphs":["Prospect: «Στείλε email.» Salesperson: «Βεβαίως. Ποιο θέμα θα είχε περισσότερο νόημα να καλύψω ώστε να μη σας στείλω generic material;»"]},{"heading":"294. ROLEPLAY 4","paragraphs":["Prospect: «Τι πουλάτε;» Salesperson: «Custom software and integrations γύρω από operational problems που standard systems δεν λύνουν καλά. Στη δική σας περίπτωση δεν ξέρω ακόμα αν υπάρχει fit, γι' αυτό σας πήρα για το συγκεκριμένο θέμα της επέκτασης.»"]},{"heading":"295. ROLEPLAY 5","paragraphs":["Prospect: «Ποιος σας είπε ότι έχουμε πρόβλημα;» Salesperson: «Κανείς. Δεν γνωρίζω ότι έχετε πρόβλημα. Είδα την επέκταση και είναι απλώς μία hypothesis based on the change. Γι' αυτό ρωτάω αντί να υποθέσω.»"]},{"heading":"296. EXCELLENT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"297. ROLEPLAY 6","paragraphs":["Prospect: «Έχουμε δικό μας IT.» Salesperson: «Τότε μπορεί να μη χρειάζεστε external supplier. Το question είναι αν υπάρχει capacity or specialist gap σε κάποιο συγκεκριμένο initiative.»"]},{"heading":"298. ROLEPLAY 7","paragraphs":["CIO: «Δεν θέλω άλλους vendors.» Salesperson: «Κατανοητό. Αν το υπάρχον vendor landscape καλύπτει τις ανάγκες, δεν θα προσθέταμε αξία. Υπάρχει κάποιο area όπου σήμερα έχετε unresolved capacity or integration issue;»"]},{"heading":"299. ROLEPLAY 8","paragraphs":["COO: «Έχω 2 λεπτά.» Salesperson: «Τότε μία μόνο ερώτηση. Καθώς μεγαλώνετε τις operations, ποια process δυσκολεύεται περισσότερο να scale χωρίς περισσότερο manual coordination;»"]},{"heading":"300. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 301–325 · ROLEPLAY 9",[{"heading":"301. ROLEPLAY 9","paragraphs":["CFO: «Δεν έχω ιδέα ποιοι είστε.» Salesperson: «Φυσικά. Είμαστε technology delivery company, αλλά δεν σας καλώ για generic presentation. Σας καλώ επειδή είδα Χ αλλαγή και ήθελα να καταλάβω αν δημιουργεί Y operational/financial issue.»"]},{"heading":"302. ROLEPLAY 10","paragraphs":["Prospect: «Καλέστε σε έξι μήνες.» Salesperson: «Βεβαίως. Τι περιμένετε να αλλάξει σε έξι μήνες ώστε να σημειώσω σωστά το trigger και να μην σας ενοχλήσω άσκοπα νωρίτερα;»"]},{"heading":"303. VERY GOOD","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"304. ROLEPLAY 11","paragraphs":["Gatekeeper: «Τι αφορά;» Salesperson: «Προσπαθώ να βρω ποιος έχει ownership για το συγκεκριμένο operational workflow. Δεν θέλω να σας δώσω λάθος όνομα. Είναι συνήθως Operations ή IT στην εταιρεία σας;»"]},{"heading":"305. ROLEPLAY 12","paragraphs":["Executive Assistant: «Στείλτε το σε εμένα.» Salesperson: «Βεβαίως. Θα σας στείλω δύο πολύ σύντομες παραγράφους με το συγκεκριμένο context, ώστε να κρίνετε εύκολα αν αξίζει να το προωθήσετε.»"]},{"heading":"306. PROFESSIONAL","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"307. ROLEPLAY 13","paragraphs":["Prospect: «Δεν θέλω παρουσίαση.» Salesperson: «Ούτε εγώ θα πρότεινα presentation χωρίς να ξέρουμε αν υπάρχει relevant problem. Θα προτιμούσα πρώτα μία σύντομη business conversation.»"]},{"heading":"308. ROLEPLAY 14","paragraphs":["Prospect: «Τι θέλετε από εμένα;» Salesperson: «Να καταλάβω αν το συγκεκριμένο process αποτελεί πραγματικό θέμα. Αν όχι, το κλείνουμε εκεί. Αν ναι, βλέπουμε αν αξίζει δεύτερη συζήτηση με τους σωστούς ανθρώπους.»"]},{"heading":"309. STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"310. ROLEPLAY 15","paragraphs":["Prospect: «Δεν παίρνω αποφάσεις για IT.» Salesperson: «Δεν ψάχνω απαραίτητα IT decision-maker. Προσπαθώ να καταλάβω ποιος owns the business process first. Ποιος έχει αυτή την ευθύνη;»"]},{"heading":"311. CRITICAL LESSON","paragraphs":["Don't automatically: start with IT."]},{"heading":"312. BUSINESS PROBLEM","paragraphs":["often: owned by business."]},{"heading":"313. IT:","paragraphs":["technical stakeholder."]},{"heading":"314. EMAIL EXERCISE","paragraphs":["Bad: «Dear Sir,We are a leading innovative company offering customized technological solutions in AI, software development, cloud, mobile applications...»"]},{"heading":"315. STOP.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"316. Better:","paragraphs":["«I saw that you're adding two new distribution centers. I'm curious how you're handling the increase in order and client-status data across WMS/TMS systems. Is that becoming more manual as the network grows?»"]},{"heading":"317. SIMPLE","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"318. LINKEDIN EXERCISE","paragraphs":["Bad connection: «Hello, I would like to offer our software-development services.»"]},{"heading":"319. Better:","paragraphs":["«Hi Maria, I follow your work around operations transformation. Glad to connect.»"]},{"heading":"320. After accepted:","paragraphs":["business question."]},{"heading":"321. DAILY TRAINING","paragraphs":["Every salesperson: select: 5 target accounts."]},{"heading":"322. For each:","paragraphs":["write: Trigger Person Hypothesis Opening Question."]},{"heading":"323. Manager:","paragraphs":["approves Tier A."]},{"heading":"324. THEN","paragraphs":["outreach."]},{"heading":"325. NOT","paragraphs":["outreach first: research later."]}]],["Σημεία 326–350 · WEEKLY EXERCISE",[{"heading":"326. WEEKLY EXERCISE","paragraphs":["Choose: one account."]},{"heading":"327. Build:","paragraphs":["CEO email CIO email COO email."]},{"heading":"328. Same company.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"329. Different:","paragraphs":["language/value lens."]},{"heading":"330. Example — logistics expansion","paragraphs":["CEO: growth/risk."]},{"heading":"331. COO:","paragraphs":["process/capacity."]},{"heading":"332. CIO:","paragraphs":["systems/integration."]},{"heading":"333. This teaches:","paragraphs":["persona relevance."]},{"heading":"334. TEAM LEADER REVIEW","paragraphs":["Before major outreach: ask salesperson: «Why this account?»"]},{"heading":"335. Then:","paragraphs":["«Why this person?»"]},{"heading":"336. Then:","paragraphs":["«Why now?»"]},{"heading":"337. Then:","paragraphs":["«What question are you trying to answer?»"]},{"heading":"338. Last:","paragraphs":["«What is the desired next step?»"]},{"heading":"339. If salesperson cannot answer:","paragraphs":["not ready."]},{"heading":"340. TIER A PROTECTION","paragraphs":["Before first contact: Account assigned. CRM checked. Research complete. Stakeholder identified. Hypothesis approved. Message reviewed."]},{"heading":"341. WHY?","paragraphs":["One bad message: can damage: strategic account."]},{"heading":"342. DON'T TEST","paragraphs":["beginner script: on biggest company."]},{"heading":"343. NEW SALESPERSON","paragraphs":["starts: Tier C."]},{"heading":"344. Learns:","paragraphs":["tone, questions, CRM discipline."]},{"heading":"345. Then:","paragraphs":["Tier B."]},{"heading":"346. Finally:","paragraphs":["Tier A."]},{"heading":"347. COLD OUTREACH GOLDEN RULE #1","paragraphs":["«Start with the customer, not with DISTILLOGIC.»"]},{"heading":"348. GOLDEN RULE #2","paragraphs":["«Use a real trigger whenever possible.»"]},{"heading":"349. GOLDEN RULE #3","paragraphs":["«A trigger creates a hypothesis — not proof of pain.»"]},{"heading":"350. GOLDEN RULE #4","paragraphs":["«The first call is not a product demo.»"]}]],["Σημεία 351–358 · GOLDEN RULE #5",[{"heading":"351. GOLDEN RULE #5","paragraphs":["«Ask one good question, then listen.»"]},{"heading":"352. GOLDEN RULE #6","paragraphs":["«Don't pitch everyone in the account with the same message.»"]},{"heading":"353. GOLDEN RULE #7","paragraphs":["«Never lie to a gatekeeper.»"]},{"heading":"354. GOLDEN RULE #8","paragraphs":["«Don't spam follow-ups that add no value.»"]},{"heading":"355. GOLDEN RULE #9","paragraphs":["«A meeting is valuable only if there is a clear objective.»"]},{"heading":"356. GOLDEN RULE #10","paragraphs":["«Protect the account even when the prospect says no.»"]},{"heading":"357. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["SELECT ACCOUNT ↓ CHECK CRM ↓ RESEARCH ↓ FIND TRIGGER ↓ BUILD VALUE HYPOTHESIS ↓ SELECT STAKEHOLDER ↓ WRITE ROLE-SPECIFIC OPENING ↓ CALL / EMAIL / LINKEDIN ↓ ASK BUSINESS QUESTION ↓ LISTEN ↓ IDENTIFY RELEVANCE ↓ IF NO FIT → EXIT PROFESSIONALLY ↓ IF POSSIBLE FIT → ASK 1–2 DISCOVERY QUESTIONS ↓ AGREE SPECIFIC NEXT MEETING ↓ RECORD EVERYTHING IN CRM ↓ CONTINUE ACCOUNT STRATEGY."]},{"heading":"358. Η ΜΙΑ ΦΡΑΣΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΘΥΜΑΤΑΙ Ο ΠΩΛΗΤΗΣ","paragraphs":["«Στο enterprise cold outreach δεν παίρνω τηλέφωνο για να εξηγήσω τι κάνει η DISTILLOGIC. Επικοινωνώ επειδή έχω βρει έναν συγκεκριμένο λόγο για τον οποίο ίσως αξίζει να μιλήσουμε, κάνω μία έξυπνη ερώτηση για να δω αν υπάρχει πραγματικό business problem και, μόνο αν υπάρχει, κερδίζω το δικαίωμα για την επόμενη συζήτηση.» ΑΥΤΟ ΕΙΝΑΙ ENTERPRISE PROSPECTING."]}]],["Πριν απαντήσεις στο quiz",["Ξανασκέψου το εισαγωγικό περιστατικό. Ποιο γεγονός είναι επιβεβαιωμένο, ποια πληροφορία λείπει και ποια ενέργεια θα μείωνε την αβεβαιότητα; Μία απάντηση μπορεί να ακούγεται εμπορικά ελκυστική αλλά να προηγείται της απαιτούμενης επιβεβαίωσης.","Οι δύο ερωτήσεις εφαρμογής γενικών αρχών συνδέονται και με τις προαιρετικές «Γενικές σημειώσεις». Το PDF βρίσκεται μόνιμα στο μενού, δεν αποτελεί ξεχωριστό υποχρεωτικό μάθημα και η ανάγνωσή του δεν βαθμολογείται.","Η παρουσίαση πρέπει να αποδεικνύει ότι άκουσες και να βοηθά συγκεκριμένη απόφαση. Γενικές σημειώσεις: παρουσίαση χωρίς feature dump.","Η κοινωνική απόδειξη είναι χρήσιμη όταν το πλαίσιο και η τεκμηρίωση παραμένουν σαφή. Γενικές σημειώσεις: social proof και storytelling."]]],"scenario":["Βρίσκεις ανακοίνωση νέου εργοστασίου και θέλεις να επικοινωνήσεις με τον υπεύθυνο λειτουργίας χωρίς γενικό μήνυμα μαζικής πώλησης.","Αναφέρω την επιβεβαιωμένη επέκταση, πιθανό σχετικό πρόβλημα ως υπόθεση και μία ερώτηση διερεύνησης. Γεγονός, υπόθεση και ερώτηση παραμένουν διακριτά."],"minutes":32,"version":1,"additional_curriculum":37,"question_rows":[["Βρίσκεις ανακοίνωση νέου εργοστασίου και θέλεις να επικοινωνήσεις με τον υπεύθυνο λειτουργίας χωρίς γενικό μήνυμα μαζικής πώλησης. Ποιο άνοιγμα διατηρεί ειλικρίνεια και συνάφεια;","Αναφέρω την επιβεβαιωμένη επέκταση, πιθανό σχετικό πρόβλημα ως υπόθεση και μία ερώτηση διερεύνησης.","Δηλώνω ότι γνωρίζω πως το εργοστάσιο έχει σοβαρές καθυστερήσεις.","Παρουσιάζω όλο το portfolio πριν ζητήσω άδεια συζήτησης.","Υπονοώ ότι υπάρχει ήδη συμφωνία με τη διοίκηση.","Γεγονός, υπόθεση και ερώτηση παραμένουν διακριτά."],["Βρίσκεις ανακοίνωση νέου εργοστασίου και θέλεις να επικοινωνήσεις με τον υπεύθυνο λειτουργίας χωρίς γενικό μήνυμα μαζικής πώλησης. Ποιος είναι ο λογικός πρώτος στόχος επικοινωνίας;","Ο αρμόδιος του συγκεκριμένου προβλήματος, με επαλήθευση του ρόλου του.","Πάντα ο CEO ανεξάρτητα από το αντικείμενο.","Όλοι οι εργαζόμενοι ταυτόχρονα με το ίδιο μήνυμα.","Ο πιο ενεργός χρήστης κοινωνικών δικτύων ανεξάρτητα από αρμοδιότητα.","Το σημείο εισόδου επιλέγεται με βάση τη σχετική ευθύνη."],["Βρίσκεις ανακοίνωση νέου εργοστασίου και θέλεις να επικοινωνήσεις με τον υπεύθυνο λειτουργίας χωρίς γενικό μήνυμα μαζικής πώλησης. Τι δεν αποδεικνύει μια δημόσια εταιρική διεύθυνση email;","Αυτόματη άδεια για κάθε είδος προωθητικής αποστολής.","Ότι μπορούμε να ερευνήσουμε δημόσια εταιρικά στοιχεία.","Ότι η εταιρεία έχει online παρουσία.","Ότι χρειάζεται να ελέγξουμε την καταλληλότητα του παραλήπτη.","Η διαθεσιμότητα στοιχείων δεν υποκαθιστά τον έλεγχο των κανόνων επικοινωνίας."],["Μετά από discovery ο πελάτης ζητά παρουσίαση. Ποια διάταξη είναι πιο χρήσιμη για αξιολόγηση;","Επιβεβαιωμένο πρόβλημα, σχετική διαδρομή λύσης, τεκμήριο/όρια και συγκεκριμένο επόμενο βήμα.","Πλήρης κατάλογος λειτουργιών από τη λιγότερο στη περισσότερο τεχνική.","Ιστορικό εταιρείας και όλα τα λογότυπα πελατών πριν αναφερθεί η ανάγκη.","Όλες οι διαθέσιμες τιμές χωρίς σύνδεση με το συμφωνημένο αντικείμενο.","Η παρουσίαση πρέπει να αποδεικνύει ότι άκουσες και να βοηθά συγκεκριμένη απόφαση. Γενικές σημειώσεις: παρουσίαση χωρίς feature dump."],["Ένα case study πέτυχε μεγάλη εξοικονόμηση σε διαφορετική εταιρεία. Πώς το χρησιμοποιείς υπεύθυνα;","Εξηγώ το πλαίσιο και τις διαφορές και το χρησιμοποιώ ως ένδειξη προς αξιολόγηση, όχι εγγύηση ίδιου αποτελέσματος.","Μεταφέρω το ίδιο ποσοστό στο νέο business case επειδή πρόκειται για τον ίδιο κλάδο.","Αφαιρώ τους περιορισμούς για να μην αποδυναμωθεί η παρουσίαση.","Θεωρώ περιττή τη συλλογή baseline αφού υπάρχει προηγούμενο αποτέλεσμα.","Η κοινωνική απόδειξη είναι χρήσιμη όταν το πλαίσιο και η τεκμηρίωση παραμένουν σαφή. Γενικές σημειώσεις: social proof και storytelling."]],"source_note":"Πηγή: ΜΑΘΗΜΑ 31.docx, κεφάλαιο 53. Διατηρείται το κείμενο των αριθμημένων σημείων, με ενοποίηση των σπασμένων γραμμών και αφαίρεση επαναλαμβανόμενης μορφοποίησης. Τα παραδείγματα δεν αλλάζουν τους κανόνες της εφαρμογής."},"di-enterprise-54":{"pillar":"distillogic","title":"54. Πρώτο meeting και διερεύνηση αναγκών","goal":"Να αναγνωρίζεις πραγματικές ανάγκες, να διερευνάς τα στοιχεία και να επιλέγεις υπεύθυνο επόμενο βήμα.","sections":[["Από την έννοια στην επαγγελματική πράξη",["Σε συνάντηση 30 λεπτών ο πελάτης ζητά demo αμέσως, αλλά δεν έχει εξηγήσει ποια διαδικασία θέλει να βελτιώσει.","Στη μελέτη που ακολουθεί σύνδεσε κάθε πιθανή λύση με συγκεκριμένη διαδικασία, υπεύθυνο, επίπτωση και στοιχεία που μπορούν να επαληθευτούν. Η τεχνική δυνατότητα, η οικονομική αξία και η εξουσιοδότηση για απόφαση είναι διαφορετικά ερωτήματα. Τα παραδείγματα του κεφαλαίου σε βοηθούν να τα διερευνάς χωρίς να υπόσχεσαι κάτι που δεν έχει εγκριθεί.","Η ύλη περιγράφει ενδεικτικές επιχειρηματικές ανάγκες και μεθόδους πώλησης. Δεν αποτελεί κατάλογο έτοιμων λειτουργιών των δύο CRM, δεσμευτική προσφορά, αλλαγή αμοιβών ή νέα πολιτική πιστοποίησης. Για πραγματική εργασία ισχύουν οι εγκεκριμένοι εταιρικοί όροι και οι αρμοδιότητες. Το μάθημα 60 είναι προετοιμασία, όχι δεύτερη επίσημη τελική εξέταση."]],["Το αντικείμενο του κεφαλαίου",["ΠΡΩΤΟ MEETING ΚΑΙ DISCOVERY ΣΤΗΝ ΠΡΑΞΗ Πώς κάνουμε ένα 30λεπτο enterprise meeting που οδηγεί σε πραγματικό επόμενο βήμα"]],["Σημεία 1–25 · Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ",[{"heading":"1. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ","paragraphs":["Το πρώτο meeting: δεν είναι: PRESENTATION. Είναι: DIAGNOSIS."]},{"heading":"2. Ο ΣΤΟΧΟΣ","paragraphs":["Στο τέλος του meeting: πρέπει να ξέρουμε: Τι συμβαίνει σήμερα. Πού υπάρχει πρόβλημα. Τι impact έχει. Πόσο σημαντικό είναι. Ποιοι εμπλέκονται. Ποιο είναι το σωστό επόμενο βήμα."]},{"heading":"3. ΔΕΝ ΧΡΕΙΑΖΕΤΑΙ","paragraphs":["να ξέρουμε: τα πάντα."]},{"heading":"4. ΧΡΕΙΑΖΕΤΑΙ","paragraphs":["να ξέρουμε: αρκετά: ώστε να αποφασίσουμε: CONTINUE OR NOT."]},{"heading":"5. ΤΟ 30-MINUTE MEETING","paragraphs":["Μπορεί να χωριστεί:"]},{"heading":"6. 0–3 MINUTES","paragraphs":["Opening."]},{"heading":"7. 3–20 MINUTES","paragraphs":["Discovery."]},{"heading":"8. 20–25 MINUTES","paragraphs":["Summary / validation."]},{"heading":"9. 25–30 MINUTES","paragraphs":["Next step."]},{"heading":"10. FIRST 2 MINUTES","paragraphs":["Ο salesperson: δεν πρέπει: να αρχίσει: με 15 slides."]},{"heading":"11. SIMPLE OPENING","paragraphs":["«Ευχαριστώ για τον χρόνο σας. Ο στόχος μου σήμερα δεν είναι να σας κάνω generic παρουσίαση. Θα ήθελα πρώτα να καταλάβω πώς λειτουργεί σήμερα το συγκεκριμένο process, πού υπάρχουν δυσκολίες και αν υπάρχει κάτι που αξίζει να εξετάσουμε μαζί. Αν στο τέλος δεν υπάρχει fit, το λέμε ξεκάθαρα.»"]},{"heading":"12. WHY THIS WORKS","paragraphs":["Removes pressure."]},{"heading":"13. Then:","paragraphs":["brief context."]},{"heading":"14. > «Από την έρευνά μας είδαμε Χ αλλαγή και αυτό μας έκανε να υποθέσουμε ότι ίσως υπάρχει Υ challenge. Δεν ξέρουμε αν ισχύει.»","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"15. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["HYPOTHESIS ≠ FACT."]},{"heading":"16. THEN","paragraphs":["agenda."]},{"heading":"17. > «Αν σας είναι εντάξει, θα ήθελα πρώτα να καταλάβω το current process, μετά το impact και στο τέλος να δούμε ποιο επόμενο βήμα έχει νόημα.»","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"18. AGENDA","paragraphs":["creates: structure."]},{"heading":"19. DON'T OVERDO","paragraphs":["agenda."]},{"heading":"20. No:","paragraphs":["10 bullets."]},{"heading":"21. FIRST QUESTION","paragraphs":["One of the strongest: «Μπορείτε να μου περιγράψετε πώς λειτουργεί σήμερα η διαδικασία από την αρχή μέχρι το τέλος;»"]},{"heading":"22. EXCELLENT","paragraphs":["because: customer speaks."]},{"heading":"23. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["«Walk me through one real recent example.»"]},{"heading":"24. EVEN BETTER","paragraphs":["than: abstract process."]},{"heading":"25. WHY REAL EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Because customer says: what actually happens."]}]],["Σημεία 26–50 · Not:",[{"heading":"26. Not:","paragraphs":["what policy says: should happen."]},{"heading":"27. DISCOVERY LAYER 1","paragraphs":["CURRENT STATE Ask: How does it work today? Who is involved? Which systems? Which approvals? Which documents?"]},{"heading":"28. EXAMPLE — LOGISTICS","paragraphs":["«Walk me through one order from customer receipt μέχρι final delivery.»"]},{"heading":"29. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Order comes by API or email.»"]},{"heading":"30. Don't jump.","paragraphs":["Ask: «What happens to the email orders?»"]},{"heading":"31. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Someone enters them into WMS.»"]},{"heading":"32. NOW","paragraphs":["possible pain."]},{"heading":"33. Ask:","paragraphs":["«How many orders arrive that way?»"]},{"heading":"34. NOW","paragraphs":["quantification starts."]},{"heading":"35. DISCOVERY LAYER 2","paragraphs":["FRICTION Ask: «Πού καθυστερεί συνήθως;»"]},{"heading":"36. Another:","paragraphs":["«Which step creates the most manual work?»"]},{"heading":"37. Another:","paragraphs":["«Where do mistakes occur most often?»"]},{"heading":"38. Another:","paragraphs":["«What requires the most follow-up between teams?»"]},{"heading":"39. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Don't ask: all four."]},{"heading":"40. Follow:","paragraphs":["customer answer."]},{"heading":"41. CUSTOMER","paragraphs":["«Approvals are slow.»"]},{"heading":"42. Weak salesperson:","paragraphs":["writes: “slow approvals” and moves on."]},{"heading":"43. Strong salesperson:","paragraphs":["asks: «Which approval specifically?»"]},{"heading":"44. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Finance approval.»"]},{"heading":"45. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What is Finance usually waiting for?»"]},{"heading":"46. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Supporting documents.»"]},{"heading":"47. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Where do those documents come from?»"]},{"heading":"48. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Three departments.»"]},{"heading":"49. NOW","paragraphs":["real issue: cross-department information gathering."]},{"heading":"50. NOT","paragraphs":["finance approval."]}]],["Σημεία 51–75 · GOLDEN RULE",[{"heading":"51. GOLDEN RULE","paragraphs":["KEEP GOING UNTIL YOU FIND THE REAL BOTTLENECK."]},{"heading":"52. DISCOVERY LAYER 3","paragraphs":["IMPACT Now ask: «What happens because of this delay?»"]},{"heading":"53. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Projects start later.»"]},{"heading":"54. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What does that affect?»"]},{"heading":"55. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Customer delivery.»"]},{"heading":"56. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Can you quantify how often or how long?»"]},{"heading":"57. IMPACT CAN BE","paragraphs":["Time Cost Revenue Risk Customer experience Capacity Rework."]},{"heading":"58. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Pain without impact: may be: annoyance."]},{"heading":"59. Enterprise opportunity:","paragraphs":["usually needs: meaningful impact."]},{"heading":"60. DISCOVERY LAYER 4","paragraphs":["VOLUME Ask: How often? How many? How long? How much?"]},{"heading":"61. Example","paragraphs":["«How many cases per month go through this process?»"]},{"heading":"62. > «How many people touch each case?»","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"63. > «How much time does one case require?»","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"64. Customer provides:","paragraphs":["baseline."]},{"heading":"65. NEVER INVENT","paragraphs":["baseline."]},{"heading":"66. DISCOVERY LAYER 5","paragraphs":["PRIORITY Ask: «Why is this important now?»"]},{"heading":"67. VERY IMPORTANT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"68. Customer:","paragraphs":["may say: «We're opening two locations.»"]},{"heading":"69. Real trigger.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"70. Or:","paragraphs":["«It isn't really priority.»"]},{"heading":"71. Then:","paragraphs":["requalify."]},{"heading":"72. Don't push.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"73. OTHER PRIORITY QUESTION","paragraphs":["«What happens if nothing changes over the next 12 months?»"]},{"heading":"74. Powerful.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"75. But ask:","paragraphs":["naturally."]}]],["Σημεία 76–100 · Don't sound:",[{"heading":"76. Don't sound:","paragraphs":["dramatic."]},{"heading":"77. DISCOVERY LAYER 6","paragraphs":["PREVIOUS ATTEMPTS Ask: «What have you already tried?»"]},{"heading":"78. Very useful.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"79. Customer may say:","paragraphs":["New tool. Internal automation. Consultant. Nothing."]},{"heading":"80. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What worked and what didn't?»"]},{"heading":"81. This prevents:","paragraphs":["repeating failed solution."]},{"heading":"82. DISCOVERY LAYER 7","paragraphs":["DESIRED STATE Ask: «If this process worked the way you wanted, what would be different?»"]},{"heading":"83. Customer:","paragraphs":["defines: success."]},{"heading":"84. Examples:","paragraphs":["Process completes same day. No manual re-entry. Management sees live status. Customer can self-serve."]},{"heading":"85. THAT BECOMES","paragraphs":["success criteria."]},{"heading":"86. DISCOVERY LAYER 8","paragraphs":["STAKEHOLDERS Ask: «Who else is affected by this process?»"]},{"heading":"87. Then:","paragraphs":["«Who owns the process?»"]},{"heading":"88. Then:","paragraphs":["«Who would need to be comfortable with a change?»"]},{"heading":"89. We are building:","paragraphs":["buying committee."]},{"heading":"90. Customer says:","paragraphs":["«Operations owns it, but IT and Finance need to approve.»"]},{"heading":"91. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"92. Now:","paragraphs":["stakeholder map begins."]},{"heading":"93. DISCOVERY LAYER 9","paragraphs":["DECISION PROCESS Ask: naturally: «If you decided to improve this, how would a project like this normally be approved internally?»"]},{"heading":"94. Not:","paragraphs":["«Who signs the cheque?»"]},{"heading":"95. Better:","paragraphs":["professional language."]},{"heading":"96. Customer may explain:","paragraphs":["Business case CIO review Security Procurement CFO."]},{"heading":"97. This information:","paragraphs":["critical."]},{"heading":"98. DISCOVERY LAYER 10","paragraphs":["TECHNICAL LANDSCAPE Only when relevant."]},{"heading":"99. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which systems currently support the process?»"]},{"heading":"100. > «Where is the source of truth?»","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 101–125 · > «Are integrations already available?»",[{"heading":"101. > «Are integrations already available?»","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"102. Salesperson does not:","paragraphs":["architect."]},{"heading":"103. They identify:","paragraphs":["technical questions: for specialist."]},{"heading":"104. IF CUSTOMER ASKS","paragraphs":["«Can you integrate with SAP?»"]},{"heading":"105. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["yes automatically."]},{"heading":"106. Say:","paragraphs":["«We work with enterprise integrations, but we'd want our technical team to validate the specific SAP environment, interfaces and constraints before committing.»"]},{"heading":"107. CORRECT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"108. THE 70/30 RULE","paragraphs":["As a general coaching target: customer speaks: around 70%. Salesperson: 30%."]},{"heading":"109. Not mathematical law.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"110. But if salesperson talks:","paragraphs":["20 minutes: something is wrong."]},{"heading":"111. SALESPERSON'S JOB","paragraphs":["is: ask listen connect."]},{"heading":"112. ACTIVE LISTENING","paragraphs":["Customer says: «The process is chaotic.»"]},{"heading":"113. Don't say:","paragraphs":["«We can automate it.»"]},{"heading":"114. Say:","paragraphs":["«When you say chaotic, what does that look like in practice?»"]},{"heading":"115. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"116. Customer says:","paragraphs":["«Too much manual work.»"]},{"heading":"117. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which manual step consumes the most time?»"]},{"heading":"118. Customer says:","paragraphs":["«We don't have visibility.»"]},{"heading":"119. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Visibility into what specifically?»"]},{"heading":"120. LANGUAGE MATTERS","paragraphs":["Words like: inefficient slow manual bad visibility are: too broad."]},{"heading":"121. We need:","paragraphs":["specific."]},{"heading":"122. NEVER ASSUME","paragraphs":["what customer means."]},{"heading":"123. MIRRORING","paragraphs":["Use customer wording."]},{"heading":"124. Customer:","paragraphs":["«We have order fallout.»"]},{"heading":"125. Salesperson:","paragraphs":["«When an order falls out, what happens next?»"]}]],["Σημεία 126–150 · Good.",[{"heading":"126. Good.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"127. SUMMARIZING DURING DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Every few minutes: «So if I understood correctly...»"]},{"heading":"128. Example:","paragraphs":["«So currently the order enters automatically, but around 15% needs manual intervention because address and inventory data don't match. Correct?»"]},{"heading":"129. Customer:","paragraphs":["corrects."]},{"heading":"130. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"131. DON'T FEAR CORRECTION","paragraphs":["Correction: improves understanding."]},{"heading":"132. NOTE TAKING","paragraphs":["Take notes: but don't: stare at laptop entire meeting."]},{"heading":"133. Capture:","paragraphs":["Facts Pain Impact Metrics People Systems Unknowns Next steps."]},{"heading":"134. SIMPLE NOTE FORMAT","paragraphs":["FACT:"]},{"heading":"135. PAIN:","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"136. IMPACT:","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"137. METRIC:","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"138. STAKEHOLDERS:","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"139. SYSTEMS:","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"140. UNKNOWN:","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"141. NEXT STEP:","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"142. DON'T MIX","paragraphs":["fact with: assumption."]},{"heading":"143. Example:","paragraphs":["FACT: Customer processes 4,000 orders/day."]},{"heading":"144. FACT:","paragraphs":["200 require manual review."]},{"heading":"145. ASSUMPTION:","paragraphs":["Automation could reduce manual review."]},{"heading":"146. Keep separate.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"147. IMPORTANT FOR CRM","paragraphs":["Do not write: assumption: as customer fact."]},{"heading":"148. MULTIPLE PEOPLE IN MEETING","paragraphs":["If 4 customer attendees: don't only talk: to senior person."]},{"heading":"149. Ask:","paragraphs":["Operations: process."]},{"heading":"150. IT:","paragraphs":["systems."]}]],["Σημεία 151–175 · Finance:",[{"heading":"151. Finance:","paragraphs":["impact."]},{"heading":"152. But:","paragraphs":["don't interrogate each person."]},{"heading":"153. CONNECT VIEWS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"154. Example","paragraphs":["Operations: «Approval is slow.»"]},{"heading":"155. Ask Finance:","paragraphs":["«From your side, what usually prevents approval from happening faster?»"]},{"heading":"156. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"157. Now we uncover:","paragraphs":["different perspective."]},{"heading":"158. CONFLICT IN MEETING","paragraphs":["Operations says: «IT is the problem.»"]},{"heading":"159. IT says:","paragraphs":["«Business requirements are unclear.»"]},{"heading":"160. Salesperson should not:","paragraphs":["choose side."]},{"heading":"161. Say:","paragraphs":["«It sounds like the handoff between requirement definition and technical execution may be the issue. Could we map one recent example together?»"]},{"heading":"162. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"163. REMAIN NEUTRAL","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"164. DISCOVERY IS NOT","paragraphs":["customer therapy."]},{"heading":"165. Stay:","paragraphs":["business-focused."]},{"heading":"166. EXECUTIVE IN MEETING","paragraphs":["CEO joins: for 10 minutes."]},{"heading":"167. Don't ask:","paragraphs":["15 operational questions."]},{"heading":"168. Ask:","paragraphs":["«From your perspective, what business outcome makes this initiative important?»"]},{"heading":"169. Then:","paragraphs":["«What would make this project worth the investment?»"]},{"heading":"170. Excellent executive questions.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"171. CFO","paragraphs":["Ask: «What impact matters enough to justify investment — cost, working capital, revenue, risk or capacity?»"]},{"heading":"172. CIO","paragraphs":["Ask: «What architecture or supportability concerns would prevent this from moving forward even if the business case is strong?»"]},{"heading":"173. COO","paragraphs":["Ask: «Which process constraint is currently hardest to scale operationally?»"]},{"heading":"174. ROLE-BASED DISCOVERY","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"175. DON'T ASK CFO","paragraphs":["about: button layout."]}]],["Σημεία 176–200 · DON'T ASK CEO",[{"heading":"176. DON'T ASK CEO","paragraphs":["which database."]},{"heading":"177. DON'T ASK CIO","paragraphs":["only: ROI."]},{"heading":"178. ADAPT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"179. CUSTOMER ASKS EARLY","paragraphs":["«Tell us about Distillogic.»"]},{"heading":"180. Answer:","paragraphs":["short."]},{"heading":"181. > «DISTILLOGIC designs and delivers custom software, integrations, data and AI solutions around business processes where existing systems don't cover the requirement well. Rather than assume which technology you need, we'd like to understand the workflow first.»","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"182. Then:","paragraphs":["back to discovery."]},{"heading":"183. 30–60 seconds.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"184. Not:","paragraphs":["10 minutes."]},{"heading":"185. CUSTOMER ASKS","paragraphs":["«What solutions have you got?»"]},{"heading":"186. Answer:","paragraphs":["capability categories."]},{"heading":"187. But:","paragraphs":["don't present catalog."]},{"heading":"188. > «Depending on the problem, that can mean workflow automation, system integrations, custom web applications, data platforms or carefully scoped AI. Which of those becomes relevant depends on what we discover in the process.»","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"189. GOOD","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"190. DISCOVERY MISTAKE #1","paragraphs":["ASKING LEADING QUESTIONS Bad: «Wouldn't automation save you lots of time?»"]},{"heading":"191. This pushes:","paragraphs":["desired answer."]},{"heading":"192. Better:","paragraphs":["«How much time does the current process consume?»"]},{"heading":"193. MISTAKE #2","paragraphs":["PITCHING AFTER FIRST PAIN Customer: «We use Excel.» Sales: «We can build app!»"]},{"heading":"194. Wrong.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"195. Excel:","paragraphs":["may be fine."]},{"heading":"196. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What problem does Excel create today?»"]},{"heading":"197. Maybe:","paragraphs":["none."]},{"heading":"198. MISTAKE #3","paragraphs":["ASKING TOO MANY QUESTIONS 20 questions: without conversation."]},{"heading":"199. Feels:","paragraphs":["like survey."]},{"heading":"200. Ask:","paragraphs":["one. Listen. Follow."]}]],["Σημεία 201–225 · MISTAKE #4",[{"heading":"201. MISTAKE #4","paragraphs":["SOLVING DURING DISCOVERY Customer: describes pain. Salesperson: starts designing."]},{"heading":"202. Too early.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"203. Capture:","paragraphs":["don't solve: everything live."]},{"heading":"204. MISTAKE #5","paragraphs":["NO QUANTIFICATION Great conversation. No metrics."]},{"heading":"205. Then:","paragraphs":["business case weak."]},{"heading":"206. Ask:","paragraphs":["«How often?» «How much time?» «How many people?»"]},{"heading":"207. MISTAKE #6","paragraphs":["IGNORING NO-DECISION Need understand: what happens if: they do nothing."]},{"heading":"208. If:","paragraphs":["nothing serious: project priority: may be low."]},{"heading":"209. MISTAKE #7","paragraphs":["TALKING ONLY TO CHAMPION Need: other stakeholders."]},{"heading":"210. MISTAKE #8","paragraphs":["NO BUYING PROCESS Then: proposal goes: into black hole."]},{"heading":"211. MISTAKE #9","paragraphs":["ENDING WITH «We'll be in touch.»"]},{"heading":"212. Terrible.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"213. Need:","paragraphs":["specific next step."]},{"heading":"214. MISTAKE #10","paragraphs":["SENDING PROPOSAL JUST BECAUSE CUSTOMER ASKED Need enough scope."]},{"heading":"215. NOW","paragraphs":["THE LAST 10 MINUTES"]},{"heading":"216. STOP DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["before meeting ends."]},{"heading":"217. Don't continue asking:","paragraphs":["until minute 30."]},{"heading":"218. Around minute 20–22:","paragraphs":["summarize."]},{"heading":"219. SUMMARY FORMAT","paragraphs":["«Let me make sure I've understood this correctly.»"]},{"heading":"220. Then:","paragraphs":["Current process. Main pain. Impact. Priority. Stakeholders."]},{"heading":"221. Example:","paragraphs":["«Today customer requests come through email and portal. Around 25% need manual re-entry into the ERP, which takes about 40 team hours per week and creates delays during peak periods. With the new site launching in Q1, your priority is to reduce this workload before volume grows. Operations owns the process, IT owns integration and Finance needs to approve the business case. Is that accurate?»"]},{"heading":"222. THIS IS POWERFUL","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"223. Customer says:","paragraphs":["yes."]},{"heading":"224. Now:","paragraphs":["next step."]},{"heading":"225. DO NOT SAY","paragraphs":["«We'll send proposal.» unless ready."]}]],["Σημεία 226–250 · Ask:",[{"heading":"226. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Based on what we've discussed, I think the next logical step would be a technical/process workshop to validate the ERP integration and map the 25% exception cases. Does that make sense from your side?»"]},{"heading":"227. Specific.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"228. Then:","paragraphs":["who attends?"]},{"heading":"229. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Who needs to join?»"]},{"heading":"230. Then:","paragraphs":["objective."]},{"heading":"231. > «The objective would be to leave the workshop with confirmed scope, integrations and pilot success criteria.»","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"232. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"233. NEXT STEP TYPES","paragraphs":["Depending stage: Second discovery Technical discovery Solution workshop Data workshop Business-case session Demo PoC definition Proposal review."]},{"heading":"234. Choose:","paragraphs":["right one."]},{"heading":"235. DON'T DEFAULT","paragraphs":["to: demo."]},{"heading":"236. WHEN DEMO IS RIGHT","paragraphs":["Customer: understands problem. Need: evaluate approach/product capability."]},{"heading":"237. WHEN TECHNICAL WORKSHOP","paragraphs":["Integration/security: unknown."]},{"heading":"238. WHEN BUSINESS CASE SESSION","paragraphs":["Pain confirmed: investment needs justification."]},{"heading":"239. WHEN SECOND DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Missing: stakeholders/process details."]},{"heading":"240. WHEN PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["Scope: sufficiently defined."]},{"heading":"241. WHEN TO STOP","paragraphs":["If customer says: problem not priority, no meaningful impact, no change desired."]},{"heading":"242. Say:","paragraphs":["«It sounds like this isn't something you need to invest in right now. I'd rather leave it there than manufacture a project.»"]},{"heading":"243. VERY STRONG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"244. ROLEPLAY 1","paragraphs":["LOGISTICS Customer: «We want a customer portal.»"]},{"heading":"245. Weak salesperson:","paragraphs":["«Great, we build portals.»"]},{"heading":"246. Strong salesperson:","paragraphs":["«What customer problem are you trying to solve with the portal?»"]},{"heading":"247. Customer:","paragraphs":["«They call constantly for status.»"]},{"heading":"248. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which status information do they ask for most?»"]},{"heading":"249. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Order and stock.»"]},{"heading":"250. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Does that information already exist reliably in WMS/TMS?»"]}]],["Σημεία 251–275 · Customer:",[{"heading":"251. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Not always.»"]},{"heading":"252. Insight:","paragraphs":["portal alone: not enough."]},{"heading":"253. Need:","paragraphs":["data reliability."]},{"heading":"254. ROLEPLAY 2","paragraphs":["MANUFACTURING Customer: «We want AI for predictive maintenance.»"]},{"heading":"255. Seller:","paragraphs":["«What equipment failure problem are you trying to reduce today?»"]},{"heading":"256. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Unexpected downtime.»"]},{"heading":"257. Ask:","paragraphs":["«How much downtime and what equipment drives it?»"]},{"heading":"258. Customer:","paragraphs":["«We don't measure it well.»"]},{"heading":"259. First opportunity:","paragraphs":["data foundation."]},{"heading":"260. Not AI model.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"261. ROLEPLAY 3","paragraphs":["PROFESSIONAL SERVICES CEO: «We need better resource planning.»"]},{"heading":"262. Seller:","paragraphs":["«What decision is difficult today because of poor resource visibility?»"]},{"heading":"263. CEO:","paragraphs":["«We don't know whether we can staff new projects.»"]},{"heading":"264. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Where is availability data today?»"]},{"heading":"265. CEO:","paragraphs":["«Project managers' spreadsheets.»"]},{"heading":"266. Root:","paragraphs":["fragmented capacity data."]},{"heading":"267. ROLEPLAY 4","paragraphs":["CORPORATE GROUP CFO: «I need one dashboard.»"]},{"heading":"268. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Which decision do you want the dashboard to improve first?»"]},{"heading":"269. CFO:","paragraphs":["«Customer profitability.»"]},{"heading":"270. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Can customers be matched reliably across subsidiaries today?»"]},{"heading":"271. CFO:","paragraphs":["«No.»"]},{"heading":"272. Root:","paragraphs":["MDM/data."]},{"heading":"273. ROLEPLAY 5","paragraphs":["HOTEL COO: «Guest complaints increased.»"]},{"heading":"274. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Which complaint categories increased most?»"]},{"heading":"275. COO:","paragraphs":["«Room readiness.»"]}]],["Σημεία 276–300 · Ask:",[{"heading":"276. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Walk me through room status from checkout to next check-in.»"]},{"heading":"277. Now:","paragraphs":["process discovery."]},{"heading":"278. ROLEPLAY 6","paragraphs":["TELECOM Customer Operations: «Fiber activation is too slow.»"]},{"heading":"279. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Where does an order spend most of its time from signed order to live service?»"]},{"heading":"280. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Waiting for field installation.»"]},{"heading":"281. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Is the constraint technician capacity, scheduling, equipment, or address/network readiness?»"]},{"heading":"282. Root:","paragraphs":["must be found."]},{"heading":"283. ROLEPLAY 7","paragraphs":["HEALTHCARE Hospital COO: «Patients wait too long.»"]},{"heading":"284. Seller:","paragraphs":["«At which step — check-in, consultation, diagnostics, discharge or billing?»"]},{"heading":"285. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Discharge.»"]},{"heading":"286. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What happens between clinical discharge decision and actual patient departure?»"]},{"heading":"287. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"288. ROLEPLAY 8","paragraphs":["PHARMA Quality Director: «Deviations stay open too long.»"]},{"heading":"289. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Where do they typically stall — investigation, root cause, CAPA assignment, approval or effectiveness check?»"]},{"heading":"290. Specific.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"291. ROLEPLAY 9","paragraphs":["BANK Operations: «Onboarding takes 3 days.»"]},{"heading":"292. Seller:","paragraphs":["«What part of those 3 days is actual review versus waiting between teams or systems?»"]},{"heading":"293. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"294. ROLEPLAY 10","paragraphs":["CONSTRUCTION Commercial Director: «We lose money on variations.»"]},{"heading":"295. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Walk me through one recent variation from site instruction to final commercial approval.»"]},{"heading":"296. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"297. NOW","paragraphs":["DIFFICULT DISCOVERY SITUATIONS"]},{"heading":"298. CUSTOMER GIVES ONE-WORD ANSWERS","paragraphs":["Don't panic."]},{"heading":"299. Use:","paragraphs":["specific process question."]},{"heading":"300. > «Let's take one recent example.»","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 301–325 · Easier to answer.",[{"heading":"301. Easier to answer.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"302. CUSTOMER TALKS TOO MUCH","paragraphs":["Need guide politely."]},{"heading":"303. Say:","paragraphs":["«That's useful context. Can I bring us back specifically to what happens after the request enters the system?»"]},{"heading":"304. Professional.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"305. CUSTOMER JUMPS TO SOLUTION","paragraphs":["«We need dashboard.»"]},{"heading":"306. Say:","paragraphs":["«We can absolutely explore that. Before we define it, what decision is currently difficult because you don't have that visibility?»"]},{"heading":"307. Bring back:","paragraphs":["to business problem."]},{"heading":"308. CUSTOMER ASKS PRICE EARLY","paragraphs":["Say: «Happy to discuss price. Before I give you a misleading number, can I understand the scope drivers — users, workflows and integrations?»"]},{"heading":"309. CUSTOMER ASKS","paragraphs":["«Can you do it?»"]},{"heading":"310. Say:","paragraphs":["«Potentially, but I'd want technical validation before giving you a commitment. Let's identify the critical requirements first.»"]},{"heading":"311. CUSTOMER ASKS","paragraphs":["«How long?»"]},{"heading":"312. Same principle.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"313. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«We just need something simple.»"]},{"heading":"314. Ask:","paragraphs":["«What makes it simple from your perspective?»"]},{"heading":"315. Important.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"316. “Simple”","paragraphs":["can hide: 5 integrations."]},{"heading":"317. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«No integrations.»"]},{"heading":"318. Later:","paragraphs":["«It just needs customer data from SAP.»"]},{"heading":"319. That's integration.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"320. Clarify.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"321. MEETING WITH NO PAIN","paragraphs":["Maybe: networking conversation."]},{"heading":"322. Don't force:","paragraphs":["opportunity."]},{"heading":"323. Record:","paragraphs":["no current fit."]},{"heading":"324. Maintain:","paragraphs":["relationship."]},{"heading":"325. MEETING WITH MULTIPLE PAINS","paragraphs":["Customer gives: 10 problems."]}]],["Σημεία 326–350 · Don't sell:",[{"heading":"326. Don't sell:","paragraphs":["10 projects."]},{"heading":"327. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which of these has the highest business impact and is most important to address first?»"]},{"heading":"328. Prioritize.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"329. Another:","paragraphs":["«If we could solve only one this quarter, which would you choose?»"]},{"heading":"330. Strong.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"331. CHAMPION DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Possible champion says: «This problem is driving me crazy.»"]},{"heading":"332. Not enough.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"333. Test:","paragraphs":["«Who else would need to support a project like this?»"]},{"heading":"334. If they:","paragraphs":["offer introductions: good sign."]},{"heading":"335. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Would you be comfortable bringing them into the next discussion?»"]},{"heading":"336. Champion action.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"337. ECONOMIC BUYER DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Don't ask: «Who's the Economic Buyer?»"]},{"heading":"338. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Who normally approves investment of this type?»"]},{"heading":"339. Natural.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"340. PAPER PROCESS DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: «Once business and technical teams agree, what procurement, legal or security steps usually remain?»"]},{"heading":"341. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"342. COMPETITION DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: «Are you considering other vendors, an internal build, or keeping the current process?»"]},{"heading":"343. Neutral.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"344. CUSTOMER MAY SAY","paragraphs":["«We're talking to 3 suppliers.»"]},{"heading":"345. Good.","paragraphs":["Ask: «What criteria will you use to compare the options?»"]},{"heading":"346. Decision criteria.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"347. DON'T ASK","paragraphs":["«Who are they?» immediately."]},{"heading":"348. If useful:","paragraphs":["later."]},{"heading":"349. BUSINESS CASE DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["Ask: «If this improves, which metric should change?»"]},{"heading":"350. Great.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 351–375 · Could be:",[{"heading":"351. Could be:","paragraphs":["Cycle time Headcount capacity Error rate Revenue Downtime Customer contacts."]},{"heading":"352. Then ask baseline.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"353. > «What's the current number?»","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"354. If customer doesn't know:","paragraphs":["that's okay."]},{"heading":"355. Make it:","paragraphs":["action item."]},{"heading":"356. > «Could we get that baseline before the next meeting so we can build the business case properly?»","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"357. GREAT","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"358. MUTUAL ACTION","paragraphs":["Customer: also has homework."]},{"heading":"359. Enterprise selling:","paragraphs":["is not: supplier doing everything."]},{"heading":"360. DISCOVERY OUTPUT","paragraphs":["After meeting: salesperson must produce:"]},{"heading":"361. PROBLEM STATEMENT","paragraphs":["One paragraph."]},{"heading":"362. Example:","paragraphs":["«The company processes ~4,000 daily orders across portal, API and email. Email orders require manual re-entry into WMS, creating approximately 40 team-hours per week and additional delays during peak volume. With a second warehouse launching in Q1, Operations wants to reduce manual processing before volume increases.»"]},{"heading":"363. GREAT PROBLEM STATEMENT","paragraphs":["contains: Process Pain Metric Trigger Desired outcome."]},{"heading":"364. BAD PROBLEM STATEMENT","paragraphs":["«Customer needs automation.»"]},{"heading":"365. Meaningless.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"366. AFTER-MEETING CRM","paragraphs":["Within: same day."]},{"heading":"367. Record:","paragraphs":["Confirmed facts Pain Impact Metrics Stakeholders Systems Decision process Risks Unknowns Next action."]},{"heading":"368. DO NOT WRITE","paragraphs":["only: «Good meeting.»"]},{"heading":"369. USELESS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"370. FOLLOW-UP EMAIL","paragraphs":["Short."]},{"heading":"371. Include:","paragraphs":["Thank you What we understood Next step Owners/date."]},{"heading":"372. Example:","paragraphs":["«Thank you for today. My understanding is that the key issue is not the WMS itself but the manual handling of email orders, which currently creates around 40 team-hours of work per week and is expected to become more difficult when the new warehouse goes live. We agreed the next step is a 60-minute process/technical workshop with Operations and IT to map exception cases and validate integration options.»"]},{"heading":"373. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"374. This prevents:","paragraphs":["misunderstanding."]},{"heading":"375. DO NOT WRITE","paragraphs":["3-page meeting recap."]}]],["Σημεία 376–400 · Keep:",[{"heading":"376. Keep:","paragraphs":["decision-focused."]},{"heading":"377. DISCOVERY MEETING SCORECARD","paragraphs":["Opening & agenda __/5"]},{"heading":"378. Current-state understanding","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"379. Root-cause discovery","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"380. Impact/quantification","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"381. Stakeholder/decision understanding","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"382. Next-step quality","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"383. TOTAL","paragraphs":["__/30."]},{"heading":"384. 26–30","paragraphs":["Ready for strategic accounts."]},{"heading":"385. 21–25","paragraphs":["Strong."]},{"heading":"386. 16–20","paragraphs":["Needs more coaching."]},{"heading":"387. Below 16","paragraphs":["Do not lead Tier A discovery alone."]},{"heading":"388. MANAGER ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Manager plays: difficult customer."]},{"heading":"389. Seller gets:","paragraphs":["20 minutes."]},{"heading":"390. Manager should NOT","paragraphs":["give information easily."]},{"heading":"391. Seller must:","paragraphs":["earn detail: with questions."]},{"heading":"392. CUSTOMER CHARACTER #1","paragraphs":["Busy COO."]},{"heading":"393. Gives short answers.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"394. CUSTOMER CHARACTER #2","paragraphs":["Technical CIO."]},{"heading":"395. Wants architecture early.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"396. CUSTOMER CHARACTER #3","paragraphs":["Friendly manager."]},{"heading":"397. Likes solution:","paragraphs":["but no authority."]},{"heading":"398. CUSTOMER CHARACTER #4","paragraphs":["CFO."]},{"heading":"399. Wants ROI.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"400. CUSTOMER CHARACTER #5","paragraphs":["Operations manager."]}]],["Σημεία 401–425 · Complains about everything.",[{"heading":"401. Complains about everything.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"402. Seller must:","paragraphs":["prioritize."]},{"heading":"403. CUSTOMER CHARACTER #6","paragraphs":["Customer thinks solution already known."]},{"heading":"404. Seller must:","paragraphs":["validate need."]},{"heading":"405. CUSTOMER CHARACTER #7","paragraphs":["No real pain."]},{"heading":"406. Seller must:","paragraphs":["disqualify."]},{"heading":"407. DISCOVERY EXAM","paragraphs":["Salesperson gets: company + trigger."]},{"heading":"408. 5 minutes prep.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"409. 20 minutes roleplay.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"410. Must discover:","paragraphs":["Current process Main pain Impact Why now Stakeholders Next step."]},{"heading":"411. Automatic fail if:","paragraphs":["Invents customer problem. Promises technical capability without validation. Talks most of meeting. Gives proposal without scope. Leaves with vague next step."]},{"heading":"412. BONUS SCORE","paragraphs":["if salesperson: discovers: that there is: no deal."]},{"heading":"413. Because:","paragraphs":["that is: good qualification."]},{"heading":"414. DISCOVERY GOLDEN RULE #1","paragraphs":["«Start with the process, not the product.»"]},{"heading":"415. GOLDEN RULE #2","paragraphs":["«A symptom is not always the root cause.»"]},{"heading":"416. GOLDEN RULE #3","paragraphs":["«Pain without measurable impact may not justify an enterprise project.»"]},{"heading":"417. GOLDEN RULE #4","paragraphs":["«Never assume what “slow”, “manual” or “poor visibility” means.»"]},{"heading":"418. GOLDEN RULE #5","paragraphs":["«Ask about one real recent example.»"]},{"heading":"419. GOLDEN RULE #6","paragraphs":["«Listen for handoffs between people, departments and systems.»"]},{"heading":"420. GOLDEN RULE #7","paragraphs":["«Do not solve the problem while you are still discovering it.»"]},{"heading":"421. GOLDEN RULE #8","paragraphs":["«Before ending, summarize what you understood and let the customer correct you.»"]},{"heading":"422. GOLDEN RULE #9","paragraphs":["«Every meeting needs a specific mutual next step.»"]},{"heading":"423. GOLDEN RULE #10","paragraphs":["«If there is no meaningful problem, do not manufacture a project.»"]},{"heading":"424. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ ΡΟΗ ΤΟΥ FIRST MEETING","paragraphs":["OPEN ↓ SET AGENDA ↓ CURRENT PROCESS ↓ FIND FRICTION ↓ FOLLOW THE ROOT CAUSE ↓ QUANTIFY IMPACT ↓ UNDERSTAND WHY NOW ↓ ASK WHAT THEY TRIED ↓ DEFINE DESIRED STATE ↓ MAP STAKEHOLDERS ↓ UNDERSTAND DECISION PROCESS ↓ IDENTIFY TECHNICAL UNKNOWNS ↓ SUMMARIZE ↓ CUSTOMER CONFIRMS / CORRECTS ↓ AGREE SPECIFIC NEXT STEP ↓ CRM + FOLLOW-UP."]},{"heading":"425. Η ΜΙΑ ΦΡΑΣΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΘΥΜΑΤΑΙ Ο ΠΩΛΗΤΗΣ","paragraphs":["«Στο πρώτο enterprise meeting δεν προσπαθώ να δείξω πόσα ξέρω ούτε να παρουσιάσω όσο περισσότερα μπορώ. Προσπαθώ να καταλάβω μία πραγματική επιχειρηματική διαδικασία τόσο καλά ώστε, μέχρι το τέλος της συζήτησης, ο πελάτης και εγώ να συμφωνούμε ποιο είναι το πραγματικό πρόβλημα, τι επίπτωση έχει και ποιο είναι το πιο λογικό επόμενο βήμα.» ΑΥΤΟ ΕΙΝΑΙ ENTERPRISE DISCOVERY."]}]],["Πριν απαντήσεις στο quiz",["Ξανασκέψου το εισαγωγικό περιστατικό. Ποιο γεγονός είναι επιβεβαιωμένο, ποια πληροφορία λείπει και ποια ενέργεια θα μείωνε την αβεβαιότητα; Μία απάντηση μπορεί να ακούγεται εμπορικά ελκυστική αλλά να προηγείται της απαιτούμενης επιβεβαίωσης.","Οι δύο ερωτήσεις εφαρμογής γενικών αρχών συνδέονται και με τις προαιρετικές «Γενικές σημειώσεις». Το PDF βρίσκεται μόνιμα στο μενού, δεν αποτελεί ξεχωριστό υποχρεωτικό μάθημα και η ανάγνωσή του δεν βαθμολογείται.","Η επάνοδος χρειάζεται λόγο, συνάφεια και σεβασμό ορίων. Γενικές σημειώσεις: follow-up.","Μια ερμηνεία δεν είναι ακόμη τεκμηριωμένη αιτία. Γενικές σημειώσεις: learning orientation και ανασκόπηση."]]],"scenario":["Σε συνάντηση 30 λεπτών ο πελάτης ζητά demo αμέσως, αλλά δεν έχει εξηγήσει ποια διαδικασία θέλει να βελτιώσει.","Συμφωνώ σύντομη ατζέντα, διερευνώ ένα πραγματικό περιστατικό και συνδέω την παρουσίαση με αυτό. Η δομή υπηρετεί την κατανόηση και όχι τον όγκο της παρουσίασης."],"minutes":32,"version":1,"additional_curriculum":37,"question_rows":[["Σε συνάντηση 30 λεπτών ο πελάτης ζητά demo αμέσως, αλλά δεν έχει εξηγήσει ποια διαδικασία θέλει να βελτιώσει. Πώς οργανώνεις τον διαθέσιμο χρόνο;","Συμφωνώ σύντομη ατζέντα, διερευνώ ένα πραγματικό περιστατικό και συνδέω την παρουσίαση με αυτό.","Κάνω ολόκληρη την εταιρική παρουσίαση για να μη λείψει δυνατότητα.","Αρνούμαι κάθε επίδειξη μέχρι να υπάρχει πλήρες τεχνικό brief.","Δείχνω το πιο εντυπωσιακό feature και υποθέτω τη χρήση του.","Η δομή υπηρετεί την κατανόηση και όχι τον όγκο της παρουσίασης."],["Σε συνάντηση 30 λεπτών ο πελάτης ζητά demo αμέσως, αλλά δεν έχει εξηγήσει ποια διαδικασία θέλει να βελτιώσει. Ποια ερώτηση δίνει καλύτερα δεδομένα;","Τι συνέβη την τελευταία φορά που καθυστέρησε αυτή η διαδικασία;","Συμφωνείτε ότι χρειάζεστε μια σύγχρονη λύση;","Δεν είναι προφανές ότι χάνετε πολλά χρήματα;","Θέλετε όλα τα συστήματα να είναι καλύτερα;","Ένα συγκεκριμένο περιστατικό αποκαλύπτει βήματα, εμπλεκόμενους και επιπτώσεις."],["Σε συνάντηση 30 λεπτών ο πελάτης ζητά demo αμέσως, αλλά δεν έχει εξηγήσει ποια διαδικασία θέλει να βελτιώσει. Ποιο κλείσιμο συνάντησης είναι επαγγελματικό;","Επιβεβαίωση όσων κατανοήθηκαν, ανοικτών θεμάτων και επόμενης ενέργειας με υπεύθυνο και ημερομηνία.","Θεώρηση της ευγένειας ως αποδοχής προσφοράς.","Υπόσχεση τιμής χωρίς έλεγχο αντικειμένου.","Αόριστο «θα τα πούμε» χωρίς συμφωνία συνέχειας.","Η συνέχεια πρέπει να είναι κατανοητή και από τις δύο πλευρές."],["Ο πελάτης δεν απαντά μετά από αίτημα προσφοράς. Έχεις νέο στοιχείο σχετικό με την ανάγκη και δεν υπάρχει αίτημα διακοπής. Ποιο follow-up έχει μεγαλύτερη αξία;","Σύντομη σύνδεση με την προηγούμενη συζήτηση, νέο χρήσιμο στοιχείο και εύκολη πρόταση επόμενου βήματος μέσω επιτρεπόμενου καναλιού.","Το ίδιο «είδατε την προσφορά;» κάθε ημέρα σε όλα τα κανάλια.","Αυτόματη δήλωση αποδοχής αν δεν υπάρξει απάντηση.","Αποστολή νέας έκπτωσης πριν διευκρινιστεί ο λόγος σιωπής.","Η επάνοδος χρειάζεται λόγο, συνάφεια και σεβασμό ορίων. Γενικές σημειώσεις: follow-up."],["Σε ανασκόπηση χαμένης ευκαιρίας ο πωλητής λέει «μας κέρδισε η τιμή». Ποιο επόμενο βήμα παράγει μάθηση;","Ελέγχουμε στοιχεία και feedback για κριτήρια απόφασης, ανταγωνισμό, αδράνεια και στάδια που δεν επιβεβαιώθηκαν.","Καταγράφουμε αυτόματα ανταγωνιστή ως αιτία χωρίς στοιχεία.","Μειώνουμε οριζόντια όλες τις μελλοντικές τιμές.","Διαγράφουμε την ευκαιρία ώστε να μη μειώσει το ποσοστό επιτυχίας.","Μια ερμηνεία δεν είναι ακόμη τεκμηριωμένη αιτία. Γενικές σημειώσεις: learning orientation και ανασκόπηση."]],"source_note":"Πηγή: ΜΑΘΗΜΑ 31.docx, κεφάλαιο 54. Διατηρείται το κείμενο των αριθμημένων σημείων, με ενοποίηση των σπασμένων γραμμών και αφαίρεση επαναλαμβανόμενης μορφοποίησης. Τα παραδείγματα δεν αλλάζουν τους κανόνες της εφαρμογής."},"di-enterprise-55":{"pillar":"distillogic","title":"55. Προσφορές και εμπορική στρατηγική","goal":"Να αναγνωρίζεις πραγματικές ανάγκες, να διερευνάς τα στοιχεία και να επιλέγεις υπεύθυνο επόμενο βήμα.","sections":[["Από την έννοια στην επαγγελματική πράξη",["Ο πελάτης ζητά χαμηλότερη τιμή διατηρώντας όλο το scope και συντομότερη παράδοση, ενώ η τεχνική ομάδα δεν έχει εκτιμήσει τις αλλαγές.","Στη μελέτη που ακολουθεί σύνδεσε κάθε πιθανή λύση με συγκεκριμένη διαδικασία, υπεύθυνο, επίπτωση και στοιχεία που μπορούν να επαληθευτούν. Η τεχνική δυνατότητα, η οικονομική αξία και η εξουσιοδότηση για απόφαση είναι διαφορετικά ερωτήματα. Τα παραδείγματα του κεφαλαίου σε βοηθούν να τα διερευνάς χωρίς να υπόσχεσαι κάτι που δεν έχει εγκριθεί.","Η ύλη περιγράφει ενδεικτικές επιχειρηματικές ανάγκες και μεθόδους πώλησης. Δεν αποτελεί κατάλογο έτοιμων λειτουργιών των δύο CRM, δεσμευτική προσφορά, αλλαγή αμοιβών ή νέα πολιτική πιστοποίησης. Για πραγματική εργασία ισχύουν οι εγκεκριμένοι εταιρικοί όροι και οι αρμοδιότητες. Το μάθημα 60 είναι προετοιμασία, όχι δεύτερη επίσημη τελική εξέταση."]],["Το αντικείμενο του κεφαλαίου",["ΠΡΟΣΦΟΡΑ, ΤΙΜΟΛΟΓΗΣΗ ΚΑΙ ΕΜΠΟΡΙΚΗ ΣΤΡΑΤΗΓΙΚΗ Πώς δίνουμε σωστή προσφορά χωρίς να καταστρέφουμε margin, scope και delivery"]],["Σημεία 1–25 · Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ",[{"heading":"1. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ","paragraphs":["Proposal: δεν είναι: PRICE PDF. Είναι: DECISION DOCUMENT."]},{"heading":"2. ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΑΠΑΝΤΑ","paragraphs":["Τι πρόβλημα λύνουμε; Τι ακριβώς θα κάνουμε; Τι δεν θα κάνουμε; Τι θα παραδώσουμε; Πότε; Με ποιες προϋποθέσεις; Πόσο κοστίζει; Πώς πληρώνεται; Τι χρειάζεται από τον πελάτη;"]},{"heading":"3. BAD PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["Custom software development — €80,000."]},{"heading":"4. CUSTOMER THINKS","paragraphs":["Τι περιλαμβάνει; Πόσες integrations; Τι γίνεται αν αλλάξει κάτι; Πότε παραδίδεται;"]},{"heading":"5. GOOD PROPOSAL","paragraphs":["removes ambiguity."]},{"heading":"6. ΠΡΙΝ ΤΗΝ ΠΡΟΣΦΟΡΑ","paragraphs":["Πρέπει να έχουμε: Confirmed problem Scope Users Integrations Critical requirements Dependencies Stakeholders Commercial model."]},{"heading":"7. ΑΝ ΔΕΝ ΞΕΡΟΥΜΕ ΑΡΚΕΤΑ","paragraphs":["δεν δίνουμε: fake precision."]},{"heading":"8. ΔΙΝΟΥΜΕ","paragraphs":["Discovery phase ή Indicative range."]},{"heading":"9. PROPOSAL GATE","paragraphs":["Πριν επιτρέψει manager: final proposal, πρέπει να απαντάμε:"]},{"heading":"10. What problem?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"11. Why now?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"12. Who owns it?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"13. What scope?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"14. What systems?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"15. What assumptions?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"16. What success criteria?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"17. Who approves?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"18. If these are unclear:","paragraphs":["risk high."]},{"heading":"19. PROPOSAL STRUCTURE","paragraphs":["A strong enterprise proposal:"]},{"heading":"20. 1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY","paragraphs":["Very short."]},{"heading":"21. Include:","paragraphs":["Current situation Business problem Proposed approach Expected outcome."]},{"heading":"22. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["«Η εταιρεία σήμερα διαχειρίζεται customer requests μέσω email και portal, με σημαντικό manual re-entry στο ERP. Η προτεινόμενη πρώτη φάση στοχεύει στην αυτοματοποίηση των βασικών request types και στη σύνδεση του portal με το ERP, ώστε να μειωθεί το manual processing και να αυξηθεί η visibility.»"]},{"heading":"23. DON'T START","paragraphs":["with: «DISTILLOGIC was founded...»"]},{"heading":"24. Start with:","paragraphs":["customer."]},{"heading":"25. 2. BUSINESS CONTEXT","paragraphs":["What we understood."]}]],["Σημεία 26–50 · Example:",[{"heading":"26. Example:","paragraphs":["4,000 transactions/day 25% manual handling New site in Q1 Current team workload."]},{"heading":"27. Use only:","paragraphs":["confirmed information."]},{"heading":"28. DON'T INVENT","paragraphs":["customer pain."]},{"heading":"29. 3. OBJECTIVES","paragraphs":["Example: Reduce manual entry Improve processing visibility Integrate portal and ERP Create audit trail."]},{"heading":"30. OBJECTIVES","paragraphs":["must be: business-focused."]},{"heading":"31. Not:","paragraphs":["«Build React app.»"]},{"heading":"32. 4. SCOPE","paragraphs":["The most important section."]},{"heading":"33. Scope includes:","paragraphs":["what: we will build/do."]},{"heading":"34. Example","paragraphs":["Phase 1 scope: Authentication Request submission ERP integration Status tracking Admin workspace Basic reporting."]},{"heading":"35. Each item:","paragraphs":["clear enough: that both sides know: what is included."]},{"heading":"36. 5. OUT OF SCOPE","paragraphs":["Critical."]},{"heading":"37. Example:","paragraphs":["Mobile native app Historical data migration AI chatbot New ERP configuration 24/7 support."]},{"heading":"38. Why?","paragraphs":["Avoid: «We thought it was included.»"]},{"heading":"39. OUT OF SCOPE","paragraphs":["does not mean: never."]},{"heading":"40. It means:","paragraphs":["not in current commercial agreement."]},{"heading":"41. 6. DELIVERABLES","paragraphs":["What customer receives."]},{"heading":"42. Examples:","paragraphs":["Web application API integrations Admin portal Documentation Deployment Testing Training."]},{"heading":"43. DON'T WRITE","paragraphs":["«Complete digital transformation.»"]},{"heading":"44. Too vague.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"45. 7. MILESTONES","paragraphs":["Example: Discovery & design Build Integration UAT Production release."]},{"heading":"46. Each milestone:","paragraphs":["should have: output."]},{"heading":"47. 8. TIMELINE","paragraphs":["Timeline: based on: known scope."]},{"heading":"48. NEVER","paragraphs":["give timeline: because customer asks: «Can you do it in 8 weeks?»"]},{"heading":"49. Technical/delivery:","paragraphs":["must validate."]},{"heading":"50. Timeline should show:","paragraphs":["Work stages Dependencies Customer actions."]}]],["Σημεία 51–75 · EXAMPLE",[{"heading":"51. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Week 1–2: Requirements confirmation."]},{"heading":"52. Week 3–6:","paragraphs":["Build."]},{"heading":"53. Week 7:","paragraphs":["Integration testing."]},{"heading":"54. Week 8:","paragraphs":["UAT."]},{"heading":"55. But only:","paragraphs":["after validation."]},{"heading":"56. 9. ASSUMPTIONS","paragraphs":["Very important."]},{"heading":"57. Examples:","paragraphs":["Customer provides API access. Customer provides test environment. Required stakeholders available. Scope remains as agreed. Data quality meets minimum requirements."]},{"heading":"58. IF ASSUMPTION FAILS","paragraphs":["timeline/cost: may change."]},{"heading":"59. 10. CUSTOMER RESPONSIBILITIES","paragraphs":["Examples: Provide access Review requirements Give feedback Approve UAT Provide content/data Assign business owner."]},{"heading":"60. Enterprise project:","paragraphs":["is not: supplier-only activity."]},{"heading":"61. 11. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA","paragraphs":["What means: delivered?"]},{"heading":"62. Example:","paragraphs":["«User can submit a request, data is transferred successfully to ERP and the resulting status is visible in portal.»"]},{"heading":"63. Better than:","paragraphs":["«System works.»"]},{"heading":"64. Acceptance:","paragraphs":["must be: testable."]},{"heading":"65. 12. COMMERCIAL MODEL","paragraphs":["Now: price."]},{"heading":"66. MAIN MODELS","paragraphs":["Fixed Price Time & Materials Retainer Dedicated Team Discovery Fee Milestone-Based Project."]},{"heading":"67. FIXED PRICE","paragraphs":["Best when: scope clear."]},{"heading":"68. Customer knows:","paragraphs":["budget."]},{"heading":"69. Supplier carries:","paragraphs":["more estimation risk."]},{"heading":"70. Fixed price requires:","paragraphs":["strong scope discipline."]},{"heading":"71. WRONG","paragraphs":["Fixed price: with unclear: requirements."]},{"heading":"72. Result:","paragraphs":["scope fights."]},{"heading":"73. TIME & MATERIALS","paragraphs":["Customer pays: actual effort."]},{"heading":"74. Good when:","paragraphs":["scope evolves."]},{"heading":"75. More flexibility.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 76–100 · But customer may fear:",[{"heading":"76. But customer may fear:","paragraphs":["uncontrolled cost."]},{"heading":"77. Need:","paragraphs":["Budget tracking Sprint visibility Estimate-to-complete Approval control."]},{"heading":"78. T&M DOES NOT MEAN","paragraphs":["blank cheque."]},{"heading":"79. Example:","paragraphs":["monthly budget cap."]},{"heading":"80. DEDICATED TEAM","paragraphs":["Customer pays: for team/capacity."]},{"heading":"81. Useful:","paragraphs":["ongoing product development."]},{"heading":"82. Example:","paragraphs":["1 senior developer 2 full stack QA PM."]},{"heading":"83. Need define:","paragraphs":["Roles Seniority Capacity Rate Minimum term."]},{"heading":"84. RETAINER","paragraphs":["Recurring: monthly fee."]},{"heading":"85. Useful for:","paragraphs":["Support Continuous improvements Application management Small ongoing development."]},{"heading":"86. Need define:","paragraphs":["what retainer includes."]},{"heading":"87. Not:","paragraphs":["«Unlimited anything.»"]},{"heading":"88. DISCOVERY FEE","paragraphs":["Very important."]},{"heading":"89. When project:","paragraphs":["large/uncertain, sell: discovery first."]},{"heading":"90. Discovery deliverables may include:","paragraphs":["Requirements Process map Technical assessment Architecture proposal Integration map Delivery plan Final implementation estimate."]},{"heading":"91. This protects:","paragraphs":["customer and: supplier."]},{"heading":"92. CUSTOMER MAY SAY","paragraphs":["«Why should we pay you to tell us what it costs?»"]},{"heading":"93. RESPONSE","paragraphs":["«Because in a complex project the discovery itself produces valuable requirements, architecture and implementation clarity. Without it, both sides would be pricing uncertainty rather than scope.»"]},{"heading":"94. Good.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"95. HYBRID MODEL","paragraphs":["Can use: Discovery: fixed fee. Then: implementation: fixed/T&M."]},{"heading":"96. Often strong model.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"97. PRICING PRINCIPLE #1","paragraphs":["PRICE IS NOT COST + RANDOM MARGIN."]},{"heading":"98. Need understand:","paragraphs":["Delivery cost Risk Complexity Commercial value Support burden Opportunity cost."]},{"heading":"99. DELIVERY COST","paragraphs":["Includes: Salaries/contractor cost PM QA Architecture DevOps Support Internal overhead."]},{"heading":"100. DON'T PRICE","paragraphs":["only developer hours."]}]],["Σημεία 101–125 · PROJECT REQUIRES",[{"heading":"101. PROJECT REQUIRES","paragraphs":["sales, management, review, testing, support."]},{"heading":"102. COST EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Suppose: developer cost: €5,000/month."]},{"heading":"103. If bill:","paragraphs":["€5,500: not: 10% healthy margin necessarily."]},{"heading":"104. Need include:","paragraphs":["overhead, non-billable time, risk, management."]},{"heading":"105. SALES PERSON","paragraphs":["should not independently: calculate final project price."]},{"heading":"106. Need:","paragraphs":["commercial/delivery approval."]},{"heading":"107. PRICING PRINCIPLE #2","paragraphs":["RISK HAS A PRICE."]},{"heading":"108. More unknown:","paragraphs":["more risk."]},{"heading":"109. Examples:","paragraphs":["Legacy system Unknown API Bad data Tight deadline Undefined requirements."]},{"heading":"110. Don't price high-risk project:","paragraphs":["like standard build."]},{"heading":"111. Either:","paragraphs":["add contingency or: reduce uncertainty first."]},{"heading":"112. BEST OPTION:","paragraphs":["discovery."]},{"heading":"113. PRICING PRINCIPLE #3","paragraphs":["DON'T UNDERPRICE TO WIN LOGO."]},{"heading":"114. Famous client:","paragraphs":["can still be: bad project."]},{"heading":"115. If project:","paragraphs":["loses money and destroys team, logo doesn't save you."]},{"heading":"116. STRATEGIC DISCOUNT","paragraphs":["can exist."]},{"heading":"117. But:","paragraphs":["deliberate."]},{"heading":"118. Not:","paragraphs":["panic."]},{"heading":"119. Example reasons:","paragraphs":["Reference value Long-term contract Multiple projects Fast payment Reduced acquisition cost."]},{"heading":"120. Must be:","paragraphs":["real."]},{"heading":"121. NEVER SAY","paragraphs":["«We'll lose on first project and make money later.» without actual strategy."]},{"heading":"122. PRICING PRINCIPLE #4","paragraphs":["PRICE SHOULD MATCH SCOPE."]},{"heading":"123. If customer wants:","paragraphs":["lower price: reduce: scope."]},{"heading":"124. Example:","paragraphs":["Full project: €120k."]},{"heading":"125. Budget:","paragraphs":["€80k."]}]],["Σημεία 126–150 · Option:",[{"heading":"126. Option:","paragraphs":["Phase 1: €75k."]},{"heading":"127. Not:","paragraphs":["same project for: €80k."]},{"heading":"128. Unless:","paragraphs":["commercial decision supports it."]},{"heading":"129. PRICING PRINCIPLE #5","paragraphs":["NEVER DISCOUNT BEFORE ASKING WHY."]},{"heading":"130. Customer:","paragraphs":["«Too expensive.»"]},{"heading":"131. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Compared with budget, competitor or expected value?»"]},{"heading":"132. Different problem:","paragraphs":["different response."]},{"heading":"133. PRICING PRINCIPLE #6","paragraphs":["CREATE OPTIONS."]},{"heading":"134. Instead of:","paragraphs":["one offer."]},{"heading":"135. Could have:","paragraphs":["Option A — Essential Option B — Recommended Option C — Extended."]},{"heading":"136. OPTION A","paragraphs":["Core business outcome."]},{"heading":"137. OPTION B","paragraphs":["Core + important integrations/reporting."]},{"heading":"138. OPTION C","paragraphs":["Broader transformation."]},{"heading":"139. Benefits:","paragraphs":["customer chooses: trade-off."]},{"heading":"140. But:","paragraphs":["don't create: fake bad option."]},{"heading":"141. All options:","paragraphs":["must be: viable."]},{"heading":"142. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Essential — €60k Core workflow."]},{"heading":"143. ### Recommended — €85k","paragraphs":["Workflow + ERP integration + reporting."]},{"heading":"144. ### Extended — €120k","paragraphs":["Above + advanced analytics + second business unit."]},{"heading":"145. IMPORTANT","paragraphs":["Don't confuse: customer."]},{"heading":"146. 2–3 options:","paragraphs":["enough."]},{"heading":"147. COMMERCIAL ANCHORING","paragraphs":["Show: value/scope: before: price."]},{"heading":"148. Don't start:","paragraphs":["proposal presentation: with number."]},{"heading":"149. First:","paragraphs":["reconfirm: problem."]},{"heading":"150. Then:","paragraphs":["solution."]}]],["Σημεία 151–175 · Then:",[{"heading":"151. Then:","paragraphs":["investment."]},{"heading":"152. PROPOSAL PRESENTATION","paragraphs":["Don't just email: strategic proposal."]},{"heading":"153. Present it:","paragraphs":["live."]},{"heading":"154. Why?","paragraphs":["Can: explain, answer, see reactions."]},{"heading":"155. EMAIL AFTER","paragraphs":["contains: formal document."]},{"heading":"156. PROPOSAL MEETING FLOW","paragraphs":["Reconfirm business problem. Reconfirm desired outcome. Explain scope. Explain assumptions. Explain timeline. Explain commercial model. Discuss concerns. Agree next step."]},{"heading":"157. Don't spend:","paragraphs":["20 minutes: talking about Distillogic."]},{"heading":"158. CUSTOMER SHOULD SEE","paragraphs":["their own problem: inside proposal."]},{"heading":"159. IF CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«This isn't what we discussed.» Bad."]},{"heading":"160. Means:","paragraphs":["discovery/handoff failed."]},{"heading":"161. PRICING MODEL — FIXED PRICE EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Project: €100,000."]},{"heading":"162. Milestones:","paragraphs":["20% kickoff 30% design/build milestone 30% UAT 20% production release."]},{"heading":"163. Example only.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"164. Payment model:","paragraphs":["must align: cash flow and: risk."]},{"heading":"165. DON'T LEAVE","paragraphs":["90% payment: at final delivery."]},{"heading":"166. Huge supplier risk.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"167. For longer projects:","paragraphs":["milestone billing."]},{"heading":"168. T&M EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Team: €25,000/month."]},{"heading":"169. Monthly:","paragraphs":["actual capacity."]},{"heading":"170. Customer sees:","paragraphs":["Sprint progress Hours/capacity Budget consumption Forecast."]},{"heading":"171. RETAINER EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["€8,000/month."]},{"heading":"172. Includes:","paragraphs":["defined capacity: and support."]},{"heading":"173. Don't use:","paragraphs":["«Unlimited changes.»"]},{"heading":"174. DEDICATED TEAM","paragraphs":["Rate: by role."]},{"heading":"175. Example:","paragraphs":["Senior dev: X. QA: Y. PM: Z."]}]],["Σημεία 176–200 · But actual rates:",[{"heading":"176. But actual rates:","paragraphs":["internal commercial decision."]},{"heading":"177. RATE CARD","paragraphs":["Useful: large enterprise/MSA."]},{"heading":"178. Includes:","paragraphs":["roles: and day/month rates."]},{"heading":"179. But:","paragraphs":["rate card alone: doesn't define project."]},{"heading":"180. PROJECT ESTIMATE","paragraphs":["still needed."]},{"heading":"181. CONTINGENCY","paragraphs":["Projects: with uncertainty: may require: contingency."]},{"heading":"182. Example:","paragraphs":["10–20%."]},{"heading":"183. But don't automatically:","paragraphs":["use fixed number."]},{"heading":"184. Based on:","paragraphs":["risk."]},{"heading":"185. Better:","paragraphs":["remove uncertainty."]},{"heading":"186. CHANGE REQUEST","paragraphs":["Critical commercial mechanism."]},{"heading":"187. Customer asks:","paragraphs":["new feature."]},{"heading":"188. Team evaluates:","paragraphs":["Effort Timeline Cost Dependency."]},{"heading":"189. Customer approves:","paragraphs":["before work."]},{"heading":"190. Not:","paragraphs":["after."]},{"heading":"191. CHANGE REQUEST FLOW","paragraphs":["Request ↓ Impact analysis ↓ Commercial impact ↓ Approval ↓ Delivery."]},{"heading":"192. NEVER","paragraphs":["let developers: accept scope changes: directly."]},{"heading":"193. They can discuss:","paragraphs":["technical need."]},{"heading":"194. But:","paragraphs":["commercial/scope changes: need governance."]},{"heading":"195. SCOPE CREEP","paragraphs":["is often: not customer maliciousness."]},{"heading":"196. Sometimes:","paragraphs":["scope simply: evolves."]},{"heading":"197. Need:","paragraphs":["process."]},{"heading":"198. CUSTOMER SAYS","paragraphs":["«It's only one small change.»"]},{"heading":"199. Response:","paragraphs":["«We'll assess it quickly. If there's no material impact, we can include it. If it affects scope/time