Define:","paragraphs":["specific systems."]},{"heading":"328. CUSTOMER ADDS","paragraphs":["fifth integration: later."]},{"heading":"329. That's:","paragraphs":["scope change."]},{"heading":"330. DELIVERY LOCATION","paragraphs":["Remote/on-site: affects cost."]},{"heading":"331. Define:","paragraphs":["expected model."]},{"heading":"332. TRAVEL COSTS","paragraphs":["specify."]},{"heading":"333. TRAINING","paragraphs":["Define: how many sessions/users."]},{"heading":"334. Not:","paragraphs":["«Training included.»"]},{"heading":"335. Better:","paragraphs":["«2 remote admin training sessions up to X participants.»"]},{"heading":"336. SUPPORT","paragraphs":["same."]},{"heading":"337. REPORTING","paragraphs":["same."]},{"heading":"338. EVERYTHING VAGUE","paragraphs":["becomes: future dispute."]},{"heading":"339. PROPOSAL REVIEW CHECKLIST","paragraphs":["Before send:"]},{"heading":"340. Does executive summary:","paragraphs":["describe customer?"]},{"heading":"341. Is scope:","paragraphs":["clear?"]},{"heading":"342. Is out-of-scope:","paragraphs":["clear?"]},{"heading":"343. Are integrations:","paragraphs":["named?"]},{"heading":"344. Are assumptions:","paragraphs":["listed?"]},{"heading":"345. Is timeline:","paragraphs":["validated?"]},{"heading":"346. Is price:","paragraphs":["approved?"]},{"heading":"347. Are payment terms:","paragraphs":["clear?"]},{"heading":"348. Are customer responsibilities:","paragraphs":["clear?"]},{"heading":"349. Are acceptance criteria:","paragraphs":["clear?"]},{"heading":"350. Are risks:","paragraphs":["acknowledged?"]}]],["Σημεία 351–375 · Is proposal:",[{"heading":"351. Is proposal:","paragraphs":["internally deliverable?"]},{"heading":"352. LAST ONE","paragraphs":["most important."]},{"heading":"353. SALES CAN SELL","paragraphs":["only what: Delivery can deliver."]},{"heading":"354. INTERNAL APPROVAL","paragraphs":["Before major proposal: Sales + Technical + Delivery + Commercial."]},{"heading":"355. For sensitive:","paragraphs":["Security + Legal."]},{"heading":"356. Proposal sign-off.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"357. WHY?","paragraphs":["Avoid: sales committing: impossible scope."]},{"heading":"358. ROLEPLAY 1","paragraphs":["Customer: «Budget is €50k. Proposal is €80k.»"]},{"heading":"359. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Then let's identify which capabilities are essential for the first business outcome. We can create a Phase 1 that fits closer to your budget rather than pretend the full scope costs €50k.»"]},{"heading":"360. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"361. ROLEPLAY 2","paragraphs":["Customer: «Can you reduce by 15%?»"]},{"heading":"362. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Potentially, but I'd want to understand what can move in return — scope, term, payment or rollout. Which is most flexible?»"]},{"heading":"363. ROLEPLAY 3","paragraphs":["Customer: «Fixed price only.»"]},{"heading":"364. Seller:","paragraphs":["«That's workable once scope is sufficiently defined. For the uncertain integration areas, I'd suggest a short fixed-price discovery so the implementation price is based on validated requirements.»"]},{"heading":"365. ROLEPLAY 4","paragraphs":["Customer: «We want T&M but a guaranteed maximum.»"]},{"heading":"366. Seller:","paragraphs":["«We can structure a not-to-exceed budget with clear assumptions and change control, as long as scope and customer dependencies remain within the agreed boundaries.»"]},{"heading":"367. ROLEPLAY 5","paragraphs":["Customer: «Why is PM 15% of cost?»"]},{"heading":"368. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Let's review what project-management activities are actually required: coordination, dependencies, decisions, reporting, risk and customer communication. If scope is simpler, we can adjust the model. We shouldn't charge management effort that isn't needed.»"]},{"heading":"369. ROLEPLAY 6","paragraphs":["Customer: «Remove testing to save money.»"]},{"heading":"370. Seller:","paragraphs":["«We can prioritize testing based on risk, but removing it entirely would increase production risk. Let's identify which test layers are essential and which could reasonably be reduced.»"]},{"heading":"371. ROLEPLAY 7","paragraphs":["Customer: «We'll pay everything after go-live.»"]},{"heading":"372. Seller:","paragraphs":["«For a multi-month custom project, that creates an unbalanced financing risk. We can align payments to tangible milestones so you pay as value is delivered.»"]},{"heading":"373. ROLEPLAY 8","paragraphs":["Customer: «90-day payment is company policy.»"]},{"heading":"374. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Understood. Then we need to factor that into the commercial structure and milestone model so the project remains sustainable.»"]},{"heading":"375. ROLEPLAY 9","paragraphs":["Customer: «We need unlimited revisions.»"]}]],["Σημεία 376–400 · Seller:",[{"heading":"376. Seller:","paragraphs":["«We can include review cycles, but unlimited change makes scope and timeline impossible to manage. Let's define a practical review-and-change process.»"]},{"heading":"377. ROLEPLAY 10","paragraphs":["Customer: «Can you include future integrations for free?»"]},{"heading":"378. Seller:","paragraphs":["«We can design the platform to support future integrations, but each new integration needs separate assessment because effort depends on the target system and interfaces.»"]},{"heading":"379. ROLEPLAY 11","paragraphs":["Procurement: «Your day rate is too high.»"]},{"heading":"380. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Let's look at total project economics rather than rate alone. A lower rate doesn't necessarily mean lower project cost if delivery takes longer or requires more people. Which total commercial metric are you optimizing for?»"]},{"heading":"381. Good.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"382. ROLEPLAY 12","paragraphs":["CFO: «Why shouldn't I choose the cheapest vendor?»"]},{"heading":"383. Seller:","paragraphs":["«You should if the offers are genuinely equivalent in scope, risk and delivery capability. The useful comparison is total cost, responsibilities, assumptions and likelihood of achieving the business outcome.»"]},{"heading":"384. Strong.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"385. ROLEPLAY 13","paragraphs":["Customer: «Give us your best price now.»"]},{"heading":"386. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Our best price depends on the actual deal structure. If scope and terms are unchanged, I'll give you the strongest commercial position we can responsibly support. If variables can move, we can look at different packages.»"]},{"heading":"387. ROLEPLAY 14","paragraphs":["Customer: «We need 5% off to sign today.»"]},{"heading":"388. Seller:","paragraphs":["«If signature today removes real sales/procurement cost or gives us a commercial benefit, we can assess it. I wouldn't create a fake “today only” discount without an actual trade-off.»"]},{"heading":"389. INTERNAL RULE","paragraphs":["No fake: deadline discount."]},{"heading":"390. ROLEPLAY 15","paragraphs":["Customer: «Another vendor is half the price.»"]},{"heading":"391. Seller:","paragraphs":["«Then we should compare scope carefully. If the deliverables and responsibilities are genuinely equivalent and they can deliver at that level, they may be the better commercial choice. Let's identify what is actually different.»"]},{"heading":"392. Confidence.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"393. NOT DESPERATION","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"394. BUSINESS CASE AND PRICE","paragraphs":["Price should be: seen against: business impact."]},{"heading":"395. If project:","paragraphs":["costs €100k and confirmed: business value: €1m/year, easier discussion."]},{"heading":"396. But:","paragraphs":["do not invent: €1m."]},{"heading":"397. Customer data:","paragraphs":["required."]},{"heading":"398. ROI","paragraphs":["Example: Benefit: €200k/year. Investment: €100k."]},{"heading":"399. Simple ROI:","paragraphs":["(200 - 100) / 100 = 100%."]},{"heading":"400. But:","paragraphs":["real business case: may be more complex."]}]],["Σημεία 401–425 · PAYBACK",[{"heading":"401. PAYBACK","paragraphs":["Investment: €100k. Monthly benefit: €20k. Payback: 5 months."]},{"heading":"402. Again:","paragraphs":["only if: numbers validated."]},{"heading":"403. PRICE ≠ VALUE","paragraphs":["Value: can be: Cost reduction Capacity Revenue Risk reduction Time Customer experience."]},{"heading":"404. Some benefits:","paragraphs":["hard to monetize."]},{"heading":"405. Be honest.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"406. RISK AVOIDANCE","paragraphs":["Don't assign: made-up value: to risk."]},{"heading":"407. Use:","paragraphs":["scenario."]},{"heading":"408. Example:","paragraphs":["«The business values the ability to respond to audits within hours rather than days.»"]},{"heading":"409. Fine.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"410. DON'T SAY","paragraphs":["«This saves €5m risk.» without evidence."]},{"heading":"411. PRICE INCREASE","paragraphs":["Sometimes: customer adds scope."]},{"heading":"412. Don't be afraid:","paragraphs":["to increase price."]},{"heading":"413. Say:","paragraphs":["«This adds two integrations and a second user group, so scope and effort have materially changed. We'll revise the commercial model accordingly.»"]},{"heading":"414. Professional.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"415. PRICE REDUCTION","paragraphs":["when: scope reduces."]},{"heading":"416. Fair.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"417. COMMERCIAL TRANSPARENCY","paragraphs":["builds trust."]},{"heading":"418. DON'T:","paragraphs":["hide: scope reduction: inside same price."]},{"heading":"419. PROJECT PROFITABILITY AFTER CLOSE","paragraphs":["Sales role: doesn't end: at signature."]},{"heading":"420. Handoff:","paragraphs":["must preserve: commercial assumptions."]},{"heading":"421. PM needs know:","paragraphs":["Scope Budget Rates Assumptions Customer obligations Change rules."]},{"heading":"422. Otherwise:","paragraphs":["margin: leaks."]},{"heading":"423. SALES SHOULD NOT","paragraphs":["promise: free extras: during delivery."]},{"heading":"424. Account relationship:","paragraphs":["doesn't mean: commercial chaos."]},{"heading":"425. STRATEGIC ACCOUNT","paragraphs":["can receive: commercial flexibility."]}]],["Σημεία 426–450 · But:",[{"heading":"426. But:","paragraphs":["controlled."]},{"heading":"427. RENEWAL / EXPANSION PRICING","paragraphs":["Existing client: does not automatically: receive lower price."]},{"heading":"428. Consider:","paragraphs":["Lower acquisition cost Existing integration Existing MSA Relationship value Scope."]},{"heading":"429. Could be:","paragraphs":["better economics."]},{"heading":"430. But:","paragraphs":["new project: needs: new business case."]},{"heading":"431. PROCUREMENT TACTIC","paragraphs":["«Give us your absolute lowest price.»"]},{"heading":"432. Don't reveal floor:","paragraphs":["casually."]},{"heading":"433. Say:","paragraphs":["«We'll provide our final commercial position based on the complete scope and terms.»"]},{"heading":"434. PROCUREMENT","paragraphs":["may ask: breakdown."]},{"heading":"435. Decide:","paragraphs":["level of transparency."]},{"heading":"436. Don't reveal:","paragraphs":["internal salaries/margins: unless strategic reason."]},{"heading":"437. Can explain:","paragraphs":["work packages."]},{"heading":"438. Example:","paragraphs":["Discovery Build Integration QA Deployment."]},{"heading":"439. CUSTOMER WANTS","paragraphs":["hour breakdown."]},{"heading":"440. T&M:","paragraphs":["normal."]},{"heading":"441. Fixed price:","paragraphs":["may provide effort assumptions: without exposing every internal cost."]},{"heading":"442. CONTRACT SCOPE","paragraphs":["must match: proposal."]},{"heading":"443. If legal contract:","paragraphs":["says something different: danger."]},{"heading":"444. Sales must verify:","paragraphs":["final SOW."]},{"heading":"445. SOW","paragraphs":["Statement of Work."]},{"heading":"446. Should contain:","paragraphs":["Scope Deliverables Timeline Acceptance Commercials."]},{"heading":"447. MSA","paragraphs":["governs: general relationship."]},{"heading":"448. SOW","paragraphs":["governs: specific project."]},{"heading":"449. Don't confuse.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"450. CUSTOMER PO","paragraphs":["must match: agreed commercial terms."]}]],["Σημεία 451–475 · Check:",[{"heading":"451. Check:","paragraphs":["Amount Entity Currency Tax Payment Reference."]},{"heading":"452. NEVER START","paragraphs":["because: «They promised PO later.» unless authorized internal exception."]},{"heading":"453. Commercial discipline.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"454. PROPOSAL EXPIRY","paragraphs":["When expired: revalidate: Team availability Rates Timeline Scope."]},{"heading":"455. Don't automatically honor:","paragraphs":["old offer: six months later."]},{"heading":"456. MULTI-YEAR CONTRACT","paragraphs":["Need consider: Rate adjustment Inflation Capacity commitment Termination Renewal."]},{"heading":"457. Legal/commercial:","paragraphs":["handles."]},{"heading":"458. CURRENCY RISK","paragraphs":["If: contract EUR but costs: other currency."]},{"heading":"459. Finance:","paragraphs":["should assess."]},{"heading":"460. CUSTOMER CREDIT RISK","paragraphs":["Large project: need: payment reliability."]},{"heading":"461. Finance checks:","paragraphs":["where appropriate."]},{"heading":"462. SALES IS RESPONSIBLE","paragraphs":["for: good revenue, not: just signed revenue."]},{"heading":"463. BAD DEAL EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["€500k contract."]},{"heading":"464. Customer pays:","paragraphs":["after 180 days."]},{"heading":"465. Unlimited scope.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"466. Unlimited liability.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"467. 24/7 support.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"468. Fixed price.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"469. Unknown integrations.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"470. This may be:","paragraphs":["terrible deal."]},{"heading":"471. BIG REVENUE","paragraphs":["does not mean: good business."]},{"heading":"472. GOOD DEAL","paragraphs":["has: Real customer value Deliverable scope Fair economics Controlled risk Clear responsibilities."]},{"heading":"473. COMMERCIAL RED FLAGS","paragraphs":["Undefined scope No business owner Impossible deadline Huge unpaid PoC No access to systems Unlimited revisions Payment after final completion only Customer refuses responsibilities Large legal exposure."]},{"heading":"474. Another:","paragraphs":["customer says: «We'll define requirements during build but price must stay fixed.»"]},{"heading":"475. RED FLAG","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 476–500 · Another:",[{"heading":"476. Another:","paragraphs":["«Any integration we need is included.»"]},{"heading":"477. RED FLAG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"478. Another:","paragraphs":["«24/7 support included forever.»"]},{"heading":"479. RED FLAG","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"480. PROPOSAL SCORECARD","paragraphs":["Customer problem __/5"]},{"heading":"481. Scope clarity","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"482. Assumptions/dependencies","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"483. Commercial viability","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"484. Delivery feasibility","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"485. Decision clarity","paragraphs":["__/5 Total: __/30."]},{"heading":"486. 26–30","paragraphs":["Strong proposal."]},{"heading":"487. 21–25","paragraphs":["Good."]},{"heading":"488. 16–20","paragraphs":["Risky."]},{"heading":"489. Below 16","paragraphs":["Do not send."]},{"heading":"490. PRICING ROLEPLAY EXAM","paragraphs":["Salesperson receives: Customer budget: €100k."]},{"heading":"491. Internal estimate:","paragraphs":["€125k."]},{"heading":"492. Must decide:","paragraphs":["Discount? Scope reduction? Phasing? Discovery?"]},{"heading":"493. Good salesperson:","paragraphs":["does not automatically: cut €25k."]},{"heading":"494. SECOND EXAM","paragraphs":["Customer wants: fixed price."]},{"heading":"495. API:","paragraphs":["unknown."]},{"heading":"496. Good answer:","paragraphs":["discovery/assumption."]},{"heading":"497. THIRD EXAM","paragraphs":["Customer wants: 20% discount."]},{"heading":"498. Good answer:","paragraphs":["Give/Get."]},{"heading":"499. FOURTH EXAM","paragraphs":["Customer promises: future work."]},{"heading":"500. Good answer:","paragraphs":["future promise: doesn't equal current commitment."]}]],["Σημεία 501–525 · FIFTH EXAM",[{"heading":"501. FIFTH EXAM","paragraphs":["Customer wants: free PoC."]},{"heading":"502. Salesperson must:","paragraphs":["evaluate strategic value."]},{"heading":"503. Not:","paragraphs":["automatic yes."]},{"heading":"504. SIXTH EXAM","paragraphs":["Customer wants: delivery in half timeline."]},{"heading":"505. Seller:","paragraphs":["cannot: just double developers."]},{"heading":"506. Need:","paragraphs":["technical delivery input."]},{"heading":"507. SEVENTH EXAM","paragraphs":["Customer asks: «Can you reduce support cost?»"]},{"heading":"508. Seller:","paragraphs":["asks: what support level actually needed."]},{"heading":"509. Maybe:","paragraphs":["reduce: coverage."]},{"heading":"510. EIGHTH EXAM","paragraphs":["Customer wants: custom feature."]},{"heading":"511. Seller:","paragraphs":["does change request."]},{"heading":"512. NINTH EXAM","paragraphs":["Customer asks: «Why is your proposal higher?»"]},{"heading":"513. Seller:","paragraphs":["compares: scope/responsibility."]},{"heading":"514. TENTH EXAM","paragraphs":["Customer: «We'll sign if you remove 10%.»"]},{"heading":"515. Seller:","paragraphs":["does not say: yes."]},{"heading":"516. Internal:","paragraphs":["check: floor, strategic value, trade."]},{"heading":"517. PROPOSAL GOLDEN RULE #1","paragraphs":["«Never price what you don't understand.»"]},{"heading":"518. GOLDEN RULE #2","paragraphs":["«Fixed price requires defined scope.»"]},{"heading":"519. GOLDEN RULE #3","paragraphs":["«If uncertainty is high, sell discovery before certainty.»"]},{"heading":"520. GOLDEN RULE #4","paragraphs":["«A discount is not a strategy.»"]},{"heading":"521. GOLDEN RULE #5","paragraphs":["«When price goes down, something should normally move in return.»"]},{"heading":"522. GOLDEN RULE #6","paragraphs":["«Never sell work below sustainable economics just to win the logo.»"]},{"heading":"523. GOLDEN RULE #7","paragraphs":["«Out-of-scope is as important as scope.»"]},{"heading":"524. GOLDEN RULE #8","paragraphs":["«A proposal should make the customer's decision easier, not just describe our services.»"]},{"heading":"525. GOLDEN RULE #9","paragraphs":["«Sales can only commit to what Delivery can actually deliver.»"]}]],["Σημεία 526–528 · GOLDEN RULE #10",[{"heading":"526. GOLDEN RULE #10","paragraphs":["«A large contract is not a good contract if the economics, risk and responsibilities are bad.»"]},{"heading":"527. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ PROPOSAL ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["CONFIRMED PROBLEM ↓ DEFINED OUTCOME ↓ VALIDATED SCOPE ↓ TECHNICAL INPUT ↓ DELIVERY ESTIMATE ↓ RISK / ASSUMPTIONS ↓ COMMERCIAL MODEL ↓ MARGIN CHECK ↓ INTERNAL APPROVAL ↓ CUSTOMER PROPOSAL ↓ LIVE PRESENTATION ↓ CUSTOMER QUESTIONS ↓ NEGOTIATION ↓ GIVE / GET ↓ FINAL SCOPE ↓ CONTRACT / SOW ↓ PO ↓ SALES → DELIVERY HANDOFF."]},{"heading":"528. Η ΜΙΑ ΦΡΑΣΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΘΥΜΑΤΑΙ Ο ΠΩΛΗΤΗΣ","paragraphs":["«Δεν στέλνω προσφορά για να δείξω μία τιμή. Στέλνω προσφορά όταν μπορώ να εξηγήσω με καθαρό τρόπο ποιο πρόβλημα λύνουμε, τι ακριβώς θα παραδώσουμε, τι χρειάζεται από τον πελάτη, ποιο ρίσκο αναλαμβάνουμε και ποια εμπορική συμφωνία επιτρέπει και στον πελάτη να πάρει αξία και στη DISTILLOGIC να παραδώσει σωστά και κερδοφόρα.» ΑΥΤΟ ΕΙΝΑΙ ENTERPRISE COMMERCIAL STRATEGY."]}]],["Πριν απαντήσεις στο quiz",["Ξανασκέψου το εισαγωγικό περιστατικό. Ποιο γεγονός είναι επιβεβαιωμένο, ποια πληροφορία λείπει και ποια ενέργεια θα μείωνε την αβεβαιότητα; Μία απάντηση μπορεί να ακούγεται εμπορικά ελκυστική αλλά να προηγείται της απαιτούμενης επιβεβαίωσης.","Οι δύο ερωτήσεις εφαρμογής γενικών αρχών συνδέονται και με τις προαιρετικές «Γενικές σημειώσεις». Το PDF βρίσκεται μόνιμα στο μενού, δεν αποτελεί ξεχωριστό υποχρεωτικό μάθημα και η ανάγνωσή του δεν βαθμολογείται.","Προσαρμοστική πώληση σημαίνει καλύτερη κατανόηση, όχι διαφορετική αλήθεια. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Adaptive Selling.","Η αναγνώριση μοτίβου δεν αντικαθιστά την επιβεβαίωση της συγκεκριμένης περίπτωσης. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Active Listening."]]],"scenario":["Ο πελάτης ζητά χαμηλότερη τιμή διατηρώντας όλο το scope και συντομότερη παράδοση, ενώ η τεχνική ομάδα δεν έχει εκτιμήσει τις αλλαγές.","Διευκρίνιση προτεραιοτήτων και αξιολόγηση επιλογών scope/χρόνου/κόστους πριν από εξουσιοδοτημένη δέσμευση. Οι εμπορικές παραχωρήσεις πρέπει να είναι εκτελέσιμες και εγκεκριμένες."],"minutes":36,"version":1,"additional_curriculum":37,"question_rows":[["Ο πελάτης ζητά χαμηλότερη τιμή διατηρώντας όλο το scope και συντομότερη παράδοση, ενώ η τεχνική ομάδα δεν έχει εκτιμήσει τις αλλαγές. Ποια κίνηση προστατεύει την αξιοπιστία της πρότασης;","Διευκρίνιση προτεραιοτήτων και αξιολόγηση επιλογών scope/χρόνου/κόστους πριν από εξουσιοδοτημένη δέσμευση.","Αποδοχή όλων επειδή ο μεγάλος πελάτης θα φέρει μελλοντική δουλειά.","Μείωση τιμής και μεταφορά του κόστους σιωπηρά στην υλοποίηση.","Υπόσχεση παράδοσης τώρα και επαναδιαπραγμάτευση μετά την υπογραφή.","Οι εμπορικές παραχωρήσεις πρέπει να είναι εκτελέσιμες και εγκεκριμένες."],["Ο πελάτης ζητά χαμηλότερη τιμή διατηρώντας όλο το scope και συντομότερη παράδοση, ενώ η τεχνική ομάδα δεν έχει εκτιμήσει τις αλλαγές. Ποιο στοιχείο πρέπει να περιλαμβάνει η προσφορά;","Παραδοτέα, εξαιρέσεις, προϋποθέσεις, ευθύνες, κριτήρια αποδοχής και εμπορικούς όρους.","Μόνο τελική τιμή και εντυπωσιακές εικόνες.","Όλες τις πιθανές λειτουργίες χωρίς διαχωρισμό.","Αόριστη υπόσχεση πλήρους αυτοματοποίησης.","Το σαφές αντικείμενο μειώνει τον κίνδυνο διαφορετικών προσδοκιών."],["Ο πελάτης ζητά χαμηλότερη τιμή διατηρώντας όλο το scope και συντομότερη παράδοση, ενώ η τεχνική ομάδα δεν έχει εκτιμήσει τις αλλαγές. Μια αλλαγή μετά την έγκριση αφορά χρόνο πληρωμής. Τι χρειάζεται;","Νέα ελεγχόμενη έκδοση και η αντίστοιχη έγκριση των αλλαγμένων όρων.","Απλή αντικατάσταση του PDF με την παλιά έγκριση.","Προφορική σημείωση μόνο στο ημερολόγιο του πωλητή.","Καμία ενέργεια επειδή δεν άλλαξε η τιμή.","Οι όροι πληρωμής είναι ουσιώδες μέρος της εγκεκριμένης πρότασης."],["Ο τεχνικός και ο οικονομικός υπεύθυνος θέλουν διαφορετική παρουσίαση της ίδιας πρότασης. Τι προσαρμόζεις;","Γλώσσα, βάθος και παραδείγματα στον ρόλο, κρατώντας ίδιες τις αληθείς δυνατότητες, τους όρους και τους περιορισμούς.","Τις πραγματικές δυνατότητες ώστε κάθε συνομιλητής να ακούσει αυτό που επιθυμεί.","Τους εγκεκριμένους όρους χωρίς εσωτερική έγκριση.","Την ύπαρξη τεχνικού ρίσκου μόνο στον τεχνικό, κρύβοντάς το από τον οικονομικό αγοραστή.","Προσαρμοστική πώληση σημαίνει καλύτερη κατανόηση, όχι διαφορετική αλήθεια. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Adaptive Selling."],["Σε meeting ο πελάτης περιγράφει καθυστέρηση, ενώ εσύ αναγνωρίζεις μια γνώριμη χρήση του προϊόντος. Ποια αντίδραση διατηρεί ενεργητική ακρόαση;","Συνοψίζω όσα άκουσα, ζητώ επιβεβαίωση και διερευνώ επίπτωση πριν συνδέσω τη λύση.","Διακόπτω για demo επειδή γνωρίζω ήδη την κατάλληλη λειτουργία.","Συμπληρώνω μόνος μου τα άγνωστα από προηγούμενο πελάτη.","Μεταφέρω τη συζήτηση στην τιμή πριν καταλάβω τη διαδικασία.","Η αναγνώριση μοτίβου δεν αντικαθιστά την επιβεβαίωση της συγκεκριμένης περίπτωσης. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Active Listening."]],"source_note":"Πηγή: ΜΑΘΗΜΑ 31.docx, κεφάλαιο 55. Διατηρείται το κείμενο των αριθμημένων σημείων, με ενοποίηση των σπασμένων γραμμών και αφαίρεση επαναλαμβανόμενης μορφοποίησης. Τα παραδείγματα δεν αλλάζουν τους κανόνες της εφαρμογής."},"di-enterprise-56":{"pillar":"distillogic","title":"56. CRM pipeline και προβλέψεις πωλήσεων","goal":"Να αναγνωρίζεις πραγματικές ανάγκες, να διερευνάς τα στοιχεία και να επιλέγεις υπεύθυνο επόμενο βήμα.","sections":[["Από την έννοια στην επαγγελματική πράξη",["Ευκαιρία δηλώνεται Commit επειδή ο πελάτης είπε ότι του αρέσει η λύση, αλλά δεν έχουν επιβεβαιωθεί προμήθειες, εγκρίσεις ή επόμενο βήμα.","Στη μελέτη που ακολουθεί σύνδεσε κάθε πιθανή λύση με συγκεκριμένη διαδικασία, υπεύθυνο, επίπτωση και στοιχεία που μπορούν να επαληθευτούν. Η τεχνική δυνατότητα, η οικονομική αξία και η εξουσιοδότηση για απόφαση είναι διαφορετικά ερωτήματα. Τα παραδείγματα του κεφαλαίου σε βοηθούν να τα διερευνάς χωρίς να υπόσχεσαι κάτι που δεν έχει εγκριθεί.","Η ύλη περιγράφει ενδεικτικές επιχειρηματικές ανάγκες και μεθόδους πώλησης. Δεν αποτελεί κατάλογο έτοιμων λειτουργιών των δύο CRM, δεσμευτική προσφορά, αλλαγή αμοιβών ή νέα πολιτική πιστοποίησης. Για πραγματική εργασία ισχύουν οι εγκεκριμένοι εταιρικοί όροι και οι αρμοδιότητες. Το μάθημα 60 είναι προετοιμασία, όχι δεύτερη επίσημη τελική εξέταση."]],["Το αντικείμενο του κεφαλαίου",["Πώς οργανώνουμε Accounts, Opportunities, Stages, Next Steps και Forecast χωρίς να κοροϊδεύουμε τον εαυτό μας"]],["Σημεία 1–25 · Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ",[{"heading":"1. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ","paragraphs":["CRM: δεν είναι: ΤΗΛΕΦΩΝΙΚΟΣ ΚΑΤΑΛΟΓΟΣ. Είναι: ΣΥΣΤΗΜΑ ΕΛΕΓΧΟΥ ΤΗΣ ΕΜΠΟΡΙΚΗΣ ΠΡΑΓΜΑΤΙΚΟΤΗΤΑΣ."]},{"heading":"2. ΤΟ CRM ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΑΠΑΝΤΑ","paragraphs":["Ποια accounts δουλεύουμε; Ποιος τα owns; Με ποιους μιλάμε; Τι πρόβλημα έχει επιβεβαιωθεί; Σε ποιο stage βρίσκεται κάθε opportunity; Ποιο είναι το επόμενο βήμα; Πότε; Ποιος το κάνει; Πόσο πιθανό είναι πραγματικά να κλείσει;"]},{"heading":"3. BAD CRM","paragraphs":["Company: ABC SA. Contact: John. Status: Interested."]},{"heading":"4. USELESS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"5. GOOD CRM","paragraphs":["Account: ABC SA."]},{"heading":"6. Account Owner:","paragraphs":["Maria."]},{"heading":"7. Tier:","paragraphs":["A."]},{"heading":"8. Trigger:","paragraphs":["New warehouse expansion."]},{"heading":"9. Confirmed Pain:","paragraphs":["Client status requests require manual WMS/TMS reconciliation."]},{"heading":"10. Business Impact:","paragraphs":["40+ support requests/day."]},{"heading":"11. Champion:","paragraphs":["Head of Customer Operations."]},{"heading":"12. Economic Buyer:","paragraphs":["COO."]},{"heading":"13. Technical Stakeholder:","paragraphs":["CIO."]},{"heading":"14. Stage:","paragraphs":["Discovery Complete."]},{"heading":"15. Next Step:","paragraphs":["Technical workshop."]},{"heading":"16. Date:","paragraphs":["October 14."]},{"heading":"17. Objective:","paragraphs":["Validate WMS/TMS integration and pilot scope."]},{"heading":"18. THIS","paragraphs":["is useful CRM."]},{"heading":"19. ACCOUNT ≠ OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["Very important."]},{"heading":"20. ACCOUNT","paragraphs":["is: company/organization."]},{"heading":"21. OPPORTUNITY","paragraphs":["is: specific commercial project."]},{"heading":"22. Example:","paragraphs":["Account: BigLogistics SA."]},{"heading":"23. Opportunity 1:","paragraphs":["Customer portal."]},{"heading":"24. Opportunity 2:","paragraphs":["Warehouse automation."]},{"heading":"25. Opportunity 3:","paragraphs":["Data platform."]}]],["Σημεία 26–50 · Same account:",[{"heading":"26. Same account:","paragraphs":["multiple opportunities."]},{"heading":"27. ONE ACCOUNT","paragraphs":["should have: ONE ACCOUNT STRATEGY."]},{"heading":"28. Not:","paragraphs":["random salespeople: opening random opportunities."]},{"heading":"29. ACCOUNT OWNER","paragraphs":["is responsible for: Relationship coordination Stakeholder map Account strategy Opportunity coordination Internal communication."]},{"heading":"30. ACCOUNT OWNER","paragraphs":["doesn't have to: do everything."]},{"heading":"31. But knows:","paragraphs":["everything important happening: in account."]},{"heading":"32. CRM RULE #1","paragraphs":["NO ACCOUNT WITHOUT OWNER."]},{"heading":"33. CRM RULE #2","paragraphs":["NO OPPORTUNITY WITHOUT NEXT STEP."]},{"heading":"34. CRM RULE #3","paragraphs":["NO NEXT STEP WITHOUT DATE."]},{"heading":"35. CRM RULE #4","paragraphs":["NO FORECAST WITHOUT EVIDENCE."]},{"heading":"36. CRM RULE #5","paragraphs":["NEVER WRITE ASSUMPTION AS FACT."]},{"heading":"37. ACCOUNT RECORD","paragraphs":["Should include: Company Name Industry Size Geography Tier Owner Website Strategic Importance."]},{"heading":"38. ALSO","paragraphs":["Current relationship Existing projects Key stakeholders Known systems Triggers Account notes."]},{"heading":"39. TIER A","paragraphs":["Strategic."]},{"heading":"40. Requires:","paragraphs":["deep research."]},{"heading":"41. TIER B","paragraphs":["Good fit."]},{"heading":"42. Worth:","paragraphs":["structured effort."]},{"heading":"43. TIER C","paragraphs":["Exploratory/lower priority."]},{"heading":"44. Why tiering?","paragraphs":["Because: time is limited."]},{"heading":"45. You cannot:","paragraphs":["treat: 500 accounts: as Tier A."]},{"heading":"46. CONTACT RECORD","paragraphs":["Should include: Name Role Department Email Phone LinkedIn Relationship Strength."]},{"heading":"47. ALSO","paragraphs":["Stakeholder Type Influence Attitude Last Contact Next Action."]},{"heading":"48. STAKEHOLDER TYPE","paragraphs":["Could be: Champion Problem Owner User Technical Buyer Economic Buyer Procurement Blocker."]},{"heading":"49. CONTACT RECORD","paragraphs":["should not say only: «Nice guy.»"]},{"heading":"50. Need:","paragraphs":["business relevance."]}]],["Σημεία 51–75 · OPPORTUNITY RECORD",[{"heading":"51. OPPORTUNITY RECORD","paragraphs":["Core fields: Opportunity Name Account Owner Value Stage Expected Close Date Probability Next Step."]},{"heading":"52. Enterprise opportunities also need:","paragraphs":["Confirmed Pain Metrics Why Now Champion Economic Buyer Decision Process Competition Technical Fit Procurement Process."]},{"heading":"53. OPPORTUNITY NAME","paragraphs":["Bad: «ABC Deal.»"]},{"heading":"54. Better:","paragraphs":["«ABC — Warehouse Client Portal Phase 1.»"]},{"heading":"55. Clear.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"56. STAGES","paragraphs":["Pipeline stages: must represent: CUSTOMER PROGRESS. Not: seller activity."]},{"heading":"57. BAD STAGE","paragraphs":["«Email Sent.»"]},{"heading":"58. That's activity.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"59. Better stage:","paragraphs":["Target Account Engaged Discovery Qualified Solution Validation Proposal Commercial / Procurement Commit Closed Won Closed Lost."]},{"heading":"60. STAGE 1","paragraphs":["TARGET ACCOUNT We identified: potential account."]},{"heading":"61. Need:","paragraphs":["research."]},{"heading":"62. No opportunity value:","paragraphs":["should automatically be forecast."]},{"heading":"63. STAGE 2","paragraphs":["ENGAGED Meaning: meaningful response/conversation exists."]},{"heading":"64. NOT","paragraphs":["LinkedIn connection accepted."]},{"heading":"65. NOT","paragraphs":["email opened."]},{"heading":"66. Need:","paragraphs":["real interaction."]},{"heading":"67. STAGE 3","paragraphs":["DISCOVERY Customer: is discussing: process/problem."]},{"heading":"68. We are learning:","paragraphs":["pain, impact, stakeholders."]},{"heading":"69. STAGE 4","paragraphs":["QUALIFIED Must have: confirmed business problem."]},{"heading":"70. Also:","paragraphs":["reason to act."]},{"heading":"71. And:","paragraphs":["credible path: toward decision."]},{"heading":"72. QUALIFIED DOES NOT MEAN","paragraphs":["«They liked the idea.»"]},{"heading":"73. STAGE 5","paragraphs":["SOLUTION VALIDATION Includes: Technical discovery Workshop PoC definition Architecture validation Business-case validation."]},{"heading":"74. STAGE 6","paragraphs":["PROPOSAL Proposal: has been: requested/appropriate and: presented."]},{"heading":"75. Not:","paragraphs":["random PDF sent."]}]],["Σημεία 76–100 · STAGE 7",[{"heading":"76. STAGE 7","paragraphs":["COMMERCIAL / PROCUREMENT Customer: is actively: working toward purchase."]},{"heading":"77. Could include:","paragraphs":["Negotiation Legal Security Vendor onboarding Procurement."]},{"heading":"78. STAGE 8","paragraphs":["COMMIT Use carefully."]},{"heading":"79. Means:","paragraphs":["strong evidence: that deal is expected to close."]},{"heading":"80. Need:","paragraphs":["clear remaining steps."]},{"heading":"81. Not:","paragraphs":["«Customer said probably yes.»"]},{"heading":"82. STAGE 9","paragraphs":["CLOSED WON Only when: commercial agreement: is complete enough: to start."]},{"heading":"83. Depending business:","paragraphs":["signed contract/PO."]},{"heading":"84. CLOSED LOST","pa