"paragraphs":["Could track: Calls Emails Meetings."]},{"heading":"341. Useful:","paragraphs":["for coaching."]},{"heading":"342. But:","paragraphs":["not: final sales outcome."]},{"heading":"343. OUTCOME METRICS","paragraphs":["Qualified opportunities Pipeline Win rate Revenue Margin Sales cycle."]},{"heading":"344. QUALITY METRICS","paragraphs":["Champion rate Economic buyer access Next-step coverage Stage aging Forecast accuracy."]},{"heading":"345. NEXT-STEP COVERAGE","paragraphs":["Percentage of active opportunities: with: specific future next action."]},{"heading":"346. If:","paragraphs":["only 40%: have next step, pipeline health: poor."]},{"heading":"347. FORECAST ACCURACY","paragraphs":["Compare: forecast: vs actual."]},{"heading":"348. Example:","paragraphs":["forecast €500k. Actual €250k."]},{"heading":"349. Need ask:","paragraphs":["why?"]},{"heading":"350. Common reasons:","paragraphs":["Close dates too optimistic Weak qualification Procurement ignored Proposal ≠ decision Zombie deals."]}]],["Σημεία 351–375 · Forecast accuracy:",[{"heading":"351. Forecast accuracy:","paragraphs":["improves: with discipline."]},{"heading":"352. NOT","paragraphs":["by: pressuring sellers: to guess better."]},{"heading":"353. SALES TARGET","paragraphs":["should not: cause: fake CRM."]},{"heading":"354. Culture matters.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"355. If seller punished:","paragraphs":["for closing bad deal: lost, they may: hide reality."]},{"heading":"356. Management should reward:","paragraphs":["accurate qualification."]},{"heading":"357. Even:","paragraphs":["early disqualification."]},{"heading":"358. Because:","paragraphs":["saves: time."]},{"heading":"359. PIPELINE GENERATION","paragraphs":["Need balance: Existing pipeline progression and New pipeline creation."]},{"heading":"360. Seller cannot:","paragraphs":["spend: 100% time: chasing old deals."]},{"heading":"361. Otherwise:","paragraphs":["future quarter: empty."]},{"heading":"362. PIPELINE BY TIME HORIZON","paragraphs":["Current quarter."]},{"heading":"363. Next quarter.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"364. Longer-term strategic.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"365. This helps:","paragraphs":["planning."]},{"heading":"366. ENTERPRISE DEAL","paragraphs":["may start: now but close: in six months."]},{"heading":"367. That's okay.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"368. Don't force:","paragraphs":["wrong close date: to hit quarter."]},{"heading":"369. ACCOUNT PLANNING","paragraphs":["Separate from: opportunity management."]},{"heading":"370. Account plan asks:","paragraphs":["Where can relationship grow? Who are key stakeholders? What strategic initiatives exist?"]},{"heading":"371. Opportunity asks:","paragraphs":["Is there a real project? What value? What decision?"]},{"heading":"372. Keep distinction.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"373. LOST DEAL REVIEW","paragraphs":["After important loss: do: short review."]},{"heading":"374. Ask:","paragraphs":["Why did we lose? Was opportunity qualified? Did we know decision criteria? Did we have champion? Was our scope right? Was pricing issue real? What do we learn?"]},{"heading":"375. No blame.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 376–400 · Learn.",[{"heading":"376. Learn.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"377. WON DEAL REVIEW","paragraphs":["Also useful."]},{"heading":"378. Ask:","paragraphs":["Why did customer choose us? What mattered most? Which stakeholder helped? What nearly stopped deal?"]},{"heading":"379. Then:","paragraphs":["improve process."]},{"heading":"380. CRM CLOSED-WON","paragraphs":["Should trigger: Sales → Delivery handoff."]},{"heading":"381. Include:","paragraphs":["Final proposal SOW PO Stakeholders Scope Assumptions Risks Promises made."]},{"heading":"382. CRM should preserve:","paragraphs":["commercial truth."]},{"heading":"383. HANDOFF FIELD","paragraphs":["Useful: «What must Delivery know before kickoff?»"]},{"heading":"384. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"385. EXPANSION OPPORTUNITIES","paragraphs":["Do not create: automatically: after close."]},{"heading":"386. Wait:","paragraphs":["for: real signal."]},{"heading":"387. Example:","paragraphs":["customer asks: additional integration."]},{"heading":"388. That's:","paragraphs":["new opportunity."]},{"heading":"389. CUSTOMER HEALTH","paragraphs":["could be tracked: for existing accounts."]},{"heading":"390. Example:","paragraphs":["Delivery health Relationship health Commercial health Expansion signals."]},{"heading":"391. But:","paragraphs":["don't overcomplicate: early CRM."]},{"heading":"392. START SIMPLE","paragraphs":["and useful."]},{"heading":"393. DISTILLOGIC BASIC CRM STRUCTURE","paragraphs":["Could have:"]},{"heading":"394. ACCOUNTS","paragraphs":["Company-level."]},{"heading":"395. CONTACTS","paragraphs":["People."]},{"heading":"396. OPPORTUNITIES","paragraphs":["Projects."]},{"heading":"397. ACTIVITIES","paragraphs":["Calls/emails/meetings."]},{"heading":"398. TASKS","paragraphs":["Next actions."]},{"heading":"399. PROPOSALS","paragraphs":["Commercial docs/status."]},{"heading":"400. ACCOUNT TIERS","paragraphs":["A/B/C."]}]],["Σημεία 401–425 · PIPELINE DASHBOARD",[{"heading":"401. PIPELINE DASHBOARD","paragraphs":["Should show: Open pipeline Qualified pipeline Stage distribution Forecast Close dates Stale deals."]},{"heading":"402. MANAGEMENT DASHBOARD","paragraphs":["Could show: Pipeline by seller Pipeline by stage New pipeline created Win rate Sales cycle Forecast accuracy."]},{"heading":"403. ALSO","paragraphs":["Opportunities without next step Opportunities with close date slipped Tier A account activity."]},{"heading":"404. THIS","paragraphs":["helps management: see issues."]},{"heading":"405. DON'T BUILD","paragraphs":["dashboard: with 100 charts."]},{"heading":"406. Focus:","paragraphs":["action."]},{"heading":"407. EXAMPLE ALERT","paragraphs":["7 opportunities over €50k have no future meeting scheduled."]},{"heading":"408. Useful.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"409. EXAMPLE ALERT","paragraphs":["4 Commit deals have unknown Economic Buyer."]},{"heading":"410. Very useful.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"411. EXAMPLE ALERT","paragraphs":["35% of Proposal-stage deals have been there more than 60 days."]},{"heading":"412. Useful.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"413. CRM AUTOMATION IDEA","paragraphs":["When opportunity: moves to Proposal, require: Confirmed scope Economic Buyer Decision Process Next step."]},{"heading":"414. Good governance.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"415. But don't create:","paragraphs":["bureaucracy: for tiny deals."]},{"heading":"416. Enterprise-specific controls:","paragraphs":["appropriate."]},{"heading":"417. ROLEPLAY 1","paragraphs":["Salesperson: «This deal is 80%.» Manager: «Why?»"]},{"heading":"418. Bad answer:","paragraphs":["«They loved us.»"]},{"heading":"419. Good answer:","paragraphs":["«Business and technical teams approved the scope, CFO confirmed budget, procurement review is booked for Tuesday and only legal terms remain.»"]},{"heading":"420. Evidence.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"421. ROLEPLAY 2","paragraphs":["Salesperson: «Close date is end of month.» Manager: «What customer event makes that date credible?»"]},{"heading":"422. Seller:","paragraphs":["must answer."]},{"heading":"423. ROLEPLAY 3","paragraphs":["Salesperson: «Client asked for proposal.» Manager: «Do we know decision criteria?»"]},{"heading":"424. If no:","paragraphs":["proposal may be premature."]},{"heading":"425. ROLEPLAY 4","paragraphs":["Salesperson: «We have a champion.» Manager: «What has that person actually done?»"]}]],["Σημεία 426–450 · Strong question.",[{"heading":"426. Strong question.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"427. ROLEPLAY 5","paragraphs":["Salesperson: «They don't answer.» Manager: «Why is it still open?»"]},{"heading":"428. Exactly.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"429. ROLEPLAY 6","paragraphs":["Salesperson: «It's strategic.» Manager: «What makes it strategic?»"]},{"heading":"430. Need:","paragraphs":["reason."]},{"heading":"431. ROLEPLAY 7","paragraphs":["Salesperson: «I think budget exists.» Manager: «Fact or assumption?»"]},{"heading":"432. Excellent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"433. ROLEPLAY 8","paragraphs":["Salesperson: «CEO is interested.» Manager: «Is CEO the Economic Buyer for this project or simply supportive?»"]},{"heading":"434. Different.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"435. ROLEPLAY 9","paragraphs":["Salesperson: «No competitor.» Manager: «What about internal build or doing nothing?»"]},{"heading":"436. Competition:","paragraphs":["broader."]},{"heading":"437. ROLEPLAY 10","paragraphs":["Salesperson: «Proposal sent.» Manager: «When is proposal review meeting?»"]},{"heading":"438. If none:","paragraphs":["risk."]},{"heading":"439. ROLEPLAY 11","paragraphs":["Seller: «Customer will sign after security.» Manager: «Has Security reviewed anything yet?»"]},{"heading":"440. If no:","paragraphs":["big unknown."]},{"heading":"441. ROLEPLAY 12","paragraphs":["Seller: «Procurement is just formality.» Manager: «What evidence do we have?»"]},{"heading":"442. Never dismiss:","paragraphs":["paper process."]},{"heading":"443. PIPELINE REVIEW SCORECARD","paragraphs":["Pain evidence __/5"]},{"heading":"444. Stakeholder coverage","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"445. Decision-process clarity","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"446. Technical/commercial readiness","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"447. Next-step quality","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"448. Forecast credibility","paragraphs":["__/5"]},{"heading":"449. TOTAL","paragraphs":["__/30."]},{"heading":"450. 26–30","paragraphs":["Healthy deal."]}]],["Σημεία 451–475 · 21–25",[{"heading":"451. 21–25","paragraphs":["Promising."]},{"heading":"452. 16–20","paragraphs":["Risky."]},{"heading":"453. Below 16","paragraphs":["Probably not forecastable."]},{"heading":"454. CRM DISCIPLINE EXAM","paragraphs":["Salesperson receives: 10 opportunities."]},{"heading":"455. Must decide:","paragraphs":["Keep Move stage Move close date Nurture Close lost."]},{"heading":"456. Goal:","paragraphs":["clean reality."]},{"heading":"457. Not:","paragraphs":["maximize pipeline number."]},{"heading":"458. EXAM CASE","paragraphs":["Opportunity: €100k."]},{"heading":"459. Last contact:","paragraphs":["90 days ago."]},{"heading":"460. No next meeting.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"461. Customer:","paragraphs":["«We'll revisit later.»"]},{"heading":"462. Correct:","paragraphs":["not: Commit."]},{"heading":"463. Likely:","paragraphs":["nurture/close lost for now."]},{"heading":"464. SECOND CASE","paragraphs":["€50k."]},{"heading":"465. Discovery complete.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"466. Champion active.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"467. Technical workshop:","paragraphs":["next week."]},{"heading":"468. Qualified/solution validation.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"469. THIRD CASE","paragraphs":["€250k."]},{"heading":"470. Proposal sent.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"471. No Economic Buyer contact.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"472. Procurement unknown.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"473. High risk.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"474. Don't forecast:","paragraphs":["as near-certain."]},{"heading":"475. FOURTH CASE","paragraphs":["€80k."]}]],["Σημεία 476–491 · Procurement complete.",[{"heading":"476. Procurement complete.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"477. Contract final.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"478. PO date confirmed.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"479. Strong:","paragraphs":["Commit."]},{"heading":"480. CRM GOLDEN RULE #1","paragraphs":["«If it's not in the CRM, the company cannot reliably act on it.»"]},{"heading":"481. GOLDEN RULE #2","paragraphs":["«Pipeline must represent opportunities, not hopes.»"]},{"heading":"482. GOLDEN RULE #3","paragraphs":["«Stage is based on customer evidence, not seller activity.»"]},{"heading":"483. GOLDEN RULE #4","paragraphs":["«Every active opportunity needs a specific future next step.»"]},{"heading":"484. GOLDEN RULE #5","paragraphs":["«A close date without a customer-backed path is fiction.»"]},{"heading":"485. GOLDEN RULE #6","paragraphs":["«Unknown is better than invented.»"]},{"heading":"486. GOLDEN RULE #7","paragraphs":["«A large pipeline with weak qualification is dangerous, not impressive.»"]},{"heading":"487. GOLDEN RULE #8","paragraphs":["«Forecast accuracy matters more than optimism.»"]},{"heading":"488. GOLDEN RULE #9","paragraphs":["«A deal that should be closed-lost should not be kept alive to protect pipeline numbers.»"]},{"heading":"489. GOLDEN RULE #10","paragraphs":["«CRM exists to improve decisions, not to create administration for its own sake.»"]},{"heading":"490. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ CRM ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["SELECT ACCOUNT ↓ ASSIGN OWNER ↓ RESEARCH / TIER ↓ CREATE CONTACTS ↓ LOG ENGAGEMENT ↓ CREATE OPPORTUNITY ONLY WHEN REAL NEED EMERGES ↓ DISCOVERY ↓ RECORD PAIN / IMPACT / WHY NOW ↓ MAP STAKEHOLDERS ↓ SET STAGE FROM EVIDENCE ↓ DEFINE SPECIFIC NEXT STEP ↓ UPDATE CLOSE DATE FROM REAL BUYING PROCESS ↓ QUALIFY WITH MEDDPICC ↓ REVIEW RISKS ↓ FORECAST ONLY WHAT IS SUPPORTED ↓ CLEAN STALE DEALS ↓ CLOSE WON / LOST ACCURATELY ↓ LEARN FROM RESULTS ↓ HAND OFF WON DEALS TO DELIVERY."]},{"heading":"491. Η ΜΙΑ ΦΡΑΣΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΘΥΜΑΤΑΙ Η ΟΜΑΔΑ","paragraphs":["«Το CRM δεν υπάρχει για να δείχνουμε ότι έχουμε πολλά deals. Υπάρχει για να ξέρουμε ποια εταιρεία δουλεύουμε, ποιο πραγματικό πρόβλημα προσπαθούμε να λύσουμε, ποιος παίρνει την απόφαση, ποιο είναι το επόμενο συγκεκριμένο βήμα και αν έχουμε πραγματικά στοιχεία ότι το deal μπορεί να κλείσει. Αν το CRM δείχνει αυτό που θέλουμε να συμβεί αντί για αυτό που συμβαίνει, τότε δεν έχουμε pipeline — έχουμε φαντασία.» ΑΥΤΟ ΕΙΝΑΙ ENTERPRISE PIPELINE MANAGEMENT."]}]],["Πριν απαντήσεις στο quiz",["Ξανασκέψου το εισαγωγικό περιστατικό. Ποιο γεγονός είναι επιβεβαιωμένο, ποια πληροφορία λείπει και ποια ενέργεια θα μείωνε την αβεβαιότητα; Μία απάντηση μπορεί να ακούγεται εμπορικά ελκυστική αλλά να προηγείται της απαιτούμενης επιβεβαίωσης.","Οι δύο ερωτήσεις εφαρμογής γενικών αρχών συνδέονται και με τις προαιρετικές «Γενικές σημειώσεις». Το PDF βρίσκεται μόνιμα στο μενού, δεν αποτελεί ξεχωριστό υποχρεωτικό μάθημα και η ανάγνωσή του δεν βαθμολογείται.","Η καλή σχέση δεν αποδεικνύει εσωτερική επιρροή. Εξετάζουμε πράξεις, πρόσβαση και γνώση της διαδικασίας. Γενικές σημειώσεις: B2B και χαρτογράφηση εμπλεκομένων.","Η αβεβαιότητα επιλογής μειώνεται με σαφήνεια και διαχείριση κινδύνου, όχι κατ’ ανάγκη με περισσότερες επιλογές. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Buyer Indecision."]]],"scenario":["Ευκαιρία δηλώνεται Commit επειδή ο πελάτης είπε ότι του αρέσει η λύση, αλλά δεν έχουν επιβεβαιωθεί προμήθειες, εγκρίσεις ή επόμενο βήμα.","Καταγράφω την πραγματική ένδειξη ενδιαφέροντος και τα κενά, χωρίς να παρουσιάζω βέβαιο κλείσιμο. Το forecast απαιτεί αποδεικτικά στοιχεία, όχι αισιοδοξία ή πίεση στόχου."],"minutes":32,"version":1,"additional_curriculum":37,"question_rows":[["Ευκαιρία δηλώνεται Commit επειδή ο πελάτης είπε ότι του αρέσει η λύση, αλλά δεν έχουν επιβεβαιωθεί προμήθειες, εγκρίσεις ή επόμενο βήμα. Ποια διόρθωση είναι τεκμηριωμένη;","Καταγράφω την πραγματική ένδειξη ενδιαφέροντος και τα κενά, χωρίς να παρουσιάζω βέβαιο κλείσιμο.","Κρατώ Commit για να μην επηρεαστεί ο στόχος μήνα.","Κλείνω τη συμφωνία ως won και αλλάζω αργότερα αν χρειαστεί.","Διαγράφω την ευκαιρία επειδή η αβεβαιότητα δεν επιτρέπεται.","Το forecast απαιτεί αποδεικτικά στοιχεία, όχι αισιοδοξία ή πίεση στόχου."],["Ευκαιρία δηλώνεται Commit επειδή ο πελάτης είπε ότι του αρέσει η λύση, αλλά δεν έχουν επιβεβαιωθεί προμήθειες, εγκρίσεις ή επόμενο βήμα. Ποια διαφορά έχει το pipeline από το forecast;","Το pipeline οργανώνει ευκαιρίες· το forecast εκτιμά αποτελέσματα με συγκεκριμένα στοιχεία και χρονικό ορίζοντα.","Είναι τα ίδια ποσά με διαφορετικό χρώμα.","Το forecast περιλαμβάνει μόνο όλες τις εταιρείες της λίστας στόχων.","Το pipeline περιέχει μόνο υπογεγραμμένες και πληρωμένες συμφωνίες.","Η ύπαρξη ευκαιρίας δεν σημαίνει προβλεπόμενο έσοδο στην ίδια περίοδο."],["Ευκαιρία δηλώνεται Commit επειδή ο πελάτης είπε ότι του αρέσει η λύση, αλλά δεν έχουν επιβεβαιωθεί προμήθειες, εγκρίσεις ή επόμενο βήμα. Ποια καταχώριση βελτιώνει τη συνέχεια;","Επόμενη ενέργεια, ιδιοκτήτης, ημερομηνία και τεκμήριο συμφωνίας με τον πελάτη.","Μόνο υψηλό ποσοστό πιθανότητας.","Μόνο μεγάλο εκτιμώμενο ποσό.","Μόνο σημείωση «καλό meeting».","Η συγκεκριμένη δέσμευση είναι χρησιμότερη από γενική εντύπωση."],["Σε σύνθετη πώληση ο συνομιλητής απαντά πάντα γρήγορα, αλλά δεν μπορεί να φέρει άλλους αρμοδίους ή να εξηγήσει τη διαδικασία απόφασης. Πώς τον αξιολογείς;","Ως χρήσιμη επαφή, με ακόμη ανεπιβεβαίωτη δυνατότητα να λειτουργήσει ως εσωτερικός υποστηρικτής της απόφασης.","Ως ισχυρό champion, επειδή η ταχύτητα απάντησης αποδεικνύει επιρροή.","Ως οικονομικό αγοραστή, επειδή διαθέτει χρόνο για συζήτηση.","Ως ακατάλληλη επαφή που πρέπει να διαγραφεί άμεσα.","Η καλή σχέση δεν αποδεικνύει εσωτερική επιρροή. Εξετάζουμε πράξεις, πρόσβαση και γνώση της διαδικασίας. Γενικές σημειώσεις: B2B και χαρτογράφηση εμπλεκομένων."],["Έχεις δύο συμβατές λύσεις και ο πελάτης καθυστερεί από φόβο λανθασμένης επιλογής. Ποια παρέμβαση βοηθά περισσότερο;","Συγκρίνω τις δύο σε συμφωνημένα κριτήρια, εξηγώ το σκεπτικό μιας σύστασης και προτείνω ελεγχόμενο επόμενο βήμα.","Προσθέτω άλλες πέντε λύσεις ώστε να αισθανθεί πλήρη ελευθερία.","Προσφέρω έκπτωση χωρίς να συζητήσω τον φόβο της απόφασης.","Παρουσιάζω τον φόβο ως απόδειξη ότι δεν έχει πραγματική ανάγκη.","Η αβεβαιότητα επιλογής μειώνεται με σαφήνεια και διαχείριση κινδύνου, όχι κατ’ ανάγκη με περισσότερες επιλογές. Γενικές σημειώσεις: Buyer Indecision."]],"source_note":"Πηγή: ΜΑΘΗΜΑ 31.docx, κεφάλαιο 56. Διατηρείται το κείμενο των αριθμημένων σημείων, με ενοποίηση των σπασμένων γραμμών και αφαίρεση επαναλαμβανόμενης μορφοποίησης. Τα παραδείγματα δεν αλλάζουν τους κανόνες της εφαρμογής."},"di-enterprise-57":{"pillar":"distillogic","title":"57. Διοίκηση πωλήσεων και coaching","goal":"Να αναγνωρίζεις πραγματικές ανάγκες, να διερευνάς τα στοιχεία και να επιλέγεις υπεύθυνο επόμενο βήμα.","sections":[["Από την έννοια στην επαγγελματική πράξη",["Πωλητής πραγματοποιεί πολλές κλήσεις αλλά λίγες χρήσιμες συναντήσεις. Ο Team Leader πρέπει να εντοπίσει τι χρειάζεται βελτίωση.","Στη μελέτη που ακολουθεί σύνδεσε κάθε πιθανή λύση με συγκεκριμένη διαδικασία, υπεύθυνο, επίπτωση και στοιχεία που μπορούν να επαληθευτούν. Η τεχνική δυνατότητα, η οικονομική αξία και η εξουσιοδότηση για απόφαση είναι διαφορετικά ερωτήματα. Τα παραδείγματα του κεφαλαίου σε βοηθούν να τα διερευνάς χωρίς να υπόσχεσαι κάτι που δεν έχει εγκριθεί.","Η ύλη περιγράφει ενδεικτικές επιχειρηματικές ανάγκες και μεθόδους πώλησης. Δεν αποτελεί κατάλογο έτοιμων λειτουργιών των δύο CRM, δεσμευτική προσφορά, αλλαγή αμοιβών ή νέα πολιτική πιστοποίησης. Για πραγματική εργασία ισχύουν οι εγκεκριμένοι εταιρικοί όροι και οι αρμοδιότητες. Το μάθημα 60 είναι προετοιμασία, όχι δεύτερη επίσημη τελική εξέταση."]],["Το αντικείμενο του κεφαλαίου",["ΔΙΟΙΚΗΣΗ ΠΩΛΗΣΕΩΝ, TEAM LEADERS ΚΑΙ ΣΥΣΤΗΜΑ COACHING Πώς χτίζουμε ομάδα πωλήσεων που μαθαίνει, βελτιώνεται και προστατεύει τα strategic accounts"]],["Σημεία 1–25 · Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ",[{"heading":"1. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ","paragraphs":["Team Leader: δεν είναι: Ο ΚΑΛΥΤΕΡΟΣ ΠΩΛΗΤΗΣ ΤΗΣ ΟΜΑΔΑΣ. Είναι: Ο ΑΝΘΡΩΠΟΣ ΠΟΥ ΚΑΝΕΙ ΚΑΛΥΤΕΡΟΥΣ ΤΟΥΣ ΥΠΟΛΟΙΠΟΥΣ ΠΩΛΗΤΕΣ."]},{"heading":"2. TEAM LEADER RESPONSIBILITIES","paragraphs":["Coaching Pipeline review Account protection Quality control Escalation Training Performance management CRM discipline."]},{"heading":"3. Ο TEAM LEADER ΔΕΝ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ","paragraphs":["να παίρνει: όλα τα καλά deals: για τον εαυτό του."]},{"heading":"4. Ο ΡΟΛΟΣ ΤΟΥ","paragraphs":["είναι: να κάνει: την ομάδα: stronger."]},{"heading":"5. SALES MANAGEMENT","paragraphs":["δεν είναι: «Πόσα τηλέφωνα έκανες;»"]},{"heading":"6. SALES MANAGEMENT","paragraphs":["είναι: «Τι έμαθες;» «Ποιο account προχώρησε;» «Ποιο pain επιβεβαίωσες;» «Ποιο είναι το επόμενο βήμα;»"]},{"heading":"7. ACTIVITY","paragraphs":["≠ PROGRESS."]},{"heading":"8. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["100 calls. No qualified conversations."]},{"heading":"9. Another salesperson:","paragraphs":["10 targeted calls. 2 discoveries. 1 qualified opportunity."]},{"heading":"10. Who performed better?","paragraphs":["Probably: second."]},{"heading":"11. BUT","paragraphs":["activity still matters: because: without activity: no pipeline."]},{"heading":"12. We need:","paragraphs":["QUALITY + CONSISTENCY."]},{"heading":"13. TEAM LEADER HAS 5 MAIN JOBS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"14. JOB 1","paragraphs":["PROTECT THE BRAND"]},{"heading":"15. JOB 2","paragraphs":["DEVELOP PEOPLE"]},{"heading":"16. JOB 3","paragraphs":["IMPROVE DEAL QUALITY"]},{"heading":"17. JOB 4","paragraphs":["MAINTAIN PIPELINE DISCIPLINE"]},{"heading":"18. JOB 5","paragraphs":["ESCALATE RISKS EARLY"]},{"heading":"19. BRAND PROTECTION","paragraphs":["means: salespeople do not: Lie Overpromise Spam Fake references Invent capabilities Promise price/timeline alone."]},{"heading":"20. Team Leader:","paragraphs":["must stop: bad behavior: immediately."]},{"heading":"21. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Salesperson tells customer: «Ναι, μπορούμε να κάνουμε SAP integration σε δύο εβδομάδες.»"]},{"heading":"22. Without technical validation.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"23. Team Leader:","paragraphs":["must correct."]},{"heading":"24. Not after:","paragraphs":["proposal."]},{"heading":"25. Immediately.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 26–50 · SECOND JOB",[{"heading":"26. SECOND JOB","paragraphs":["COACHING"]},{"heading":"27. Coaching:","paragraphs":["is not: «Κάν' το καλύτερα.»"]},{"heading":"28. Coaching must be:","paragraphs":["specific."]},{"heading":"29. Bad coaching:","paragraphs":["«Μίλα με περισσότερη αυτοπεποίθηση.»"]},{"heading":"30. Better:","paragraphs":["«Στο πρώτο λεπτό μίλησες 50 δευτερόλεπτα χωρίς να κάνεις ερώτηση. Στο επόμενο call θέλω trigger + hypothesis + question μέσα σε 30 δευτερόλεπτα.»"]},{"heading":"31. ACTIONABLE","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"32. COACHING LOOP","paragraphs":["OBSERVE ↓ IDENTIFY ↓ EXPLAIN ↓ PRACTICE ↓ REPEAT ↓ MEASURE."]},{"heading":"33. OBSERVE","paragraphs":["Listen to: real calls or: roleplays."]},{"heading":"34. IDENTIFY","paragraphs":["one or two: specific weaknesses."]},{"heading":"35. Don't correct:","paragraphs":["20 things at once."]},{"heading":"36. EXPLAIN","paragraphs":["why it matters."]},{"heading":"37. PRACTICE","paragraphs":["again."]},{"heading":"38. REPEAT","paragraphs":["until: natural."]},{"heading":"39. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Weakness: salesperson pitches too early."]},{"heading":"40. Coach says:","paragraphs":["«For the next three roleplays, you are not allowed to explain a solution until you've discovered process, pain and impact.»"]},{"heading":"41. Excellent drill.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"42. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["Weakness: seller asks shallow questions."]},{"heading":"43. Drill:","paragraphs":["customer says: «Our process is slow.»"]},{"heading":"44. Seller must ask:","paragraphs":["five follow-up questions: without pitching."]},{"heading":"45. ANOTHER","paragraphs":["Weakness: seller discounts quickly."]},{"heading":"46. Drill:","paragraphs":["manager says: «You're 20% too expensive.»"]},{"heading":"47. Seller must:","paragraphs":["clarify: before offering concession."]},{"heading":"48. COACHING SHOULD BE","paragraphs":["based on: behavior."]},{"heading":"49. Not personality.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"50. Don't say:","paragraphs":["«You aren't a natural salesperson.»"]}]],["Σημεία 51–75 · Say:",[{"heading":"51. Say:","paragraphs":["«You need more practice in discovery follow-up.»"]},{"heading":"52. Behavior:","paragraphs":["can improve."]},{"heading":"53. WEEKLY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM","paragraphs":["A strong sales team: needs rhythm."]},{"heading":"54. MONDAY","paragraphs":["Pipeline / priorities."]},{"heading":"55. TUESDAY","paragraphs":["Prospecting review."]},{"heading":"56. WEDNESDAY","paragraphs":["Roleplay / call coaching."]},{"heading":"57. THURSDAY","paragraphs":["Strategic account review."]},{"heading":"58. FRIDAY","paragraphs":["Results / lessons / next week."]},{"heading":"59. This is example.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"60. Company can:","paragraphs":["adapt."]},{"heading":"61. MONDAY PIPELINE REVIEW","paragraphs":["Questions: What moved last week? What must move this week? Which deal is stuck? Which account needs management support?"]},{"heading":"62. Don't review:","paragraphs":["every tiny detail."]},{"heading":"63. Focus:","paragraphs":["important opportunities."]},{"heading":"64. WEEKLY PRIORITIES","paragraphs":["Each salesperson: should have: 3–5 priorities."]},{"heading":"65. Example:","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"1. Complete technical workshop for Account A.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"2. Reach COO at Account B.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"3. Create 2 new qualified opportunities.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"66. Better than:","paragraphs":["«Make more calls.»"]},{"heading":"67. TUESDAY PROSPECTING REVIEW","paragraphs":["Review: Target accounts Research quality Trigger Stakeholder Message."]},{"heading":"68. Team Leader asks:","paragraphs":["«Why this account?»"]},{"heading":"69. Then:","paragraphs":["«Why this person?»"]},{"heading":"70. Then:","paragraphs":["«Why now?»"]},{"heading":"71. If seller:","paragraphs":["can't answer: do not: contact Tier A."]},{"heading":"72. WEDNESDAY CALL COACHING","paragraphs":["Listen to: calls."]}]],["Σημεία 76–100 · Score:",[{"heading":"73. Score:","paragraphs":["Opening Relevance Question quality Listening Objection handling Next step."]},{"heading":"74. Pick:","paragraphs":["one improvement goal."]},{"heading":"75. Example:","paragraphs":["«This week focus only on asking better follow-up questions.»"]},{"heading":"76. THURSDAY STRATEGIC ACCOUNT REVIEW","paragraphs":["For Tier A: review: Account map Stakeholder gaps Current opportunity Risks Multi-threading Next executive action."]},{"heading":"77. FRIDAY REVIEW","paragraphs":["Ask: What worked? What didn't? What did we learn? What changes next week?"]},{"heading":"78. Continuous improvement.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"79. TEAM LEADER MUST KNOW","paragraphs":["difference between: COACHING and MANAGEMENT."]},{"heading":"80. MANAGEMENT","paragraphs":["sets: expectations, targets, accountability."]},{"heading":"81. COACHING","paragraphs":["helps: person improve skill."]},{"heading":"82. Example management:","paragraphs":["«All CRM opportunities must have next step by Friday.»"]},{"heading":"83. Coaching:","paragraphs":["«Let's practice how to secure a specific next step at the end of discovery.»"]},{"heading":"84. Both:","paragraphs":["needed."]},{"heading":"85. ONE-TO-ONE MEETING","paragraphs":["Each salesperson: regularly."]},{"heading":"86. Could be:","paragraphs":["30–45 minutes."]},{"heading":"87. Structure:","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"88. 1. Results","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"89. 2. Pipeline","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"90. 3. Skill development","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"91. 4. Obstacles","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"92. 5. Support needed","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"93. 6. Commitments.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"94. Don't make:","paragraphs":["one-to-one: only numbers."]},{"heading":"95. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which sales situation is hardest for you right now?»"]},{"heading":"96. Great coaching question.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"97. Ask:","paragraphs":["«Which account do you feel least confident approaching? Why?»"]}]],["Σημεία 101–125 · This reveals:",[{"heading":"98. This reveals:","paragraphs":["skill gaps."]},{"heading":"99. PERFORMANCE METRICS","paragraphs":["Need: balanced scorecard."]},{"heading":"100. Not only:","paragraphs":["revenue."]},{"heading":"101. CATEGORY 1","paragraphs":["ACTIVITY Examples: Calls Emails Research completed Meetings."]},{"heading":"102. CATEGORY 2","paragraphs":["QUALITY Discovery quality CRM completeness Next-step quality Stakeholder coverage."]},{"heading":"103. CATEGORY 3","paragraphs":["PIPELINE Qualified opportunities Pipeline created Pipeline progression Stage aging."]},{"heading":"104. CATEGORY 4","paragraphs":["OUTCOMES Revenue Margin Win rate Closed won."]},{"heading":"105. CATEGORY 5","paragraphs":["BEHAVIOR Teamwork Account discipline Honesty Brand protection."]},{"heading":"106. Don't reward:","paragraphs":["seller: who hits revenue: by: destroying margin or: lying."]},{"heading":"107. SALES QUALITY","paragraphs":["is: part of performance."]},{"heading":"108. EXAMPLE SCORECARD","paragraphs":["Revenue: 30%."]},{"heading":"109. Qualified pipeline:","paragraphs":["25%."]},{"heading":"110. Opportunity progression:","paragraphs":["15%."]},{"heading":"111. CRM/account discipline:","paragraphs":["10%."]},{"heading":"112. Skill quality:","paragraphs":["10%."]},{"heading":"113. Team/brand behavior:","paragraphs":["10%."]},{"heading":"114. Example only.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"115. Company must define:","paragraphs":["actual model."]},{"heading":"116. EARLY-STAGE SALESPERSON","paragraphs":["should not be judged: mainly on revenue."]},{"heading":"117. Because:","paragraphs":["enterprise sales cycle: may be long."]},{"heading":"118. Early KPIs:","paragraphs":["Research quality Relevant conversations Discoveries Qualified opportunities."]},{"heading":"119. Experienced seller:","paragraphs":["more outcome responsibility."]},{"heading":"120. KPI DANGER","paragraphs":["If you pay only: per meeting: salesperson books: bad meetings."]},{"heading":"121. If you pay only:","paragraphs":["per lead: quality collapses."]},{"heading":"122. If only revenue:","paragraphs":["seller may: discount too much."]}]],["Σημεία 126–150 · Incentives create:",[{"heading":"123. Incentives create:","paragraphs":["behavior."]},{"heading":"124. Team Leader must understand this.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"125. TARGET SETTING","paragraphs":["Targets should be: challenging but: connected to: funnel mathematics."]},{"heading":"126. Example","paragraphs":["Goal: €1M annual sales."]},{"heading":"127. Average deal:","paragraphs":["€100k."]},{"heading":"128. Need:","paragraphs":["10 wins."]},{"heading":"129. If win rate:","paragraphs":["25%."]},{"heading":"130. Need:","paragraphs":["~40 qualified opportunities."]},{"heading":"131. Then:","paragraphs":["how many discoveries?"]},{"heading":"132. How many conversations?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"133. How many target accounts?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"134. Work backwards.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"135. This is:","paragraphs":["sales capacity planning."]},{"heading":"136. DON'T SET","paragraphs":["«Do €1M.» without: funnel logic."]},{"heading":"137. FORECAST COACHING","paragraphs":["Manager asks: «Why is this Commit?»"]},{"heading":"138. Seller:","paragraphs":["must provide: evidence."]},{"heading":"139. Team Leader:","paragraphs":["must challenge: optimism."]},{"heading":"140. But not:","paragraphs":["destroy confidence."]},{"heading":"141. Say:","paragraphs":["«I like the account. I'm challenging the forecast, not the opportunity.»"]},{"heading":"142. Good distinction.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"143. FORECAST SHOULD BE","paragraphs":["accurate."]},{"heading":"144. Not:","paragraphs":["motivational."]},{"heading":"145. PIPELINE REVIEW MISTAKE","paragraphs":["Manager says: «Move it to Commit. We need the number.»"]},{"heading":"146. Terrible.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"147. CRM should not:","paragraphs":["serve fantasy."]}]],["Σημεία 151–175 · If management corrupts CRM:",[{"heading":"148. If management corrupts CRM:","paragraphs":["salespeople stop trusting: system."]},{"heading":"149. TEAM LEADER SHOULD PROTECT","paragraphs":["data integrity."]},{"heading":"150. ACCOUNT REVIEW","paragraphs":["For strategic account: ask: What changed in account? Who do we know? Who do we not know? What do they care about? What are they doing strategically? Where is opportunity?"]},{"heading":"151. Don't ask:","paragraphs":["only: «How much is the deal?»"]},{"heading":"152. ACCOUNT RELATIONSHIP","paragraphs":["may be: worth: years."]},{"heading":"153. Deal:","paragraphs":["one event."]},{"heading":"154. TIER A REVIEW","paragraphs":["should include: stakeholder heatmap."]},{"heading":"155. Example:","paragraphs":["COO: Supportive."]},{"heading":"156. CIO:","paragraphs":["Neutral."]},{"heading":"157. Procurement:","paragraphs":["Unknown."]},{"heading":"158. CFO:","paragraphs":["No relationship."]},{"heading":"159. This tells:","paragraphs":["team: what to do next."]},{"heading":"160. TEAM LEADER AND MULTI-THREADING","paragraphs":["Ensure: multiple contacts: but: coordinated."]},{"heading":"161. No random:","paragraphs":["LinkedIn messages: from 4 salespeople."]},{"heading":"162. One account owner:","paragraphs":["controls strategy."]},{"heading":"163. TEAM LEADER AND TIER A","paragraphs":["Before: new seller contacts Tier A: approve: Message Stakeholder Objective."]},{"heading":"164. Not micromanagement.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"165. Brand protection.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"166. TIER C","paragraphs":["More freedom."]},{"heading":"167. Learning environment.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"168. SELLER DEVELOPMENT LEVELS","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"169. LEVEL 1","paragraphs":["PROSPECTING TRAINEE Can: research, identify stakeholders, write simple outreach."]},{"heading":"170. Cannot:","paragraphs":["lead strategic meeting alone."]},{"heading":"171. LEVEL 2","paragraphs":["SDR / JUNIOR SELLER Can: cold outreach, qualify basic relevance, book discovery."]},{"heading":"172. Still needs:","paragraphs":["coaching."]}]],["Σημεία 176–200 · LEVEL 3",[{"heading":"173. LEVEL 3","paragraphs":["ACCOUNT EXECUTIVE Can: run discovery, qualify, manage proposal."]},{"heading":"174. LEVEL 4","paragraphs":["SENIOR ENTERPRISE SELLER Can: multi-thread, business case, procurement, negotiation."]},{"heading":"175. LEVEL 5","paragraphs":["STRATEGIC ACCOUNT LEAD Can: manage: complex group relationship, executive stakeholders, multi-opportunity account."]},{"heading":"176. PROMOTION","paragraphs":["should be: skill-based."]},{"heading":"177. Not:","paragraphs":["just: time served."]},{"heading":"178. CERTIFICATION","paragraphs":["before seller: handles Tier A."]},{"heading":"179. Could require:","paragraphs":["passing: Cold call test Discovery test Objection test Proposal test CRM test."]},{"heading":"180. Great idea.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"181. TIER A CERTIFICATION EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Seller must score: ≥25/30: in discovery roleplay."]},{"heading":"182. ≥25/30:","paragraphs":["objection roleplay."]},{"heading":"183. CRM:","paragraphs":["no major errors."]},{"heading":"184. Then:","paragraphs":["can join Tier A meetings."]},{"heading":"185. First:","paragraphs":["with Team Leader."]},{"heading":"186. Later:","paragraphs":["alone."]},{"heading":"187. This protects:","paragraphs":["strategic accounts."]},{"heading":"188. CALL REVIEW SYSTEM","paragraphs":["Team Leader picks: 2–3 calls/week: per seller."]},{"heading":"189. Not only:","paragraphs":["bad calls."]},{"heading":"190. Review:","paragraphs":["good calls too."]},{"heading":"191. Ask seller first:","paragraphs":["«How do you think it went?»"]},{"heading":"192. Let them:","paragraphs":["self-assess."]},{"heading":"193. Then:","paragraphs":["coach."]},{"heading":"194. CALL REVIEW FORMAT","paragraphs":["What worked? What missed? One improvement. Repeat roleplay."]},{"heading":"195. Don't lecture:","paragraphs":["30 minutes."]},{"heading":"196. Practice:","paragraphs":["is better."]},{"heading":"197. ROLEPLAY LIBRARY","paragraphs":["Team should have: scenarios."]}]],["Σημεία 201–225 · Examples:",[{"heading":"198. Examples:","paragraphs":["Busy COO Skeptical CIO Procurement negotiator Friendly non-decision-maker CFO demanding ROI Customer wanting AI."]},{"heading":"199. Rotate.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"200. ROLEPLAY SHOULD FEEL","paragraphs":["difficult."]},{"heading":"201. Not:","paragraphs":["customer agreeing: to everything."]},{"heading":"202. Manager gives:","paragraphs":["partial information."]},{"heading":"203. Seller must:","paragraphs":["discover."]},{"heading":"204. DISCOVERY ROLEPLAY SCORING","paragraphs":["Opening Process mapping Follow-ups Quantification Stakeholders Next step."]},{"heading":"205. OBJECTION ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Listen Clarify Respond Protect value Next step."]},{"heading":"206. PROPOSAL ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Customer says: budget lower."]},{"heading":"207. Seller must:","paragraphs":["phase, scope, trade."]},{"heading":"208. NEGOTIATION ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Procurement: asks: 20% discount."]},{"heading":"209. Seller uses:","paragraphs":["Give/Get."]},{"heading":"210. CRM ROLEPLAY","paragraphs":["Seller gets: 10 messy deals."]},{"heading":"211. Must:","paragraphs":["clean pipeline."]},{"heading":"212. COACHING SCOREBOARD","paragraphs":["For each salesperson: track: Prospecting Discovery Qualification Technical/business communication Objections Proposal Negotiation CRM."]},{"heading":"213. Score:","paragraphs":["1–5."]},{"heading":"214. Example","paragraphs":["Prospecting: 4."]},{"heading":"215. Discovery:","paragraphs":["2."]},{"heading":"216. Objections:","paragraphs":["3."]},{"heading":"217. CRM:","paragraphs":["5."]},{"heading":"218. Coaching focus:","paragraphs":["Discovery."]},{"heading":"219. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"220. Don't train:","paragraphs":["everyone: same way."]},{"heading":"221. Person A:","paragraphs":["needs tone."]},{"heading":"222. Person B:","paragraphs":["needs business understanding."]}]],["Σημεία 226–250 · Person C:",[{"heading":"223. Person C:","paragraphs":["needs closing."]},{"heading":"224. Personalized coaching.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"225. SALES TRAINING","paragraphs":["should never end: after onboarding."]},{"heading":"226. Continuous:","paragraphs":["weekly."]},{"heading":"227. Why?","paragraphs":["Because: markets, industries, customers: change."]},{"heading":"228. INDUSTRY TRAINING","paragraphs":["Each seller: should master: few sectors: first."]},{"heading":"229. Example:","paragraphs":["Seller A: Manufacturing + Logistics."]},{"heading":"230. Seller B:","paragraphs":["Hospitality + Retail."]},{"heading":"231. Seller C:","paragraphs":["Banking + Insurance."]},{"heading":"232. Over time:","paragraphs":["expand."]},{"heading":"233. Why?","paragraphs":["Deep understanding: beats: generic pitch."]},{"heading":"234. INDUSTRY CERTIFICATION","paragraphs":["Ask seller: «Explain the customer process without mentioning software.»"]},{"heading":"235. If they can't:","paragraphs":["they don't: understand industry."]},{"heading":"236. Great test.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"237. Example:","paragraphs":["Logistics seller: must explain: Order → warehouse → picking → dispatch → delivery."]},{"heading":"238. Manufacturing:","paragraphs":["plan → production → quality → warehouse."]},{"heading":"239. Banking:","paragraphs":["application → KYC → risk → approval → servicing."]},{"heading":"240. Then:","paragraphs":["identify: typical pains."]},{"heading":"241. TEAM LEADER SHOULD TEST","paragraphs":["industry vocabulary."]},{"heading":"242. But:","paragraphs":["not for memorization."]},{"heading":"243. For:","paragraphs":["conversation credibility."]},{"heading":"244. WEEKLY KNOWLEDGE SESSION","paragraphs":["20–30 minutes."]},{"heading":"245. One seller:","paragraphs":["teaches: one sector/problem."]},{"heading":"246. Example:","paragraphs":["«How does warehouse order flow work?»"]},{"heading":"247. Team learns.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 251–275 · Peer teaching:",[{"heading":"248. Peer teaching:","paragraphs":["powerful."]},{"heading":"249. WIN SHARE","paragraphs":["When seller wins: present: why."]},{"heading":"250. What trigger?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"251. What pain?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"252. What champion?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"253. What objection?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"254. Why customer chose us?","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"255. This creates:","paragraphs":["organizational learning."]},{"heading":"256. LOST DEAL SHARE","paragraphs":["Same."]},{"heading":"257. Without:","paragraphs":["shaming."]},{"heading":"258. Ask:","paragraphs":["What did we miss? What would we do differently?"]},{"heading":"259. No blame culture.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"260. But:","paragraphs":["accountability."]},{"heading":"261. DIFFERENCE","paragraphs":["No-blame: doesn't mean: no standards."]},{"heading":"262. Example:","paragraphs":["Seller repeatedly: doesn't update CRM."]},{"heading":"263. That's:","paragraphs":["performance issue."]},{"heading":"264. Not:","paragraphs":["learning issue forever."]},{"heading":"265. PERFORMANCE MANAGEMENT","paragraphs":["Step 1: Clear expectation."]},{"heading":"266. Step 2:","paragraphs":["Coaching."]},{"heading":"267. Step 3:","paragraphs":["Measurement."]},{"heading":"268. Step 4:","paragraphs":["Improvement plan."]},{"heading":"269. Step 5:","paragraphs":["Decision."]},{"heading":"270. Don't:","paragraphs":["let low performance: continue indefinitely."]},{"heading":"271. But first:","paragraphs":["understand: cause."]},{"heading":"272. Causes:","paragraphs":["Skill Effort Process Targeting Tool Motivation."]}]],["Σημεία 276–300 · Different cause:",[{"heading":"273. Different cause:","paragraphs":["different solution."]},{"heading":"274. Example","paragraphs":["Low meetings."]},{"heading":"275. Could be:","paragraphs":["bad message."]},{"heading":"276. Or:","paragraphs":["not enough calls."]},{"heading":"277. Or:","paragraphs":["bad accounts."]},{"heading":"278. Don't assume:","paragraphs":["laziness."]},{"heading":"279. Diagnose.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"280. TEAM LEADER DISCOVERY","paragraphs":["same logic: as customer discovery."]},{"heading":"281. DATA FIRST","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"282. REP A","paragraphs":["Makes: 50 calls/week."]},{"heading":"283. Gets:","paragraphs":["10 conversations."]},{"heading":"284. 0 meetings.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"285. Problem:","paragraphs":["probably: conversation quality."]},{"heading":"286. REP B","paragraphs":["Makes: 5 calls/week."]},{"heading":"287. Gets:","paragraphs":["1 meeting."]},{"heading":"288. Problem:","paragraphs":["activity volume."]},{"heading":"289. Different coaching.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"290. REP C","paragraphs":["Gets: 10 meetings."]},{"heading":"291. 0 qualified opportunities.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"292. Problem:","paragraphs":["targeting/discovery."]},{"heading":"293. REP D","paragraphs":["Creates: many proposals."]},{"heading":"294. Few wins.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"295. Problem:","paragraphs":["qualification/value/proposal."]},{"heading":"296. FUNNEL COACHING","paragraphs":["Use data: to find: skill gap."]},{"heading":"297. SELLER MOTIVATION","paragraphs":["Not everyone: motivated only: by commission."]}]],["Σημεία 301–325 · Some value:",[{"heading":"298. Some value:","paragraphs":["Growth Recognition Responsibility Learning Money."]},{"heading":"299. Team Leader:","paragraphs":["should know: people."]},{"heading":"300. But:","paragraphs":["management remains: professional."]},{"heading":"301. PRAISE","paragraphs":["should be: specific."]},{"heading":"302. Bad:","paragraphs":["«Good job.»"]},{"heading":"303. Better:","paragraphs":["«You handled the procurement objection well because you clarified whether the issue was budget or price before negotiating.»"]},{"heading":"304. Reinforces behavior.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"305. CORRECTION","paragraphs":["also: specific."]},{"heading":"306. Don't:","paragraphs":["publicly humiliate."]},{"heading":"307. Correct:","paragraphs":["privately: when appropriate."]},{"heading":"308. Team learning:","paragraphs":["can discuss: anonymized mistakes."]},{"heading":"309. MANAGER SHOULD MODEL","paragraphs":["the behavior."]},{"heading":"310. If manager:","paragraphs":["lies, team lies."]},{"heading":"311. If manager:","paragraphs":["pushes fake forecast, team fakes CRM."]},{"heading":"312. If manager:","paragraphs":["discounts instantly, team discounts."]},{"heading":"313. Culture:","paragraphs":["comes: from leadership."]},{"heading":"314. SALES MANAGER MUST NOT SAY","paragraphs":["«I don't care how you get it, just close it.»"]},{"heading":"315. Dangerous.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"316. Better:","paragraphs":["«Win it if it's a good deal and protect the relationship if it isn't.»"]},{"heading":"317. TEAM LEADER ESCALATION","paragraphs":["Seller should know: when to escalate."]},{"heading":"318. Escalate when:","paragraphs":["Technical commitment requested Security question beyond knowledge Legal term Major discount High-risk customer complaint Strategic account issue."]},{"heading":"319. Not every question:","paragraphs":["needs CEO."]},{"heading":"320. Clear escalation ladder.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"321. Example:","paragraphs":["Technical: Solution Architect."]},{"heading":"322. Pricing:","paragraphs":["Commercial Manager."]}]],["Σημεία 326–350 · Legal:",[{"heading":"323. Legal:","paragraphs":["Legal."]},{"heading":"324. Security:","paragraphs":["Security Lead."]},{"heading":"325. Strategic exception:","paragraphs":["CEO."]},{"heading":"326. Seller:","paragraphs":["doesn't need: to know everything."]},{"heading":"327. They need:","paragraphs":["to know: who knows."]},{"heading":"328. INTERNAL SLA","paragraphs":["for sales support: useful."]},{"heading":"329. Example:","paragraphs":["technical presales request: response: within agreed window."]},{"heading":"330. Why?","paragraphs":["Sales cannot: wait: days: without customer update."]},{"heading":"331. PRESALES MANAGEMENT","paragraphs":["Technical team: time: is expensive."]},{"heading":"332. Don't bring:","paragraphs":["Solution Architect: to every cold call."]},{"heading":"333. Gate:","paragraphs":["technical resources."]},{"heading":"334. Example:","paragraphs":["Need: qualified opportunity: before: deep technical workshop."]},{"heading":"335. Protect:","paragraphs":["technical capacity."]},{"heading":"336. BUT","paragraphs":["don't wait too long: if technical feasibility: critical."]},{"heading":"337. Balance.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"338. TEAM LEADER DECIDES","paragraphs":["when: specialist enters."]},{"heading":"339. ACCOUNT ESCALATION","paragraphs":["Strategic prospect: responds: with executive interest."]},{"heading":"340. Team Leader:","paragraphs":["may join."]},{"heading":"341. CEO:","paragraphs":["only: when adds value."]},{"heading":"342. Don't bring CEO:","paragraphs":["just to look big."]},{"heading":"343. Executive involvement:","paragraphs":["must have: purpose."]},{"heading":"344. CEO role might be:","paragraphs":["Executive alignment Strategic commitment Final negotiation."]},{"heading":"345. NOT:","paragraphs":["basic discovery: every time."]},{"heading":"346. TEAM LEADER AND CUSTOMER MEETINGS","paragraphs":["Before meeting: 5-minute prep."]},{"heading":"347. Ask:","paragraphs":["Objective? Participants? Questions? Desired next step?"]}]],["Σημεία 351–375 · After meeting:",[{"heading":"348. After meeting:","paragraphs":["10-minute debrief."]},{"heading":"349. Ask:","paragraphs":["What learned? What changed? What is unknown? Next step?"]},{"heading":"350. This alone:","paragraphs":["improves: sales quality."]},{"heading":"351. PRE-CALL PLAN","paragraphs":["Simple: Account Stage Participants Meeting objective Top 3 questions Desired next step."]},{"heading":"352. POST-CALL REVIEW","paragraphs":["New facts Pain Impact Stakeholders Risks Next action."]},{"heading":"353. TEAM LEADER DOES NOT NEED","paragraphs":["to join: every call."]},{"heading":"354. If they do:","paragraphs":["seller never develops."]},{"heading":"355. Join:","paragraphs":["strategically."]},{"heading":"356. Then:","paragraphs":["seller leads: where appropriate."]},{"heading":"357. MANAGER TAKING OVER CALL","paragraphs":["is bad habit."]},{"heading":"358. Seller asks question.","paragraphs":["Customer hesitates. Manager jumps in."]},{"heading":"359. Seller never learns.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"360. Team Leader:","paragraphs":["should allow: productive struggle."]},{"heading":"361. Unless:","paragraphs":["brand/deal risk."]},{"heading":"362. TEAM LEADER ROLE IN 