ading":"417. Monthly:","paragraphs":["full simulation."]},{"heading":"418. Quarterly:","paragraphs":["certification."]},{"heading":"419. This creates:","paragraphs":["system."]},{"heading":"420. ONBOARDING NEW SELLER","paragraphs":["Week 1: Company + sectors + ethics."]},{"heading":"421. Week 2:","paragraphs":["Research/prospecting."]},{"heading":"422. Week 3:","paragraphs":["Cold outreach."]}]],["Σημεία 426–450 · Week 4:",[{"heading":"423. Week 4:","paragraphs":["Discovery basics."]},{"heading":"424. Then:","paragraphs":["roleplays."]},{"heading":"425. Only after passing:","paragraphs":["live outreach."]},{"heading":"426. Start:","paragraphs":["Tier C."]},{"heading":"427. This is better:","paragraphs":["than: «Here is phone, start calling.»"]},{"heading":"428. SHADOWING","paragraphs":["New seller: listens: experienced calls."]},{"heading":"429. Then:","paragraphs":["takes: part of call."]},{"heading":"430. Then:","paragraphs":["leads: with manager present."]},{"heading":"431. Then:","paragraphs":["independent."]},{"heading":"432. Graduated responsibility.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"433. NEW SELLER CERTIFICATION","paragraphs":["Before live calls: must: Explain DISTILLOGIC simply Give opening Handle 5 objections Log CRM properly."]},{"heading":"434. Before discovery:","paragraphs":["must pass: discovery roleplay."]},{"heading":"435. Before Tier A:","paragraphs":["advanced certification."]},{"heading":"436. TEAM LEADER KPI","paragraphs":["Team Leader also: needs: performance metrics."]},{"heading":"437. Not only:","paragraphs":["team revenue."]},{"heading":"438. Could include:","paragraphs":["Team pipeline quality Forecast accuracy Seller improvement CRM discipline Tier A quality Team retention."]},{"heading":"439. Important:","paragraphs":["if Team Leader: only measured: revenue, they may: take deals: from team."]},{"heading":"440. Need:","paragraphs":["leadership incentives."]},{"heading":"441. TEAM LEADER SHOULD CREATE","paragraphs":["more capable sellers."]},{"heading":"442. SUCCESS:","paragraphs":["team performs: even when leader: not in every call."]},{"heading":"443. LEADERSHIP MATURITY","paragraphs":["Level 1: checks activity."]},{"heading":"444. Level 2:","paragraphs":["checks outcomes."]},{"heading":"445. Level 3:","paragraphs":["coaches skills."]},{"heading":"446. Level 4:","paragraphs":["improves system."]},{"heading":"447. Level 5:","paragraphs":["creates future leaders."]}]],["Σημεία 451–475 · DISTILLOGIC TARGET",[{"heading":"448. DISTILLOGIC TARGET","paragraphs":["Level 4–5."]},{"heading":"449. ROLEPLAY — MANAGER COACHING #1","paragraphs":["Seller: «Customer said we're too expensive.» Bad manager: «Give 10% discount.»"]},{"heading":"450. Good manager:","paragraphs":["«What exactly did they compare us with?»"]},{"heading":"451. ROLEPLAY #2","paragraphs":["Seller: «They don't answer.» Bad manager: «Call more.»"]},{"heading":"452. Good manager:","paragraphs":["«What was the last customer action and why should they reply now?»"]},{"heading":"453. ROLEPLAY #3","paragraphs":["Seller: «I need CEO to join.» Manager: «Why? What value will CEO add to the next meeting?»"]},{"heading":"454. Great.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"455. ROLEPLAY #4","paragraphs":["Seller: «I want to send proposal.» Manager: «What scope has customer confirmed?»"]},{"heading":"456. ROLEPLAY #5","paragraphs":["Seller: «It's 90%.» Manager: «What remains before signature and who confirmed the dates?»"]},{"heading":"457. ROLEPLAY #6","paragraphs":["Seller: «The customer has no budget.» Manager: «Is that confirmed no budget or no current priority?»"]},{"heading":"458. ROLEPLAY #7","paragraphs":["Seller: «I think CIO is the decision-maker.» Manager: «What evidence do you have?»"]},{"heading":"459. ROLEPLAY #8","paragraphs":["Seller: «Customer wants AI.» Manager: «What business task are they trying to improve?»"]},{"heading":"460. Team Leader:","paragraphs":["teaches: thinking."]},{"heading":"461. NOT:","paragraphs":["answers."]},{"heading":"462. COACHING QUESTIONS","paragraphs":["Great coaches ask: What did you notice? Why do you think they said that? What did you miss? What could you ask next? What evidence do you have? What would you do differently?"]},{"heading":"463. These questions:","paragraphs":["develop judgment."]},{"heading":"464. NOT DEPENDENCE","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"465. TEAM LEADER GOLDEN RULE #1","paragraphs":["«Do not manage only activity. Manage quality, progression and learning.»"]},{"heading":"466. GOLDEN RULE #2","paragraphs":["«Coach behavior, not personality.»"]},{"heading":"467. GOLDEN RULE #3","paragraphs":["«Correct one or two things at a time and practice them.»"]},{"heading":"468. GOLDEN RULE #4","paragraphs":["«Protect Tier A accounts from beginner mistakes.»"]},{"heading":"469. GOLDEN RULE #5","paragraphs":["«Never pressure salespeople to falsify pipeline or forecast.»"]},{"heading":"470. GOLDEN RULE #6","paragraphs":["«A Team Leader should make the seller stronger, not take the seller's call away.»"]},{"heading":"471. GOLDEN RULE #7","paragraphs":["«Use funnel data to diagnose the real sales problem.»"]},{"heading":"472. GOLDEN RULE #8","paragraphs":["«Reward good disqualification as well as good closing.»"]}]],["Σημεία 476–479 · GOLDEN RULE #9",[{"heading":"473. GOLDEN RULE #9","paragraphs":["«Escalate technical, legal, security and commercial questions to the right owner.»"]},{"heading":"474. GOLDEN RULE #10","paragraphs":["«The goal is not a team that follows scripts. The goal is a team that thinks correctly.»"]},{"heading":"475. Η ΤΕΛΙΚΗ SALES MANAGEMENT ΡΟΗ","paragraphs":["SET EXPECTATIONS ↓ TRAIN ↓ PRACTICE ↓ OBSERVE REAL BEHAVIOR ↓ COACH SPECIFIC SKILL ↓ MEASURE FUNNEL ↓ REVIEW PIPELINE ↓ CHALLENGE ASSUMPTIONS ↓ PROTECT STRATEGIC ACCOUNTS ↓ ESCALATE SPECIALIST NEEDS ↓ REWARD GOOD BEHAVIOR ↓ CORRECT BAD DISCIPLINE ↓ CERTIFY HIGHER RESPONSIBILITY ↓ DEVELOP FUTURE TEAM LEADERS."]},{"heading":"476. Η ΜΙΑ ΦΡΑΣΗ ΠΟΥ ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΘΥΜΑΤΑΙ Ο TEAM LEADER","paragraphs":["«Η δουλειά μου δεν είναι να κάνω εγώ όλες τις δύσκολες πωλήσεις. Η δουλειά μου είναι να δημιουργήσω πωλητές που μπορούν να ερευνούν σωστά, να κάνουν καλό discovery, να προστατεύουν το brand, να ξεχωρίζουν πραγματικό deal από ψεύτικο pipeline και να χειρίζονται όλο και πιο σημαντικούς accounts χωρίς να χρειάζεται να τους κρατάω το χέρι σε κάθε βήμα.» ΑΥΤΟ ΕΙΝΑΙ ENTERPRISE SALES LEADERSHIP."]}]],["Πριν απαντήσεις στο quiz",["Ξανασκέψου το εισαγωγικό περιστατικό. Ποιο γεγονός είναι επιβεβαιωμένο, ποια πληροφορία λείπει και ποια ενέργεια θα μείωνε την αβεβαιότητα; Μία απάντηση μπορεί να ακούγεται εμπορικά ελκυστική αλλά να προηγείται της απαιτούμενης επιβεβαίωσης.","Οι δύο ερωτήσεις εφαρμογής γενικών αρχών συνδέονται και με τις προαιρετικές «Γενικές σημειώσεις». Το PDF βρίσκεται μόνιμα στο μενού, δεν αποτελεί ξεχωριστό υποχρεωτικό μάθημα και η ανάγνωσή του δεν βαθμολογείται.","Η παραχώρηση εξετάζεται μαζί με αξία, κόστος και εξουσιοδότηση. Γενικές σημειώσεις: διαπραγμάτευση και παραχωρήσεις.","Ανάγκη και χρονική προτεραιότητα δεν είναι το ίδιο. Γενικές σημειώσεις: κόστος αδράνειας και πραγματική δέσμευση."]]],"scenario":["Πωλητής πραγματοποιεί πολλές κλήσεις αλλά λίγες χρήσιμες συναντήσεις. Ο Team Leader πρέπει να εντοπίσει τι χρειάζεται βελτίωση.","Παρατηρώ δείγμα συμπεριφοράς, εντοπίζω συγκεκριμένο κενό, εξασκούμαστε και επανελέγχουμε. Το coaching μετατρέπει παρατήρηση σε συγκεκριμένη αλλαγή δεξιότητας."],"minutes":31,"version":1,"additional_curriculum":37,"question_rows":[["Πωλητής πραγματοποιεί πολλές κλήσεις αλλά λίγες χρήσιμες συναντήσεις. Ο Team Leader πρέπει να εντοπίσει τι χρειάζεται βελτίωση. Ποια προσέγγιση coaching είναι ισχυρότερη;","Παρατηρώ δείγμα συμπεριφοράς, εντοπίζω συγκεκριμένο κενό, εξασκούμαστε και επανελέγχουμε.","Ζητώ περισσότερες κλήσεις χωρίς διερεύνηση της ποιότητας.","Αναλαμβάνω όλες τις επαφές για να ανέβει ο δείκτης της ομάδας.","Συγκρίνω δημόσια τα άτομα χωρίς πλαίσιο.","Το coaching μετατρέπει παρατήρηση σε συγκεκριμένη αλλαγή δεξιότητας."],["Πωλητής πραγματοποιεί πολλές κλήσεις αλλά λίγες χρήσιμες συναντήσεις. Ο Team Leader πρέπει να εντοπίσει τι χρειάζεται βελτίωση. Ποιο συμπέρασμα επιτρέπουν μόνο οι πολλές κλήσεις;","Υπάρχει δραστηριότητα, όχι κατ’ ανάγκη σωστή στόχευση ή αποτελεσματικό discovery.","Ο πωλητής έχει αποδεδειγμένα υψηλή απόδοση σε κάθε στάδιο.","Οι πελάτες είναι ακατάλληλοι χωρίς να εξεταστεί δείγμα.","Δεν χρειάζεται έλεγχος της ποιότητας καταγραφής.","Ο όγκος είναι ένας δείκτης και χρειάζεται συσχέτιση με ποιότητα και μετατροπή."],["Πωλητής πραγματοποιεί πολλές κλήσεις αλλά λίγες χρήσιμες συναντήσεις. Ο Team Leader πρέπει να εντοπίσει τι χρειάζεται βελτίωση. Πώς προστατεύεται η σχέση coaching;","Σαφής παρατήρηση συμπεριφοράς και συμφωνημένο πλάνο, χωρίς προσωπικούς χαρακτηρισμούς.","Αξιολόγηση μόνο βάσει προσωπικής συμπάθειας.","Αφαίρεση ιδιοκτησίας ευκαιριών ως γενικό εργαλείο πίεσης.","Δημόσια έκθεση κάθε αποτυχίας για παραδειγματισμό.","Η ανατροφοδότηση χρειάζεται συγκεκριμένα στοιχεία και σεβασμό."],["Στη διαπραγμάτευση ζητείται μικρότερη τιμή. Ποια παραχώρηση διατηρεί καθαρή εμπορική λογική;","Εγκεκριμένη ανταλλαγή με συγκεκριμένο αντίκρισμα, όπως διαφορετικό scope ή όρους, καταγεγραμμένη στην προσφορά.","Έκπτωση τώρα με αόριστη προσδοκία μελλοντικών έργων.","Μείωση τιμής που θα αντισταθμιστεί με μη συμφωνημένη μείωση ποιότητας.","Προσωρινή τιμή που θα αλλάξει μετά την υπογραφή.","Η παραχώρηση εξετάζεται μαζί με αξία, κόστος και εξουσιοδότηση. Γενικές σημειώσεις: διαπραγμάτευση και παραχωρήσεις."],["Ο πελάτης λέει «το πρόβλημα είναι σημαντικό» αλλά δεν επιθυμεί αλλαγή φέτος. Ποια ερώτηση διερευνά τη χρονική προτεραιότητα χωρίς πίεση;","Τι θα συμβεί αν η διαδικασία παραμείνει όπως είναι και ποιο γεγονός θα έκανε την αλλαγή προτεραιότητα;","Να γράψω ότι συμφωνήσατε για να κρατήσουμε την τιμή;","Θέλετε να χάσετε την ευκαιρία που παίρνουν οι ανταγωνιστές σας;","Αφού υπάρχει πρόβλημα, γιατί δεν υπογράφετε σήμερα;","Ανάγκη και χρονική προτεραιότητα δεν είναι το ίδιο. Γενικές σημειώσεις: κόστος αδράνειας και πραγματική δέσμευση."]],"source_note":"Πηγή: ΜΑΘΗΜΑ 31.docx, κεφάλαιο 57. Διατηρείται το κείμενο των αριθμημένων σημείων, με ενοποίηση των σπασμένων γραμμών και αφαίρεση επαναλαμβανόμενης μορφοποίησης. Τα παραδείγματα δεν αλλάζουν τους κανόνες της εφαρμογής."},"di-enterprise-58":{"pillar":"distillogic","title":"58. Δείκτες απόδοσης και κίνητρα","goal":"Να αναγνωρίζεις πραγματικές ανάγκες, να διερευνάς τα στοιχεία και να επιλέγεις υπεύθυνο επόμενο βήμα.","sections":[["Από την έννοια στην επαγγελματική πράξη",["Ομάδα ανταμείβεται μόνο για τον αριθμό meetings και αρχίζει να κλείνει συναντήσεις χωρίς ανάγκη ή αρμόδιο συνομιλητή.","Στη μελέτη που ακολουθεί σύνδεσε κάθε πιθανή λύση με συγκεκριμένη διαδικασία, υπεύθυνο, επίπτωση και στοιχεία που μπορούν να επαληθευτούν. Η τεχνική δυνατότητα, η οικονομική αξία και η εξουσιοδότηση για απόφαση είναι διαφορετικά ερωτήματα. Τα παραδείγματα του κεφαλαίου σε βοηθούν να τα διερευνάς χωρίς να υπόσχεσαι κάτι που δεν έχει εγκριθεί.","Η ύλη περιγράφει ενδεικτικές επιχειρηματικές ανάγκες και μεθόδους πώλησης. Δεν αποτελεί κατάλογο έτοιμων λειτουργιών των δύο CRM, δεσμευτική προσφορά, αλλαγή αμοιβών ή νέα πολιτική πιστοποίησης. Για πραγματική εργασία ισχύουν οι εγκεκριμένοι εταιρικοί όροι και οι αρμοδιότητες. Το μάθημα 60 είναι προετοιμασία, όχι δεύτερη επίσημη τελική εξέταση."]],["Το αντικείμενο του κεφαλαίου",["KPIs, ΑΜΟΙΒΕΣ, BONUS ΚΑΙ ΑΞΙΟΛΟΓΗΣΗ ΠΩΛΗΤΩΝ Πώς μετράμε απόδοση χωρίς να δημιουργούμε λάθος κίνητρα"]],["Σημεία 1–25 · Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ",[{"heading":"1. Η ΒΑΣΙΚΗ ΑΡΧΗ","paragraphs":["Ό,τι πληρώνεις: συνήθως: παίρνεις περισσότερο."]},{"heading":"2. Αν πληρώνεις:","paragraphs":["μόνο: για meetings, η ομάδα: θα φέρνει: ΠΟΛΛΑ MEETINGS. Όχι απαραίτητα: καλά meetings."]},{"heading":"3. Αν πληρώνεις:","paragraphs":["μόνο: για revenue, κάποιοι πωλητές: μπορεί να: Κάνουν υπερβολικές εκπτώσεις. Υπόσχονται πράγματα που δεν μπορούμε να παραδώσουμε. Κυνηγούν κακά projects."]},{"heading":"4. Άρα:","paragraphs":["ΤΟ COMPENSATION SYSTEM ΔΗΜΙΟΥΡΓΕΙ ΣΥΜΠΕΡΙΦΟΡΑ."]},{"heading":"5. Ο ΣΤΟΧΟΣ","paragraphs":["Δεν θέλουμε: salespeople: που απλώς: κάνουν δραστηριότητα."]},{"heading":"6. Θέλουμε:","paragraphs":["salespeople: που δημιουργούν: ΚΑΛΟ ΚΕΡΔΟΦΟΡΟ BUSINESS."]},{"heading":"7. ΠΡΕΠΕΙ ΝΑ ΜΕΤΡΑΜΕ","paragraphs":["όλη τη διαδρομή: ACTIVITY ↓ CONVERSATION ↓ DISCOVERY ↓ QUALIFIED OPPORTUNITY ↓ PROPOSAL ↓ WIN ↓ REVENUE ↓ MARGIN ↓ HEALTHY CUSTOMER."]},{"heading":"8. KPI CATEGORY 1","paragraphs":["ACTIVITY"]},{"heading":"9. Examples:","paragraphs":["Calls Emails LinkedIn outreach Accounts researched Follow-ups."]},{"heading":"10. Activity:","paragraphs":["είναι: leading indicator."]},{"heading":"11. Δεν είναι:","paragraphs":["τελικό αποτέλεσμα."]},{"heading":"12. 100 calls:","paragraphs":["δεν σημαίνει: 100 καλές προσπάθειες."]},{"heading":"13. Team Leader:","paragraphs":["πρέπει να βλέπει: VOLUME + QUALITY."]},{"heading":"14. ACTIVITY KPI EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Salesperson target: 20 researched calls/day."]},{"heading":"15. Better than:","paragraphs":["100 random calls/day."]},{"heading":"16. ΑΛΛΑ","paragraphs":["το σωστό activity level: εξαρτάται από: Sector Account tier Sales cycle Role."]},{"heading":"17. SDR:","paragraphs":["περισσότερο activity."]},{"heading":"18. Senior enterprise seller:","paragraphs":["λιγότερο, πιο στοχευμένο."]},{"heading":"19. DON'T COMPARE","paragraphs":["Tier A account manager: με: junior outbound researcher: μόνο από call count."]},{"heading":"20. KPI CATEGORY 2","paragraphs":["RELEVANT CONVERSATIONS"]},{"heading":"21. Better KPI:","paragraphs":["πόσες πραγματικές συνομιλίες: με: σωστούς ανθρώπους."]},{"heading":"22. Not:","paragraphs":["«Μίλησα στη γραμματεία.»"]},{"heading":"23. Relevant conversation:","paragraphs":["με: stakeholder: που μπορεί να μας δώσει: business information."]},{"heading":"24. Example:","paragraphs":["Operations Manager."]},{"heading":"25. CIO.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 26–50 · Finance Director.",[{"heading":"26. Finance Director.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"27. KPI:","paragraphs":["Relevant conversations/week."]},{"heading":"28. This begins:","paragraphs":["measuring quality."]},{"heading":"29. KPI CATEGORY 3","paragraphs":["DISCOVERY MEETINGS"]},{"heading":"30. Important distinction:","paragraphs":["Meeting booked ≠ Discovery completed."]},{"heading":"31. Discovery completed:","paragraphs":["when: we learned: Current process Pain Impact Why now Stakeholders Next step."]},{"heading":"32. A meeting where:","paragraphs":["we talked: 20 minutes: about DISTILLOGIC: is not: successful discovery."]},{"heading":"33. KPI:","paragraphs":["Qualified discoveries/month."]},{"heading":"34. Better than:","paragraphs":["meetings/month alone."]},{"heading":"35. KPI CATEGORY 4","paragraphs":["QUALIFIED PIPELINE CREATED"]},{"heading":"36. One of the most important KPIs.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"37. Qualified opportunity:","paragraphs":["must have: Confirmed problem Real stakeholder Meaningful impact Reason to act Credible next step."]},{"heading":"38. Don't create:","paragraphs":["€500k opportunity: because: customer said: «Interesting.»"]},{"heading":"39. Qualified pipeline:","paragraphs":["should be: reviewed: by Team Leader."]},{"heading":"40. KPI EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["€200k new qualified pipeline/month."]},{"heading":"41. Example only.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"42. Actual number:","paragraphs":["must come from: target economics."]},{"heading":"43. KPI CATEGORY 5","paragraphs":["PIPELINE PROGRESSION"]},{"heading":"44. Salesperson:","paragraphs":["should not: only create pipeline."]},{"heading":"45. Must move:","paragraphs":["good opportunities: forward."]},{"heading":"46. Example metric:","paragraphs":["percentage of qualified opportunities: that progress: to solution validation."]},{"heading":"47. Another:","paragraphs":["Qualified → Proposal conversion."]},{"heading":"48. Another:","paragraphs":["Proposal → Win conversion."]},{"heading":"49. If seller:","paragraphs":["creates many opportunities: but none progress, problem exists."]},{"heading":"50. Could be:","paragraphs":["Bad qualification Weak discovery No business case Wrong accounts."]}]],["Σημεία 51–75 · KPI CATEGORY 6",[{"heading":"51. KPI CATEGORY 6","paragraphs":["WIN RATE"]},{"heading":"52. Simple:","paragraphs":["Won opportunities: ÷ relevant closed opportunities."]},{"heading":"53. Example:","paragraphs":["4 won. 6 lost."]},{"heading":"54. Win rate:","paragraphs":["40%."]},{"heading":"55. But:","paragraphs":["need define: which stage: counts."]},{"heading":"56. Don't include:","paragraphs":["every random cold account."]},{"heading":"57. Better:","paragraphs":["measure: Qualified → Won."]},{"heading":"58. Also:","paragraphs":["Proposal → Won."]},{"heading":"59. Different metrics:","paragraphs":["show different things."]},{"heading":"60. LOW QUALIFIED-TO-WIN RATE","paragraphs":["could mean: Bad qualification Weak value proposition Pricing issue Competition Technical fit."]},{"heading":"61. LOW PROPOSAL-TO-WIN","paragraphs":["often means: Proposal too early Poor decision criteria understanding Price/value mismatch Procurement issues."]},{"heading":"62. KPI CATEGORY 7","paragraphs":["SALES CYCLE"]},{"heading":"63. How long:","paragraphs":["from: qualified opportunity: to: closed won/lost."]},{"heading":"64. Example:","paragraphs":["Average: 120 days."]},{"heading":"65. But:","paragraphs":["by sector: may differ."]},{"heading":"66. By deal size:","paragraphs":["also."]},{"heading":"67. Analyze:","paragraphs":["Small projects Mid-size projects Strategic enterprise projects."]},{"heading":"68. Don't pressure:","paragraphs":["a healthy enterprise deal: to close in 30 days: because: dashboard looks bad."]},{"heading":"69. Instead:","paragraphs":["understand: stage aging."]},{"heading":"70. KPI CATEGORY 8","paragraphs":["STAGE AGING"]},{"heading":"71. How long:","paragraphs":["does opportunity: stay in: each stage."]},{"heading":"72. Example:","paragraphs":["Discovery: 20 days."]},{"heading":"73. Proposal:","paragraphs":["60 days."]},{"heading":"74. Procurement:","paragraphs":["45 days."]},{"heading":"75. This reveals:","paragraphs":["bottlenecks."]}]],["Σημεία 76–100 · If proposal stage:",[{"heading":"76. If proposal stage:","paragraphs":["takes: 100 days, maybe: proposal was: too early."]},{"heading":"77. KPI CATEGORY 9","paragraphs":["FORECAST ACCURACY"]},{"heading":"78. Very important:","paragraphs":["for management."]},{"heading":"79. Salesperson says:","paragraphs":["«I will close €300k this quarter.»"]},{"heading":"80. Actual:","paragraphs":["€120k."]},{"heading":"81. Forecast accuracy:","paragraphs":["poor."]},{"heading":"82. Why matters?","paragraphs":["Company plans: Hiring Cash Delivery capacity Revenue."]},{"heading":"83. Forecast:","paragraphs":["is not: game."]},{"heading":"84. KPI:","paragraphs":["Forecast vs actual."]},{"heading":"85. Need measure:","paragraphs":["seller and: team leader."]},{"heading":"86. Because:","paragraphs":["manager: also owns: forecast quality."]},{"heading":"87. KPI CATEGORY 10","paragraphs":["REVENUE"]},{"heading":"88. Revenue:","paragraphs":["is important."]},{"heading":"89. But:","paragraphs":["not alone."]},{"heading":"90. Example:","paragraphs":["Seller A: sells: €1m."]},{"heading":"91. Seller B:","paragraphs":["sells: €800k."]},{"heading":"92. But Seller A:","paragraphs":["uses: huge discounts and: low-margin projects."]},{"heading":"93. Seller B:","paragraphs":["creates: healthy margin."]},{"heading":"94. Seller B:","paragraphs":["may be: better commercial performer."]},{"heading":"95. KPI CATEGORY 11","paragraphs":["GROSS MARGIN"]},{"heading":"96. Critical.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"97. Revenue:","paragraphs":["€100k."]},{"heading":"98. Delivery cost:","paragraphs":["€70k."]},{"heading":"99. Gross margin:","paragraphs":["€30k."]},{"heading":"100. Margin percentage:","paragraphs":["30%."]}]],["Σημεία 101–125 · If Seller:",[{"heading":"101. If Seller:","paragraphs":["wins: many: 10% margin projects, company: may suffer."]},{"heading":"102. Sales should understand:","paragraphs":["GOOD REVENUE."]},{"heading":"103. Don't incentivize:","paragraphs":["revenue: with no margin control."]},{"heading":"104. BONUS","paragraphs":["may include: margin modifier."]},{"heading":"105. Example:","paragraphs":["Full commission: only if: project margin: above internal minimum."]},{"heading":"106. Or:","paragraphs":["commission: lower: if discount: reduces margin."]},{"heading":"107. Actual structure:","paragraphs":["Finance/CEO: should define."]},{"heading":"108. KPI CATEGORY 12","paragraphs":["COLLECTION / PAYMENT QUALITY"]},{"heading":"109. Depending business:","paragraphs":["salesperson: may influence: commercial terms."]},{"heading":"110. A €200k sale:","paragraphs":["with: very bad payment terms: can hurt cash flow."]},{"heading":"111. But salesperson:","paragraphs":["should not: be solely responsible: for collections."]},{"heading":"112. Could track:","paragraphs":["Payment terms quality Overdue invoice awareness Commercial support."]},{"heading":"113. KPI CATEGORY 13","paragraphs":["CUSTOMER RETENTION / EXPANSION"]},{"heading":"114. For account managers:","paragraphs":["important."]},{"heading":"115. Metrics:","paragraphs":["Renewal Expansion revenue Account retention Customer health."]},{"heading":"116. BUT","paragraphs":["don't incentivize: upsell: when delivery: is failing."]},{"heading":"117. Expansion:","paragraphs":["should follow: value."]},{"heading":"118. KPI CATEGORY 14","paragraphs":["CRM DISCIPLINE"]},{"heading":"119. Important:","paragraphs":["but: should not be: huge bonus driver."]},{"heading":"120. Could track:","paragraphs":["Opportunities updated Next steps present Close dates credible Stakeholders recorded."]},{"heading":"121. CRM discipline:","paragraphs":["is: minimum operating standard."]},{"heading":"122. Not necessarily:","paragraphs":["something to pay: large bonus for."]},{"heading":"123. KPI CATEGORY 15","paragraphs":["BRAND / SALES QUALITY"]},{"heading":"124. Includes:","paragraphs":["No overpromising No false claims Professional communication Correct escalation Account protection."]},{"heading":"125. If seller:","paragraphs":["wins revenue: but: creates delivery disaster, their performance: is not excellent."]}]],["Σημεία 126–150 · NEED",[{"heading":"126. NEED","paragraphs":["quality gate."]},{"heading":"127. EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["Seller hits: 120% revenue target."]},{"heading":"128. But:","paragraphs":["2 projects: were mis-sold."]},{"heading":"129. Team:","paragraphs":["must not: automatically rate: top performer."]},{"heading":"130. SALES PERFORMANCE","paragraphs":["should include: WHAT THEY SOLD + HOW THEY SOLD IT."]},{"heading":"131. COMPENSATION STRUCTURE","paragraphs":["Usually: BASE SALARY + VARIABLE."]},{"heading":"132. Base:","paragraphs":["provides: stability."]},{"heading":"133. Variable:","paragraphs":["rewards: commercial outcomes."]},{"heading":"134. Enterprise sales:","paragraphs":["often needs: meaningful base."]},{"heading":"135. Because:","paragraphs":["sales cycle: long."]},{"heading":"136. If variable:","paragraphs":["too dominant: seller may: force: bad deals."]},{"heading":"137. If variable:","paragraphs":["too small: may not: motivate performance."]},{"heading":"138. Balance.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"139. EXAMPLE ONLY","paragraphs":["60–70%: base."]},{"heading":"140. 30–40%:","paragraphs":["variable."]},{"heading":"141. This is:","paragraphs":["illustrative."]},{"heading":"142. Actual package:","paragraphs":["depends on: market, seniority, role."]},{"heading":"143. SDR COMPENSATION","paragraphs":["Should not: depend: only on: closed revenue."]},{"heading":"144. Because SDR:","paragraphs":["doesn't control: full sale."]},{"heading":"145. Better variable components:","paragraphs":["Qualified meetings Qualified pipeline Quality acceptance by AE."]},{"heading":"146. Not:","paragraphs":["raw meetings."]},{"heading":"147. Example:","paragraphs":["Meeting pays: only if: meets qualification criteria."]},{"heading":"148. Prevents:","paragraphs":["calendar spam."]},{"heading":"149. SDR KPI EXAMPLE","paragraphs":["20% activity consistency 30% relevant conversations 30% accepted qualified opportunities 20% pipeline created."]},{"heading":"150. Example only.","paragraphs":[]}]],["Σημεία 151–175 · ACCOUNT EXECUTIVE",[{"heading":"151. ACCOUNT EXECUTIVE","paragraphs":["owns: more: of sales cycle."]},{"heading":"152. Variable could focus:","paragraphs":["Closed revenue Margin Qualified pipeline Forecast quality."]},{"heading":"153. Example:","paragraphs":["60%: closed revenue."]},{"heading":"154. 20%:","paragraphs":["gross-margin quality."]},{"heading":"155. 10%:","paragraphs":["qualified pipeline."]},{"heading":"156. 10%:","paragraphs":["forecast/CRM quality."]},{"heading":"157. Example only.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"158. SENIOR ENTERPRISE SELLER","paragraphs":["May be measured: on: Strategic revenue Margin Multi-year account value Expansion Forecast."]},{"heading":"159. TEAM LEADER","paragraphs":["should not: be compensated: exactly: like salesperson."]},{"heading":"160. Otherwise:","paragraphs":["they compete: with team."]},{"heading":"161. Team Leader variable:","paragraphs":["should depend: more on: TEAM PERFORMANCE."]},{"heading":"162. Could include:","paragraphs":["Team revenue Team margin Forecast accuracy Pipeline quality Development of sellers."]},{"heading":"163. Example:","paragraphs":["40% team revenue."]},{"heading":"164. 20% team margin.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"165. 15% qualified pipeline.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"166. 15% forecast accuracy.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"167. 10% coaching/team quality.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"168. Example only.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"169. TEAM LEADER SHOULD NOT THINK","paragraphs":["«If I take this deal myself, I earn more.»"]},{"heading":"170. Bad design.","paragraphs":[]},{"heading":"171. Compensation:","paragraphs":["should encourage: leader: to help: seller win."]},{"heading":"172. COMMISSION ON R